msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It grew and grew, louder and louder. It drove out every other sensation, it build to a peak and then, crossing some unknown threshold, the feeling exploded."
msgstr "Se hacía más intenso y más intenso. Arrastraba consigo cada otra sensación, subió hasta su punto máximo y luego, al cruzar un umbral desconocido, el placer estalló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It grew, with each passing day, it grew."
msgstr "Creció, con cada día que pasaba, creció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It grinned."
msgstr "Sonrió."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "It had a few Gods, and there lived people that were not very different from Humans."
msgstr "Tenía unos pocos dioses, y vivían personas que no eran muy diferentes de los humanos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had all been for nothing."
msgstr "Todo había sido en vano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had all been stacked and stuffed in the corner of the room. If there was any system to it, it eluded her."
msgstr "Todo había estado apilado y amontonado en la esquina de la habitación. Si existía algún sistema detrás de ello, se le escapaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had all seemd so utterly important, and now it was all dwarfed by the latest proposal."
msgstr "Todo había parecido tan absolutamente importante, y ahora todo era insignificante comparado con la última propuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had already gotten this far...and she needed his help."
msgstr "Ya había llegado tan lejos... y necesitaba su ayuda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had always seemed like a fantasy, but seeing the Khan's mountainous body, it now seemed absurd."
msgstr "Siempre pareció un sueño, pero al ver el cuerpo montañoso del Khan, ahora parecía absurdo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had an almost magnetic pull on her."
msgstr "Tenía un atractivo casi magnético sobre ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been Vaelen who ultimately bore the responsibility."
msgstr "Ha sido Vaelen quien finalmente ha asumido la responsabilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a decent throw."
msgstr "Ha sido un lanzamiento decente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a favorite of herself when she was younger."
msgstr "Fue una de sus favoritas cuando era más joven."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a few weeks since she had last seen Lily."
msgstr "Han pasado unas semanas desde que la vio por última vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a gift from Caleb and Ephraim."
msgstr "Fue un regalo de Caleb y Efraín."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a gift from Kate, one of her old suits of armor."
msgstr "Había sido un regalo de Kate, uno de sus antiguos trajes de armadura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a long day, and she could bear no more."
msgstr "Fue un largo día y no podía soportar más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a long time since Sarah had been in a crowd like this."
msgstr "Hacía mucho tiempo que Sarah no se encontraba en una multitud como esta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a long tradition that the people of Rosanna were permitted to offer up their grievances to their king or queen."
msgstr "Siempre había sido tradición que el pueblo de Rosanna pudiera ofrecer sus quejas a su rey o reina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a mistake to have gotten involved with him, she knew that much."
msgstr "Saber que se había involucrado con él fue un error, lo sabía bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a noble lady's room once, or so Sarah suspected given its extravagent interior, but it was hers now, if only for a time."
msgstr "Antes había sido el cuarto de una dama noble, o eso sospechaba Sarah dada su interior extravagante, pero ahora era suyo, aunque solo por un tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a tribe of orcs and goblins that had captured her, and a good number of them now sat and watched."
msgstr "Había sido una tribu de orcos y goblins quienes la habían capturado, y un buen número de ellos ahora se sentaban y observaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been a very long time, perhaps years, since she'd slept in a bed like this."
msgstr "Había pasado mucho tiempo, quizás años, desde que dormía en una cama como esta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been all too real."
msgstr "Había sido demasiado real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been another one of those things that she had once imagined unthinkable."
msgstr "Había sido otra de esas cosas que alguna vez había imaginado inimaginables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been centuries since the Union had last seen a single leader."
msgstr "Habían pasado siglos desde que la Unión había visto a un único líder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been dangerous. One slip up and who knows what might have happened."
msgstr "Fue peligroso. Un solo error y quién sabe qué podría haber pasado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been designed special for the day, and special for the man, drawing out his martial features, strong face and broad shoulders."
msgstr "Fue diseñado especialmente para el día y para el hombre, resaltando sus rasgos marciales, su rostro fuerte y sus anchos hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been designed with secrecy in mind, giving no space for anyone to hide, but it had unintentionally gave the room a claustrophobic feeling."
msgstr "Fue diseñado con la discreción en mente, sin dejar espacio para que nadie se ocultara, pero tuvo el efecto no deseado de conferirle a la habitación una sensación claustrofóbica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been hard to get to this point, even with an entire army behind her, bringing supplies. The idea of one man managing to survive just for a few days..."
msgstr "Había sido difícil llegar a este punto, incluso con un ejército entero detrás de ella, trayendo suministros. La idea de que un solo hombre lograra sobrevivir solo por unos días..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been here for millenia. The fact that it had endured at all was impressive."
msgstr "Había estado aquí durante milenios. El hecho de que hubiera resistido era impresionante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been in part designed just so that it would come off easy."
msgstr "En parte había sido diseñado para que todo fuera fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been like this ever since the fall of Rosanna to the eastern tribesmen. Everywhere you went, mentioning Rosanna would invite stares of pity."
msgstr "Así había sido desde la caída de Rosanna ante los tribus del este. En cualquier lugar al que fueras, mencionar a Rosanna provocaba miradas de lástima."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been like this over the years, ever since they had first begun their encounter."
msgstr "Así había sido durante años, desde que iniciaron su encuentro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been little over a week since Sarah had convinced Atilla to train her."
msgstr "Hacía poco más de una semana que Sarah había convencido a Atilla para que la entrenara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been little over two months since the old houses had revolted, but there had been next to no communication from the other side."
msgstr "Han pasado poco más de dos meses desde que las antiguas casas se rebelaron, pero casi no ha habido comunicación del otro lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been more than a few days since Sarah had rested in the bathhouse, and even longer since she had come across Xan's writings."
msgstr "Había pasado más de unos días desde que Sarah descansó en el baño público, y mucho más tiempo desde que encontró los escritos de Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been rough coming down from it, but it was hard to deny how it had made her feel."
msgstr "Ha sido duro bajar de eso, pero es difícil negar cómo te hizo sentir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been so long. Ever since the uprising, nothing but one damned meeting after the other, always busy."
msgstr "Ha pasado tanto tiempo. Desde el levantamiento, nada más que una maldita reunión tras otra, siempre ocupados."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "It had been some time since your last visit. Long delays often mean either good news or bad news."
msgstr "Ha pasado algún tiempo desde tu última visita. Los largos retrasos suelen significar buenas o malas noticias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been someone's room once, most likely a noble lady, but it was hers for now."
msgstr "Fue una vez la habitación de alguien, probablemente una dama noble, pero ahora era suya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been the capital of multiple empires, now long faded and forgotten. The city, despite being long past its peak, was larger than any Sarah had ever seen in her life."
msgstr "Había sido la capital de múltiples imperios, ahora largamente desvanecida y olvidada. La ciudad, aunque ya había pasado su cénit, era más grande de lo que alguna vez Sarah había visto en su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been the first time all day that she had some modicum of modesty."
msgstr "Fue la primera vez hoy que tenía un mínimo de modestia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been the first time since she and Kate had gone on the run, that she had actually been alone."
msgstr "Fue la primera vez desde que Sarah y Kate huyeron que ella estuvo realmente sola."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been torture, walking there before."
msgstr "Había sido tortura caminar allí antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been weeks since Sarah first visited the library."
msgstr "Habían pasado semanas desde que Sarah visitó la biblioteca por primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been weeks, Sarah realized. Weeks since Rosanna fell. Whatever resistance might have existed, had long been stamped out."
msgstr "Habían pasado semanas, pensó Sarah. Semanas desde que cayó Rosanna. Cualquier resistencia que pudiera haber existido, había sido aplastada hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been what was expected of her. What she had been raised to learn, in castle Reinmeer."
msgstr "Había sido lo que se esperaba de ella. Lo que había aprendido desde niña en el castillo Reinmeer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been year, a lifetime ago, since anyone had ever known her...really known her."
msgstr "Había pasado un año, una eternidad, desde que alguien la conociera... de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been years ago. She had moved past it."
msgstr "Hacía años que había pasado de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been years now since he had trained her and they had been together."
msgstr "Han pasado años desde que él la entrenó y pasaron tiempo juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been years since she had last seen him, but she had never stopped thinking of him."
msgstr "Han pasado años desde que la vio por última vez, pero nunca dejó de pensar en él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been years since she had seen anyone from her old life."
msgstr "Habían pasado años desde que había visto a alguien de su vida anterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been years since she wore anything like this."
msgstr "Hacía años que no vestía nada como esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had begun years ago...a moment of trust turned into something more."
msgstr "Todo había comenzado hace años...un momento de confianza convertido en algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had bothered neither of them, and before the thunderous rage of their father, she had seen him smile more broadly at her than he ever had."
msgstr "Ninguna de las dos le había importado, y antes de la furia truenante de su padre, ella lo había visto sonreírle con más amplitud que nunca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had by now been year since the first time Kate had seduced her."
msgstr "Ya había pasado un año desde la primera vez que Kate la sedujo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had come to her with a warning. It would be wise to heed it."
msgstr "Llegó a ella con una advertencia. Sería sabio escucharla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had felt so easy, Sarah now realized. Easy to give in to him, submit to this new part of her life, because nobody had ever really known."
msgstr "Ahora Sarah se daba cuenta de que había sido tan fácil. Fácil entregarse a él, rendirse ante esta nueva faceta de su vida, porque nadie la había conocido realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had gone quiet, not so segregated from the outside world."
msgstr "Había vuelto al silencio, sin estar tan aislada del mundo exterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had gotten to the point where she no longer even considered rejecting his request to follow her. She simply did as he told her."
msgstr "Ya había llegado al punto en que ya ni siquiera pensaba rechazar su petición de seguirla. Simplemente hacía lo que él le decía."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "It had just been so long...I was like a young man again."
msgstr "Hacía tanto tiempo... Sentía que era un joven otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had nearly been a week since Sarah had first begun living in what passed for her new home."
msgstr "Habían pasado casi una semana desde que Sarah comenzó a vivir en lo que pasaba por su nuevo hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had never even dawned on her that she might stay here and make a life for herself."
msgstr "Nunca le había ocurrido a ella que pudiera quedarse aquí y construirse una vida propia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had never occured to her before...but in the moment...she doesn't say no."
msgstr "Nunca antes se le había ocurrido... pero en el momento... no dice que no."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had reset the relationship between them. It made Sarah realize she had gotten too comfortable with the captain, mistaking her place on the ship."
msgstr "Había restablecido la relación entre ambos. Hizo que Sarah se diera cuenta de que había estado demasiado cómoda con el capitán, confundiendo su lugar en el barco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had resumed its regular form, no longer distressed. Back to its unreadable state."
msgstr "Había retomado su forma habitual, sin más angustia. Volvería a ser inescrutable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had said that it waited by a dark fountain, but Sarah was a stranger to the city."
msgstr "Había dicho que esperaba junto a una fuente oscura, pero Sarah era ajena a la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had sat upon a great reservoir, causing many lakes to spring up around it, and painting the land green."
msgstr "Se había sentado sobre un gran embalse, provocando que surgieran muchos lagos a su alrededor y pintando la tierra de verde."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had some closets. A table. A couple of chairs. And a bed in the corner."
msgstr "Tenía algunos armarios. Una mesa. Unas cuantas sillas. Y una cama en la esquina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had sounded like the kind of place she wanted to go."
msgstr "Sonaba como el tipo de lugar que ella quería visitar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had spend the night here..."
msgstr "Pasó la noche aquí..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had struck her, but did not pierce her armor."
msgstr "Le había impactado, pero no atravesó su armadura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had surprised Sarah when she first came to Bagrad, how the days could be scorching hot, and the nights freezing cold."
msgstr "Le sorprendió a Sarah cuando llegó por primera vez a Bagrad, lo caluroso de los días y lo helado de las noches."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had surprised her at first, but she genuinly loved sucking the orc's cock. The way she could bring him to completion with only her mouth, aroused her."
msgstr "Al principio la sorprendió, pero genuinamente amaba chupar la polla del orco. La forma en que podía llevarlo a la culminación solo con su boca la excitaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had taken every last fraction of her power."
msgstr "Había agotado cada última fracción de su poder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had taken him less time to fix her dress than she had sucked him off."
msgstr "Le había costado menos tiempo arreglarle el vestido que el tiempo que ella le había dedicado a chuparle la polla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had taken several servants to put it on her, taking it off would be no easy feat."
msgstr "Le había llevado a varios sirvientes ponerla en ella; quitársela sería una tarea nada fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had taken them several days to prepare the ship. Purchasing supplies, onboarding the cargo and managing all the travel papers."
msgstr "Les había llevado varios días preparar el barco. Adquirir los suministros, cargar la mercancía y gestionar toda la documentación de viaje."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had tasted sweet, and so to her, it had been obvious as a drink..."
msgstr "Saborizaba dulce, y para ella fue obvio como un trago..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had to be done...to save...so many..."
msgstr "Tenía que hacerse... para salvar... a tantos..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had to."
msgstr "Tuvo que ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had worked."
msgstr "Funcionó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't been that long since she woke to a castle with an army of servants, eager to serve her every whim."
msgstr "No había pasado tanto tiempo desde que despertó en un castillo con una horda de sirvientes ansiosos por satisfacer cada uno de sus caprichos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't been the first time Samayra slept in her bed. Despite how big the house was, it just seemed to make sense."
msgstr "No había sido la primera vez que Samayra dormía en su cama. A pesar de lo grande que era la casa, todo parecía tener sentido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't been the first time she'd felt it."
msgstr "No había sido la primera vez que lo sintiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't escaped Sarah that her life outside of Rosanna, outside of the court, had been so very different."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't even been that long, and still she found her days seemingly bleeding into one another."
msgstr "Aún no había pasado tanto tiempo y, sin embargo, seguía sintiendo que sus días se mezclaban como si estuvieran sangrando el uno en el otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't taken Sarah long to learn that this was one way to get out from under a task."
msgstr "No tardó Sarah en aprender que esta era una forma de librarse de una tarea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hadn't taken long before she was losing herself in the moment, the building pleasure driving out her awareness of her surroundings."
msgstr "No tardó en perderse en el momento, con el placer creciente ahuyentando su conciencia de los alrededores."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "It has a magical, healing property."
msgstr "Tiene una propiedad mágica y curativa."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "It has a way of drawing out the melancholy in me."
msgstr "Tiene una manera de sacar la melancolía que hay en mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It has been a pleasure to make your acquaintance."
msgstr "Ha sido un placer hacer tu conocimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It has been over a century since the last Union Council, and yet, it does not change that I have received an invitation from Queen Maeiv."
msgstr "Ha pasado más de un siglo desde el último Consejo de la Unión, y sin embargo, no cambia que he recibido una invitación de la Reina Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "It has been plaguing us for months now..."
msgstr "Nos ha atormentado durante meses ahora..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It has been very kind of you to let me stay here."
msgstr "Ha sido muy amable de tu parte dejarme quedarme aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "It has been years since my wife passed...since any other woman has been here, under my roof..."
msgstr "Ha sido años desde que mi esposa partió...desde que otra mujer haya estado aquí, bajo mi techo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It has long been forgotten, one of the first cities to fall to the advance of the desert, many centuries ago."
msgstr "Hace mucho tiempo que se ha olvidado, una de las primeras ciudades en caer ante el avance del desierto, hace muchos siglos atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "It has not been the first time that there was a plot against your father, but the odd thing is, we always picked up rumors whenever there were plans for an assassination."
msgstr "No ha sido la primera vez que hubo un complot contra tu padre, pero lo extraño es que siempre surgían rumores cuando existían planes para un asesinato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It held up her mouth and fucked it, pressing deep into her mouth and her throat. She imagined she could feel him on her tongue, sliding in and out, pumping her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It helped that he was easy to look at and easy to listen to."
msgstr "Ayudaba que fuera fácil de mirar y fácil de escuchar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It horrified Sarah, if only because she could see herself so easily in those women."
msgstr "Le horrorizaba a Sarah, si no fuera porque podía verse tan fácilmente en esas mujeres."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "It hosts no higher intelligent life. No creatures that could pose any threat to us, well, magically speaking at least."
msgstr "No alberga vida inteligente superior. No hay criaturas que puedan representar alguna amenaza para nosotros... bueno, mágicamente hablando, al menos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It hurt for a moment, but only in a good way."
msgstr "Dolió por un momento, pero solo de una manera buena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It improved their situation, but only by so much."
msgstr "Mejoró su situación, pero solo en esa medida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is Lord Greytower's right to collect on this debts, and should you pass in his domain, he may do as he sees fit to extract it from you."
msgstr "Es derecho de Lord Greytower cobrar estas deudas, y si pasas por su dominio, podrá hacer lo que estime conveniente para extorsionártelas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It is Sarah, bend over the steering wheel with the captain's cock plunged into her ass, who first discovers their salvation."
msgstr "Es Sarah, la que primero descubre su salvación, inclinada sobre el volante con la polla del capitán hundida en su culo."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "It is a cruel thing, really, how little they prepare the women of your country for matter such as these."
msgstr "Es verdaderamente cruel, en efecto, cómo tan poco preparan a las mujeres de tu país para asuntos como estos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is a kind offer, but I fear I am still on my shift."
msgstr "Es una oferta generosa, pero temo que aún estoy de turno."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is a waste for a girl of your age to spend her time with dusty old books."
msgstr "Es una pérdida de tiempo que una chica de tu edad pase su tiempo con viejos libros polvorientos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It is after more than an hour before anyone dares to try to move her."
msgstr "No es hasta más de una hora cuando alguien se atreve a intentar moverla."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "It is all the things this place is not. So I much rather remain here."
msgstr "Son todas las cosas que este lugar no es. Por eso prefiero quedarme aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "It is also true, that if all the people of all the world, shared their wealthy equally, this world would be a paradise."
msgstr "También es cierto que, si todas las personas de todo el mundo compartieran su riqueza por igual, este mundo sería un paraíso."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "It is and it ain't, if ya know what I mean."
msgstr "Es y no es, si entiendes lo que quiero decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is as I said, Marius...the problem isn't you. It's me."
msgstr "Es como dije, Marius... el problema no eres tú. Soy yo."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It is because you know as well as any other, the good you can do from that throne."
msgstr "Es porque sabes tan bien como cualquiera otro el bien que puedes hacer desde ese trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "It is different this time."
msgstr "Esta vez es diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is done."
msgstr "Está hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is done."
msgstr "Está hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "It is done."
msgstr "Ya está hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is done..."
msgstr "Ya está hecho..."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "It is fine, think no more of it. Let the matter rest. Please, continue to partake."
msgstr "Está bien, no pienses más en ello. Déjalo así. Por favor, continúa bebiendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is fine, you could not have known."
msgstr "Está bien, no podrías haberlo sabido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is fine."
msgstr "Está bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is fine...I suppose. My father...his death still lingers."
msgstr "Está bien... supongo. Mi padre... su muerte aún persiste."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "It is important that we are unified. For that, I will throw in my vote as well."
msgstr "Es importante que estemos unidos. Para ello, aportaré también mi voto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It is in the second week when a man, a leader among the others, spots her."
msgstr "Es en la segunda semana cuando un hombre, un líder entre los demás, la avista."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It is like a loan."
msgstr "Es como un préstamo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It is more than an hour before anyone dares to try to move her."
msgstr "Es más de una hora antes de que alguien se atreva a intentar moverla."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is no gift at all."
msgstr "No es ningún regalo en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It is not as crude a system as you imagine, Sarah."
msgstr "No es un sistema tan crudo como imaginas, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "It is not just a story, Sarah."
msgstr "No es solo una historia, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is not lust that drives my kind."
msgstr "No es el deseo lo que impulsa a mi especie."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "It is not so simple."
msgstr "No es tan sencillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "It is not the real thing, but you will find it can mimic it closely enough."
msgstr "No es lo real, pero descubrirás que puede imitarlo con suficiente precisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "It is not up for barbarians from the desert to come to the land of civilized men and utter threats."
msgstr "No le corresponde a bárbaros del desierto venir a la tierra de los hombres civilizados y lanzar amenazas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is odd to me, even after all these years, that I can speak more with you in a gesture than I can speak with most in a conversation."
msgstr "Es extraño para mí, incluso después de todos estos años, que pueda hablar más contigo con un gesto que con la mayoría en una conversación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It is only nine days later that the ship arrives in Lethram, and the women disembark."
msgstr "Solo nueve días después llega el barco a Lethram y las mujeres desembarcan."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is only the beginning."
msgstr "Solo es el comienzo."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "It is possible, but extremely dangerous."
msgstr "Es posible, pero extremadamente peligroso."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "It is possible."
msgstr "Es posible."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "It is real. I just mean you're lucky that you ran into me."
msgstr "Es real. Solo quiero decir que tienes suerte de haberme encontrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is settled."
msgstr "Está decidido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is still yours, should you ask for it."
msgstr "Aún es tuya, si lo pides."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "It is strength that determines who rules and who submits."
msgstr "La fuerza es lo que determina quién manda y quién se rinde."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It is that I see so much of your family in your face, or I would never have recognized you to be the girl from all those years ago."
msgstr "Es que veo tanto de tu familia en tu rostro, o nunca te habría reconocido como la chica de hace tantos años."

msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "It is that very task that I now aid him in, Gods willing."
msgstr "Es esa misma tarea en la que ahora le presto mi ayuda, si los dioses lo permiten."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is the foundational text of their order."
msgstr "Es el texto fundacional de su orden."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It is the name of the new province of the Khan's empire...the new name of your former homeland."
msgstr "Es el nombre de la nueva provincia del imperio del Kan... el nuevo nombre de tu antigua patria."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is the very Art that produced the welding of the worlds. The ritual that drew my world into yours."
msgstr "Es el mismo Arte que forjó la unión de los mundos. El ritual que trajo mi mundo a ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is the wisest decision, given what little information we have."
msgstr "Es la decisión más sabia, dada la poca información de la que disponemos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is this fact that makes them know the world and all its elements, for they are imbued within it."
msgstr "Es este hecho lo que les permite conocer el mundo y todos sus elementos, pues están impregnados por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is true that I am seeking allies to help push back against this void incursion."
msgstr "Es cierto que busco aliados para ayudar a repeler esta incursión del vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "It is true that Rosanna has done much to elevate the poor from their condition, these last few years."
msgstr "Es cierto que Rosanna ha hecho mucho para elevar a los pobres de su condición en estos últimos años."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "It is true that out of the two of you...I trust you more. You might actually be stupid enough to be a good person."
msgstr "Es cierto que entre los dos... confío más en ti. Podrías ser incluso estúpido lo suficiente para ser una buena persona."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "It is true that we will take the walls, and move into the city, but we will not be seizing these objectives."
msgstr "Es cierto que tomaremos las murallas y entraremos en la ciudad, pero no nos apoderaremos de estos objetivos."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "It is true, if there was nothing to complain, but there is discord in you. Such alone is evidence that something is amiss."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is under these dire circumstances that I will be crowned today."
msgstr "Es bajo estas circunstancias tan desesperadas que me coronaré hoy."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "It is what it is, I suppose."
msgstr "Es lo que es, supongo."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It is whatever the master of the house wills it to be. What do you will it to be?"
msgstr "Es lo que el señor de la casa decida que sea. ¿Qué deseas que sea?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is you who is the coward for uttering such poison in the presence of a lady, and a peer no less."
msgstr "Eres tú el cobarde que pronuncia tal veneno delante de una dama, y no menos que un par."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "It is, and I'm glad you agree."
msgstr "Es así, y me alegra que estés de acuerdo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "It is."
msgstr "Es así."

msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "It is. But just like a dance, when it's all going good, it can feel simple. Natural."
msgstr "Es cierto. Pero es como una danza; cuando todo va bien, puede sentirse simple y natural."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It is. Lady Carolyn's office is deep enough inside the castle that I doubt anyone could penetrate."
msgstr "Sí. La oficina de la dama Carolyn está tan adentro del castillo que dudo que nadie pueda penetrarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "It is. You can marry anyone you want, you know that. I'd never object. It's just, you know, I would only want to know that you were happy."
msgstr "Es así. Puedes casarte con quien quieras, lo sabes. Nunca pondré objeción. Solo quiero saber que eres feliz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It isn't long before Sarah hears the first soldier let out a deep grunt."
msgstr "No tarda en oír el primer soldado soltar un profundo gruñido."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "It just goes to prove what I said before, I should have taken you to the citadel a long time ago."
msgstr "Acaba de confirmar lo que dije antes: debí llevarte al castillo hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It just happened that in this case her body was his material."
msgstr "Simplemente sucedió que, en este caso, su cuerpo era su materia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It just seemed like an ordinary door."
msgstr "Parecía simplemente una puerta común."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It just, it happened so fast. He said they would take you to the auction houses...and Sarah, I began to recall all these memories..."
msgstr "Solo... solo pasó tan rápido. Dijo que te llevarían a las casas de subastas... y Sarah, empecé a recordar todos esos recuerdos..."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "It kept working, so I thought I was so incredible..."
msgstr "Seguía funcionando, así que pensé que era tan increíble..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It landed there, but Sarah did not bow down to pick it up."
msgstr "Cayó allí, pero Sarah no se inclinó para recogerla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It lashed out with such force that the bodies of its victims exploded into mist and gore."
msgstr "Lanzó un golpe con tanta fuerza que los cuerpos de sus víctimas explotaron en niebla y sangre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It lasted so long, everyone in the room began to grew nervous."
msgstr "Duró tanto que todos en la sala comenzaron a sentirse nerviosos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It liked to speak, but now it seemed hesitant."
msgstr "Le gustaba hablar, pero ahora parecía dubitativo."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "It likely won't be a full out attack. They'll start by launching some smaller skirmishes, see if there are any weak points in the defense."
msgstr "Probablemente no será un ataque total. Comenzarán lanzando algunos pequeños enfrentamientos para ver si hay puntos débiles en la defensa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It lived up to its name."
msgstr "Cumplió con su nombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It looked at her, as if in a trance."
msgstr "La miró, como si estuviera en trance."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It looked like a mess, but Sarah had seen him work enough to know there was a method to his madness."
msgstr "Parecía un desastre, pero Sarah lo había visto trabajar lo suficiente para saber que había método en su locura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It looked nice, she concluded."
msgstr "Parecía bien, concluyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It looked similar to the thing she had killed in the throne room."
msgstr "Parecía igual a la cosa que había matado en el salón del trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It looks amazing."
msgstr "Se ve increíble."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It looks black to me, like obsidian."
msgstr "A mí me parece negra, como obsidiana."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It looks like one, but it is not a house. Not really."
msgstr "Parece una, pero no es una casa. No del todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made Sarah feel safe. But it also made her happy, reminding her that there were good people in the world, despite everything."
msgstr "Le hizo sentir segura a Sarah, pero también la hizo feliz, recordándole que había buenas personas en el mundo, a pesar de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made Sarah wonder, which part was the real Xan, if there was any."
msgstr "Le hizo preguntarse a Sarah qué parte era el verdadero Xan, si había alguno."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made a howling sound as it rushed through the entrance way."
msgstr "Hizo un sonido aullante mientras se precipitaba por el pasillo de entrada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made for a pleasant dulling of the senses, but each time it was used, its addictive properties grew stronger."
msgstr "Era un aturdimiento placentero de los sentidos, pero cada vez que se usaba, sus propiedades adictivas crecían más intensas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her angry."
msgstr "La enfurecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her feel instantly refreshed."
msgstr "La hacía sentir instantáneamente renovada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her feel safe in this otherwise strange place."
msgstr "La hizo sentir segura en este lugar, de otro modo extraño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her feel uneasy, realizing that this woman's fate as a slave had likely barely been more than an incidental report that her father had once read and dismissed."
msgstr "La hizo sentir incómoda, al darse cuenta de que el destino de esa mujer como esclava probablemente había sido apenas un informe incidental que su padre alguna vez leyó y descartó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her feel uneasy. Sarah shifted around in her seat."
msgstr "Le hizo sentir incómoda. Sarah se movió en su asiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her proud to see the changes that came over the country by her hand. To see it flourish."
msgstr "Le hizo sentir orgullosa ver los cambios que el país había sufrido por su mano, verlo florecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her want to confess things."
msgstr "Le hizo querer confesar cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made it ever more obvious that they had never stood a chance."
msgstr "Hizo que fuera aún más evidente que nunca tuvieron posibilidades."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made sense, Sarah thought to herself. She could meet with Lady Carolyn again, longer, and whatever spying eyes there were, they'd likely be aimed at Vaelen, their leader."
msgstr "Tenía sentido, pensó Sarah para sí misma. Podía volver a reunirse con Lady Carolyn por más tiempo, y cualquiera que fuera el espionaje, probablemente estaría dirigido hacia Vaelen, su líder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made sense, Sarah thought. He'd spend his life navigating these alleys. Of course he knew them like the back of his hand."
msgstr "Tenía sentido, pensó Sarah. Él pasaría su vida navegando por estos callejones. Por supuesto que los conocía como la palma de su mano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made some degree of sense."
msgstr "Tenía cierto sentido."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "It makes for a fine story of heroism to most in the capital, but for me, it meant slaughtering the people that were my friends."
msgstr "Para la mayoría en la capital, esto constituye una historia heroica, pero para mí significó masacrar a las personas que eran mis amigos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It makes the Gods blind to the the space around it."
msgstr "Hace que los dioses se vuelvan ciegos al espacio que la rodea."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "It makes the world simple, reducing everyone down to one or two things."
msgstr "Hace sencillo el mundo, reduciendo a todos a una o dos cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It means I'm willing to listen to your offer. What more can one ask for?"
msgstr "Significa que estoy dispuesta a escuchar tu propuesta. ¿Qué más se puede pedir?"

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It means Land of Roses in the language of the Tribes."
msgstr "Significa Tierra de Rosas en el idioma de las Tribus."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It means a feast for everyone of import that took part in the campaign."
msgstr "Significa un banquete para todos los de importancia que participaron en la campaña."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "It means a lot to hear you say that, Sarah."
msgstr "Significa mucho para mí oírte decir eso, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It means distributing loot."
msgstr "Significa repartir el botín."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It means nothing, dear."
msgstr "No significa nada, cariño."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It means that your race, as well as mine, was forever trapped. Trapped to walk down a road that only led to one outcome."
msgstr "Significa que tu raza, así como la mía, quedó atrapada para siempre. Atrapada en un camino que solo conducía a un único destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It meant a lot to me too."
msgstr "También significó mucho para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "It meant nothing."
msgstr "No significaba nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It meant that the Tribesmen had likely not spotted them yet."
msgstr "Significaba que los tribales probablemente no los habían visto aún."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It meant wealth and land, sure. But Sarah also knew the customs of the Tribes well by now."
msgstr "Significaba riqueza y tierra, claro. Pero Sarah también conocía bien las costumbres de los tribales en este punto."

msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "It might not be quite up to your standards..."
msgstr "Puede que no cumpla del todo con tus estándares..."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "It might not tonight, but perhaps this week."
msgstr "Tal vez no esta noche, pero quizás sí esta semana."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It might sound strange to you, but I see some of myself in you."
msgstr "Puede sonar extraño para ti, pero veo algo de mí mismo en ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Camp Guard"
msgid "It might surprise you to learn, but there aren't a lot of people here matching that description."
msgstr "Te sorprendería saberlo, pero no hay muchos aquí que encajen con esa descripción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It missed her by only a fraction as she ducked underneath it."
msgstr "La pasó por alto apenas un milímetro mientras se agachaba bajo ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It moved past her, along the sharp rocks of the alien world."
msgstr "Se deslizó junto a ella, siguiendo las afiladas rocas del planeta alienígena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It moved with such speed that no sooner had the soldiers turned to it, that it had already positioned itself anew."
msgstr "Se movía con tanta velocidad que apenas los soldados se volvían hacia él, ya había tomado una nueva posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It moved, and again, Sarah flinched."
msgstr "Se movió y, otra vez, Sarah se estremeció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It moved, not as an animale might, but like flowing water."
msgstr "Se movía, no como lo haría un animal, sino como agua que fluye."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It must be fun, running an Inn with your family."
msgstr "Debe ser divertido, administrar una posada con tu familia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It must takes hours to put on."
msgstr "Debe tomar horas ponerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It named no explicit names, but the description of the bandit leader matched only one man."
msgstr "No nombra nombres explícitos, pero la descripción del líder de los bandidos coincide con un solo hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It need not be."
msgstr "No es necesario."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "It needs a whetstone to remain sharp. Without conflict, it grows dull."
msgstr "Necesita una piedra de afilar para mantenerse afilado. Sin conflicto, se vuelve torpe."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It numbed the pain, and it let me survive when things got too bad. But over time, the cure got worse than the disease."
msgstr "Adormeció el dolor y me permitió sobrevivir cuando las cosas se ponían demasiado mal. Pero con el tiempo, la cura se volvió peor que la enfermedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It oddly seemed brighter to her now."
msgstr "Extrañamente, ahora le parecía más brillante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It offended her. Then she began to enjoy it."
msgstr "Le ofendió. Luego comenzó a disfrutarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It offered them safety, if only the illusion of it."
msgstr "Ofrecía seguridad, si solo era una ilusión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It often is."
msgstr "A menudo es así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It one motion, it tore the fabric from her body."
msgstr "De un solo movimiento, la arrancó de su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It only appeared as such to those unfamiliar with the city."
msgstr "Solo parecía así para aquellos que no conocían la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "It only has one entrance point, through the throne room."
msgstr "Solo tiene una entrada: la sala del trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It only made her feel more powerful. Every man in the camp wanted her, and none could have her."
msgstr "Solo eso la hacía sentir más poderosa. Cada hombre en el campamento quería a ella, y ninguno podía tenerla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It only took him a moment before he came, spraying what little cum he had left onto her tits."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It opened the lock."
msgstr "Abrió la cerradura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pained Sarah to hear her talk about her father like that, but given her circumstance, she could hardly blame her."
msgstr "Le dolía a Sarah escuchar hablar de su padre de esa manera, pero dada su situación, no podía culparla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pained Sarah to realize that whatever parts of those she had once possessed, the progress of time had sanded those softer edges off."
msgstr "Le dolía a Sarah darse cuenta de que, cualquiera que fuese parte de aquellas cualidades que alguna vez había poseído, el paso del tiempo las había desgastado hasta pulir esas aristas más suaves."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pained her heart to do this, but if it meant improving her odds of saving Thomas, she would do it."
msgstr "Le dolía el corazón hacerlo, pero si eso significaba mejorar sus posibilidades de salvar a Thomas, lo haría."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "It pains me, same it does you. You might not believe it, but I'm human too."
msgstr "Me duele igual que a ti. Quizás no lo creas, pero también soy humana."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It pains you to look at me?"
msgstr "¿Te duele mirarme?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It paused before speaking."
msgstr "Pausó antes de hablar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It paused, before continueing."
msgstr "Pausó antes de continuar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It paused."
msgstr "Se detuvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It perhaps imitated a man, but there was nothing but female beauty about the woman."
msgstr "Quizás imitaba a un hombre, pero no había nada más que belleza femenina en la mujer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pierced what little armor he wore, the tip of it stabbing out through his chest."
msgstr "Perforó la poca armadura que llevaba puesta, clavando su punta a través de su pecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pleased him to know that even in his old age, he still managed to bed women, and if he didn't have to pay, all the better."
msgstr "Le complacía saber que, incluso en su vejez, aún lograba acostarse con mujeres, y si no tenía que pagar, mejor aún."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It plunged so deep, Sarah nearly gagged."
msgstr "Se hundió tan profundo que Sarah casi se ahogó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pressed up against her, but he didn't enter her."
msgstr "Presionaba contra ella, pero no la penetraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It prevents them from...well, you understand."
msgstr "Impide que... bueno, entiendes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It produced a soft, rhythmic sound, as he drew the whetstone past it, again, again, again."
msgstr "Produce un sonido suave y rítmico mientras pasa la piedra afiladora por ella, una vez, otra vez, otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pulled away, and just as it had come, it now faded."
msgstr "Se retiró y, tal como había llegado, ahora se desvaneció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pulled back, giving her a chance to breathe, only for him to impale her throat again."
msgstr "Se retiró, dándole un respiro, solo para que él la impalara de nuevo en la garganta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pulled on the threads of her conservative upbringing."
msgstr "Arrancó de los hilos de su educación conservadora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It ran along the length of a sewer canal."
msgstr "Se deslizó por el largo de un canal de alcantarilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It ran on sharp claw along the side of her face."
msgstr "Se deslizó con garras afiladas a lo largo de su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reached its hands into her cage, holding up a piece of stale bread."
msgstr "Sus manos se adentraron en su jaula, sosteniendo un trozo de pan rancio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reaches so high, it nearly touches the ceiling of the cave."
msgstr "Alcanza tan alto que casi toca el techo de la cueva."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It read \"The Blunt Harpoon\"."
msgstr "Leía 'El arpón torpe'."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It really isn't."
msgstr "En realidad no lo es."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It really just depends where you want."
msgstr "Depende realmente de dónde quieras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It remained quiet."
msgstr "Permaneció en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It remained there, searing itself into her body and mind. A moment so profound, she knew she would never forget it as it happened."
msgstr "Permaneció allí, quemándose en su cuerpo y en su mente. Un momento tan profundo que sabía que nunca lo olvidaría mientras ocurría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her of Thomas. She pushed down the thought."
msgstr "Lo recordaba a Thomas. Represó el pensamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her of the hearth, back home."
msgstr "Le recordaba la lumbre, en casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her that the brother she knew, the easy-going quick-to-laugh brother, was still in there, despite the trauma."
msgstr "Le recordaba que el hermano que ella conocía, aquel de buen humor y risas fáciles, seguía estando allí, a pesar del trauma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her that there was a whole world outside of these walls, one where all the pomp and pretense of the court wasn't taken so seriously."
msgstr "Le recordaba que existía un mundo entero más allá de estas paredes, un lugar donde todo el alarde y la pretensión de la corte no eran tomados tan en serio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her that this place was strange to her, and she a stranger to it."
msgstr "Le recordaba que aquel lugar era extraño para ella, y ella, una extraña para él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It reminded her that this was real."
msgstr "Le recordaba que aquello era real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It repeated a few more times before his thirst seemed finally sated."
msgstr "Se repitió un par de veces más antes de que su sed pareciera finalmente saciada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It roared, sending out shockwaves of sound that rattled the stone foundations."
msgstr "rugió, enviando ondas de choque que hicieron temblar los cimientos de piedra."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "It runs along Ridgehaven, deeper into the interior of Rosanna, all the way up to the capital."
msgstr "Cruza por Ridgehaven, adentrándose en el interior de Rosanna hasta llegar a la capital."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It rushed up to them, then crashing against the barrier, like water slamming against the coastline."
msgstr "Se abalanzó sobre ellos y luego estrelló contra la barrera, como el agua golpeando con violencia la costa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sat atop one of the larger hills that the city had been build on, towering over most everything else, and so alien in its design it almost looked as if some other culture had left it there."
msgstr "Se sentaba sobre una de las colinas más grandes en las que había sido construida la ciudad, dominando casi todo lo demás, y tan ajeno en su diseño que parecía como si alguna otra cultura lo hubiera dejado allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It screamed more loudly than it ever had before."
msgstr "Gritó con más fuerza que nunca antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed a cruel act, given that it had been Marius that had worked himself to the bone."
msgstr "Parecía un acto cruel, considerando que había sido Marius el que se había trabajado hasta la médula."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed about as good an idea as any to her."
msgstr "Parecía una buena idea tanto como cualquier otra para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed as if the space had been cleared out by hand. Small remnants of a campfire remained."
msgstr "Parecía que el espacio había sido despejado a mano. Pequeños restos de un fuego campal permanecían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed complicated, but the men made it look easy. As though they had done it a hundred times over."
msgstr "Parecía complicado, pero los hombres lo hacían parecer fácil. Como si lo hubieran hecho un centenar de veces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed cruel to her."
msgstr "Parecía cruel para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed cruel to let others suffer their fate, even if it was the right strategic move."
msgstr "Parecía cruel permitir que otros sufrieran su destino, incluso si era la decisión estratégica correcta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed fair, she thought, given her new role in this house."
msgstr "Parecía justo, pensó, dado su nuevo papel en esa casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed impossible that she couldn't, but perhaps for Lily such things were more common."
msgstr "Parecía imposible que no pudiera hacerlo, pero quizás para Lily esas cosas eran más comunes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed like a castle, or perhaps a former fortress."
msgstr "Parecía un castillo, o quizás una antigua fortaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed like a small price for a place to stay."
msgstr "Parecía un precio bajo por un lugar donde quedarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed like an absurdity, and yet Hecate spoke it so casually."
msgstr "Parecía una absurdez, y sin embargo Hécate lo decía con tanta naturalidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed obvious that played a part in it."
msgstr "Parecía obvio que ella jugaba un papel en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed so odd to Sarah, to be exchanging pleasantries with these women as thought this was all completely normal."
msgstr "Le pareció tan extraño a Sarah intercambiar cortesías con esas mujeres como si todo fuera completamente normal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed strang to Sarah. Castle Reinmeer had always buzzed with and endless coming-and-going of nobles from all over Rosanna and its neighbouring kingdoms."
msgstr "Parecía extraño para Sarah. El castillo Reinmeer siempre había estado lleno de actividad, con una incesante entrada y salida de nobles de todo Rosanna y sus reinos vecinos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed the only thing that mattered."
msgstr "Parecía que lo único que importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed to her closer to a castle than a tent."
msgstr "A ella le pareció más un castillo que una tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed to her that any word further might break this moment. And Sarah would have done anything to prevent that."
msgstr "Parecía que cualquier palabra adicional podría romper este momento, y Sarah habría hecho cualquier cosa para evitarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed to last forever."
msgstr "Pareció durar para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed to mark the entrance into a new part of the city."
msgstr "Parecía marcar la entrada a una nueva parte de la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seemed to require all its power just to utter these few words."
msgstr "Parecía que necesitaba todo su poder para pronunciar tan pocas palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It seems a silver cup was reported stolen, you wouldn't happen to know anything about that, would you?"
msgstr "Parece que se reportó el robo de una copa de plata; ¿no sabrías nada al respecto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "It sees some usage, but it's never too busy."
msgstr "Tiene utilidad, pero nunca está demasiado ocupada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It seized on their bodies, knew their desires, but there was also a trust here."
msgstr "Se apoderaba de sus cuerpos, conocía sus deseos, pero también había una confianza aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It served him right for what he had tried to do to her."
msgstr "Se lo merecía por lo que intentó hacerle."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It shines like bright crimson."
msgstr "Brilla como un rojo carmesí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It shook its body, dusting off the gravel and stone."
msgstr "Sacudió su cuerpo, deshaciéndose de la grava y las piedras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It shot out from the darkness, rushing across the room at a blinding speed."
msgstr "Se lanzó desde la oscuridad, cruzando la habitación a una velocidad deslumbrante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It should have been a handsome prince. A kind knight. On her wedding night."
msgstr "Debería haber sido un príncipe apuesto. Un caballero bondadoso. En la noche de su boda."

msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "It should have been me."
msgstr "Debería haber sido yo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It should have been you..."
msgstr "Hubiera debido ser tú..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It should not have mattered, she thought, but she was glad still."
msgstr "No debería haber importado, pensó, pero aún estaba contenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It shouldn't be."
msgstr "No debería ser así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It shouldn't have been remarkable, but in a mercenary company, women were generally perceived with suspicion."
msgstr "No debería haber sido nada extraordinario, pero en una compañía de mercenarios, las mujeres eran generalmente vistas con sospecha."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It shouldn't have felt any different from sleeping out on the field, and yet Sarah couldn't help but feel different about it."
msgstr "No debería sentirse diferente que dormir al aire libre, y sin embargo Sarah no pudo evitar sentirlo de otra manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Official"
msgid "It shouldn't matter where!"
msgstr "¡No debería importar el lugar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It showed the town, the surrounding areas, the forest, and a few red markers."
msgstr "Mostraba la ciudad, las zonas circundantes, el bosque y algunos marcadores rojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It slid down, his head pressing up against her sex."
msgstr "Se deslizó hacia abajo, con su cabeza presionada contra su coño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It slid in with ease."
msgstr "Entró con facilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It smashed a rock against the metal lock with a stunning force."
msgstr "Destrozó una roca contra la cerradura metálica con una fuerza abrumadora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It smashed against a rock, loudly shattering as shards of glass exploded in every direction."
msgstr "Se estrelló contra una roca, rompiendo con estruendo mientras los fragmentos de cristal volaban en todas direcciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sold valuable clothing materials, silk, satin and refined wool. Raw materials for a clothing shop."
msgstr "Vendía materiales de ropa valiosos: seda, satén y lana refinada. Materias primas para una tienda de ropa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It soon began to dawn on Sarah, that the only people Alaric was managing to rob, were the idiots."
msgstr "Pronto se hizo de día para Sarah que los únicos a quienes Alaric lograba estafar eran los idiotas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded easy enough."
msgstr "Sonaba fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded harmless enough."
msgstr "Sonaba inocente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded like a nightmare to Sarah."
msgstr "Sonaba como una pesadilla para Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded like it came from inside the palace."
msgstr "Sonaba como si viniera desde dentro del palacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded rough and unnatural coming from the orc. She doubted it knew many more words in her language."
msgstr "Sonaba áspero e innatural viniendo del orco. Dudaba que supiera muchas más palabras en su idioma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded soft and gentle, yet there also seemed to be a hint of something other."
msgstr "Sonaba suave y gentil, aunque también parecía haber un toque de algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It sounds fun."
msgstr "Suena divertido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It sounds like a fantasy."
msgstr "Suena como una fantasía."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It sounds like a paradise...how can such a thing even be?"
msgstr "Suena como un paraíso... ¿cómo puede existir algo así?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It sounds like fun."
msgstr "Suena divertido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounds more than a command than a question."
msgstr "Suena más a una orden que a una pregunta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sparked memories in Sarah, memories of when he had bounced her head up against the headboard."
msgstr "Eso despertó recuerdos en Sarah, de cuando él la había hecho chocar la cabeza contra el cabecero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It spat out the words in its guttural voice."
msgstr "Soltó las palabras con su voz gutural."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It spat out the words."
msgstr "Lo escupió con las palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It splatters, creeps across her skin, and then..."
msgstr "Se esparce, se arrastra por su piel y luego..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It spoke no language she had ever heard before, and yet, she understood it perfectly."
msgstr "No hablaba ningún idioma que ella hubiera oído antes, y sin embargo, lo entendía perfectamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It spun around to face Sarah."
msgstr "Se giró para mirar a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It stared at her through the bars."
msgstr "La miró a través de las barras."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "It started about half a year ago...the first attack I mean."
msgstr "Comenzó hace casi medio año..."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "It started almost half a year ago..."
msgstr "Comenzó hace casi medio año..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "It started when we were talking late at night, about your mother, and what her loss meant to me."
msgstr "Comenzó cuando estábamos hablando muy tarde en la noche, sobre tu madre y lo que su pérdida significaba para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It started with the old connections that visited their wedding."
msgstr "Todo comenzó con las viejas conexiones que visitaron su boda."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It still didn't stick."
msgstr "Aún no lo aceptaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It still felt no less real to Sarah."
msgstr "Aún le pareció real a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It still felt strange to her, to call him that, out loud or even in her mind."
msgstr "Aún le parecía extraño llamarlo así, en voz alta o incluso en su mente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It still gleamed from wetness."
msgstr "Aún brillaba por la humedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It still hurts, what you did..."
msgstr "Aún duele lo que hiciste..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It still surprised her just how large the world was. How many millions of people lived out their lives, each sparing her nation as much a thought as she had previously spared their city."
msgstr "Todavía la sorprendía lo grande que era el mundo. Cuántos millones de personas vivían sus vidas, dedicando cada una de ellas tan poco pensamiento a su nación como ella había dedicado anteriormente a su ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It still troubled her how little she really knew of this world before her time."
msgstr "Aún la inquietaba lo poco que realmente conocía de este mundo antes de su tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It stopped, roared, and clawed the earth. But he did not harm her."
msgstr "Se detuvo, rugió y desgarró la tierra. Pero no le hizo daño a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It stretched across the surface of the world and all peoples of this world fell under it."
msgstr "Se extendió por la superficie del mundo y todos los pueblos de este mundo cayeron bajo su dominio."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "It strikes at night, and there are some confusing reports. It's big, we know that much."
msgstr "Ataca de noche, y hay informes confusos. Es grande, eso sí que sabemos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It struck her how odd it was, that on the far end of the world, the void horrors continued their carnage."
msgstr "Le pareció extraño que, en el extremo opuesto del mundo, los horrores del vacío continuaran su carnicería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It stung her face which had gotten used to the warmth of inside the tent."
msgstr "Le dolía el rostro, acostumbrado al calor del interior de la tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It suddenly dawn on Sarah that she was fully nude, her dress and underwear piled around her ankles, skillfully disrobed by Kate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It suddenly dawned on Sarah that she was."
msgstr "De repente, a Sarah se le ocurrió que estaba completamente desnuda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It suddenly dawned on her, standing behind him, that she had never really seen his body from this perspective."
msgstr "De repente se dio cuenta de que, estando detrás de él, nunca había visto su cuerpo desde esa perspectiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It suddenly looked so very lonely."
msgstr "De repente, pareció tan muy solitario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It suddenly looked very lonely."
msgstr "De repente, pareció muy solitario."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "It sure looks like pyrrite enough to me."
msgstr "¡A mí parece que hay suficiente pirita!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It surprised Sarah that this would be any concern of them."
msgstr "Le sorprendió a Sarah que eso fuera cosa de ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It surprised Sarah to hear it. Kate had always seemed fearless to her."
msgstr "Le sorprendió a Sarah oírlo. Kate siempre había parecido intrépida para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It surprised her how young many of the soldiers were, barely much older than Thomas. Children really, she thought."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swayed back and forth and she couldn't look away. It almost left her speechless. The smell alone..."
msgstr "Se balanceaba de lado a lado y no podía apartar la mirada. Casi le quitó las palabras. Solo el olor..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swayed only inches from her face."
msgstr "Se movía apenas a pulgadas de su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swelled nearly instantly."
msgstr "Se hincharon casi instantáneamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swept through the air but caught nothing but rock and sand."
msgstr "Barrió por el aire pero no encontró nada más que roca y arena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swept with its great claws, tearing apart the earth, taking out entire buildings."
msgstr "Se abalanzaba con sus garras gigantes, desgarrando la tierra y derribando edificios enteros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It swiped at Gabriel with its massive, leathery claw."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It takes a few moments for the two to find their rhythm."
msgstr "Toma unos segundos para que los dos encuentren su ritmo."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "It takes a while to get used to it, but in time you'll lear the proper rhythm."
msgstr "Tarda un poco en acostumbrarse, pero con el tiempo aprenderás el ritmo adecuado."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It takes about a dozen servants, just to keep the whole thing from falling apart."
msgstr "Necesita una docena de sirvientes solo para evitar que todo se desmorone."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It takes another nine days before they will reach Lethram."
msgstr "Tocan otros nueve días antes de llegar a Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It takes her a moment to realize its water and cloth."
msgstr "Le toma un momento darse cuenta de que es agua y tela."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It takes her a moment to understand that one of the soldiers, having reached however much he could offer, had decided to settle the matter through steel instead."
msgstr "Le toma un momento comprender que uno de los soldados, tras ofrecer todo lo que podía, había decidido zanjar el asunto con el acero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It takes nine days before they reach Lethram. The days pass uneventfully."
msgstr "Tardan nueve días en llegar a Lethram. Los días pasan sin incidentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It tightend its grip around her ankles."
msgstr "Apretó con fuerza sus tobillos."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "It told me what I could become, what the stars themselves had decreed for me."
msgstr "Me dijo lo que podría llegar a ser, lo que las estrellas mismas habían decretado para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took Sarah a brief moment to wonder why it felt so familiar to her in its design."
msgstr "Le tomó a Sarah un breve instante para preguntarse por qué su diseño le resultaba tan familiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took Sarah a moment to realize what it was."
msgstr "Le tomó a Sarah un momento darse cuenta de qué era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took Sarah a moment to understand."
msgstr "Le tomó a Sarah un momento comprenderlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took Sarah all of her strength to relearn to speak, just to offer some awed words of praise for his performance."
msgstr "Le costó a Sarah todo su esfuerzo volver a hablar, solo para ofrecer unas palabras de admiración por su actuación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took a long time before she finally made her way to one of the nearby towers."
msgstr "Tardó mucho tiempo antes de que finalmente se dirigiera a una de las torres cercanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took a lot to make the citizens take notice of anything in particular, but this, they took note of."
msgstr "Le tomó mucho que los ciudadanos prestaran atención a algo en particular, pero esto sí que les llamó la atención."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took a moment before it dawned on Sarah what he meant."
msgstr "Tardó un momento en darse cuenta de lo que quería decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took a moment for her to realize these were improvised shower stalls."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de que eran duchas improvisadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took a short moment before Sarah finally understood."
msgstr "Le tomó un breve instante antes de que Sarah finalmente lo entendiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took every part of Sarah's remaining willpower not to grab onto him and keep him here."
msgstr "Le costó a Sarah todo lo que le quedaba de voluntad para agarrarlo y quedarse con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a bit to get used to not wearing her ship clothes, but Belmont insisted that no wife of his would look as if she worked for a living."
msgstr "Le tomó un poco acostumbrarse a no usar sus ropas de barco, pero Belmont insistió en que ninguna esposa suya se viera como si trabajara para ganarse la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a minute until she finally spotted him walking quickly through the room, carrying a crate full of fresh produce from the market."
msgstr "Le tomó un minuto hasta que finalmente lo vio caminar rápidamente por la habitación, cargando una caja llena de frutas y verduras frescas del mercado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to realize everyone wasn't just standing there."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de que no todos simplemente estaban allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to realize her mouth was hanging open."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de que su boca estaba entreabierta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to realize what it was."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de qué era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to realize what she was looking at."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de lo que estaba mirando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to realize, these were more children than adults. The oldest near the front was a woman, but even she was only Sarah's age, twenty or so, she estimated."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento darse cuenta de que había más jóvenes que adultos. La mayor, casi al frente, era una mujer, pero incluso ella apenas tenía la edad de Sarah, unos veinte años, estimó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a moment to understand. Campfires."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento comprender. Fogatas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a while before she remembered."
msgstr "Tardó un buen rato en recordarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her a while, half drunk and lost in darkness, before Sarah finally found her way back to her bed."
msgstr "Le tomó un buen rato, medio borracha y perdida en la oscuridad, antes de que Sarah encontrara finalmente su camino de regreso a su cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her all of her strength to lift the crate up and drop it onto the cargo section of the wagon."
msgstr "Le costó todo su esfuerzo levantar la caja y dejarla caer sobre la sección de carga del carro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her eyes a moment longer to recognize it."
msgstr "Le tomó un instante más a sus ojos para reconocerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her mind a moment to make sense of what her eyes could see."
msgstr "Le tomó un momento a su mente comprender lo que sus ojos podían ver."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took her more than a moment to realize that it was herself."
msgstr "Llevaron más de un momento darse cuenta de que era ella misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took its toll on both sides, but the Tribesmen did not have the numbers to spare for such a grinding conflict."
msgstr "Le costó a ambas partes, pero los tribales no tenían reservas de efectivos para un conflicto tan agotador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took moments more before she finally opened her eyes enough to see the restraints that kept her tried to something."
msgstr "Tardó unos momentos más antes de abrir los ojos lo suficiente para ver las ataduras que la mantenían atada a algo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It took nearly a dozen servants to get me into this dress, I'm not so sure I'll manage to get myself out of it."
msgstr "Tuvieron que poner a casi una docena de sirvientes para vestirme con este vestido, y no estoy muy segura de que pueda quitármelo por mí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It took one step in her direction."
msgstr "Dio un paso hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It troubled Sarah to hear a man speak of an institution like slavery, as if it was anything other than barbaric."
msgstr "Perturbaba a Sarah escuchar a un hombre hablar de una institución como la esclavitud, como si no fuera bárbara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It troubled her more than it did them."
msgstr "La inquietaba más que a ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It turned around one last time before leaving."
msgstr "Se dio la vuelta una última vez antes de irse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It turned her on."
msgstr "La excitó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It turned its face-mask back towards Samayra."
msgstr "Volvió a girar su máscara de rostro hacia Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It turned its wicked face mask towards her."
msgstr "Dirigió su máscara perversa hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It used to be that in the days after his death, you would hear people whisper his name everywhere you went."
msgstr "Antes, en los días que siguieron a su muerte, se escuchaba susurrar su nombre por todas partes donde fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It used to."
msgstr "Antes solía ser así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It uttered out a word in broken speech."
msgstr "Dijo una palabra con voz entrecortada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It voice was sharp."
msgstr "Su voz era cortante."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It warms my heart to hear such kind words. Thank you for so graciously receiving us."
msgstr "Me conmueve el corazón escuchar palabras tan amables. Gracias por recibirnos con tanta generosidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It warms my heart to know you think of me like that."
msgstr "Me conmueve saber que me ves de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "It was I who detected the Mythran invasion. I was the one who set out to put together this Union Council."
msgstr "Fue yo quien detectó la invasión de los Mythran. Yo fui la que se puso a organizar este Consejo de la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was Nick, it was all him!"
msgstr "¡Fue Nick, fue todo él!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was Sakar who moved first."
msgstr "Fue Sakar quien actuó primero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was Sakar, now sitting off the back side of the cart."
msgstr "Era Sakar, ahora sentado en el extremo trasero del carro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was Samayra that finally leaned forward, pressing her lips up against Sarah's."
msgstr "Fue Samayra la que finalmente se inclinó hacia adelante, presionando sus labios contra los de Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was Sarah who finally decided to move forward."
msgstr "Fue Sarah quien finalmente decidió avanzar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was Varga who now reared himself."
msgstr "Fue Varga quien ahora se alzó."

msgctxt "speaker:Scout"
msgid "It was a Tribesman soldier. He identified himself as the leader of the regiment."
msgstr "Era un soldado de la tribu. Se identificó como el líder del regimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a balance that had worked well enough over the centuries to maintain a peace."
msgstr "Era un equilibrio que había funcionado bastante bien durante siglos para mantener la paz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a balancing act, to keep Nick remembering his place and yet also remind him that he only needed to endure for a week or two more."
msgstr "Era un equilibrio difícil, mantener que Nick recordara su lugar y, al mismo tiempo, hacerle saber que solo debía aguantar una semana o dos más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a battle for only a moment. Then it was a slaughter."
msgstr "Fue una batalla por un solo instante. Luego fue una matanza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a bit like an ant colony, she'd come to realize."
msgstr "Era como una colonia de hormigas, llegó a comprender."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a brief report from one of the provinces."
msgstr "Fue un breve informe de una de las provincias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a cage. A comfortable one, but a cage all the same."
msgstr "Era una jaula. Una cómoda, pero una jaula al fin y al cabo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a casual question, but she feared saying too much. She didn't want these men to know her origins."
msgstr "Fue una pregunta casual, pero temía decir demasiado. No quería que esos hombres supieran de sus orígenes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a celebration in Sarah's honor, and the greater it would be, the more glory it would heap on her."
msgstr "Era una celebración en honor de Sarah, y cuanto más grande fuera, mayor sería el brillo que se acumularía sobre ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a complicated routine at first."
msgstr "Al principio fue una complicada rutina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a different one than the orc before, but she had trouble telling them apart."
msgstr "Era diferente al orco anterior, pero le resultaba difícil distinguirlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a fear so deep she had never known it before."
msgstr "Era un miedo tan profundo que nunca había conocido antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a few hours later then the old soldier finally emerged from his bedroom and lazily walked into the kitchen."
msgstr "Pasaron unas horas y el viejo soldado finalmente salió de su habitación, caminando con pereza hacia la cocina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a few hours later when a knock at the door finally awakened Sarah from her solemn thoughts."
msgstr "Fueron unas horas más tarde cuando un golpe en la puerta finalmente despertó a Sarah de sus solemnes pensamientos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a few months after she had taken up as his student, when the inevitable happened."
msgstr "Pasaron varios meses desde que se convirtió en su alumna, cuando finalmente ocurrió lo inevitable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was a gift."
msgstr "Era un regalo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a good sign."
msgstr "Era un buen augurio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a hollow wish."
msgstr "Era un deseo vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a horrifying thought, that this house was in fact a living thing, but at the same time, the more she thought, the more it appeared to her as a powerful ally."
msgstr "Era un pensamiento aterrador que esa casa fuera, de hecho, una cosa viva, pero al mismo tiempo, cuanto más pensaba, tanto más le aparecía como una poderosa aliada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a life where softness was viewed as weakness, and kindness meant being taken advantage of."
msgstr "Era una vida en la que la suavidad se consideraba debilidad y la bondad significaba ser aprovechada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a little later on the day, just as promised and with the sun beginning to set, that Sarah arrived with Belmont at the church."
msgstr "Un poco más tarde, ese mismo día, justo como se había prometido y con el sol comenzando a ponerse, Sarah llegó a la iglesia junto con Belmont."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a little later when Sarah heard a knock at the door and found Sophia delivering her the promised water."
msgstr "Fue un poco más tarde cuando Sarah oyó un golpe en la puerta y encontró a Sophia entregándole el agua prometida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a little over a week later when the first council meeting that included Marion and Varga began."
msgstr "Fue un poco más de una semana después cuando comenzó la primera reunión del consejo que incluía a Marion y Varga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a long and tiring process, mostly designed to filter out the endless trivial requests that people would submit."
msgstr "Fue un proceso largo y agotador, diseñado principalmente para filtrar las interminables peticiones triviales que la gente presentaría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a long time and much more spit before he had even managed to fit all of himself inside of her ass."
msgstr "Fue un largo tiempo y mucha más saliva antes de que siquiera lograra meterse por completo en su culo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a long time befor either of them realized how dark it had gotten."
msgstr "Fue mucho tiempo antes de que ninguno de los dos se diera cuenta de qué tan oscuro había llegado a ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a lot, but Sarah was eager for the challenge. Finally she had something to put her mind to."
msgstr "Era mucho, pero Sarah estaba ansiosa por el desafío. Finalmente tenía algo en qué poner su mente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a lot."
msgstr "Era mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a map of the Union, that much was obvious. But it was covered in markings. Small figurines placed atop it."
msgstr "Era un mapa de la Unión, eso era evidente. Pero estaba cubierto de marcas. Pequeñas figuritas colocadas sobre él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a marvel to behold, if only for the skill with which they did it."
msgstr "Fue una maravilla de contemplar, si no fuera por la habilidad con que lo habían hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a massacre."
msgstr "Fue una masacre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a mess, she concluded."
msgstr "Fue un desastre, concluyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a miracle nobody else had woken up, or perhaps, much like Sarah, they kept themselves quiet."
msgstr "Fue un milagro que nadie más se hubiera despertado, o quizás, al igual que Sarah, habían mantenido el silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "It was a mistake and we shouldn't have done it. I shouldn't have done it. Or you. I don't...I don't remember who did what..."
msgstr "Fue un error y no debimos hacerlo. Yo no debí hacerlo. O tú. No recuerdo... no recuerdo quién hizo qué..."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It was a necklace made out of gold and jade, I thought it was pretty..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a pleasant quiet."
msgstr "Era una tranquilidad agradable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a price to pay."
msgstr "Era el precio que había que pagar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a prison, she reminded herself."
msgstr "Era una prisión, se repetía a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a rare few that managed to survive decade after decade and still soldier on."
msgstr "eran pocos los que lograban sobrevivir década tras década y seguir luchando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a reflex he performed, but there was never anything real behind it."
msgstr "Era un reflejo que él realizaba, pero nunca había nada real detrás de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a run down camp. Perhaps it had seen better days, but Sarah was just as certain that it had always been a ruin."
msgstr "Era un campamento descuidado. Quizás hubiera visto mejores días, pero Sarah estaba tan segura de que siempre había sido una ruina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a set of heavy, durable, armor covered with the metal plating."
msgstr "Era un conjunto de armadura pesada y duradera, cubierta con placas de metal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a sharp pain, but Sarah excercised control over her own body, and dominated the pain, pushing it back."
msgstr "Era un dolor agudo, pero Sarah ejerció control sobre su propio cuerpo y dominó el dolor, empujándolo hacia atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a single shot, fired same as another other and none would remember by which crew, that buried into the great walls."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a sizeable plot, she realized."
msgstr "Era una parcela considerable, lo comprendió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a small act of resistance to defy the man that called himself her master."
msgstr "Fue un pequeño acto de resistencia desafiar al hombre que se llamaba a sí mismo su amo."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "It was a small mistake, let it go"
msgstr "Fue un pequeño error, déjalo ir"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a soft culling, as soft as such a thing could be."
msgstr "Fue un sacrificio suave, tan suave como tal cosa podía ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a solid skill that most any decent mage should know."
msgstr "Era una habilidad sólida que cualquier mago decente debería conocer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a soothing sound."
msgstr "Era un sonido reconfortante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a state of mind with which she had become far too familiar by now."
msgstr "Era un estado de ánimo con el que había llegado a ser demasiado familiar por ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a strange kind of coldness, the kind that only existed in places that never knew anything other than cold."
msgstr "Era un frío extraño, el tipo que solo existe en lugares que nunca han conocido nada más que el frío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a strange realization for Sarah, that the ship that had been her entire world for nearly two weeks, was in fact a laughably small one compared to most others."
msgstr "Fue una extraña revelación para Sarah: el barco que había sido su mundo entero durante casi dos semanas era, de hecho, ridículamente pequeño en comparación con la mayoría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a strangely content feeling, she realized."
msgstr "Era una sensación de satisfacción extraña, lo comprendió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a tender kiss. Part passion, part confession. Sarah was showing Samayra what she wanted."
msgstr "Fue un beso tierno. Parte pasión, parte confesión. Sarah le mostraba a Samayra lo que deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a tiny tent, on the other side of the world, in a camp full of strangers..."
msgstr "Era una pequeña tienda de campaña, en el otro lado del mundo, en un campamento lleno de extraños..."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "It was a town here in Rosanna, a distance away from the capital."
msgstr "Era una ciudad aquí en Rosanna, lejos de la capital."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a warm smile, one that seemed strangely familiar to Sarah. It made her feel happy, but she struggled to know why."
msgstr "Era una sonrisa cálida, que parecía extrañamente familiar para Sarah. Le hizo sentir feliz, pero luchaba por saber por qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a way for her to be safe, while she planned on how she could reclaim her home."
msgstr "Era una forma de mantenerse segura mientras planeaba cómo recuperar su hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a weakness that had exposed them to the occupation of the Tribesmen."
msgstr "Era una debilidad que los había expuesto a la ocupación de los Tribales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a wicked bargain, but one Sarah felt she could strike."
msgstr "Era un trato perverso, pero uno que Sarah sentía que podía aceptar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was about sensing the energies around herself, those that resided within, learning to seize them, bend them, reshape them."
msgstr "Se trataba de percibir las energías que la rodeaban, aquellas que residían en su interior, aprendiendo a apoderarse de ellas, doblarlas y remodelarlas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was after nearly half-an-hour of marching that they met any opposition at all."
msgstr "Fue tras casi media hora de marcha cuando encontraron cualquier tipo de oposición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was after several hours when she finally noticed something different."
msgstr "Fue después de varias horas cuando ella finalmente notó algo diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was after that first week when their luck began to turn."
msgstr "Fue después de esa primera semana cuando su suerte comenzó a cambiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was all he needed to hear."
msgstr "Todo lo que necesitaba oír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was all hers...her prize..."
msgstr "Era todo suyo...su premio..."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It was all over your face."
msgstr "Estaba todo escrito en tu rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was all she could manage in restraining her body. To keep herself from flailing about."
msgstr "Era todo lo que podía controlar para contener su cuerpo y evitar que se descontrolara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was all she could manage in this strange place."
msgstr "Era todo lo que podía lograr en este lugar extraño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was all she could manage."
msgstr "Era todo lo que podía manejar."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It was almost a year ago when I first heard the rumors and I began to suspect that you might still live."
msgstr "Fue hace casi un año cuando escuché por primera vez los rumores y comencé a sospechar que aún podías estar vivo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was almost an hour later when the two finally emerged from below deck."
msgstr "Fue casi una hora después cuando ambos finalmente emergieron de la cubierta inferior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was almost hypnotic."
msgstr "Era casi hipnótico."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was almost...warm."
msgstr "Era casi... cálido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was already dark, and Dalia was sleeping."
msgstr "Ya era de noche y Dalia dormía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was already late, but enough candles were burning to keep out the dark."
msgstr "Ya era tarde, pero había suficientes velas encendidas para ahuyantar la oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was already the afternoon by the time that Sarah suddenly heard a commotion by the entrance gate."
msgstr "Ya era tarde cuando Sarah escuchó de repente un alboroto en la entrada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was also the end of the world, or as close as one could get."
msgstr "Era también el fin del mundo, o lo más cercano que se podía llegar a ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was also what made her a valuable ally, if she could be trusted. Strong in all the areas that Sarah was weak."
msgstr "También era lo que la hacía una aliada valiosa, si se podía confiar en ella. Fuerte en todas las áreas donde Sarah era débil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always hard to grasp the spirit's shape, if it even had such a thing as a true form."
msgstr "Era siempre difícil captar la forma del espíritu, si es que incluso tenía algo así como una verdadera forma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always like this when Lady Carolyn visited her."
msgstr "Siempre era así cuando la Dama Carolyn la visitaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always remarkable to Sarah by how little Samayra's clothes were tied together."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always the kind ones that suffered the most, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Siempre eran las buenas las que sufrían más, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always worrying how even the slightest mistake sometimes caused her to be found out."
msgstr "Siempre resultaba preocupante que incluso el más mínimo error la delatara a veces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an all encompassing need."
msgstr "Era una necesidad abarcadora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an army."
msgstr "Era un ejército."

msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "It was an decent pact, once the son came of age, he would have an acceptable match for his station."
msgstr "Era un pacto decente: una vez que el hijo alcanzara la edad adulta, tendría una pareja aceptable para su estamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an endless task, and yet, Sarah was glad for the distraction."
msgstr "Era una tarea interminable, y sin embargo, Sarah estaba agradecida por la distracción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an honest answer."
msgstr "Fue una respuesta sincera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an idea she had never given much thought to before."
msgstr "Era una idea a la que nunca había prestado mucha atención antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an idle question. Sarah knew exactly what the man wanted from her."
msgstr "Era una pregunta trivial. Sarah sabía exactamente lo que el hombre quería de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd and new sensation for Sarah."
msgstr "Fue una sensación extraña y nueva para Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd mix of pain and pleasure at being taken raw."
msgstr "Era una extraña mezcla de dolor y placer al ser tomada cruda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd sensation, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Fue una sensación extraña, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd sound, that for a moment, she couldn't place."
msgstr "Era un sonido extraño, algo que por un momento no pudo identificar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd thing, Sarah had come to realize."
msgstr "Era algo extraño, como había llegado a comprender Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an odd thing, the way in which the dimensions from the house betrayed its outward appearance."
msgstr "Era algo extraño, la manera en que las dimensiones de la casa traicionaban su apariencia exterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an older map, not the one they had used before in planning the campaign."
msgstr "Era un mapa más antiguo, no el que habían utilizado antes para planificar la campaña."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was an unacceptable solution."
msgstr "Era una solución inaceptable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was another familiar voice that woke her up."
msgstr "Fue otra voz conocida la que la despertó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was another frenzied hour later when Lady Carolyn arrived."
msgstr "Fue otra hora frenética más tarde cuando llegó la Dama Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was answers that she craved."
msgstr "Eran respuestas que anhelaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as Vaelen had said a stone that shone with light of crimson, but it was also not quite a gemstone or a ruby."
msgstr "Era como Vaelen había dicho: una piedra que brillaba con luz carmesí, pero no era exactamente una joya ni un rubí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as Xan had said a stone that shone with light of crimson, but it was also not quite a gemstone or a ruby."
msgstr "Era como Xan había dicho: una piedra que brillaba con luz carmesí, pero tampoco era exactamente una gema ni un rubí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as close a thing as the creature had to a face."
msgstr "Era lo más parecido a un rostro que la criatura podía tener."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as good of a promise as she was going to get out of him."
msgstr "Fue tan buena promesa como ella iba a recibir de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "It was as if I could read her mind and she mine. A glance. A small gesture. Enough to speak volumes."
msgstr "Era como si pudiera leer su mente y ella la mía. Una mirada. Un pequeño gesto. Suficiente para decir mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as if a current ran through every part of her body."
msgstr "Era como si una corriente recorriera cada parte de su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as if he saved it all up for her. Maybe he had."
msgstr "Era como si guardara todo para ella. Quizás lo hubiera hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as if he was looking at her and her alone, like she was the only person in the world."
msgstr "Era como si la estuviera mirando solo a ella, como si fuera la única persona en el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as much a fortress as it was a death trap."
msgstr "Era tanto una fortaleza como una trampa mortal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was better than sleeping on hay."
msgstr "Era mejor que dormir en paja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was better than to be beaten."
msgstr "Era mejor que ser azotada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was better this way, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Era mejor así, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was better to just let the matter rest, if only for tonight."
msgstr "Era mejor dejar que la cosa se calmara, aunque fuera solo por esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was busy, but to Sarah, it felt like the good kind."
msgstr "Estaba ocupado, pero para Sarah, sentía que era de la buena clase."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was by the ninth day that there was a knock on the door that finally brought some news."
msgstr "Fue al noveno día cuando un golpe en la puerta trajo finalmente alguna noticia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was caught loosely in her grip, spinning from side to side as she twirled it around."
msgstr "Estaba sujeta por ella con un agarre flojo, girando de lado a lado mientras la hacía dar vueltas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was chaos, but it could not have been more different than from what had come before. This was a happy disorder."
msgstr "Era caos, pero no podía ser más diferente de lo que había precedido. Era un desorden feliz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was clear that his mother had sewn and adjusted the dress to make it more than it had been."
msgstr "Era evidente que su madre había cosido y ajustado el vestido para hacerlo más de lo que ya era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was clear they were all experienced on the road, the way they worked together without speaking a word."
msgstr "Era evidente que todos tenían experiencia en el camino, la forma en que trabajaban juntos sin decir ni una palabra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was clear to Sarah that this was hardly Carolyn's first attempt at such a thing."
msgstr "Era evidente para Sarah que aquello no era la primera vez que Carolyn intentaba hacer eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was clearly woven from powerful magics, but to the touch, she could feel no magic within it at all."
msgstr "Era claramente tejido con magias poderosas, pero al tacto no podía sentir ninguna magia en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was closer to two animals breeding."
msgstr "Era más bien como dos animales apareándose."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was cold. It made her feel more aware of her nakedness."
msgstr "Estaba frío. Le hizo sentir más expuesta en su desnudez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was comforting to think there was a strategy, a plan. And who was she to argue? Alaric had years of experience, compared to her few weeks."
msgstr "Era reconfortante pensar que había una estrategia, un plan. ¿Y quién era ella para argumentar? Alaric tenía años de experiencia, comparado con sus pocas semanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "It was concerning the tribes of the eastern desert."
msgstr "Se trataba de las tribus del desierto oriental."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "It was concerning...the military, was it?"
msgstr "—Preocupaba... ¿a la milicia, verdad? —preguntó con curiosidad, observándola."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was constant, it was everywhere."
msgstr "Era constante, estaba en todas partes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was cruel, she thought."
msgstr "Era cruel, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was decided. A brief moment of respite, away from all the business of ruling. It would to her good."
msgstr "Se decidió. Un breve momento de respiro, lejos de todo el negocio del gobierno. Le haría bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was deep in the night, and after the festivities had ended, the castle was silent as the grave."
msgstr "Era muy tarde en la noche y, tras haber terminado las fiestas, el castillo estaba silencioso como una tumba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was different for her, because she could still vaguely remember her mother. Thomas had been too small before she passed."
msgstr "Para ella era diferente, porque aún podía recordar vagamente a su madre. Thomas había sido demasiado pequeño cuando ella murió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was different in style from where she had grown up, and yet, she could recognize it. The wealth, the opulence."
msgstr "Era diferente en estilo al lugar donde había crecido, y sin embargo, podía reconocerlo. La riqueza, la opulencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "It was different when I was first assigned to her."
msgstr "Era diferente cuando me asignaron por primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was different, but not all that much. It seemed like a library, more desks, books, but the style reminded her of the house she had been in only moments earlier."
msgstr "Era diferente, pero no tanto. Parecía una biblioteca, más escritorios y libros, pero el estilo le recordaba a la casa en la que había estado momentos antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was different. But she could make it work."
msgstr "Era diferente. Pero ella podía hacer que funcionara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was done, no point wasting more time on it."
msgstr "Ya estaba hecho, no había punto en perder más tiempo con ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was done."
msgstr "Estaba hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was early in the morning when Sarah woke to the first rays of light sneaking through the buildings."
msgstr "Era temprano en la mañana cuando Sarah despertó con los primeros rayos de luz filtrándose entre los edificios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was early next morning when the last of the preparations were finished and the final battle of the war began."
msgstr "Era temprano la mañana siguiente cuando finalizaron los últimos preparativos y comenzó la batalla final de la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was early. Only ever so slightly."
msgstr "Era temprano. Solo un poco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy enough, she realized, to step out into the crowd and vanish in a place like this. One more face among the millions."
msgstr "Era fácil, se dio cuenta, salir entre la multitud y desaparecer en un lugar así. Solo otra cara entre millones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy for Lady Carolyn to pretend that there were no strings attached to it, but Sarah knew better."
msgstr "Era fácil para Lady Carolyn fingir que no había compromisos con ello, pero Sarah sabía mejor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy for her to scream out, for it was no lie."
msgstr "Era fácil para ella gritar, porque no era mentira."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy to look at him like that, for his eyes were often harsh and every part of him dominant."
msgstr "Era fácil mirarlo de esa manera, pues sus ojos eran a menudo duros y cada parte de él era dominante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy with him, Sarah thought, because he always knew exactly what he wanted from her."
msgstr "Era fácil con él, pensó Sarah, porque siempre sabía exactamente lo que quería de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy work, perhaps even beneath her as a mage, but the truth was that she liked the excuse."
msgstr "Era un trabajo sencillo, quizás incluso por debajo de sus capacidades como maga, pero la verdad es que le gustaba la excusa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy, for a man like him."
msgstr "Era fácil, para un hombre como él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was easy, to forget, when she was with him."
msgstr "Era fácil olvidar, cuando estaba con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was easy. Two guys like that don't stand a chance against even a little bit of magic."
msgstr "Era fácil. Dos tipos como ese no tienen ninguna oportunidad contra ni siquiera un poco de magia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was enough to bring anyone to rage."
msgstr "Era suficiente para llevar a cualquiera a la rabia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was exactly that advantage that Kate was now trying to play into, leaping forward again as she swiped the blade at Sarah's legs."
msgstr "Fue exactamente esa ventaja la que Kate intentaba aprovechar ahora, saltando de nuevo y asestando un tajo con la hoja hacia las piernas de Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was exactly the kind of room that was build to keep in secrets."
msgstr "Era exactamente el tipo de habitación construida para guardar secretos."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "It was exhilarating."
msgstr "Era exaltante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was far from the first time she had spend her night in his bed."
msgstr "Lejos de ser la primera vez que había pasado la noche en su cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was far from the first time that she had undressed herself before Lady Carolyn, but there was always something embarassing about it."
msgstr "Lejos estaba de ser la primera vez que se había desnudado ante Lady Carolyn, pero siempre hubo algo vergonzoso en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was fast. So fast."
msgstr "Fue rápido. Tan rápido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was fine, fitting of her station, but it all felt rather clinical to her. No life."
msgstr "Estaba bien, acorde a su condición, pero todo le parecía bastante clínico para ella. Sin vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was food, she tried to convince herself."
msgstr "Era comida, se intentó convencerse a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was foolishness, born from a delusion that her life had not fundamentally changed, that she could go back to the way things were."
msgstr "Era una tontería, nacida de la ilusión de que su vida no había cambiado fundamentalmente y de que podría volver a como eran las cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was fortunate then for the rest of the world that Mythra was so prone to infighting, or else every living soul would have to answer to them."
msgstr "Fue afortunado entonces para el resto del mundo que Mythra fuera tan propensa a las disputas internas, o de lo contrario cada alma viva tendría que rendir cuentas ante ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was fucking her mouth, she realized, and had little other care for her."
msgstr "Era su boca la que se follaba, lo comprendió, y poco más le importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was functional, but she doubted she'd ever have chosen to wear something like this in her life. That is, if her life had not turned out the way that it had."
msgstr "Era funcional, pero dudaba que en su vida hubiera elegido jamás usar algo así. Es decir, si su vida no hubiera terminado siendo como terminó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was funny to Sarah, that there was this side to him. To the warrior. The killer."
msgstr "Era gracioso para Sarah que él tuviera ese lado. El del guerrero. El asesino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was general Barion who rose first."
msgstr "Fue el general Barion quien se levantó primero."

msgctxt "speaker:Servant"
msgid "It was handmade by one of the finest tailors in the Weaving district."
msgstr "Fue cosida por uno de los mejores sastres del distrito del Tejido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard for her to have lived an entire life, safe and secure, to now suddenly see danger in every direction."
msgstr "Era difícil para ella haber vivido toda una vida segura y tranquila, solo para ver ahora peligro en todas direcciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard for her to imagine what these people must have endured."
msgstr "Le resultaba difícil imaginarse qué debían haber sufrido esas personas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to argue for Sarah. Maybe the thing had been a demon, what did she really know about such things?"
msgstr "Era difícil defender a Sarah. Quizá la cosa había sido un demonio; ¿qué sabía ella realmente de tales cosas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to believe she'd really just done that..."
msgstr "Era difícil creer que realmente acabara de hacer eso..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to disagree with him, given her situation."
msgstr "Era difícil discrepar con él, dada su situación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to feel sympathy for the creatures, but caught in a trap, they seemed almost animal like."
msgstr "Era difícil sentir empatía por las criaturas, pero atrapadas en una trampa, parecían casi animales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to find anyone she could trust these days."
msgstr "Era difícil encontrar a alguien en quien confiar estos días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to know who was doing what at any moment."
msgstr "Era difícil saber quién hacía qué en cualquier momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to look dignified, fully naked and bound, Sarah realized."
msgstr "Era difícil verse digna, atada y completamente desnuda, se dio cuenta Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to maintain an idea of a self. An identity. When the sum of her life was to turn her body into his perfect plaything."
msgstr "Era difícil mantener una idea de sí misma. Una identidad. Cuando la suma de su vida iba a convertir su cuerpo en el juguete perfecto para él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to make out against the darkness."
msgstr "Era difícil distinguirlo contra la oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard to make out the exact size, given that so much of it was overgrown, but even from what little she saw, Sarah knew it was massive."
msgstr "Era difícil determinar su tamaño exacto, dado que gran parte de él estaba cubierto de vegetación, pero incluso desde lo poco que veía, Sarah sabía que era enorme."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard work, even more so when done under the heat of the sun. One end of the deck to the other was easily two hours of work."
msgstr "Era un trabajo duro, aún más cuando se hacía bajo el calor del sol. De un extremo de la cubierta al otro eran fácilmente dos horas de esfuerzo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hard, even within the Union Kingdoms people struggled to come together."
msgstr "Era difícil, incluso dentro de los Reinos Unidos la gente luchaba por unirse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hardly even a compliment as much as it was a statement of fact."
msgstr "Era apenas una afirmación de hecho, más que un cumplido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was harsh on the ears, and she could make no sense of it."
msgstr "Era agudo para los oídos, y no lograba comprenderlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was heavier than she had thought."
msgstr "Era más pesado de lo que había pensado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was heavy on the air. A stench unlike any other."
msgstr "Estaba denso en el aire. Un hedor inigualable, repulsivo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was her and the others out here on the road. She needed to get to know the other men she was travelling with."
msgstr "Era ella y los demás fuera en el camino. Necesitaba conocer a los otros hombres con quienes viajaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was her body, she had come to conclude."
msgstr "Era su cuerpo, llegó a concluir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was her daughter who was first to speak again."
msgstr "Fue su hija quien habló de nuevo la primera."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "It was her idea, all of it!"
msgstr "¡Fue su idea, todo de ella!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was her own arrogance that had allowed her to deny it for so long, she concluded."
msgstr "Fue su propia arrogancia la que le permitió negarlo durante tanto tiempo, concluyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "It was her voice, but she had died in the forest and become a Woodland spirit."
msgstr "Era su voz, pero había muerto en el bosque y se había convertido en un espíritu del bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was her, giving up her body in exchange for his training."
msgstr "Era ella, entregando su cuerpo a cambio de su entrenamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was here, after nearly an hour of walking, that Sarah finally came upon the city gates of Lethram."
msgstr "Fue aquí, tras casi una hora de caminar, cuando Sarah finalmente llegó a las puertas de la ciudad de Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was his dick, as much as she didn't want to admit it. It had a degree of control over her that she could not explain."
msgstr "Era su polla, aunque no quisiera admitirlo. Tenía un dominio sobre ella que no podía explicar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was his grip on her body, soft and gentle, that made her first understand."
msgstr "Fue su agarre sobre su cuerpo, suave y gentil, lo que le hizo comprenderlo por primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was hollow and empty without him."
msgstr "Era hueco y vacío sin él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was however enough for her husband to stop working and make sure they would be provided for."
msgstr "Sin embargo, era suficiente para que su esposo dejara de trabajar y asegurara que ambos estuvieran provistos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was humiliating."
msgstr "Era humillante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was important to her that her men saw that she endure the same as they did."
msgstr "Era importante para ella que sus hombres vieran que soportaba lo mismo que ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was impossible, and her mind screamed at the unnatural sight."
msgstr "Era imposible, y su mente gritaba ante la visión antinatural."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was impossible, except for one kind of person."
msgstr "Era imposible, salvo para un tipo de persona."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in Mary that Sarah managed to find some kind of semblance of a normal life."
msgstr "Fue en Mary cuando Sarah logró encontrar cierto semblante de vida normal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in Nick's face that she saw real anger."
msgstr "Fue en la cara de Nick donde vio el verdadero enfado."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "It was in her darkest hour when a thought came to her."
msgstr "Fue en su hora más oscura cuando le vino un pensamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in many ways, everything that Rahayal was not."
msgstr "Era, de muchas maneras, todo lo que Rahayal no era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in part this steady, long lasting rule, that have given the Mythran Empire its stability."
msgstr "En parte fue esa gobernanza constante y duradera la que otorgó al Imperio Mythran su estabilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in that condition, seated up front on the wagon, when her eyes first fell upon the city of Rahayal."
msgstr "Fue en esa condición, sentada al frente del carro, cuando sus ojos se posaron por primera vez sobre la ciudad de Rahayal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was in this order, Sarah, Caleb, Ephraim, that the three ended up laying naked on Sarah's bed."
msgstr "Fue en este orden, Sarah, Caleb, Ephraim, que los tres terminaron acostados desnudos sobre la cama de Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It was incredible!"
msgstr "¡Era increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "It was incredible, Sarah, absolutely incredible."
msgstr "¡Fue increíble, Sarah, absolutamente increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was indeed far less in quality than what she was used to, but that made it perfect for cleaning."
msgstr "Era en efecto de mucha menor calidad de lo que estaba acostumbrada, pero eso la hacía perfecta para limpiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was insignificant compared to the deep pleasure of this moment."
msgstr "Era insignificante comparado con el profundo placer de este momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was intricate."
msgstr "Era intrincada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was just her and Dalia. The Master had gone."
msgstr "Solo ella y Dalia quedaban. El Maestro se había ido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was large enough that his hand nearly enveloped hers."
msgstr "Era lo suficientemente grande para que su mano casi envolviera la de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was larger than any other room on the ship."
msgstr "Era más grande que cualquier otra sala del barco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was late in the evening when Sarah stood near the entrance to the slave quarters."
msgstr "Era avanzada la noche cuando Sarah se paró cerca de la entrada a las cuadras de esclavos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was late into the night when a group of about four men stumbled into the tavern."
msgstr "Era muy tarde cuando un grupo de unos cuatro hombres tambaleó hacia la taberna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was late that when their master returned home."
msgstr "Era tarde aquella noche cuando su amo regresó a casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was laughable. She could change much, but even she could not change her homeland enough to make that acceptable."
msgstr "Era ridículo. Podía cambiar mucho, pero ni ella podía cambiar lo suficiente su tierra natal para que eso fuera aceptable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was liberating, to let go of even the notion of any modesty."
msgstr "Era liberador dejar ir incluso la noción de cualquier modestia."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "It was like a busy market, except instead of trading goods, the important people of the Empire traded favors."
msgstr "Era como un mercado bullicioso, salvo que en lugar de intercambiar mercancías, las personas importantes del Imperio intercambiaban favores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like a crack in the wall. The walls still stood, but they wouldn't hold."
msgstr "Era como una grieta en la pared. Las paredes seguían de pie, pero ya no las sostendrían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like a fragment of a rainbow, or a prism, bursting out from the edge."
msgstr "Era como un fragmento de arcoíris, o un prisma, estallando desde el borde."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like a pain, long suffered, nwo suddenly gone. Like an unending noise, suddenly quieted."
msgstr "Era como un dolor que había sufrido durante mucho tiempo y que ahora, de pronto, había desaparecido. Era como un ruido incesante que, de repente, se había callado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like a stretch, with one orc in front and another behind her, carrying her as she was restrained."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It was like a wound that just...never healed."
msgstr "Era como una herida que simplemente... nunca sanó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like an object that wasn't hot or cold, but simply had no temperature at all. As if it stood somehow outside of the rest of the world."
msgstr "Era como un objeto que no tenía calor ni frío, sino simplemente ninguna temperatura. Como si estuviera de alguna manera fuera del resto del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like nothing she had ever felt before in her entire life."
msgstr "Era como nada que hubiera sentido en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like soothing salve spread across a burn. The pain swiftly fading."
msgstr "Era como un bálsamo calmante extendido sobre una quemadura. El dolor se desvanecía rápidamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "It was like they didn't even notice me."
msgstr "Era como si no me vieran ni siquiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was like this, deep into the night and each with more than their share of wine, that Sarah finally saw her chance."
msgstr "Fue así, a media noche y cada uno con más de su justa copa de vino, cuando Sarah finalmente vio su oportunidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was made for combat more than for marching, and definitely had not been made for walking in a forest."
msgstr "Fue hecha para el combate más que para la marcha, y definitivamente no fue diseñada para caminar por un bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It was made, in full."
msgstr "Estaba hecha, por completo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was magic that gave me a way back to getting some degree of control over my life."
msgstr "Fue la magia que me dio una vía para recuperar cierto grado de control sobre mi vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was many months after their marriage when Sarah felt the signs of the changing of her body."
msgstr "Fueron muchos meses después de su matrimonio cuando Sarah sintió los signos del cambio en su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It was many of the other noble families that could not imagine running from all their holdings."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was marked by a crimson seal."
msgstr "Estaba marcado con un sello carmesí."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It was maybe a week or two before I left."
msgstr "Fue quizás una semana o dos antes de que me fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "It was me and Dio, and others like us, elite soldiers from special school branches, that would make up this new army."
msgstr "Fue yo y Dio, junto con otros como nosotros, soldados de élite procedentes de las ramas especiales de la academia, quienes formarían este nuevo ejército."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was meaningless to resist much longer."
msgstr "No tenía sentido resistir mucho más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was men like Alaric, brutes, that took what they could take, simply because nobody would stop them."
msgstr "Eran hombres como Alaric, brutos, que tomaban lo que podían tomar, simplemente porque nadie se atrevía a detenerlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was moments like these where Sarah remembred just how vulnerable she really was."
msgstr "Era en momentos como estos cuando Sarah recordaba cuán vulnerable era realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was more extravagant than even her room back in Castle Reinmeer."
msgstr "Era más extravagante que incluso su habitación en el Castillo Reinmeer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was more often than not that he dragged both of them into his bedroom, or really, most anywhere else."
msgstr "Casi siempre era él quien los arrastraba a su dormitorio, o mejor dicho, a cualquier sitio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was more than simple greed."
msgstr "Era más que una simple codicia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was more than simply a desire. It was her divine obligation."
msgstr "Era más que un simple deseo. Era su obligación divina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was more than two weeks after the victory over the eastern tribesmen, when Sarah arrived early for a council meeting, surprised to find the room already full."
msgstr "Fue más de dos semanas después de la victoria sobre los tribus del este, cuando Sarah llegó temprano a una reunión del consejo, sorprendida al encontrar la sala ya llena."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "It was my intention to discuss with you an expedition to Varany, even though I am well aware of your position."
msgstr "Mi intención era discutir contigo una expedición a Varany, aunque estoy perfectamente consciente de tu posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was near the end of her second week when she was finally called over to receive her first pay."
msgstr "Fue cerca del final de su segunda semana cuando finalmente fue convocada para recibir su primer salario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was near the end of the day when the goblin guided her through a narrow crack in the mountain, that the world changed."
msgstr "Fue cerca del final del día cuando el gobelin la guió por una grieta estrecha en la montaña, y el mundo cambió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was near the end of the night that Sarah came upon a room she had not yet encountered before."
msgstr "Fue cerca del final de la noche cuando Sarah llegó a una habitación que aún no había encontrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nice enough, speaking perhaps to Jaeid's station in life."
msgstr "Era bastante agradable, hablando quizás del estatus de Jaeid en la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nice that some things never changed, no matter where you were in the world."
msgstr "Era agradable que algunas cosas nunca cambiaran, sin importar dónde te encontraras en el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Ayaka"
msgid "It was nice to meet you Sarah, I'm sure we'll speak again."
msgstr "Fue un placer conocerte, Sarah; estoy segura de que volveremos a hablar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nice, for a moment, to realize there was someone who she understood and who could understand her back."
msgstr "Fue agradable, por un momento, darse cuenta de que había alguien que la entendía y que podía entenderla a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nice."
msgstr "Fue agradable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nicer than most others she had come across, but in Rosanna this house would not have impressed much."
msgstr "Era más agradable que la mayoría de los demás con los que había topado, pero en Rosanna esta casa no habría impresionado mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was night."
msgstr "Era de noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was no fortune that would buy her a castle, but Sarah no longer dreamed of castles."
msgstr "No era una fortuna que pudiera comprarle un castillo, pero Sarah ya no soñaba con ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was no guarantee that he would do nothing, but it made it so that he couldn't try anything too serious. Perhaps, in some part, it was also to protect Nick from himself."
msgstr "No era garantía de que no hiciera nada, pero sí de que no intentara nada demasiado serio. Quizás, en parte, también fuera para proteger a Nick de sí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was no longer a debasement for her, for she had hardly a sense of self left."
msgstr "Ya no era una degradación para ella, pues apenas le quedaba un sentido del yo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not a question of whether he would take her on a given day, but rather, only a question of how often."
msgstr "No se trataba de si él la tomaría en un día concreto, sino simplemente de con qué frecuencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not empty."
msgstr "No estaba vacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not her own will, but the will of the mark that compelled her body to obey him."
msgstr "No era su propia voluntad, sino la del marcado la que obligaba a su cuerpo a obedecerle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not just the length of him, but also his girth."
msgstr "No era solo su longitud, sino también su grosor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long after she had met Xan, that she had met Razaphel."
msgstr "No fue mucho tiempo después de conocer a Xan cuando conoció a Razafael."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long after that a messenger came to the council room, handing Kravel a letter."
msgstr "No fue mucho tiempo después de eso cuando un mensajero llegó a la sala del consejo, entregando una carta a Kravel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long after when Sarah felt him thrust his final thrust, his cock swelling one last time."
msgstr "No pasó mucho tiempo después cuando Sarah sintió cómo él la penetraba con su último empujón, su polla hinchándose una última vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long after when Sarah watched Mary throw her head back and scream out her pleasure."
msgstr "No pasó mucho tiempo después cuando Sarah vio a Mary lanzar la cabeza hacia atrás y gritar su placer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long after when the first course was begun to be put out."
msgstr "No pasó mucho tiempo después de que se comenzara a servir el primer plato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long before she cried out as she came."
msgstr "No tardó en soltar un grito cuando llegó al orgasmo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not long before the rush of the orgasm roiled over her body."
msgstr "No pasó mucho tiempo antes de que la oleada del orgasmo agitara su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not merely the beauty of Samayra, or the beauty of her performance, but Sarah could also feel an old part of herself return."
msgstr "No fue solo la belleza de Samayra, ni la de su actuación; Sarah también sintió que una parte antigua de sí misma regresaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not much. Stale. Strange. But it fed her and kept the hunger at bay."
msgstr "No fue mucho. Estancado. Extraño. Pero la alimentó y mantuvo la hambre a raya."

msgctxt "speaker:King-On-The-Outside"
msgid "It was not our race that began this war."
msgstr "No fue nuestra raza la que comenzó esta guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not simply great strength, this was impossible strength. The kind that made a ragdoll out of a body."
msgstr "No era simplemente gran fuerza; esta era una fuerza imposible. La clase que convertía un cuerpo en un muñeco de trapo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not sleep."
msgstr "No era el sueño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not so much a battle as it was a slaughter. Soldiers found the enemy trapped under their horses, and jabbed their blades into their necks, killing the enemy with ease."
msgstr "No fue tanto una batalla como un masacre. Los soldados encontraron al enemigo atrapado bajo sus caballos y clavaron sus espadas en sus cuellos, matando a los enemigos con facilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not so much within her, as it was becoming a part of her."
msgstr "No era tanto algo que estuviera dentro de ella, como algo que se estaba convirtiendo en parte de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not unheard of for mages to step unto a battlefield, but Sarah could not help wonder why this battle was worth their intervention."
msgstr "No era infrecuente que los magos pisaran un campo de batalla, pero Sarah no pudo evitar preguntarse por qué esta batalla merecía su intervención."

msgctxt "speaker:Curator"
msgid "It was not until another century later, when the book reached the early Mythran empire, when it rose to prominence."
msgstr "No fue hasta otro siglo después, cuando el libro llegó al temprano Imperio Mythran y ganó prominencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was not violence that would resolve this."
msgstr "No era la violencia lo que resolvería esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nothing like before, when Sarah had faced a small advance group of poorly armed mercenaries."
msgstr "Ya nada era igual que antes, cuando Sarah se enfrentó a un pequeño grupo de mercenarios mal armados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was nothing, but right now, it felt like heaven to her."
msgstr "Para ella era nada, pero en ese momento se sentía como el cielo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was now late, deep into the night. With clouds having gathered, even the stars and the moon offered no reprieve."
msgstr "Ya era tarde, muy entrada la noche. Con las nubes reunidas, ni siquiera las estrellas y la luna ofrecían alivio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was obvious that she was done having whatever fun she had been having with Sarah."
msgstr "Era obvio que había terminado con cualquier diversión que estuviera teniendo con Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was obvious to her that there was more than professional interest here."
msgstr "Era obvio para ella que había más que interés profesional aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was obvious to her the young man was infatuated with her."
msgstr "Era obvio para ella que el joven estaba enamorado de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was odd, because she had known her spymaster to be, above all other things, a man of few emotions."
msgstr "Era extraño, porque ella había conocido a su jefe de espionaje como un hombre que, ante todo, era poco emocional."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "It was odd. I knew that I should have been scared...but instead I was calm."
msgstr "Era extraño. Sabía que debería haber estado asustado... pero en su lugar, estaba tranquilo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was oddly like that colour, and yet, it also struck Sarah as somehow uniquely distinct, as if she had never seen anything like it before."
msgstr "Era extrañamente similar a ese color, y sin embargo, también le pareció a Sarah de alguna manera singularmente distinto, como si nunca hubiera visto nada parecido antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was of no use in this town, but perhaps she could use it in the future. Better to have the option, she thought as she stored it."
msgstr "No servía de nada en este pueblo, pero quizás podría usarlo en el futuro. Mejor tener la opción, pensó mientras lo guardaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was on such a night, where Sarah could hear the men whisper among themselves, that she had been invited to Vaelen's tent."
msgstr "Fue en una noche así, donde Sarah podía oír a los hombres susurrar entre sí, cuando la invitaron a la tienda de Vaelen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was on this second day, that suddenly, the flap to the tent was pulled back."
msgstr "Fue en este segundo día cuando, de repente, se arrancó la cortina de la tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was one more way in which she could be useful, and at the same time, it allowed her to explore the city."
msgstr "Era otra forma en la que podía ser útil, y al mismo tiempo, le permitía explorar la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was one of Sarah's constant fears, going slow."
msgstr "Era uno de los miedos constantes de Sarah: ir despacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was one of the rare few things she could still sense, for by now, her body was all but spend and her mind in tatters."
msgstr "Era una de las pocas cosas que aún podía percibir, pues ahora su cuerpo estaba casi agotado y su mente en ruinas."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "It was one thing for people to slave away for an emperor or empress that they could see themselves."
msgstr "Era una cosa que la gente podía hacer por un emperador o emperatriz que podían ver."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was one way to live a life, she thought to herself."
msgstr "Era una forma de vivir la vida, pensó para sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only a little over a month when the child finally arrived."
msgstr "Solo habían pasado un poco más de un mes cuando finalmente llegó el niño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only early the next day when she awoke again, her child neatly bathed and swaddled."
msgstr "Solo era temprano al día siguiente cuando ella despertó de nuevo, con su hijo recién bañado y envuelto en pañales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only her and her own desires that mattered in the moment. No other onlookers, no other parties."
msgstr "En ese instante, solo importaban ella y sus propios deseos. No había más espectadores, ni otras partes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only his tip and already Sarah doubted she was ever going to fit all of him inside her."
msgstr "Solo su punta y ya Sarah dudaba de que pudiera acomodarlo todo dentro de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only in the end, when their bodies had taken all they could take, that the spirit released them."
msgstr "Solo al final, cuando sus cuerpos hubieran tomado todo lo que podían, fue cuando el espíritu los liberó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only late in the day when the sun had already begun to set when a loud horn rang out."
msgstr "Solo fue al final del día, cuando el sol ya comenzaba a ocultarse, cuando sonó una bocina fuerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only later in the day when Vaelen finally found her."
msgstr "Solo fue más tarde en el día cuando Vaelen la encontró finalmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only later that Sarah realized it was obvious."
msgstr "Solo más tarde fue cuando Sarah se dio cuenta de que era obvio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only moonlight that lit the room when they finally reached the end of their argument."
msgstr "Solo la luz de la luna iluminaba la habitación cuando finalmente llegaron al final de su discusión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only near the end of the night, when the celebrations had finally begun to slow down, that Sarah found her husband again."
msgstr "Solo fue cerca del final de la noche, cuando las celebraciones habían comenzado a calmarse, cuando Sarah encontró a su marido de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only right that he punished her, she thought."
msgstr "Era justo que él la castigara, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only that last task that he ever paid any real attention to, and so Sarah knew she could manage."
msgstr "Fue la única tarea a la que él realmente prestó atención, y así Sarah supo que podía aguantarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "It was only the rare few who truly weighed the lives they held in their hands."
msgstr "Solo pocos pesaban realmente las vidas que tenían entre sus manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only towards the end of the night, when the mood suddenly shifted."
msgstr "Solo fue hacia el final de la noche cuando el ambiente cambió repentinamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only when one woman appeared from the masses, that his posture changed."
msgstr "Solo fue cuando una mujer emergió de la multitud que su postura cambió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was only when the front door opened and Jaeid entered, that Sarah became aware of the passing of the time."
msgstr "Solo fue cuando se abrió la puerta principal y entró Jaeid cuando Sarah tomó conciencia del paso del tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was outside, in the open...yet it also felt strangely isolated. Removed from the rest of the world."
msgstr "Era afuera, al aire libre... sin embargo, también se sentía extrañamente aislada. Alejada del resto del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "It was over by the bend in the road, where we passed the large tree."
msgstr "Era por la curva del camino, donde pasamos el gran árbol."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was over."
msgstr "Acabado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was overpowering, so much of it she could hardly stand it, and yet in equal measure Sarah wanted more of it."
msgstr "Era abrumadora; tenía tanta de ella que apenas podía sostenerse, y sin embargo, en igual medida, Sarah deseaba más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was pain, but a kind Sarah oddly yearned for."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was painful, but a good pain."
msgstr "Era doloroso, pero un buen dolor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was part compliment, part insult."
msgstr "Era parte de un cumplido y parte de una ofensa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was part truth and part performance."
msgstr "Era parte verdad y parte actuación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was perfect."
msgstr "Era perfecto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was plentiful and it was thick, and still, she managed."
msgstr "Era abundante y espeso, y aún así, logró hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was pointless the moment they caught her."
msgstr "Fue inútil desde el momento en que la atraparon."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was pointless, and he would be more harsh if she resisted."
msgstr "Era inútil, y sería más duro si ella se resistía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was pointless, she realized."
msgstr "Era inútil, lo comprendió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was poor, and perhaps, that was its only attraction. Cheap land and cheap homes for those too poor to manage anywhere else."
msgstr "Era pobre, y quizás eso era su única atracción. Terreno barato y casas baratas para aquellos demasiado pobres para gestionarse en cualquier otro lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was punishment, she realized. Payback for having teased the man in the desert, for having denied him what he wanted."
msgstr "Era castigo, lo comprendió. Retribución por haber burlado al hombre del desierto, por haberle negado lo que deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "It was quite something, Sis, I'll tell you that."
msgstr "Era algo bastante impresionante, hermana; te lo digo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was rare for him to have much use for her after he had finished."
msgstr "Era raro que él tuviera mucho uso para ella después de haber terminado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was rock hard and warm to the palm of her hand."
msgstr "Era dura como una roca y cálida bajo la palma de su mano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was rough, but they had only just landed. It was a miracle there was even anything to be critical about."
msgstr "Era áspero, pero apenas acababan de aterrizar. Era un milagro que hubiera algo sobre lo cual poder criticar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was rude to refuse a gift."
msgstr "Era grosero rechazar un regalo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was several days later when the deal on the house closed."
msgstr "Fueron varios días después cuando se cerró el trato sobre la casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was several hours later when they finally had to stop for the night."
msgstr "Fueron varias horas más tarde cuando finalmente tuvieron que detenerse para pasar la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was she who should be grateful."
msgstr "Era ella quien debía estar agradecida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was she, Sarah now realized, how gave him cause to be cruel to her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was signed by Kamal himself personally, the many that occupied her ancestral home."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was silent for a while, the word murder, seemingly dominating the room."
msgstr "Hubo un silencio prolongado, la palabra 'asesinato' pareciendo dominar la sala."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was simply a fact that he had no need of any chain."
msgstr "Era simplemente un hecho de que no necesitaba ninguna cadena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was simply a phrase, and yet, Sarah felt as if she was destroying something more. Some part of her inner self."
msgstr "Era simplemente una frase, y sin embargo, Sarah sintió como si estuviera destruyendo algo más. Algún fragmento de su interior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was small, Sarah noted. Not the kind of place she would have gotten married if...she didn't finish the thought."
msgstr "Era pequeño, observó Sarah. No era el tipo de lugar en el que se habría casado si... no completó la frase."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was small, and the high walls made it feel more secluded than it perhaps was."
msgstr "Era pequeño, y las altas paredes lo hacían sentir más aislado de lo que quizás fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "It was smart not to make a fire."
msgstr "Era inteligente no hacer fuego."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was smart of you to gather what information we have available to us. It can't ever hurt."
msgstr "Fue inteligente de tu parte reunir la información que tenemos disponible. No puede hacer daño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was smarter to keep going, she knew that."
msgstr "Era más inteligente seguir avanzando, lo sabía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was smarter to keep watch..."
msgstr "Era más inteligente mantener la vigilancia..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was so simple, it barely counted as a spell. But it was enough."
msgstr "Era tan sencillo que apenas podía considerarse un hechizo. Pero era suficiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "It was some other sorry bastard five months ago, and it will be another sorry bastard five months from now."
msgstr "Era otro miserable bastardo hace cinco meses, y será otro miserable bastardo dentro de otros cinco meses."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was some six years, and by now mother to three children, when Sarah watched her husband return one last time."
msgstr "Fueron seis años, y por entonces ya era madre de tres hijos, cuando Sarah vio a su esposo regresar por última vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was something she looked forward to with almost mad desperation."
msgstr "Era algo que ansiaba con una desesperación casi loca."

msgctxt "speaker:Nathan"
msgid "It was something short...I think."
msgstr "Era algo corto... creo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was something that was entirely normal. Something that he deserved."
msgstr "Era algo completamente normal. Algo que merecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still early in the morning when they were ready to depart."
msgstr "Aún era temprano por la mañana cuando estaban listos para partir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still hard for Sarah to adapt to the fact that now, all these rules seemed to fall away."
msgstr "Aún le resultaba difícil a Sarah adaptarse al hecho de que ahora todas esas reglas parecían desvanecerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still hard for her to imagine they had actually survived their ordeal."
msgstr "Le costaba aún imaginar que habían sobrevivido realmente a su calvario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still night. How long had she been out for?"
msgstr "Era aún de noche. ¿Cuánto tiempo había estado inconsciente?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still odd to her that this great seat of power, the center of her nation, was at night often empty."
msgstr "Aún le resultaba extraño que aquel gran trono de poder, el centro de su nación, estuviera a menudo vacío por la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still strange to her to consider that she had an army of her own."
msgstr "Era aún extraño para ella considerar que poseía un ejército propio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still the same girl, and yet everything about her looked different."
msgstr "Era aún la misma chica, y sin embargo todo en ella parecía diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still there, but it had begun to lessen. To transform into something else, or perhaps begin a process of transformation."
msgstr "Aún estaba allí, pero había comenzado a disminuir. A transformarse en otra cosa, o quizás a iniciar un proceso de transformación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange how for a man his size, he could be so delicate."
msgstr "Era extraño cómo, para un hombre de su tamaño, podía ser tan delicado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange how the enormous thing seemed to exist in the background of the city."
msgstr "Era extraño cómo esa enorme cosa parecía existir al fondo de la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to Sarah. Lady Carolyn was the one who was standing entirely naked, and yet, Sarah was the one who felt embarassed."
msgstr "Era extraño para Sarah. La Dama Carolyn era la que estaba completamente desnuda, y sin embargo, Sarah era la que se sentía avergonzada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to her how something that had once been so normal now sounded wrong to her."
msgstr "Era extraño para ella cómo algo que una vez había sido tan normal ahora sonaba mal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to once again just have a conversation with someone."
msgstr "Era extraño volver a tener una conversación con alguien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange walking here, in such relative calm, when she knew that just an ocean away, a horde of demons roamed free."
msgstr "Era extraño caminar por aquí, en una calma tan relativa, cuando sabía que a solo un océano de distancia, una horda de demonios vagaba libre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strangely peaceful."
msgstr "Era extrañamente pacífico."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "It was strategy. Same reason I defeated them."
msgstr "Fue estrategia. La misma razón por la que los derroté."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was stunning."
msgstr "Era impresionante."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was stupid, but my friend he...convinced me."
msgstr "Fue estúpido, pero mi amigo... me convenció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was subtle, easy to miss if she didn't know what to look for."
msgstr "Era sutil, fácil de pasar por alto si no sabía qué buscar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was subtle, the way in which people turned away from him, guarding their wallets with their bodies, or simply moving away entirely."
msgstr "Era sutil, la forma en que la gente se apartaba de él, protegiendo sus billeteras con sus cuerpos o simplemente alejándose por completo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was such, sitting and waiting, that Sarah was finally approached by one of the soldiers that worked as a messenger."
msgstr "Así, sentada y esperando, Sarah fue finalmente abordada por uno de los soldados que trabajaba como mensajero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was suicide."
msgstr "Era suicidio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was tempting to believe how simple a life she could have here."
msgstr "Era tentador creer qué tan simple podía ser su vida aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was that belief that made it possible for her to debase herself in front of the old man."
msgstr "Fue esa creencia lo que le permitió degradarse ante el viejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was that fact which had wounded her most."
msgstr "Fue ese hecho lo que la había herido más."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "It was that fucking lowlife partner of yours. He got you all twisted and on the wrong path."
msgstr "Fue ese cabrón de compañero tuyo el que te torció y te llevó por el camino equivocado."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "It was that lack of strength that caused your downfall, and that has brought you to me."
msgstr "Fue esa falta de fuerza la que provocó tu caída, y eso es lo que te ha traído hasta mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the Khan that answered."
msgstr "Fue el Kan quien respondió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the Tribesmen that had ran out of steam."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the best pain they had ever felt."
msgstr "Fue el mejor dolor que jamás habían sentido."

