msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much damage had been caused by both the invasion of the tribesmen and the uprising of the old houses."
msgstr "Muchos daños habían sido causados tanto por la invasión de los tribus como por el levantamiento de las casas antiguas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much further than that, Sarah could only see rolling hills, without so much as a soul in sight."
msgstr "Mucho más allá de eso, Sarah solo podía ver colinas onduladas, sin ni siquiera un alma a la vista."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much had changed back home. She suddenly thought of herself as foolish for having allowed herself to be so ignorant."
msgstr "Mucho había cambiado en casa. De repente, se sintió tonta por haber permitido tanta ignorancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much later, somewhere near the afternoon, the two finally rose to start their day."
msgstr "Mucho después, cerca de la tarde, los dos finalmente se levantaron para comenzar su día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much less, she can explain how she can see anything at all."
msgstr "Mucho menos, puede explicar cómo ve algo en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like her mind, her body had yielded any last traces of resistance."
msgstr "Al igual que su mente, su cuerpo había cedido cualquier último rastro de resistencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like last time, she had lost herself in the moment, but now reality was catching up to her."
msgstr "Como la última vez, se había perdido en el momento, pero ahora la realidad le iba alcanzando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like marble, her skin was a pale white that might have appeared sickly in any other, but in her only seemed to heighten her beauty."
msgstr "Como el mármol, su piel era de un blanco pálido que en cualquier otra podría parecer enfermizo, pero en ella solo servía para realzar su belleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like the empire itself, the city never really stopped moving."
msgstr "Al igual que el imperio mismo, la ciudad nunca dejó de moverse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like the fights, these fights seemed to equally only boast the celebrations."
msgstr "Al igual que los combates, estos solo parecían presumir de las celebraciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like the man himself, not a hair or a fiber, out of place."
msgstr "Al igual que el propio hombre, ni un solo cabello o fibra fuera de su lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much like the road that lead to Gallow Creek, it wasn't so much made as formed naturally."
msgstr "Al igual que el camino que conducía al Arroyo Gallow, no estaba tanto hecho como formado naturalmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Much of that however changed when they finally reached the borders of Normandi."
msgstr "Sin embargo, gran parte de eso cambió cuando finalmente llegaron a las fronteras de Normandía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Multiple times a day, he would find and drag Sarah to his cabin. Once there, she would disrobe and go down on him."
