msgstr "Sarah había estado despierta, mirando la tienda, tratando de procesar lo que había sucedido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been no stranger to her own body, at times when she had been alone, but Lady Carolyn seemed to know her body even better than she did herself."
msgstr "Sarah no era ajena a su propio cuerpo; en ocasiones, cuando estaba sola, lo conocía bien. Sin embargo, Lady Carolyn parecía conocerlo incluso mejor que ella misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been quiet as Jaeid told her his story."
msgstr "Sarah había permanecido callada mientras Jaeid le contaba su historia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been quiet for the entire time that Sigmund had spoken."
msgstr "Sarah había permanecido en silencio durante todo el tiempo que Sigmund habló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been raised on protocol, she knew enough to be polite, even when she didn't quite understand every nuance."
msgstr "Sarah había sido educada en el protocolo; sabía lo suficiente para ser cortés, incluso cuando no entendía del todo cada matiz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been ready to stand her ground. Be brave. Take whatever he might dish out."
msgstr "Sarah había estado lista para defenderse. Ser valiente. Aceptar lo que él pudiera darle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been right, both men had been about her age, but unlike Sarah, they had been surviving in this world for years now."
msgstr "Sarah tenía razón: los dos hombres tenían la misma edad que ella, pero, a diferencia de Sarah, habían sobrevivido en este mundo durante años."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been soldiering for long enough to know that there were few things more dangerous than that."
msgstr "Sarah había estado sirviendo en el ejército lo suficiente como para saber que pocas cosas eran más peligrosas que eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been sure she would have known how she would have reacted to such a thing. Rage. Scream. Hit back."
msgstr "Sarah había estado segura de que habría sabido cómo reaccionar ante algo así. Furia. Grito. Contraataque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been with Kate for so long, and she had ever so rarely see her cry."
msgstr "Sarah había estado con Kate por tanto tiempo, y apenas si la había visto llorar alguna vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been woken up early by the desert heat."
msgstr "Sarah había sido despertada temprano por el calor del desierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had been working the deck when she first spotted the harbor."
msgstr "Sarah había estado trabajando en la cubierta cuando primero avistó el puerto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had begun to slide her tongue around the orc's shaft, lubricating him with her saliva."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had begun to understand that the exam was half actual exam, and half social event for the mercenaries."
msgstr "Sarah comenzó a comprender que el examen era mitad prueba real y mitad evento social para los mercenarios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had borrowed from Kate an old suit of armor and a sword that probably didn't cut much, but was heavy enough to bash someone with."
msgstr "Sarah había prestado a Kate un viejo traje de armadura y una espada que probablemente no cortaba mucho, pero que era lo suficientemente pesada para golpear a alguien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had brought him the vase as a gift. Her small attempt to inject even a fraction of life into the otherwise desolate room."
msgstr "Sarah le había traído el jarrón como regalo, su pequeña tentativa de inyectar incluso una fracción de vida en la habitación, de otro modo desolada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come across many unnatural things since she had begun her studies under Xan."
msgstr "Sarah había encontrado muchas cosas inusuales desde que comenzó sus estudios bajo Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to expect that Krip was a man of few words."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado a esperar que Krip fuera un hombre de pocas palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to know her as a surprisingly heavy sleeper."
msgstr "Sarah había descubierto que era una durmienta sorprendentemente pesada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to learn it was less of a feeling, rather than the absence of another."
msgstr "Sarah había aprendido que era menos una sensación, que la ausencia de otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to learn that Alaric's desires regarding her body, were inexhaustible."
msgstr "Sarah había aprendido que los deseos de Alaric sobre su cuerpo eran inexhaustibles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to learn that a lot could go wrong near the end of a contract."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado a aprender que mucho podía salir mal cerca del final de un contrato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to learn that being petite was not only a downside in combat."
msgstr "Sarah había aprendido que ser pequeña no era solo una desventaja en combate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to love all of it."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado a amar todo eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to realize she really didn't know all that much about this side of the ocean."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado a darse cuenta de que realmente no sabía tanto sobre este lado del océano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had come to the Duke's room late at night."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado a la habitación del duque muy tarde en la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had completed another round of meetings. The fourth one today."
msgstr "Sarah había completado otra ronda de reuniones. La cuarta del día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had contacted the queen of Normandi, Queen Maeiv."
msgstr "Sarah había contactado a la reina de Normandía, la reina Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had decided on Botany."
msgstr "Sarah había decidido en Botánica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had decided on Daemonology."
msgstr "Sarah optó por la demonología."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had decided on Transmogrification."
msgstr "Sarah había decidido en Transmorfificación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had done as Vaelen had asked of her, secured the western wing."
msgstr "Sarah había hecho lo que Vaelen le pidió, asegurando el ala oeste."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had done her best to keep up, but ship work was no easy task even for those more experienced."
msgstr "Sarah hizo lo mejor que pudo por mantenerse al ritmo, pero el trabajo en la nave no es tarea fácil, incluso para quienes tienen más experiencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had drawn his blood, but she and he both knew it was little more than a surface injury."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado su sangre, pero ambos sabían que no era más que una herida superficial."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had eagerly welcomed it."
msgstr "Sarah lo había recibido con ansias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had even seen sides of Samayra she had never expected."
msgstr "Sarah había visto incluso aspectos de Samayra que nunca había esperado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had exhausted the last of her tricks to get him to change how he took her."
msgstr "Sarah había agotado todos sus trucos para que él cambiara la manera en que la tomaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had expected Sigmund to be strong, his body told as much despite his age, but she was stunned to see his speed."
msgstr "Sarah esperaba que Sigmund fuera fuerte; su cuerpo lo decía a pesar de su edad, pero quedó atónita al ver su velocidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had expected the man to look like a Huntsman, but she had not expected him to look almost like an exaggerated ideal of it."
msgstr "Sarah esperaba que el hombre pareciera un cazador, pero no esperaba que pareciera casi una exageración de ese ideal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had expected the same trick, but this time, Kate came for her head on."
msgstr "Sarah esperaba lo mismo, pero esta vez Kate se lanzó contra ella de frente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had expected to feel a lot of things, but she was surprised to feel a sense of pride at her performance."
msgstr "Sarah esperaba sentir muchas cosas, pero se sorprendió al experimentar un sentido de orgullo por su actuación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had failed to secure Edmond's vote, but she also saw it was impossible."
msgstr "Sarah no logró asegurar el voto de Edmond, pero también vio que era imposible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had feared that the engagement would be like a high point in their new relationship, with everything after feeling dull by comparison, but the opposite had happened."
msgstr "Sarah había temido que el compromiso fuera como un clímax en su nueva relación, con todo lo que venía después sintiéndose aburrido por comparación, pero ocurrió exactamente lo contrario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had felt Kate spank her, hard, and now she could feel her behind start to burn."
msgstr "Sarah sintió que Kate la azotaba con dureza y ahora podía sentir cómo su culo comenzaba a arder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had felt Kate's body many times before, but was still surprised she could feel her in ways she hadn't before."
msgstr "Sarah había sentido el cuerpo de Kate muchas veces antes, pero aún estaba sorprendida de poderla percibir de formas que nunca había experimentado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had finished the last of her tasks around the house and was preparing to make dinner."
msgstr "Sarah había terminado las últimas tareas de la casa y se disponía a preparar la cena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had followed him this far and stood opposite of him, watching him."
msgstr "Sarah lo había seguido hasta aquí y se paró frente a él, observándolo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had foolishly convinced herself that this performance had bought her any favors with the captain."
msgstr "Sarah se había convencido ingenuamente de que ese espectáculo le había ganado algún favor al capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had found her royal education had been a solid foundation for learning this skill."
msgstr "Sarah había descubierto que su educación real había sido una base sólida para aprender esta habilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had found herself with a rare free day. No chores, no tasks, no training."
msgstr "Sarah se había encontrado con un día libre y extraño: sin tareas, sin obligaciones, sin entrenamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had given herself fully to the captain and he seized every part of her."
msgstr "Sarah se entregó por completo al capitán y él se apoderó de cada parte de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had gone from watching to being watched, but in this moment she felt only a strange pride."
msgstr "Sarah pasó de observar a ser observada, pero en este momento solo sentía una extraña satisfacción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had gotten into the habit of simply leaving whatever she was reading on the desk."
msgstr "Sarah había adquirido el hábito de dejar simplemente lo que estaba leyendo sobre el escritorio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had grown up in Castle Reinmeer, only rarely venturing much further than the capital of Rosanna."
msgstr "Sarah creció en el castillo de Reinmeer y apenas salía de la capital de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had grown up in a castle, and even she had never known a wealth like this."
msgstr "Sarah había crecido en un castillo, y ni siquiera ella había conocido una riqueza como esta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had grown up reading books with carefully drawn images, that spoke of this impossible city."
msgstr "Sarah había crecido leyendo libros con imágenes cuidadosamente dibujadas que hablaban de esta ciudad imposible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had hated her little brother back then."
msgstr "Sarah había odiado a su pequeño hermano en aquel entonces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had heard and seen enough."
msgstr "Sarah había oído y visto bastante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had heard herself losing control, but this was the first time she heard herself while gagged."
msgstr "Sarah había escuchado a sí misma perder el control, pero esta fue la primera vez que la oyó mientras tenía la boca tapada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had heard of the place many times before, but had never been there before."
msgstr "Sarah había oído hablar del lugar muchas veces antes, pero nunca había estado allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had heard the rumors that Tribesmen were larger than most, but seeing it was different."
msgstr "Sarah había oído los rumores de que los tribales eran más grandes que la mayoría, pero verlo era diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had heard them talk about it before, but she had never read about it any book."
msgstr "Sarah había oído hablar de ello antes, pero nunca había leído sobre ello en ningún libro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had her fill, both of wine and food."
msgstr "Sarah se sació de vino y comida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had hoped to come here and discuss. Bargain. Anything to gain the votes she needed."
msgstr "Sarah había esperado llegar aquí para discutir, negociar. Cualquier cosa para conseguir los votos que necesitaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had hoped to ignore the subject, thinking that perhaps he wouldn't bring it up again."
msgstr "Sarah había esperado ignorar el tema, pensando que quizás él no volvería a mencionarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had hoped to spare him, would she have to kill him now all the same?"
msgstr "Sarah había esperado ahorrarle la vida, ¿tendría que matarlo ahora de todas formas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had hoped to yell out at the creature."
msgstr "Sarah había esperado gritar al monstruo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined a lot of things for her life, but never that."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado muchas cosas para su vida, pero nunca eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined a million ways that her revenge might play out, only to learn that perhaps her glory had been stolen by some stranger."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado un millón de formas en las que su venganza podría desarrollarse, solo para descubrir que quizás su gloria había sido robada por algún desconocido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined an awkward few minutes. Instead, now she would have to spend all night here."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado unos minutos incómodos. En su lugar, ahora tendría que pasar toda la noche aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined both victory and defeat, but she still found herself surprised by how this moment made her feel."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado tanto la victoria como la derrota, pero aún se encontró sorprendida por cómo este momento la hacía sentir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined her own magic to be powerful, and compared to ordinary people it was."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado que su propia magia era poderosa, y en comparación con las personas comunes, lo era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined quite a few scenarios."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado bastantes escenarios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined spitting it out, but with her mouth so filled up by the creature's member, there was nowhere for his seed to go."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado escupirlo, pero con la boca tan llena del miembro del monstruo, no había lugar para que su esperma fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined that between the two of them, being the far younger woman, she'd receive all his attention and urges, but clearly she had assumed wrong."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado que, entre los dos, siendo la mujer mucho más joven, recibiría toda su atención y sus impulsos, pero claramente se había equivocado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined the cage a prison, but right now, was quite sure if not for the bars, that the goblin would have had its way with her."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado que la jaula era una prisión, pero en ese momento estaba bastante segura de que, si no fuera por las barras, el goblin habría hecho su voluntad con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined the day would play out little different from the other days, until a soldier suddenly came running up."
msgstr "Sarah imaginó que el día transcurriría poco diferente de los otros, hasta que un soldado corrió repentinamente hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had imagined the spirit might want her, seize her this very moment, but she understood that was foolish of her to think."
msgstr "Sarah había imaginado que el espíritu la querría, la apoderaría en este mismo instante, pero entendía que era tonta por pensar eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had kept her word and remained in the tent, but by now, it had been 2 days."
msgstr "Sarah había cumplido su palabra y permanecido en la tienda, pero ya habían pasado dos días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had kept the vision to herself long enough, but what good had it done her?"
msgstr "Sarah había guardado la visión para sí misma lo suficiente, pero ¿qué bien le había hecho?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had killed a beast from another world, but those cheers had seemed trivial compared to the pandemonium that Vaelen had unleashed."
msgstr "Sarah había matado a una bestia de otro mundo, pero aquellos aplausos parecieron triviales comparados con el pándemonio que Vaelen desató."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had known it to be true, but she could also feel there was a great difference between knowing a truth and speaking it."
msgstr "Sarah lo sabía, pero también sentía que había una gran diferencia entre conocer una verdad y pronunciarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had known this truth, but to hear it spoken so plainly, still felt like a stab to her heart."
msgstr "Sarah había conocido esta verdad, pero escucharla dicha tan claramente aún le sentó como un puñal en el corazón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had leaned in close as Dalia told the story."
msgstr "Sarah se había inclinado hacia adelante mientras Dalia contaba la historia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had learned his name from Mary, but it was so foreign to her, she struggled to even pronounce it."
msgstr "Sarah había aprendido su nombre de Mary, pero le resultaba tan ajeno que luchaba por pronunciarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had learned over the years not to rely too much on big, complicated battle plans. Real battles were rarely so organized."
msgstr "Sarah había aprendido con los años no confiar demasiado en grandes y complicados planes de batalla. Las batallas reales rara vez están tan organizadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had liked the taste. Loved it, in fact. But she could already feel a buzz."
msgstr "Sarah había disfrutado el sabor. Lo amaba, de hecho. Pero ya podía sentir una embriaguez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had listened attentively to her friend."
msgstr "Sarah escuchó atentamente a su amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had listened intently, and felt like a fist was closing around her throat."
msgstr "Sarah escuchó atentamente, y sintió cómo un puño se cerraba alrededor de su garganta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had listened to men boasting all her lives. Of the heroics they would accomplish in war. How they would throw down their lives."
msgstr "Sarah había escuchado a los hombres presumir de sus hazañas durante toda su vida. De las proezas que realizarían en la guerra. De cómo arriesgarían sus vidas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had lived on the road for years now. She could sleep as easily in an open field as anywhere else."
msgstr "Sarah había vivido en la carretera durante años ahora. Podía dormir tan fácilmente en un campo abierto como en cualquier otro lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had long accepted giving him her body, but she now gave him more than she had ever imagined."
msgstr "Sarah había aceptado desde hace mucho tiempo darle su cuerpo, pero ahora le daba algo más de lo que jamás hubiera imaginado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had long fought to find her way back to having some fraction of power."
msgstr "Sarah había luchado durante mucho tiempo por recuperar algo de poder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had long given up any attempt to keep track of the maze she now found herself in."
msgstr "Sarah había abandonado hace mucho cualquier intento de mantenerse al tanto del laberinto en el que ahora se encontraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had lost all relation to time, perhaps even the world outside of the wizard's house."
msgstr "Sarah había perdido toda noción del tiempo, quizás incluso la del mundo exterior a la casa del mago."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had lost the speed in her step. There was nowhere for her to walk to, other then back to the tent."
msgstr "Sarah había perdido el brío en su andar. No había lugar al que caminar, salvo volver a la tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made but a few rounds when she suddenly saw a shadow move from the corner of her eyes."
msgstr "Sarah dio apenas unas vueltas cuando de repente vio cómo una sombra se movía en el rincón de su vista."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made her decision, and now she put it into action."
msgstr "Sarah tomó su decisión y ahora la puso en acción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made her decision, and now she set out to put it into action."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado su decisión y ahora se dispuso a ponerla en práctica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made her peace with the captain, with their relationship. It was the price she had to pay to escape her old life, and she had accepted that bargain."
msgstr "Sarah había hecho las paces con el capitán, con su relación. Era el precio que tenía que pagar para escapar de su vida anterior, y había aceptado ese trato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made her plan, she would go to the harbor and ask around. See if there was a ship heading back to Rosanna."
msgstr "Sarah había elaborado su plan: iría al puerto, preguntaría por todos lados y vería si había un barco que regresara a Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made up her mind and the night had set in fast."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado su decisión y la noche cayó con rapidez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had made up her mind."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado su decisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had managed to find her own alcoves and rooms in the house, but this room was where they had spend most of their time together."
msgstr "Sarah había logrado encontrar sus propios alcobas y habitaciones en la casa, pero esta era donde habían pasado la mayor parte de su tiempo juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had managed to secure her victory on the matter."
msgstr "Sarah había logrado asegurar su victoria en el asunto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had many soldiers. But numbers were only one advantage in war."
msgstr "Sarah tenía muchos soldados. Pero los números eran solo una ventaja en la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had met enough nobility to know that titles were a poor replacement for a good heart."
msgstr "Sarah había conocido a suficientes nobles como para saber que los títulos son un pobre sustituto de un buen corazón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had met some rare men like him in her life. Those who took the fortune of their noble birth, and used its priviledges to become great men."
msgstr "Sarah había conocido a algunos hombres tan raros como él en su vida. Aquellos que tomaron el destino de su nacimiento noble y utilizaron sus privilegios para convertirse en grandes hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had mostly remained near the mercenary camp and had not yet explored the rest of the city."
msgstr "Sarah había permanecido casi siempre cerca del campamento de mercenarios y aún no había explorado el resto de la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had nearly forgotten. The Union Council."
msgstr "El Consejo de la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never asked him, but she had found it remarkable how much he knew about a place that most of the world had forgotten."
msgstr "Sarah nunca le había preguntado, pero había encontrado admirable cuánto sabía de un lugar que la mayoría del mundo había olvidado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never been a great cook, but she imagined even her cooking couldn't be bad enough to justify injury, and so she committed herself to the task."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había sido una gran cocinera, pero imaginaba que ni siquiera su cocina podía ser tan mala como para justificar una lesión, por lo que se entregó a la tarea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never been much for sailing, but she couldn't deny there was a beauty to it."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había tenido mucho interés en la navegación, pero no podía negar que existía una belleza en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never been particularly pious in her life, nor given all too much thought to the Pantheon."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había sido particularmente devota en su vida, ni había pensado demasiado en el Panteón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never before known something so primal, nor a man who would appreciate that part of her."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había conocido algo tan primitivo, ni un hombre que apreciara esa parte de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never before wanted to please a man as much as him."
msgstr "Sarah nunca antes había deseado complacer a un hombre tanto como a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never considered it like that."
msgstr "Sarah nunca lo había considerado de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never had many points of reference, but she had almost implicitly understood that the captain was well-endowed."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había tenido muchos puntos de referencia, pero casi implícitamente entendía que el capitán estaba bien dotado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never had to worry about whether or not she could eat for even a single day in her life."
msgstr "Sarah nunca tuvo que preocuparse por si podría comer ni siquiera un solo día en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never heard anything more beautiful."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había oído nada más hermoso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never heard of it."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había oído hablar de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never heard the name before."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había oído ese nombre antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never known a sensation like this, and likely never would again."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había sentido algo así, y probablemente jamás volvería a hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never seen Kate like this, full of purpose, on a mission. She realized this might be the first time she what her friend was like as a soldier."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto a Kate así, llena de propósito, en misión. Se dio cuenta de que esto podría ser la primera vez que veía a su amiga como soldado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never seen a man dressed like this, but she didn't need to in order to know that this man hailed from the eastern desert."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto a un hombre vestido de tal manera, pero no necesitaba hacerlo para saber que aquel hombre provenía del desierto oriental."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never seen an economy of this scale."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto una economía de esta magnitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never seen anything like this."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto nada como esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never seen the Shah Mahda before, but she could deduce from the man's posture that he must be the one."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto al Shah Mahda antes, pero podía deducir por la postura del hombre que él debía ser el indicado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never thought of it like that before."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había pensado en ello de esa manera antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never thought of money in that way, but much of what Lady Carolyn was saying seemed to make sense to her."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había pensado en el dinero de esa manera, pero gran parte de lo que Lady Carolyn decía parecía tener sentido para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never thought the captain handsome, but she had come around on some of his odd features."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había considerado al capitán guapo, pero acabó aceptando algunos de sus rasgos extraños."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had never watched another woman experience all of this, so intimately."
msgstr "Sarah nunca había visto a otra mujer experimentar todo esto de tan íntima manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no answer."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no choice but to yield her body to them, and undergo the transformation."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía más opción que ceder su cuerpo a ellos y someterse a la transformación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no desire to get lost in any secret tunnels, certainly not the day before a battle."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ganas de perderse en ningún túnel secreto, especialmente no el día antes de una batalla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no good answers for them."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía buenas respuestas para ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no idea what she was doing, not given her current composition, but she followed her instincts instead."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ni idea de qué estaba haciendo, dado su estado actual, pero siguió sus instintos en lugar de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no illusions that her body didn't afford her certain considerations. It was a tool for her to use to her advantage."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ilusiones de que su cuerpo no le ofreciera ciertos beneficios. Era una herramienta para usarla a su conveniencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no illusions that this wasn't how this was going to end. Better to lean into it, she concluded."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ilusiones de que esto no fuera así como iba a terminar. Mejor inclinarse hacia ello, concluyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no more trouble from them."
msgstr "Sarah ya no tuvo más problemas con ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no such luck and felt her body shiver."
msgstr "Sarah no tuvo tanta suerte y sintió cómo su cuerpo temblaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had no way to fight them, all she could do was let herself be taken by them."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía forma de luchar contra ellos; todo lo que podía hacer era dejarse llevar por ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had none."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not come to it easy, but she had found her place in the world."
msgstr "Sarah no había llegado a ello con facilidad, pero había encontrado su lugar en el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not given the Empire much thought for most of her life."
msgstr "Sarah no había prestado mucha atención al Imperio durante la mayor parte de su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not seen a familiar soul from Rosanna in...Gods, she could hardly recall."
msgstr "Sarah no había visto un alma familiar de Rosanna en... los dioses, apenas podía recordarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not seen a reason to visit Rahayal before now, and Xan obviously hadn't either. Not since she..."
msgstr "Sarah no había visto razón para visitar Rahayal antes de ahora, y Xan obviamente tampoco lo había hecho. No desde que..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not spoken to Thomas about what had happened with the emissary."
msgstr "Sarah no había hablado con Thomas sobre lo que le había pasado al emisario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had not thought about it, but the moment Lady Carolyn had said it, she knew she was right."
msgstr "Sarah no había pensado en ello, pero apenas Lady Carolyn lo dijo, supo que tenía razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had often felt embarrassed at the wealth on display at her own feasts."
msgstr "Sarah había sentido a menudo vergüenza por la ostentación de riqueza en sus propias fiestas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had often wondered why. For most boys his age, war seemed to be the only thing they cared for. Soldiers, battle, glory."
msgstr "Sarah se había preguntado a menudo por qué. Para la mayoría de los chicos de su edad, la guerra parecía ser lo único que les importaba: soldados, batalla, gloria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had only just gotten started when she heard a voice."
msgstr "Sarah apenas había comenzado cuando escuchó una voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had only just sat down at the bar when Ramsey, the owner, walked up to her."
msgstr "Sarah apenas había tomado asiento en el bar cuando Ramsey, el dueño, se acercó a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had only just stepped into the room when she realized Belmont was waiting for her entirely naked."
msgstr "Sarah apenas acababa de entrar en la habitación cuando se dio cuenta de que Belmont la esperaba completamente desnuda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had only just walked out of the dining room and turned the down the hallway when she saw a familiar shape."
msgstr "Sarah acababa de salir de la sala de comedor y giró hacia el pasillo cuando vio una figura familiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had paid her price. The night was over."
msgstr "Sarah había pagado su precio. La noche había terminado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had passed that wicked place a few times. Afraid to even look at it directly, she could only glance from the corner of her eyes."
msgstr "Sarah había pasado por ese lugar maldito varias veces. Con miedo de mirarlo directamente, solo echaba una ojeada desde el rabillo del ojo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had passed the exam."
msgstr "Sarah aprobó el examen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had practiced by herself in the days after her first lesson."
msgstr "Sarah había practicado sola en los días posteriores a su primera lección."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had quickly finished getting dressed and Lady Carolyn had already been waiting for her."
msgstr "Sarah se había puesto rápidamente y Lady Carolyn ya la esperaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had quickly found him to be no less knowledgeable or reliable in his advice."
msgstr "Sarah había encontrado rápidamente que él no era menos conocedor ni fiable en sus consejos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had read her share, growing up in Castle Reinmeer."
msgstr "Sarah había leído su parte, creciendo en el castillo Reinmeer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had reasoned the orc might require convincing."
msgstr "Sarah había razonado que el orco podría necesitar persuasión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had received dancing lessons herself growing up, but she was not Samayra's equal in this matter."
msgstr "Sarah recibió lecciones de baile ella misma al crecer, pero no era igual a Samayra en este asunto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had received limited instruction on dealing with them. People knew they were dangerous, exceedingly so, but they were also rare."
msgstr "Sarah había recibido una instrucción limitada para lidiar con ellos. La gente sabía que eran peligrosos, extremadamente peligrosos, pero también eran raros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had related to Samayra, a princess like herself, cast out into a cruel world, but perhaps there was also an element of her brother in the girl."
msgstr "Sarah se había identificado con Samayra, una princesa como ella misma, expulsada a un mundo cruel, pero quizás también había un elemento de su hermano en la muchacha."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had relied on Lady Carolyn's spy network in the Capital to stay informed."
msgstr "Sarah había confiado en la red de espías de Lady Carolyn en la Capital para mantenerse informada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had retreated all the way to the far end of the cell."
msgstr "Sarah se había retirado hasta el extremo más lejano de la celda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had returned to her bedchamber."
msgstr "Sarah había regresado a su alcoba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had returned to her bedroom late that night."
msgstr "Sarah había regresado a su habitación muy tarde esa noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had returned to her room, her mind still racing with thoughts concerning the upcoming Union Council."
msgstr "Sarah había regresado a su habitación, con la mente aún acelerada por los pensamientos sobre el próximo Consejo de la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had said a prayer for her brother, praying that somehow he would be kept safe amidst the carnage that would follow."
msgstr "Sarah había dicho una oración por su hermano, rogando que de alguna manera fuera mantenido a salvo entre la carnicería que seguiría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had said a prayer, both for her husband and her brother, praying that somehow both would be kept safe amidst the carnage that would follow."
msgstr "Sarah había dicho una oración, tanto para su esposo como para su hermano, suplicando que de algún modo ambos fueran mantenidos a salvo entre la carnicería que seguiría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had scarcely thought of it when she saw in his eyes that same recognition."
msgstr "Sarah apenas había pensado en ello cuando vio en sus ojos el mismo reconocimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had scheduled her meeting with Queen Maeiv."
msgstr "Sarah había programado su reunión con la reina Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen it before in her life, the way some men would look at her, a hunger."
msgstr "Sarah había visto eso antes en su vida, la forma en que algunos hombres miraban a ella, un hambre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen it before, and it frightened her almost more than the blood did."
msgstr "Sarah había visto eso antes, y le aterrorizaba casi más que la sangre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen much in her life, especially since she had met Xan, but this place was utterly unique."
msgstr "Sarah había visto mucho en su vida, especialmente desde que conoció a Xan, pero este lugar era totalmente único."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen no spell hit it, but only then did she see."
msgstr "Sarah no había visto ningún hechizo impactarlo, pero solo entonces fue cuando lo vio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen plenty of squables in their group, mostly during the nights, but whenever out on the road, each seemed to yield to Sigmund."
msgstr "Sarah había visto bastantes squables en su grupo, principalmente durante las noches, pero cada vez que salían por el camino, todos parecían ceder ante Sigmund."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen the burned faces of a few soldiers who had just made such a mistake."
msgstr "Sarah había visto las caras quemadas de algunos soldados que acababan de cometer tal error."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen the great walls that encircled Bagrad, rising up so near to the sky that they cast a shadow across the city."
msgstr "Sarah había visto las grandes murallas que rodeaban Bagrad, alzándose tan cerca del cielo que proyectaban una sombra sobre la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen the object many times in her life, but given her circumstances, struggled to understand how it existed here."
msgstr "Sarah había visto el objeto muchas veces en su vida, pero dada su situación, luchaba por comprender cómo podía existir aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had seen the state of the castle. More ruin than anything."
msgstr "Sarah había visto el estado del castillo. Más ruina que otra cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had served her purpose and now he was done with her. Until he wouldn't be."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had set out back to the town, tracing her steps as best she could manage."
msgstr "Sarah se había puesto en camino de vuelta al pueblo, siguiendo sus pasos lo mejor que podía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had slowly come to realize, that she was able to match both of them in combat. The realization had brought her more than a little glee."
msgstr "Sarah había llegado poco a poco a la conclusión de que podía igualarles a ambos en combate. Esa revelación le había traído más que un poco de alegría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had sometimes wished that the sex had been worse. It would have made it easier to hate him. It would have made her feel less shame at being with him."
msgstr "Sarah había deseado a veces que el sexo hubiera sido peor. Le habría hecho más fácil odiarlo. Le habría hecho sentir menos vergüenza por estar con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spend many of her days studying the documents that Metis had given her."
msgstr "Sarah había pasado muchos de sus días estudiando los documentos que Metis le había dado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spend most of her day in deep thought."
msgstr "Sarah pasó la mayor parte del día en profunda reflexión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spend most of the day worrying and the night had set in fast."
msgstr "Sarah pasó la mayor parte del día preocupada y la noche cayó de golpe."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spend the rest of the day preparing."
msgstr "Sarah había pasado el resto del día preparándose."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spent her entire life in the proximity of her brother. The idea of not knowing if he was safe was alien and unsettling."
msgstr "Sarah había pasado toda su vida en la proximidad de su hermano. La idea de no saber si estaba a salvo era ajena e inquietante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spoken her name, but hardly knew what else to say."
msgstr "Sarah había pronunciado su nombre, pero apenas sabía qué más decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spoken to Vaelen on more than one occasion about it, but he had been reluctant about telling her much of anything."
msgstr "Sarah había hablado con Vaelen más de una vez al respecto, pero él había sido reacio a decirle mucho de nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spoken to her council on many occassions, trying to make sense of their strategy."
msgstr "Sarah había hablado con su consejo en muchas ocasiones, tratando de dar sentido a su estrategia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had spoken to the captain about showing restraint, but on this front, Belmont would tolerate no mercy."
msgstr "Sarah había hablado con el capitán sobre mostrar contención, pero en este asunto, Belmont no toleraba ninguna misericordia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had struck her with an open hand."
msgstr "Sarah la había golpeado con la palma de la mano abierta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had studied enough geography growing up in Rosanna that she knew Lethram and Rahayal were on the same side of the continent, so a land route had seemed obvious to her."
msgstr "Sarah había estudiado suficiente geografía creciendo en Rosanna para saber que Lethram y Rahayal estaban al mismo lado del continente, por lo que una ruta terrestre le pareció obvia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had studied the maps of the city, but down at the street level, it was harder to make sense of where they were."
msgstr "Sarah había estudiado los mapas de la ciudad, pero a nivel de calle, resultaba más difícil entender dónde se encontraban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had studied the maps of the world well enough. This was the furthest campaign she'd ever undertaken this far east."
msgstr "Sarah había estudiado los mapas del mundo lo suficiente. Esta era la campaña más lejana que jamás había emprendido tan al este."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had surrendered any attempt to force Kate to go faster, instead, she now seemed to beg with every inch of her body, hoping Kate would be merciful."
msgstr "Sarah había abandonado cualquier intento de obligar a Kate a ir más rápido; por el contrario, ahora parecía suplicar con cada centímetro de su cuerpo, esperando que Kate fuera misericordiosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had suspected there was more to his plan than simple avarice."
msgstr "Sarah había sospechado que su plan tenía más detrás de la simple codicia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken Atilla into her mouth many times by now, and she had learned ways that she could fit him deeper."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado a Atilla en su boca muchas veces hasta ahora, y había aprendido formas de poder meterlo más profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken a few more swigs of Varga's beer, and to her surprise, felt her face glowing."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado unos tragos más de la cerveza de Varga y, para su sorpresa, sintió que su rostro se ruborizaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken her place at the head of the long table that sat at the center of the council room."
msgstr "Sarah tomó su lugar al frente de la larga mesa que ocupaba el centro de la sala del consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken her place on the official dais, seated near Thomas, though on a slightly lower level."
msgstr "Sarah tomó su lugar en el estrado oficial, sentada cerca de Thomas, aunque en un nivel ligeramente inferior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken some time to get used to it, but in Bagrad, the fashion was decidedly more free than in Rosanna."
msgstr "Sarah había tomado algo de tiempo para acostumbrarse a ello, pero en Bagrad la moda era decididamente más libre que en Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken the same place as always on the front box, and watched as Sigmund got up next to her."
msgstr "Sarah ocupó el mismo lugar que siempre en la caja frontal y observó cómo Sigmund se levantaba junto a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had taken to wearing her old dress again."
msgstr "Sarah volvió a ponerse su vestido antiguo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had the fortune of working the head of the old soldier's cock and felt her mouth fill up with his semen."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo la fortuna de joder a la polla del viejo soldado y sintió cómo su boca se llenaba con su semilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had thought it in illusion, a brief deception, but instead it remained there."
msgstr "Sarah había pensado que era una ilusión, un engaño efímero, pero en realidad seguía ahí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had thought she would feel some kind of release, knowing she was free, but the act itself and its brutality had stripped her of that."
msgstr "Sarah había pensado que sentiría algún tipo de alivio, sabiendo que estaba libre, pero el acto en sí y su brutalidad le habían arrebatado eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had thrown off the awkward outfit that had been forced on her."
msgstr "Sarah se había quitado la ropa incómoda que le habían obligado a usar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to admit she hadn't actually thought about that."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que admitir que no había pensado en eso realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to admit to herself, even she had begun to salivate at the smell of the food she had prepared."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que admitirlo para consigo misma: incluso ella había comenzado a babear ante el olor de la comida que había preparado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to laugh to herself. Cassius was a soldier, whatever this business of subterfuge was, he had not been made for it."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que reírse consigo misma. Cassius era un soldado, y aunque este asunto de la trampa no le correspondía, no estaba hecho para ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to laugh."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que reír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to remind herself to be strong, but her heart wished she could cry out."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que recordarse a sí misma para ser fuerte, pero su corazón deseaba poder gritar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had to turn around to look, just to make sure she was there. Samayra walked so lightly, her footsteps seemed to make no sounds."
msgstr "Sarah tuvo que girarse para mirar, solo para asegurarse de que ella estaba allí. Samayra caminaba tan ligera que sus pasos parecían no hacer ningún sonido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had told everyone she was tired and wanted to retreat to her room for the night and not be disturbed."
msgstr "Sarah había dicho a todos que estaba cansada y quería retirarse a su habitación para la noche sin ser molestada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had told her many times over she didn't need to be so formal, but in these last few days she couldn't help herself."
msgstr "Sarah le había dicho muchas veces que no necesitaba ser tan formal, pero en estos últimos días no podía evitarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had told her many times over she didn't need to be so formal, but whenever she was officially on duty, she couldn't help herself."
msgstr "Sarah le había dicho muchas veces que no necesitaba ser tan formal, pero cada vez que estaba oficialmente de servicio, no podía evitarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had touched Samayra's body before."
msgstr "Sarah había tocado el cuerpo de Samayra antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had tried all her life to forget that fact. Now she could no longer deny it."
msgstr "Sarah había intentado toda su vida olvidar ese hecho. Ahora ya no podía negarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had tried to make an exception for the girl, but there was simply no space left anywhere."
msgstr "Sarah había intentado hacer una excepción por la chica, pero simplemente no quedaba espacio en ningún lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had urged her to block trade downstream from the river, preventing Marion's forces from being able to supply themselves."
msgstr "Sarah la instó a bloquear el comercio aguas abajo del río, impidiendo que las fuerzas de Marion pudieran abastecerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had walked away from her own country when they needed her most. She had vowed never to do so again."
msgstr "Sarah se había alejado de su propio país cuando lo necesitaban más. Se había jurado nunca volver a hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had wanted to help out with the work for the coronation, but she hadn't found any time. Officially, she was sick for the week."
msgstr "Sarah había querido ayudar con los preparativos para la coronación, pero no había encontrado tiempo. Oficialmente, estaba enferma durante la semana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had watched Samayra leave, walking back to the royal quarters to meet with her father the Shah."
msgstr "Sarah había observado cómo Samayra se alejaba, caminando de vuelta hacia las estancias reales para reunirse con su padre, el Shah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had witnessed ship after ship arrive on the shores."
msgstr "Sarah había presenciado la llegada de barco tras barco a las orillas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had woken early the next day and had begun preparing."
msgstr "Sarah se había despertado temprano al día siguiente y había comenzado a prepararse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had woken early the next day."
msgstr "Sarah se había despertado temprano al día siguiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had woken up early the next morning to the sound of knocking at her door, a small headache reminding her of the celebration from the night before."
msgstr "Sarah se despertó temprano la mañana siguiente ante el sonido de golpes en su puerta, un ligero dolor de cabeza que le recordaba la celebración de la noche anterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had worked dilligently all week to prepare for this day."
msgstr "Sarah había trabajado diligentemente toda la semana para preparar este día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah had, in secret, read some books about carnal acts, but no book could describe what she now felt."
msgstr "Sarah había leído en secreto algunos libros sobre actos carnales, pero ningún libro podía describir lo que ella sentía ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't been blind to that fact, but as a commander she always stood apart from the common soldier, more so than Kate who was an officer."
msgstr "Sarah no había sido ciega a ese hecho, pero como comandante siempre se mantenía aparte del soldado común, aún más que Kate, quien era oficial."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't even considered the option."
msgstr "Sarah ni siquiera había considerado esa opción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't even so much as considered it."
msgstr "Sarah ni siquiera lo había considerado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't even thought about such a thing."
msgstr "Sarah ni siquiera había pensado en algo así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't expected much else. The road to Ridgehaven had always been pretty safe. Uneventful."
msgstr "Sarah no esperaba nada más. El camino hacia Ridgehaven siempre había sido bastante seguro, sin incidentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't expected to get paid at all."
msgstr "Sarah no esperaba recibir ningún pago."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't given the pay much thought."
msgstr "Sarah no había prestado mucha atención al pago."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah hadn't heard either of them introduce themselves yet, so neither appeared much a master of protocol."
