msgid "Sarah kept her eyes on Metis as he continued his explanation."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la mirada fija en Metis mientras él seguía con su explicación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes on Vaelen."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la mirada en Vaelen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes on him. His body language didn't seem to give much away."
msgstr "Sarah lo miraba fijamente. Su lenguaje corporal no parecía revelar mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes on the man as she walked further into the room."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la mirada en el hombre mientras avanzaba más hacia la habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes out as she kept to the main road."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la mirada hacia afuera mientras seguía el camino principal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes to the floor."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la vista en el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her eyes to the ground."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la mirada en el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her face pressed to the ground."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo su rostro presionado contra el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her face still, revealing no emotion."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la cara inmóvil, sin revelar ninguna emoción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her friend in an embrace."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo a su amiga en un abrazo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her hands planted on the wall, and tried to bend deeper, bending her body to Kate's intentions."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo las manos apoyadas en la pared y trató de doblarse más profundo, curvando su cuerpo según los deseos de Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her mouth fixed on Samayra's sex, eagerly devouring her as she heard the girl moan hysterically above her."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la boca pegada al coño de Samayra, devorándola con avidez mientras escuchaba que la chica gemía histéricamente por encima de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her mouth wide open in hungry anticipation, her tongue extended so she wouldn't miss a drop."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo la boca abierta de par en par con hambre voraz, extendiendo la lengua para no perder ni una gota."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her mouth. That wasn't what she wanted."
msgstr "Sarah se quedó callada. Eso no era lo que quería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her own composure, though she nodded."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo su compostura, aunque asintió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept her stride, marching directly into the castle itself."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo su paso, marchando directamente hacia el castillo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept his eyes. She wasn't sure what she saw in them. Did he know anything. Was he genuinely wondering?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept his gaze."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept laying on the floor, nude, her whole body ringing."
msgstr "Sarah seguía yaciendo en el suelo, desnuda, su cuerpo entero vibrando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept looking as captain Belmont began to unrig the sails and fix the ropes."
msgstr "Sarah observaba mientras el capitán Belmont comenzaba a desarticular las velas y arreglar las cuerdas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept looking at Kate, reinforcing her request."
msgstr "Sarah seguía mirando a Kate, reforzando su petición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept looking at the deviant seedling."
msgstr "Sarah seguía mirando al brote desviado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept looking out towards the horizon, hoping something might offer her an escape. But there was none."
msgstr "Sarah seguía mirando hacia el horizonte, esperando que algo pudiera ofrecerle una salida. Pero no había ninguna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept meeting his gaze."
msgstr "Sarah mantenía la mirada fija en la suya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept moaning, the roaring sensations too much to repress."
msgstr "Sarah seguía gemiendo, las sensaciones rugientes demasiado intensas para reprimir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept pressing forward, only a handful of other soldiers continued along with her."
msgstr "Sarah siguió avanzando, solo un puñado de otros soldados continuaban con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept quiet."
msgstr "Sarah se mantuvo en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept quiet. She had no power in this moment, no matter her station."
msgstr "Sarah se mantuvo en silencio. No tenía poder en este momento, sin importar su rango."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept quiet. She knew that was true."
msgstr "Sarah calló. Sabía que eso era cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept repeating it, and over time, the creature seemed to even begin to believe her."
msgstr "Sarah seguía repitiéndolo, y con el paso del tiempo la criatura pareció incluso empezar a creerla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept riding her Master, as eager to deliver him his pleasure as to receive her own."
msgstr "Sarah seguía montando a su Maestro, con la misma ansia por darle placer que para recibir el suyo propio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept rubbing her thigs together, the feeling growing worse and worse by the minute."
msgstr "Sarah seguía frotando sus muslos, la sensación empeorando minuto a minuto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept running until she reached the mercenary camp. She fell into her bunk…she would keep what had happened today to herself."
msgstr "Sarah siguió corriendo hasta llegar al campamento de mercenarios. Se dejó caer en su litera... guardaría para sí lo que había ocurrido ese día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept running."
msgstr "Sarah siguió corriendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept staring out the window."
msgstr "Sarah seguía mirando por la ventana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept stripping as Alaric looked on from the doorway."
msgstr "Sarah siguió desnudándose mientras Alaric observaba desde el umbral."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept studying Sophia's face, looking if there were hints about what she really thought."
msgstr "Sarah seguía estudiando el rostro de Sophia, buscando si había alguna pista sobre lo que realmente pensaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept studying the book."
msgstr "Sarah seguía estudiando el libro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept to her pace, letting Samayra's sounds fill the room, echoing off the walls."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo su ritmo, dejando que los sonidos de Samayra llenaran la habitación y rebotaran contra las paredes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept to the main road."
msgstr "Sarah se mantuvo en el camino principal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept to the slow and steady pace, feeling herself entering Samayra deeper and deeper."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo el ritmo lento y constante, sintiéndose entrar en Samayra cada vez más profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept turning the questions over in her mind, hoping that she might find the answer."
msgstr "Sarah seguía dando vueltas a las preguntas en su mente, esperando encontrar la respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept up her smile, desite how curt he was with her."
msgstr "Sarah mantuvo su sonrisa, a pesar de lo cortante que era con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept up with Dalia through twisting halls, the castle was like a maze."
msgstr "Sarah siguió el camino de Dalia por los pasillos retorcidos; el castillo era como un laberinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking after the creature."
msgstr "Sarah siguió caminando tras la criatura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking besides him, listening."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba a su lado, escuchando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking down the narrow wooden hallway."
msgstr "Sarah siguió caminando por el estrecho pasillo de madera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking, stepping into the bedroom, or whatever passed for it."
msgstr "Sarah siguió caminando, entrando en la habitación, o lo que pasaba por tal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking, with each step she undied one of the leather bands that kept her armor together."
msgstr "Sarah siguió caminando, y con cada paso desabrochaba una de las bandas de cuero que mantenían su armadura unida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept walking."
msgstr "Sarah siguió caminando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept watch on Nick as she slowly faded into sleep."
msgstr "Sarah vigiló a Nick mientras se iba desvaneciendo lentamente en el sueño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kept watching, now too afraid to look away. Despite the shame, or perhaps because of it, her sex only heated more, now so nearly burning."
msgstr "Sarah siguió mirando, ahora con tanto miedo que no se atrevía a apartar la vista. A pesar de la vergüenza, o quizás por ella, su coño ardía ya casi en lo insoportable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kicked Thomas under the table."
msgstr "Sarah pateó a Thomas debajo de la mesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah killed the time by studying every inch of the room. Going over it twice, and parts of it thrice, she was finally saved from her boredom when something began to stir on the other end of the room."
msgstr "Sarah pasó el rato revisando cada centímetro de la habitación. Lo repasaba dos veces y algunas partes tres, hasta que finalmente escapó del aburrimiento cuando algo comenzó a moverse al otro extremo de la sala."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed Samayra's body as she continued to finger her."
msgstr "Sarah besó el cuerpo de Samayra mientras seguía follando con ella, observándolo todo con curiosidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed her again, softly."
msgstr "Sarah la besó de nuevo, suavemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed her back."
msgstr "Sarah le devolvió el beso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed him, pressing her tongue deep inside of his mouth, him meeting hers with his own."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed the old soldier on his cheek, and was taken away, back to the cart."
msgstr "Sarah besó al viejo soldado en la mejilla y fue llevada de vuelta al carro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kissed this man. The only man with whom she had ever felt quite this safe."
msgstr "Sarah besó a ese hombre. El único con quien había sentido alguna vez tanta seguridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kisses her."
msgstr "Sarah la besa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kneeled down and smiled."
msgstr "Sarah se arrodilló y sonrió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah kneels by the edge of the bed and reaches out to hold her father's hand."
msgstr "Sarah se arrodilla al borde de la cama y extiende la mano para agarrar la de su padre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knelt down beside him, putting one arm around him."
msgstr "Sarah se arrodilló a su lado, poniendo un brazo alrededor de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew Gideon was not for lack of female attention. If he didn't have her, he could have a pick of the others. Still, he did pick her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Gideon no carecía de atención femenina. Si ella no estaba disponible, podría haber elegido a cualquiera de las demás. Sin embargo, él sí la eligió a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew Kate still struggled with what she had done all those years ago."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Kate aún luchaba con lo que había hecho hace tantos años."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew Kate's love for Vaelen as the man who had given her purpose. His death...Sarah worried for her friend."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el amor de Kate por Vaelen era el motivo que le había dado a su existencia. Su muerte... Sarah temía por su amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew all too well the risks that the nobility posed when slighted."
msgstr "Sarah conocía demasiado bien los riesgos que suponen la nobleza cuando se siente ofendida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew almost instantly that it could not be her."
msgstr "Sarah supo casi al instante de que no podía ser ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew better than the disobey, and instead, waited on hands and feet, watching her master."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew better than to take drinks from strangers, but tonight she was in a mood for making mistakes."
msgstr "Sarah sabía mejor que tomar bebidas de extraños, pero esa noche tenía ganas de cometer errores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew deep down that stome stolen food meant nothing, it likely wouldn't even interfere with dinner that evening."
msgstr "Sarah sabía en el fondo que un bocado robado no significaba nada, probablemente ni siquiera estropearía la cena de esa noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew enough about Rahayal that there were no noble houses. At least, not in the way they existed in Rosanna or the other union countries."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo suficiente sobre Rahayal para saber que no había casas nobles. Al menos, no de la manera en que existían en Rosanna o en los demás países de la unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew enough about them to know that they offered only brutality to those they conquered."
msgstr "Sarah conocía lo suficiente sobre ellos para saber que solo ofrecían brutalidad a quienes conquistaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew exactly for what, but she could not deny enjoying the torture of this man."
msgstr "Sarah sabía exactamente por qué, pero no podía negar que disfrutaba torturando a ese hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he had been denied an outlet for these desires for so long, and now she was eager to help relieve him."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que había sido privado de una salida para esos deseos durante tanto tiempo, y ahora tenía prisa por ayudarle a aliviarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he had no more power in this place than her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que en ese lugar no tenía más poder que ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he struggled, and bore his advances no matter how frequent they became."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que luchaba y soportaba sus avances, sin importar cuán frecuentes se hicieran."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he was right, even though she hated to admit it. She longed to just wrap him in her arms and trap him here all night."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía razón, aunque le costaba admitirlo. Anhelaba simplemente envolverlo en sus brazos y atraparlo allí toda la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he was right."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew he wasn't serious, just as she knew she'd actually give it all up for him."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que él no era serio, al igual que sabía que le entregaría el coño por completo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her armor could be a pain to put on and off, but she also knew Kate was being more than friendly."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que su armadura podía ser molesta de poner y quitar, pero también sabía que Kate iba más allá de la amistad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her father frequently visited the neighbouring countries. It had been part of the reason why peace had lasted as long as it did."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que su padre visitaba con frecuencia los países vecinos. Eso había sido parte de la razón por la que la paz duró tanto tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her only chance of ever getting out of these tunnels was to keep up with Vaelen."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que su única oportunidad de salir de estos túneles era mantener el ritmo con Vaelen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her only option was to play along. To finish what she'd agreed to."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que su única opción era seguir el juego. Terminar lo que había acordado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her own position. Firmly against."
msgstr "Sarah conocía su propia posición. Firmemente en contra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew her own position. Firmly in favor."
msgstr "Sarah conocía su propia posición. Firmemente a favor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew him and wasn't surprised to see him, Marion Achillea, from the Achillea family."
msgstr "Sarah lo conocía y no le sorprendió verlo, a Marion Achillea, de la familia Achillea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew how it felt."
msgstr "Sarah sabía cómo se sentía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew how soldiers and guards sounded, their harsh voices."
msgstr "Sarah sabía cómo sonaban los soldados y las guardias, sus voces duras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew how strict the uniform was."
msgstr "Sarah sabía cuán estricto era el uniforme."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew in her heart that could be loyal to only the common folk."
msgstr "Sarah sabía en lo más profundo de su corazón que solo podía ser leal al pueblo común."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it as surely as she had ever known anything in her life. In her mind's eye, she could see it play out again and again."
msgstr "Sarah lo sabía con la misma certeza con la que había conocido algo en su vida. En su imaginación, podía verlo repetirse una y otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it could not be her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no podía ser ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it had been no idle fear. She had felt the same."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no había sido un miedo infundado. Ella lo había sentido igual."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was Vaelen, but she could no longer recognize his face."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que era Vaelen, pero ya no podía reconocer su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was a risky proposition."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que era una arriesgada propuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was true."
msgstr "Sarah lo sabía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was true. She made him that very pledge."
msgstr "Sarah lo sabía. Le hizo esa promesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was wrong, or at least, she knew it only because she had been told as much all her life."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba mal, o al menos, lo sabía solo porque se le había dicho eso toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it was wrong."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba mal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it wasn't a real offer...but even if it had been, she knew there was nothing in the world that would have made her say yes."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no era una oferta real... pero incluso si lo hubiera sido, sabía que nada en el mundo la habría hecho decir que sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it would happen, and still found herself anxious."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que ocurriría y, aun así, se sentía ansiosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew it wouldn't do her much good to be alone tonight."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no le serviría de mucho estar sola esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew little of cooking, and less still of the cuisine of the tribesmen, but she learned as best she could."
msgstr "Sarah sabía poco de cocina y aún menos de la gastronomía de los tribus, pero aprendió lo mejor que pudo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew little of magic, or the relic, but even she could conclude that it confirmed Xan's suspicion."
msgstr "Sarah sabía poco de magia o del relicario, pero incluso ella podía concluir que confirmaba la sospecha de Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew pressing further was pointless."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que insistir era inútil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could never leave Samayra to die."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que nunca podría dejar morir a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could not just be allowed to leave."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no podía simplemente ser dejada ir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could not punish her friend."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no podía castigar a su amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could not resist this man. Doing so would only invite violence."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no podía resistirse a este hombre. Hacerlo solo invitaría la violencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could wrap both her hands around his shaft with space to spare, if only because she'd done it before."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que podía envolver ambas manos alrededor de su polla con espacio para sobrar, solo porque lo había hecho antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she could, because the only things expected of her were either to clean the house, work the kitchen, or service her master in the other room."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que podía hacerlo, pues lo único que se esperaba de ella era limpiar la casa, trabajar en la cocina o servir a su amo en la otra habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she didn't need to expect much sympathy from him."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no podía esperar mucha simpatía de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had few other options other than to do what the spirit wanted."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía pocas otras opciones más que hacer lo que el espíritu deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had fought hard and long to get to where she was. Sacrificed everything, given up her dignity."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que había luchado con mucho esfuerzo y durante mucho tiempo para llegar a donde estaba. Había sacrificado todo, incluso su dignidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had leveraged as much of her advantage over him as she could."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que había aprovechado todo el margen de ventaja que le quedaba sobre él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had none, nor would she offer any if she had. She wanted him to take her right now if they could get away with it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no tenía nada, ni siquiera lo ofrecería si tuviera algo. Quería que él la tomara ahora mismo, si podían hacerlo sin ser vistos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had to act."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía que actuar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had to force herself to be strong if she wanted to survive this."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía que obligarse a ser fuerte si quería sobrevivir a esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she had to listen to the captain. She had chosen right by siding with him. Of course she had, the captain always won."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenía que escuchar al capitán. Había acertado al apoyarse en él. Por supuesto que lo había hecho, el capitán siempre ganaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she hadn't been raised like this. To be forward."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no había sido criada así. Para ser directa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she might actually do it too."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que quizás también lo hiciera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she shouldn't, but part of her couldn't help but be intrigued."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no debía hacerlo, pero una parte de ella no podía evitar sentirse intrigada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she still had a maddened expression on her face, but she also didn't mind."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que aún tenía una expresión desquiciada en el rostro, pero tampoco le importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she wanted to live a long life."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que deseaba vivir una vida larga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was in danger."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba en peligro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was never going to say something like that to the man."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que nunca le diría algo así al hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was ready, but she felt a pit in her stomach. Would she really pass? What if she made a fool out of herself in front of everyone?"
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba lista, pero sentía un vacío en el estómago. ¿Realmente aprobaría? ¿Qué pasaría si se hacía la ridícula ante todos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was ready, but still she felt a pit in her stomach. Would she really pass? What if she made a fool out of herself in front of everyone?"
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba lista, pero aún sentía un vacío en el estómago. ¿Realmente pasaría? ¿Qué pasaría si se hacía una tonta ante todos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was risking something...if anyone ever knew she had done this with an orc...nobody would ever want her again."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que arriesgaba algo... si alguien alguna vez supiera que había hecho esto con un orco, nadie la querría de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she was shrieking like a woman gone mad, but she also had lost any ability to restrain herself."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que gritaba como una mujer loca, pero también había perdido cualquier capacidad de contenerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she wasn't the weak girl from the alley anymore, but she also knew her power, great as it was, could not protect her from everything."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que ya no era la chica débil del callejón, pero también sabía que su poder, por grande que fuera, no podía protegerla de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she would for him."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que lo haría por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she would get no sleep."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no dormiría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she wouldn't."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no lo haría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew she'd be happy when this was behind her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaría feliz cuando esto quedara atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew some of the other reasons why they had been called out here, but she didn't want to trouble Kate with such things."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que había otras razones por las que habían sido llamados aquí, pero no quería molestar a Kate con tales cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Caleb was close."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Caleb estaba cerca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Carolyn couldn't force her. She could fight back if she wanted to. But she didn't. Some part of her yielded to Carolyn's authority."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Carolyn no podía obligarla. Podía resistirse si lo deseaba, pero no lo hizo. Una parte de ella cedió ante la autoridad de Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Kate understood what she was asking."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Kate entendía lo que pedía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Nick had to be punished for his mutiny, but she hoped that this would be the end of it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Nick tenía que ser castigado por su motín, pero esperaba que esto fuera el fin de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Sakar was dishonest in his intentions."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Sakar tenía intenciones deshonestas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that Thomas was never one to care much for land reform petitions, even on the best of days."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que Thomas nunca había dado mucha importancia a las peticiones de reforma agraria, incluso en los mejores días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that a spike was a poor attack, because it took a long time to produce the spell, allowing the other mage to anticipate it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que un clavo era un ataque mediocre, porque requería mucho tiempo para conjurar el hechizo, lo que permitía al otro mago anticiparlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that as one of only very few female commanders, she didn't need an introduction."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, como una de las pocas comandantes femeninas, no necesitaba presentación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that as true, but she also knew they were not her soldiers at all."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que era cierto, pero también sabía que no eran sus soldados en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that beyond the palace, gangs of soldiers, some Mythran, some from her own mercenary company, would be stalking the streets."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que más allá del palacio, bandas de soldados, algunos mythran y otros de su propia compañía mercenaria, estarían acechando las calles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that escaping was dangerous, but if she even wanted to have the option, she would need to learn more about the city."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que escapar era peligroso, pero si siquiera quería tener la opción, necesitaría aprender más sobre la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that even if she threw the strongest possible punch she could, the man would likely not even feel it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, incluso si lanzara el golpe más fuerte que pudiera, el hombre probablemente no sentiría nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that for as much as she hemmed and hawed about Nick's fate, her own role was not as clean as she pretended to herself."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, por mucho que hubiera dudado sobre el destino de Nick, su propio papel no era tan limpio como fingía ante sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that he meant it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que lo decía en serio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that he suspected that she was of high birth, but she imagined he loved that too."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que él sospechaba de su alta cuna, pero ella imaginaba que eso también le gustaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that her position was still uncertain."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que su posición seguía siendo incierta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that no matter where Thomas was on the battlefield, he would not survive."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, sin importar dónde estuviera Thomas en el campo de batalla, no sobreviviría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she didn't have the power to compel an answer from Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no tenía el poder de obligar a Lady Carolyn a dar una respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she didn't, but everything still seemed to be moving very quickly."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no lo tenía, pero todo seguía avanzando muy deprisa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she had."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que lo tenía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she owed all of this to Atilla. He had taken her from the rich spoiled girl she was, and had given her a soldier's body."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que debía todo esto a Atilla. Él la había sacado de la niña rica y caprichosa que era, y le había dado un cuerpo de soldado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she was inside, but the inside of the Imperial Palace was so vast, it almost felt as if she wasn't."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que estaba dentro, pero el interior del Palacio Imperial era tan vasto que casi parecía que no lo estuviera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that she would if he'd ask her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que lo haría si él se lo pidiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that soon he would be fucking her as he most wanted to. Violently, hard, entirely for his own pleasure."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que pronto él la follaría como más deseaba, con violencia y dureza, únicamente para su propio placer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the best option would be to side with the nobility."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que la mejor opción sería aliarse con la nobleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the captain enjoyed it whenever she joined him in humiliating Nick."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el capitán disfrutaba cada vez que ella se unía a él para humillar a Nick."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the house connected to many spaces across the world, so the spirit's words seemed obvious in hindsight."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que la casa estaba conectada a muchos espacios en todo el mundo, por lo que las palabras del espíritu parecieron obvias con la ventaja de la retrospectiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the soldiers were all on their best behavior when she was around, and even so, she felt uneasy at how crude they were."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que los soldados se portaban de lo mejor cuando ella estaba cerca, y aun así, sentía inquietud por lo crudos que eran."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the spirit understood her, but he compelled her to speak plainly."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el espíritu la comprendía, pero él la instaba a hablar con franqueza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the spirit would offer her no respite."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el espíritu no le ofrecería ningún alivio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that the thought had passed her mind. She had even asked some people, but nobody seemed to know much of Atilla's old life."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que la idea le había cruzado por la mente. Incluso había preguntado a algunas personas, pero nadie parecía saber mucho sobre la vida anterior de Atilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that they needed to keep seperate armies."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que debían mantener ejércitos separados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that unifying the armies was the only way forward."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que unificar los ejércitos era el único camino hacia adelante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that was a bad idea."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que era una mala idea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that was likely the least of his intentions."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que eso probablemente era lo menos de sus intenciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that whatever the answer might be, she would best be served to contemplate it on her own."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, cualquiera fuera la respuesta, lo mejor sería que se lo contemplara por su cuenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that with her numbers, her advantage was too significant."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que con sus números, su ventaja era demasiado significativa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that you could only push a man so far before..."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que solo se podía empujar a un hombre tan lejos antes de..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew that, whether she had admitted it to herself or not, that this was a part of it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que, sea que lo hubiera admitido ante sí misma o no, eso era parte de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the answer almost instantly."
msgstr "Sarah supo la respuesta casi al instante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the answer before she dared to speak it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía la respuesta antes de atreverse a pronunciarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the answer the captain wanted from her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía la respuesta que el capitán quería de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the girl's body well enough by now, quickly building the pace as she pistoned her fingers ever faster."
msgstr "Sarah conocía bien el cuerpo de la chica para entonces, acelerando el ritmo mientras bombeaba sus dedos cada vez más rápido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the list, murder, lies, adultery, but by now she imagined she had broken more than a few of them."
msgstr "Sarah conocía la lista: asesinato, mentiras, adulterio; pero ahora imaginaba que había roto más de una."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the orc wanted more, and she obliged. She unhooked her bra, dropping it to the ground next to her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el orco quería más, y ella se lo dio. Se desabrochó el sujetador, dejándolo caer al suelo junto a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the reports...but her only source for those had been Carolyn."
msgstr "Sarah conocía los informes... pero su única fuente para ellos había sido Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the spirit had a point there."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que el espíritu tenía razón en eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the strength of her husband and laughed as he slowly pretended to lose."
msgstr "Sarah conocía la fuerza de su marido y rió mientras él fingía perder lentamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew the topics were important, boring as they were, but she was eager for a break."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que los temas eran importantes, aburridos como lo fueran, pero ella ansiaba un descanso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew there was no reasoning with him."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no había nada que decirle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew there was town here. A small remnant of human civilization just on the edge of the bay."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que había un pueblo aquí. Un pequeño remanente de la civilización humana justo al borde de la bahía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew they had the supplies and logistics to keep this up for a week if they had to."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que tenían los suministros y la logística para mantener esto durante una semana si fuera necesario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew they would be loyal to her, but only if she took the city."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que serían leales a ella, pero solo si tomaba la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew things had gotten bad, but she hadn't imagined that bad."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que las cosas se habían puesto mal, pero no había imaginado que fueran tan malas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this painting well. It once had a prominent place in Castle Reinmeer."
msgstr "Sarah conocía bien este cuadro. Antiguamente ocupaba un lugar destacado en el Castillo Reinmeer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this too was part of it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que esto también era parte de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was no idle threat."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que no era una amenaza vacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was on the agenda. The event itself was a formality, but she worried about how Thomas would handle such an event."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que esto estaba en la agenda. El evento en sí era una formalidad, pero ella temía cómo Thomas manejaría tal situación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was the opportunity she had been looking for."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que esta era la oportunidad que había estado buscando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was true, but had given it little thought."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que eso era cierto, pero no había pensado en ello mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was true, but she had no intention of buying the silk."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que era cierto, pero no tenía intención de comprar la seda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this was wrong. She knew the type of person that made a match for her."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que esto estaba mal. Sabía el tipo de persona que se casaría con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew this world was different. There were different rules. She had to be careful. Unlike back home, her station offered her little protection."
msgstr "Sarah sabía que este mundo era diferente. Había reglas distintas. Tenía que tener cuidado. A diferencia de su hogar, su posición le ofrecía poca protección."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew well enough the effect she could have on men, and it was obvious that Marius was hardly immune to her either."
msgstr "Sarah conocía bien el efecto que podía ejercer sobre los hombres, y era obvio que Marius tampoco estaba exento de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what Kate meant."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que Kate quería decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what Lily meant. The Union Kingdoms, and with it Rosanna, were not as open to these things as some corners of the world."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que Lily quería decir. Los Reinos de la Unión, y con ellos Rosanna, no eran tan abiertos a estas cosas como algunas partes del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what had to be done."
msgstr "Sarah sabía qué tenía que hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what he meant."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que quería decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what she had to do."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que tenía que hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what she had to do. Had been trained to do, if a day like this ever came."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que tenía que hacer. Había sido entrenada para ello, por si alguna vez llegaba un día como este."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew what she had to, despite the danger of it."
msgstr "Sarah sabía lo que tenía que hacer, a pesar del peligro que ello conllevaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew where her advantage laid."
msgstr "Sarah sabía dónde radicaba su ventaja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew who she had to ask, Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Sarah sabía a quién tenía que pedirle ayuda, Lady Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew who she really wanted to see right now."
msgstr "Sarah sabía a quién realmente quería ver en ese momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew why he was here."
msgstr "Sarah sabía por qué estaba aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew why."
msgstr "Sarah sabía por qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knew."
msgstr "Sarah lo sabía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knocked on the door to Queen Maeiv's room."
msgstr "Sarah tocó la puerta de la habitación de la reina Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knocked the back of her head against the ship's deck as her entire body arched."
msgstr "Sarah golpeó la nuca contra el suelo de cubierta mientras todo su cuerpo se arqueaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knocked the wall."
msgstr "Sarah dio un golpe contra la pared."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knocked twice."
msgstr "Sarah dio dos golpes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah know who she had to talk to, Lily Highfield."
msgstr "Sarah sabía a quién tenía que hablar: Lily Highfield."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knows he will want something in return."
msgstr "Sarah sabe que querrá algo a cambio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knows her prayers won't be heard, but makes them all the same."
msgstr "Sarah sabe que sus oraciones no serán escuchadas, pero las hace de todas formas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knows in her heart that she feels the same way."
msgstr "Sarah sabe en lo más profundo de su corazón que siente lo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knows she wants to hold Kate. Feel her in her arms, touch her with her fingers."
msgstr "Sarah sabe que desea abrazar a Kate. Sentirla en sus brazos, tocarla con sus dedos."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Sarah knows that Atilla is right, something breaks between them."
msgstr "Sarah sabe que Atilla tiene razón; algo se rompe entre ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah knows that Kate is dear to her, but she also knows that her life, her destiny, is too grand for something so small as love."
msgstr "Sarah sabe que Kate es querida por ella, pero también sabe que su vida, su destino, son demasiado grandiosos para algo tan pequeño como el amor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid back down and pulled the sheets closely over her body, as if it was a shield."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó de nuevo y apretó las sábanas contra su cuerpo, como si fueran un escudo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid back down in the bed and pulled the covers over herself."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó de nuevo en la cama y cubrió su cuerpo con las sábanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid back down on the ground, closing her eyes."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó de nuevo en el suelo, cerrando los ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid back in her bed."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó en su cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid down and pulled the covers close."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó y tiró de las sábanas hacia sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid down in her bed and looked up at the ceiling."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó en su cama y miró hacia el techo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid down next to him."
msgstr "Sarah se acostó a su lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid down on her bed, or what had to pass for one."
msgstr "Sarah se acostó en su cama, o lo que tenía que pasar por una."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid down on the bed."
msgstr "Sarah se tumbó en la cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid face down on the bed, her breasts pressing against the fabric."
msgstr "Sarah se acostó boca abajo en la cama, con sus pechos presionando contra el tejido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid her body against his, and he against hers, each balanced against the other."
msgstr "Sarah se recostó contra él y él contra ella, cada uno equilibrado sobre el otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid on her back, looking up at the stars overhead."
msgstr "Sarah yacía boca arriba, mirando las estrellas que brillaban en el cielo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid on her bed...hours passing before she dared to move again."
msgstr "Sarah se tumbó en su cama... horas transcurrieron antes de que se atreviera a moverse de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid on the floor, exhausted, ragged, her blind blank."
msgstr "Sarah yacía en el suelo, exhausta, desgarrada, con su mirada ciega y vacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid on the floor, trying to regain her strength, but the spirit had sapped much out of her."
msgstr "Sarah yacía en el suelo, intentando recuperar sus fuerzas, pero el espíritu le había sacado mucho de sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laid there, sprawled out on her bed, raging at everyone else."
msgstr "Sarah yacía allí, tendida en su cama, enfadada con todos los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah landed on her back, the creature pounced and pinned her to the ground."
msgstr "Sarah cayó de espaldas; el monstruo saltó y la inmovilizó contra el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah lapped it up."
msgstr "Sarah se lo tragó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughe as she watched the spectacle unfold."
msgstr "Sarah rió al observar el espectáculo desarrollarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed a little."
msgstr "Sarah rió un poco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed again."
msgstr "Sarah rió de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed along with her brother, but more than anything, she was happy to see him smile again."
msgstr "Sarah rio junto a su hermano, pero sobre todo, estaba feliz de verlo sonreír de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed along with him."
msgstr "Sarah rió con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and began to pull away her own clothes, casting them aside."
msgstr "Sarah rió y comenzó a desabrochar su propia ropa, tirándola al suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and gently pushed Samayra. Even the light nudge was enough to cause the girl to nearly tumble."
msgstr "Sarah rió y empujó suavemente a Samayra. Incluso el ligero empujón fue suficiente para que la chica casi cayera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and gestured back at him."
msgstr "Sarah rió y le indicó que se quedara atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and kissed Lily, again and again."
msgstr "Sarah reía y besaba a Lily, una y otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and pushed herself up."
msgstr "Sarah rió y se impulsó hacia arriba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and raised her hand, calling over one of the waiters."
msgstr "Sarah rió y levantó la mano, llamando a uno de los camareros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and seized her husband's arm."
msgstr "Sarah rió y se aferró al brazo de su esposo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and tried handing him back his cloak."
msgstr "Sarah rió e intentó devolverle su capa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and walked past him, grazing his hand as she walked past him. She noticed his hand recoiling from hers like she was fire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and waved her hand."
msgstr "Sarah rió y movió la mano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and waved her hands."
msgstr "Sarah rió y agitó las manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she dropped the last piece of armor among the rest."
msgstr "Sarah rió al dejar caer la última pieza de armadura entre el resto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she felt Kate begin to kiss her stomach. With each kiss, she slowly traced her way further down."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras sentía que Kate comenzaba a besar su vientre. Con cada beso, fue trazando lentamente su camino más abajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she looked at him."
msgstr "Sarah rió al mirarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she moved towards the door."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras se acercaba a la puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she pulled another armor piece off Lily."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras desprendía otra pieza de la armadura de Lily."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she reached out with one arm, putting it under Samayra's head."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras extendía un brazo para colocarlo debajo de la cabeza de Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she rested her head on his chest, hearing the beating of his heart."
msgstr "Sarah rio mientras apoyaba su cabeza sobre el pecho de él, escuchando el latido de su corazón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she rode towards the city on her horse."
msgstr "Sarah reía mientras montaba hacia la ciudad a caballo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she said it."
msgstr "Sarah rió al decirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she stretched, cracking her own bones."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras se estiraba, crujendo sus propios huesos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she threw back her head and allowed her body to sink even deeper into the pillows."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras echaba la cabeza hacia atrás y dejaba que su cuerpo se hundiera aún más profundo en las almohadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she took the bottles from his hands."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras tomaba las botellas de sus manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she tried to hold Samayra off."
msgstr "Sarah rió mientras intentaba mantenerse alejada de Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed as she tried to run, but the armor and snow mixed poorly, and she barely managed to take more than a few steps before slipping."
