msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked down the aisle."
msgstr "Sarah caminó por el pasillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked further along."
msgstr "Sarah avanzó más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked further into the room."
msgstr "Sarah avanzó más adentro de la habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked in awe."
msgstr "Sarah entró con asombro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked inside. Thankfully, it was a good deal colder."
msgstr "Sarah entró en la habitación. Afortunadamente, hacía mucho más frío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked into the room and sat down."
msgstr "Sarah entró en la habitación y se sentó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked into the study, leaving her doubts behind her."
msgstr "Sarah entró en el estudio, dejando sus dudas atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked nearer to the monolith, instinctively."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó al monolito instintivamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked nearer to the throne."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó al trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked next to Varga. Unlike her, he seemed to have a natural affinity for remembering the name of every odd person or town they came upon."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba junto a Varga. A diferencia de ella, él parecía tener una afinidad natural para recordar el nombre de cada persona extraña o pueblo que encontraban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked onto the training ground. A fighting mat had been put down."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia la zona de entrenamiento. Una estera había sido colocada allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked out from behind the bookcases."
msgstr "Sarah salió de detrás de los estantes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked out of the house towards the nearby well."
msgstr "Sarah salió de la casa hacia el pozo cercano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over and looked at the documents."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y miró los documentos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over and placed her hand on Kate's shoulder."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y colocó su mano sobre el hombro de Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over and sat down."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y se sentó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over to Belmont and lowered her voice."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Belmont y bajó la voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over to Marion, standing apart from the crowd."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Marion, que estaba separada de la multitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over to Nick, happy to escape much of the captain's anger for the day."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Nick, contenta de escapar de gran parte del enojo del capitán para el día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over to Varga, standing apart from the crowd."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Varga, que estaba separado del resto de la multitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over to the door of her bedroom and turned the key, unlocking the door."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia la puerta de su habitación y giró la llave, desbloqueando la entrada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over towards him."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over towards the package and grabbed it off the floor. She pulled on the velvet strings and as they slipped away, they revealed an outfit."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia el paquete y lo agarró del suelo. Tiró de las cintas de terciopelo y, al deslizarlas, revelaron un atuendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over towards the side of the training ground, dropping her weapon onto the floor."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia el costado del campo de entrenamiento, dejando su arma en el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over towards them."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over, behind the covers of the crate."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó, detrás de las cubiertas de la caja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked softly, fearing to make any noise."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba con suavidad, temiendo hacer el menor ruido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked straight over towards the bed."
msgstr "Sarah caminó directamente hacia la cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked straight through her room out towards the balcony, and Lily dutifully followed."
msgstr "Sarah caminó directamente a través de su habitación hacia el balcón, y Lily la siguió con devoción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the door, leaving her room behind."
msgstr "Sarah cruzó la puerta, dejando atrás su habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the emptied out throne room."
msgstr "Sarah caminó por el salón del trono vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the grass, the cold touch healing her feet, putting her hand on one of the trees nearby. Sharp. The touch surprised her."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba por la hierba, el frío sanando sus pies, mientras ponía su mano en uno de los árboles cercanos. Agudo. El tacto la sorprendió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the hallway up to the barricade."
msgstr "Sarah caminó por el pasillo hasta la barricada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the quarter, towards her bed."
msgstr "Sarah caminó por el barrio, hacia su cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked through the room, slightly off balance, making her way to one of the wardrobes. After some searching, she fished out a bottle of wine from one of the drawers."
msgstr "Sarah caminó por la habitación, ligeramente inestable, dirigiéndose hacia uno de los armarios. Tras buscar un rato, sacó una botella de vino de uno de los cajones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked to the door and stepped outside, leaving the house and all her work behind her."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia la puerta y salió al exterior, dejando atrás la casa y todo su trabajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked towards it."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked towards the carriage. Each step felt like one closer to her doom."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia el carruaje. Cada paso sentía como si se acercara a su perdición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked towards them."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up and grabbed Samayra's wrists before she could turn to leave."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y agarró las muñecas de Samayra antes de que pudiera girarse para irse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up and sat down next to him."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y se sentó a su lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up besides Cassius and began to follow him."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Cassius y comenzó a seguirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up closer to the captain."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó más al capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up closer to the man."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó al hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up closer, walking side-by-side with the Duke."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó más, caminando de la mano con el Duque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up closer."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up next to Samayra and looked at the wall that Samayra was looking at."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Samayra y miró la pared que Samayra observaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to Kate."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to Marion before he could be dragged away."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Marion antes de que lo arrastraran."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to Varga before he could be dragged away."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a Varga antes de que pudiera ser arrastrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to her as she was still on the ground. With guards everywhere, she was smart enough not to try anything, or so Sarah hoped."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a ella mientras aún estaba en el suelo. Con guardias por todas partes, era lo bastante lista como para no intentar nada, o así esperaba Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to her brother."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a su hermano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to him and looped her arm into his."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a él y le enlazó el brazo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to him, so little space between them, she could feel his breath on her skin."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a él; tan poca distancia los separaba que podía sentir su aliento sobre su piel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to him. If he noticed her, he didn't show it."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a él. Si lo notaba, no lo mostraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to it and read it."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a ella y la leyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to it and sat down."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó y se sentó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to the plants."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a las plantas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up to the window in her room."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a la ventana de su habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up towards Samayra."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up towards him. Part of her wanted to ignore him, but she knew no good would come from that."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó a él. Parte de ella quería ignorarlo, pero sabía que no le vendría bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up towards the Headmaster."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó al Director."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up towards the only mirror in the room and stood in front of it."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia el único espejo de la habitación y se paró frente a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked up towards where she heard the voices."
msgstr "Sarah caminó hacia donde escuchaba las voces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked with Xan across every continent and every nation."
msgstr "Sarah caminó con Xan por cada continente y por cada nación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walks the familiar path."
msgstr "Sarah recorre el camino familiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walks up the plank and goes straight up to captain Belmont, pressing her finger into his chest."
msgstr "Sarah sube por la pasarela y se dirige directamente al capitán Belmont, presionando su dedo contra su pecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walks up towards Cassius."
msgstr "Sarah se acerca hacia Casio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wandered away."
msgstr "Sarah se alejó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wandered if it was genuine concern for her safety, or if he just didn't want to be inconvenienced."
msgstr "Sarah se preguntó si era genuino su interés por su seguridad, o si simplemente no quería verse incomodado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wandered off into a different direction and began considering the meeting."
msgstr "Sarah se adentró en otra dirección y comenzó a considerar la reunión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wandered over towards the desk."
msgstr "Sarah se acercó al escritorio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wandered the halls of the castle. It was too early to sleep, and she didn't want to sleep. There was too much to consider."
msgstr "Sarah se adentró en los pasillos del castillo. Era demasiado temprano para dormir, y no deseaba hacerlo. Había demasiadas cosas por considerar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanders out of the great hall in a haze, ignoring everything around her."
msgstr "Sarah deambula hacia fuera de la gran sala en un estado de confusión, ignorando todo a su alrededor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted Xan to see the insanity of this plan."
msgstr "Sarah quería que Xan viera la locura de este plan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted a day to herself, selfish as that was."
msgstr "Sarah quería un día para ella, egoísta como eso era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted a day to herself."
msgstr "Sarah quería un día para sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted her master to be proud of her."
msgstr "Sarah quería que su amo se enorgulleciera de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted her to live. But out here, what could she do? Each day she could see Samayra grow weaker."
msgstr "Sarah quería que viviera. Pero aquí fuera, ¿qué podía hacer? Cada día veía cómo Samayra se debilitaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted no company tonight. Only solitude."
msgstr "Sarah no deseaba compañía esta noche. Solo soledad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted nothing more than to escape this place. Get away from anyone that might know her, might see how she failed."
msgstr "Sarah no deseaba nada más que huir de este lugar. Alejarse de cualquiera que pudiera conocerla, que pudiera ver cómo falló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted some peace and decided to keep walking down the empty hallway."
msgstr "Sarah buscaba paz y decidió seguir caminando por el pasillo vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to approach, yet a part of her also feared to come closer."
msgstr "Sarah quería acercarse, aunque una parte de ella también temía llegar más cerca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to ask him so much, but she held it all in, remaining quiet as she guided him through the camp."
msgstr "Sarah quería preguntarle tantas cosas, pero lo guardó todo dentro, manteniéndose callada mientras le guiaba por el campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to be angry with him, but found it impossible to summon the emotion."
msgstr "Sarah quería estar enojada con él, pero no pudo encontrar la fuerza para sentirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to be closer to him."
msgstr "Sarah quería estar más cerca de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to be gone before they came, lest she'd have to kill more."
msgstr "Sarah quería haberse ido antes de que llegaran, por si tenía que matar a más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to be gone before they tried."
msgstr "Sarah quería irse antes de que intentaran."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to crawl away, but trapped in his grip, she could not."
msgstr "Sarah quería arrastrarse lejos, pero atrapada en su agarre, no podía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to cry, had she ever heard anything so sweet?"
msgstr "¿Deseaba llorar? ¿Había oído jamás algo tan dulce?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to dispute the man, but she couldn't deny that it was strange that he had survived here."
msgstr "Sarah quería disputar al hombre, pero no podía negar que era extraño que hubiera sobrevivido allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to give voice to her pleasure, but she knew that she already risked enough just by watching them."
msgstr "Sarah quería dar voz a su placer, pero sabía que ya había arriesgado demasiado solo por observarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to hold back from telling Xan everything that had happened."
msgstr "Sarah quería contenerse y no contarle a Xan todo lo que había sucedido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to keep her word to Marion, but Thomas was right. He was the king, and his order stood over hers. There was nothing she could do."
msgstr "Sarah quería cumplir su palabra con Marion, pero Thomas tenía razón. Él era el rey y su orden prevalecía sobre la suya. No había nada que pudiera hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to know where he was from, and she knew tricking him would be pointless."
msgstr "Sarah quería saber de dónde provenía, y sabía que engañarlo sería inútil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to laugh at the absurdity."
msgstr "Sarah quería reírse de la absurdidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to look away from him as much as she wanted to look at him."
msgstr "Sarah quería apartar la mirada de él tanto como quería mirarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to move, but couldn't."
msgstr "Sarah quería moverse, pero no podía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to open her mouth, but her body would not listen."
msgstr "Sarah quería abrir la boca, pero su cuerpo no obedecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to punch him, but she knew that wasn't a wise idea."
msgstr "Sarah quería darle un puñetazo, pero sabía que no era una buena idea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to punch his face in, but at the same time, had to admit he was right."
msgstr "Sarah quería darle una paliza en la cara, pero al mismo tiempo tenía que admitir que tenía razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to push back, but she could see he wasn't lying."
msgstr "Sarah quería empujarlo, pero podía ver que no mentía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to rage, but by now, she would have said or done anything to get him back into it."
msgstr "Sarah quería enfurecerse, pero a estas alturas, habría dicho o hecho cualquier cosa para volver a meterlo en eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to return the favor."
msgstr "Sarah quería devolverle el favor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to say things to Atilla that she dared not even think."
msgstr "Sarah quería decirle a Atilla cosas que no se atrevía ni siquiera a pensar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to scream."
msgstr "Sarah quería gritar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to scream. Cry. Beg."
msgstr "Sarah quería gritar. Llorar. Suplicar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to throw the money away."
msgstr "Sarah quería tirar el dinero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to turn, warn him not to finish inside of her, but it was of no use."
msgstr "Sarah quería girarse, advertirle que no se acabara dentro de ella, pero era inútil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to wilt under his dominating gaze, but she struggled to keep her eyes matching his."
msgstr "Sarah quería derretirse bajo su mirada dominante, pero luchó por mantener sus ojos al nivel de los suyos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to yell at him, but it would make no difference."
msgstr "Sarah quería gritarle, pero no serviría de nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wanted to, but she truly didn't have the energy."
msgstr "Sarah quería hacerlo, pero no tenía realmente la energía para ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wants her to know her. She begins to pull on Samayra's waist, guiding her, leading her, into a classic Rosannan dance."
msgstr "Sarah quiere que la conozca. Comienza a tirar de la cintura de Samayra, guiándola, llevándola, en una clásica danza rosana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was a natural."
msgstr "Sarah era natural."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was a quick study and had soon discoverd the motions that solicited the greatest response from the woman."
msgstr "Sarah era una alumna rápida y pronto descubrió los movimientos que provocaban la mayor respuesta en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was a slave, one among many, but she held value. As a beautiful woman, she held more than most."
msgstr "Sarah era una esclava, una entre muchas, pero tenía valor. Como mujer hermosa, poseía más que la mayoría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was almost ready to rip off his clothes herself."
msgstr "Sarah estaba a punto de arrancárselas ella misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was already halfway up the scaffolding, her feet racing."
msgstr "Sarah ya estaba a mitad de la escalera, con los pies volando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was already naked, having no clothes to speak of, and Mary quickly disrobed herself."
msgstr "Sarah ya estaba desnuda, sin apenas ropa puesta, y Mary se quitó la ropa rápidamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was already naked, standing and observing the old soldier undress."
msgstr "Sarah ya estaba desnuda, de pie y observando al viejo soldado quitarse la ropa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was angry, but mostly at herself. She should have known better than to insult him by calling him old."
msgstr "Sarah estaba furiosa, pero principalmente contra sí misma. Debería haber sabido mejor que insultarlo llamándolo viejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was angry, but she also knew she had no option to fight Xan."
msgstr "Sarah estaba enfadada, pero también sabía que no tenía opción para luchar contra Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was annoyed at his curt answer."
msgstr "Sarah estaba molesta por su respuesta cortante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was ashamed to admit that she had never really given it much thought."
msgstr "Sarah se sentía avergonzada de admitir que nunca había pensado realmente en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was beaming with pride at how quickly she had learned to service the goblin with her mouth."
msgstr "Sarah brillaba de orgullo por lo rápido que había aprendido a servir al goblino con la boca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was bucking wildly."
msgstr "Sarah se encabritaba salvajemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was by now fine with either."
msgstr "Sarah ya estaba bien con ambas cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was careful not to speak. One wrong word could cause disaster."
msgstr "Sarah se cuidaba de no hablar. Una palabra mal dicha podría causar el desastre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was careful to speak about the subject. She knew that her husband didn't enjoy talking about the very military victory that had earned him his title."
msgstr "Sarah tenía cuidado al hablar del tema. Sabía que su marido no disfrutaba hablando de la victoria militar que le había valido su título."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was circling Kate, holding her sword drawn to lunge out and strike at her."
msgstr "Sarah rodeaba a Kate, con la espada desenvainada y lista para lanzarse contra ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was close to finishing up her meal and returning back to the house, when suddenly she heard a familiar voice."
msgstr "Sarah estaba a punto de terminar su comida y regresar a casa cuando, de repente, oyó una voz familiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was close to screaming at him, but again, she swallowed her pride."
msgstr "Sarah estaba a punto de gritarle, pero una vez más tragó su orgullo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was committed to learn from him what she could while she still had him as a resource."
msgstr "Sarah se comprometió a aprender de él todo lo que pudiera mientras aún lo tuviera como recurso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused at the question, but decided to play along."
msgstr "Sarah se confundió con la pregunta, pero decidió seguir el juego."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused for a brief moment, but then heard him groan."
msgstr "Sarah se confundió por un breve instante, pero luego escuchó su gemido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused for a moment."
msgstr "Sarah se confundió por un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused, because with his cock deep inside of her, it sure felt to her like that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused."
msgstr "Sarah estaba confundida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused. He had told her the answer to all his problems, but appeared still troubled."
msgstr "Sarah estaba confundida. Le había dado la respuesta a todos sus problemas, pero seguía pareciendo inquieto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was confused. Why else did he force her down between his legs?"
msgstr "Sarah estaba confundida. ¿Por otra cosa la obligó a estar entre sus piernas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was cooking as she looked out across the room."
msgstr "Sarah cocinaba mientras miraba a través de la habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was dazed."
msgstr "Sarah estaba aturdida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was desperate."
msgstr "Sarah estaba desesperada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was distracted from Lily as she heard Spymaster Kravel enter."
msgstr "Sarah se distrajo de Lily al escuchar la entrada del espía Kravel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager for any chance to improve her odds of passing the exam and had gladly accepted it."
msgstr "Sarah estaba ansiosa por cualquier oportunidad de mejorar sus posibilidades de aprobar el examen y aceptó encantada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager not to be reprimanded again and started to lean further into him."
msgstr "Sarah estaba ansiosa por no recibir otro regañón y comenzó a inclinarse más hacia él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager to avoid such a fate."
msgstr "Sarah deseaba evitar tal destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager to change the subject, hoping to calm Samayra down by changing the subject."
msgstr "Sarah estaba ansiosa por cambiar de tema, esperando calmar a Samayra con ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager to hear the answer. Finally, a solution to her problem."
msgstr "Sarah ansiaba escuchar la respuesta. Por fin, una solución a su problema."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was eager to resume her studies. The theoretical and the practical."
msgstr "Sarah tenía prisa por retomar sus estudios: la teoría y la práctica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was entranced by the sight."
msgstr "Sarah quedó hipnotizada por la visión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was far from the strongest, but even to her, lifting Samayra off the ground and spinning her proved hardly difficult."
msgstr "Sarah estaba lejos de ser la más fuerte, pero incluso para ella, levantar a Samayra del suelo y girarla resultaba casi sin esfuerzo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was fine with that."
msgstr "Sarah estaba bien con eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was firm in her repetition."
msgstr "Sarah estaba decidida al insistir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was for a moment hesitant. Had she really won Maeiv's support so easily?"
msgstr "Sarah dudó por un momento. ¿Había ganado realmente el apoyo de Maeiv tan fácilmente?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was genuinly impressed with the old man's stamina."
msgstr "Sarah estaba genuinamente impresionada con la resistencia del anciano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was getting annoyed that he seemed to be playing around."
msgstr "Sarah se estaba irritando por el hecho de que él parecía estar jugando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was glad Kate was able to at least stand a little bit. Carrying her friend entirely on her own strength still seemed impossible."
msgstr "Sarah se alegró de que Kate pudiera al menos estar de pie un poco. Aún parecía imposible cargar a su amiga totalmente con sus propias fuerzas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was glad for it, if only because the new crowd seemed less obsessed with protocol."
msgstr "Sarah estaba contenta por ello, aunque fuera solo porque la nueva multitud parecía menos obsesionada con el protocolo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was glad he did. She had enough trouble managing her own feelings today; she didn't want to be managing his."
msgstr "Sarah estaba contenta de que lo hubiera hecho. Tenía suficiente dificultad para manejar sus propias emociones hoy; no quería tener que manejar las suyas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was glad that the captain had decided to show mercy, but seeing Nick now, she wasn't sure if he was even thankful to be alive."
msgstr "Sarah estaba agradecida de que el capitán hubiera decidido mostrar clemencia, pero al ver a Nick ahora, no estaba segura de si siquiera estaba agradecido por estar con vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was grateful for this fact, because she doubted she could survive even a single day of full exposure to this sun."
msgstr "Sarah estaba agradecida por este hecho, porque dudaba que pudiera sobrevivir ni siquiera un día entero bajo la exposición total de este sol."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was grinding her teeth, trying to keep herself from screaming out further in pain."
msgstr "Sarah apretaba los dientes, luchando por no gritar más por el dolor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy for her skilled guidance, but she disliked just how much she had to rely on Lady Carolyn's good intentions."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz por su hábil guía, pero no le gustaba en qué medida tenía que depender de las buenas intenciones de la Dama Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy for her to have a distraction."
msgstr "Sarah estaba contenta de tener una distracción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy for his kind words, even though she wanted to deflect them."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz por sus amables palabras, aunque deseaba desviarlas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy for the company. Happy she could finally talk to someone."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz de tener compañía. Feliz de poder finalmente hablar con alguien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy for the girl's presence."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz por la presencia de la chica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy that she could go to the market."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz de poder ir al mercado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to have Maeiv's support for her position."
msgstr "Sarah estaba contenta de contar con el apoyo de Maeiv en su posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to hear her say that."
msgstr "Sarah se alegró de oírla decir eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to hear it was something trivial."
msgstr "Sarah sintió un verdadero entusiasmo al escuchar que se trataba de algo trivial."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to hear she could offer Samayra at least that."
msgstr "Sarah estaba contenta de saber que podía darle al menos eso a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to hear their confirmations, though she still felt part of her fear remain."
msgstr "Sarah sintió alivio al escuchar sus confirmaciones, aunque aún sentía que parte de su miedo permanecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to notice that her body was not that different from Kate's anymore, she too now had the muscles that Kate had."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz de notar que su cuerpo ya no era tan diferente al de Kate; ella también ahora tenía los músculos que Kate poseía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy to oblige him, letting the feeling of his gripping hand on the back of her head, serve as her instruction."
msgstr "Sarah se alegró de complacerlo, dejando que la sensación de su mano apretando el cabello en la nuca sirviera como su instrucción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy, no matter what else she might think about it. But part of her also hated that this was what made her happy."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz, sin importar lo que pudiera pensar al respecto. Pero una parte de ella también odiaba que fuera eso lo que la hacía feliz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was happy. Happy that so much of the paperwork was gone, but also that Samayra seemed to find some purpose in the role."
msgstr "Sarah estaba feliz. Feliz de que tanta parte de la burocracia hubiera desaparecido, pero también de que Samayra pareciera encontrar algún propósito en el rol."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was hestitant, but as she saw the others take of their clothes, she joined them."
msgstr "Sarah estaba dubitativa, pero al ver que los demás se quitaban la ropa, se unió a ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was honest in her admiration for Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Sarah era sincera en su admiración por la Dama Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was idling for a moment, relaxing in the shade of the tent."
msgstr "Sarah se quedó un momento, relajándose a la sombra de la tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was impressed. She had only ever known kings and emperors who could trace their lines back like that."
msgstr "Sarah quedó impresionada. Solo había conocido reyes y emperadores que pudieran trazar sus linajes de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was in little mood to humor him."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ganas de complacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was in no mood for riddles."
msgstr "Sarah no tenía ganas de juegos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was inspecting her body."
msgstr "Sarah estaba inspeccionando su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was laying in bed, she had left her clothes on the floor."
msgstr "Sarah yacía en la cama, con sus prendas dejadas en el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was laying on her back, looking down at Varga as he began to strip."
msgstr "Sarah yacía boca arriba, mirando hacia abajo mientras Varga comenzaba a quitarse la ropa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was left behind, leaning against the wall, still exhausted and in no condition to give chase."
msgstr "Sarah quedó atrás, apoyada contra la pared, aún agotada y sin fuerzas para dar caza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was left to herself. Finally she could be alone."
msgstr "Sarah quedó sola. Finalmente podía estar a solas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was left, fully in heat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was losing herself in the moment, when suddenly, Kate pulled back and grabbed her shoulders."
msgstr "Sarah se perdía en el momento cuando de repente, Kate retrocedió y le agarró los hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was lost for words."
msgstr "Sarah se quedó sin palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was lost in thought, observing Atilla's gift."
msgstr "Sarah estaba perdida en sus pensamientos, observando el regalo de Atilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was loudly panting."
msgstr "Sarah jadeaba con fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was marching through the heavy snow."
msgstr "Sarah avanzaba por la pesada nieve."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was mesmerized as she watched the woman climb into the bed with her."
msgstr "Sarah se dejaba hipnotizar mientras observaba cómo la mujer subía a la cama junto a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was nearing hysterics. She needed him to take her."
msgstr "Sarah estaba a punto de perder la cabeza. Necesitaba que él la tomara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was no fool to the nature of their relationship, but she was thankful that she did not need to witness her own sale."
msgstr "Sarah no era tonta respecto a la naturaleza de su relación, pero estaba agradecida de no tener que presenciar su propia venta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was no stranger to her own body, but to feel the hands of her husband on her, was unlike anything she'd ever felt before."
msgstr "Sarah no era ajena a su propio cuerpo, pero sentir las manos de su esposo sobre ella fue algo que nunca había experimentado antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was not a zealot by any means, perhaps not even fully religious, but a part of her did always hesitate about rejecting it altogether."
msgstr "Sarah no era una fanática de ningún tipo, quizás ni siquiera completamente religiosa, pero una parte de ella siempre dudaba en rechazarlo por completo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was not blind to the world. In her travels with Xan she had learned and seen a lot."
msgstr "Sarah no era ciega al mundo. En sus viajes con Xan había aprendido y visto mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was not one who gave much value to witchcraft of any kind, but the creature seemed too serious in how it had spoken."
msgstr "Sarah no era de las que daba gran valor a la brujería de ningún tipo, pero la criatura parecía demasiado seria en cómo había hablado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was now fully awake, sitting upright in her bed."
msgstr "Sarah estaba ahora completamente despierta, sentada erguida en su cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was old enough to have learned that some men could feign interests in her words, all the while lusting after something else."
msgstr "Sarah ya era lo suficientemente mayor como para haber aprendido que algunos hombres fingían interés en sus palabras, mientras deseaban algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was on edge."
msgstr "Sarah estaba nerviosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was on her back, looking up at Varga as he turned around. Her eyes drifted down to between his legs."
msgstr "Sarah estaba boca arriba, mirando hacia arriba mientras Varga giraba para quedar de frente. Sus ojos se deslizaron hacia abajo, hasta entre sus piernas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was on her knees, her nails clawing into the wall, as the orgasm rolled over her body, seemingly a second time."
msgstr "Sarah estaba de rodillas, con las uñas clavadas en la pared, mientras el orgasmo se abalanzaba sobre su cuerpo, como si fuera una segunda vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was on the top deck when she saw the city draw closer and closer."
msgstr "Sarah estaba en la cubierta superior cuando vio cómo la ciudad se acercaba cada vez más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was only a few feet away when she spoke."
msgstr "Sarah estaba apenas a unos pocos pies de distancia cuando habló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was only geting more confused."
msgstr "Sarah solo se ponía más confundida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was only getting more confused."
msgstr "Sarah estaba cada vez más confundida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was pleased to discover the woman was far from inexperienced."
msgstr "Sarah se alegró de descubrir que la mujer estaba lejos de ser inexperta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was present when the nation's first university, the Rose University, was officially opened."
msgstr "Sarah estuvo presente cuando la primera universidad del país, la Universidad de Rose, fue oficialmente inaugurada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was pulled up to her feet by a guard."
msgstr "Sarah fue levantada del suelo por un guardia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet as she could be."
msgstr "Sarah estaba tan callada como podía ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet as she listened to Kate explain it from her perspective."
msgstr "Sarah permanecía en silencio mientras escuchaba a Kate explicarlo desde su perspectiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet as she listened to her husband explain the ways of the world. The real world, that real people have to live in."
msgstr "Sarah permaneció en silencio mientras escuchaba a su esposo explicar las reglas del mundo real, ese en el que la gente tiene que vivir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet as she pondered it. She had not thought about it like that before."
msgstr "Sarah permaneció en silencio mientras reflexionaba sobre ello. Nunca había pensado en eso de esa manera antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet for a moment, then nodded."
msgstr "Sarah permaneció en silencio por un momento y luego asintió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quiet."
msgstr "Sarah estaba callada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was quite for a while as she considered."
msgstr "Sarah permaneció en silencio durante un buen rato mientras reflexionaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was rapidly beginning to understand the many complexities of rigging and sailing a ship, but also the economy of simply managing a small cargo ship."
msgstr "Sarah estaba comprendiendo rápidamente las muchas complejidades de armar y navegar un barco, pero también la economía de simplemente gestionar un pequeño buque mercante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was rarely truly alone, helping Vaelen manage the mercenary company was equal parts soldiering and equal parts administration. Always busy."
msgstr "Sarah rara vez estaba verdaderamente sola; ayudar a Vaelen a gestionar la compañía de mercenarios era mitad soldado y mitad administración. Siempre ocupada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was relieved she'd only have to kill the arrogant one."
msgstr "Sarah aliviada de que solo tuviera que matar al arrogante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was relieved to hear that the girl took he words of warning seriously."
msgstr "Sarah alivió al escuchar que la chica tomó en serio sus advertencias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was rushed back to her seat by Jaeid."
msgstr "Sarah fue arrastrada de vuelta a su asiento por Jaeid."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was scrubbing the floor, trying to remove a particularly tough stain, when she heard the massive doors to the hallway open."
msgstr "Sarah fregaba el suelo, tratando de eliminar una mancha especialmente difícil, cuando escuchó abrirse las masivas puertas del pasillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was searching for something to say."
msgstr "Sarah buscaba algo que decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was searching her heart for the hatred that she imagined she should hold towards Kate, for robbing her and bringing her to the other side of the world."
msgstr "Sarah buscaba en su corazón el odio que imaginaba que debería sentir hacia Kate, por haberla robado y traído al otro lado del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was shaking with anger."
msgstr "Sarah temblaba de rabia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was shocked at how brazen Eula was."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sorprendida por la descarada actitud de Eula."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was simply happy to have her friend back."
msgstr "Sarah simplemente estaba feliz de tener a su amiga de vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting at Xan's former desk, studying a series of papers she had strew out across the tables."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada en el antiguo escritorio de Xan, repasando una serie de documentos que había esparcido por las mesas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting at her desk."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada en su escritorio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting behind her desk in the main study."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada detrás de su escritorio en la biblioteca principal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting behind her desk in the ship's cabin."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada detrás de su escritorio en la cabina del barco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting behind her desk, the letter from Kamal rolled up."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada detrás de su escritorio, con la carta de Kamal enrollada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting behind her desk, working at preparing the orders to resume the march."
msgstr "Sarah se sentaba detrás de su escritorio, trabajando en preparar las órdenes para reanudar la marcha."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting on a stone block, near one of the campfires."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada sobre un bloque de piedra, cerca de una de las hogueras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was sitting outside near the docks on a bench, watching the ships come and go."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sentada afuera cerca de los muelles en un banco, observando a los barcos entrar y salir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was slightly annoyed at Samayra's observations. Not because they were wrong, but because they were right."
msgstr "Sarah estaba ligeramente molesta con las observaciones de Samayra. No porque estuvieran equivocadas, sino porque tenían razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was slowly walking across the battlements of Castle Reinmeer."
msgstr "Sarah caminaba lentamente por las almenas del Castillo Reinmeer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was snapped from her thoughts by Carolyn's comment."
msgstr "Sarah fue arrancada de sus pensamientos por el comentario de Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was speaking to Samayra's loss, but she realized as she spoke the words, she equally spoke to her own."
msgstr "Sarah hablaba sobre la pérdida de Samayra, pero al pronunciar las palabras, se dio cuenta de que también lo hacía por sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stading in the middle of Atilla's tent, naked, in front of the large mirror. Mirror's were something that seemed ordinary to Sarah."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stammering."
msgstr "Sarah tartamudeaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was standing alone on a small hill, overlooking the battlefield, while all around her, the army prepared."
msgstr "Sarah estaba sola en una pequeña colina, mirando el campo de batalla, mientras que a su alrededor, el ejército se preparaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was standing alone on a small hill, overlooking the battlefield. All around her the army prepared."
msgstr "Sarah se paraba sola en una pequeña colina, contemplando el campo de batalla. A su alrededor, el ejército se preparaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was standing at the entrance of the warcamp."
msgstr "Sarah estaba de pie en la entrada del campamento de guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was standing in the alcove near the entrance to the great hall."
msgstr "Sarah estaba en el pasillo cerca de la entrada del gran salón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was startled at being caught out by Lily."
msgstr "Sarah se sobresaltó al ser sorprendida por Lily."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was startled by Sakar's sudden appearance, but tried not to let him notice."
msgstr "Sarah se sobresaltó ante la aparición repentina de Sakar, pero intentó no dejar que él lo notara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was startled by his directness."
msgstr "Sarah se sobresaltó ante su franqueza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was startled by the question."
msgstr "Sarah se sobresaltó ante la pregunta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was startled."
msgstr "Sarah se sobresaltó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still dazzling from the sight of it when she finally came upon her own room."
msgstr "Sarah seguía radiante ante el espectáculo cuando finalmente llegó a su propia habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still fuming. She wasn’t done with him yet. She stormed after him, below deck."
msgstr "Sarah seguía furiosa. No había terminado con él aún. Se lanzó tras él, hacia abajo de la cubierta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still in awe of the fact."
msgstr "Sarah seguía asombrada por el hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still reeling from how much the man seemed to know."
msgstr "Sarah aún estaba aturdida por lo mucho que el hombre parecía saber."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still shaken, and found it hard to speak. She shook her head."
msgstr "Sarah seguía conmocionada y le resultaba difícil hablar. Sacudió la cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still trying to process what was happening."
msgstr "Sarah aún intentaba procesar lo que estaba ocurriendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was still trying to recover from the pain of the last lash."
msgstr "Sarah aún intentaba recuperarse del dolor del último azote."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was struck by the words."
msgstr "Las palabras la abrumaron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned at how much the girl was able to communicate with only the touch of a hand. The press of a finger."
msgstr "Sarah quedó atónita ante la cantidad de comunicación que la chica lograba con solo el tacto de una mano. Con la presión de un dedo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned at the sight."
msgstr "Sarah quedó estupefacta ante la visión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned at the spirit's request."
msgstr "Sarah quedó atónita ante la petición del espíritu."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned by his sudden turn."
msgstr "Sarah quedó atónita ante su giro repentino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned that he could speak so calmly. The weight of the containers seemed almost not to affect him."
msgstr "Sarah estaba atóna de que pudiera hablar con tanta calma. El peso de los contenedores parecía apenas afectarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned when she watched the old tailor begin to undress."
msgstr "Sarah se quedó atónita al ver cómo el viejo sastre comenzaba a desnudarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned, and only felt her shock fade into anger."
msgstr "Sarah quedó atónita, y solo sintió cómo su asombro se desvanecía en rabia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned."
msgstr "Sarah estaba atónita."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned. Another person here. Another human."
msgstr "Sarah estaba atónita. Otra persona aquí. Otro ser humano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned. Atilla rarely called her by her name, and even more rarely made apologies."
msgstr "Sarah estaba atónita. Atilla rara vez la llamaba por su nombre, y aún menos frecuentemente se disculpaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned. Could the girl really enjoy this?"
msgstr "Sarah estaba atónita. ¿Podría la chica realmente disfrutar de esto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was stunned. She had imagined Naydeen was here on account of the same reasons as her. A conquered people."
msgstr "Sarah estaba estupefacta. Había imaginado que Naydeen había llegado por las mismas razones que ella: un pueblo conquistado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was suddenly aware of her own nakedness again."
msgstr "Sarah volvió a darse cuenta repentinamente de su desnudez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised at herself."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised at how well the goblin seemed to understand her and speak her language."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió por lo bien que el gobelín parecía entenderla y hablar su idioma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised at the fact that she found herself shocked."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió al darse cuenta de lo que acababa de sentir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised at the offer, but it felt impolite to refuse."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió por la oferta, pero le pareció poco educado rechazarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised by his harsh reaction."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió por su reacción tan dura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised by his sudden question."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió por su repentina pregunta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised by how casually Varga shared his trauma, and how little it seemed to faze him."
msgstr "Sarah se sorprendió por lo casual con que Varga compartió su trauma y por lo poco que parecía afectarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
