msgid "She had a suspicion of where her loyalties fell."
msgstr "Tenía una sospecha de dónde radicaban sus lealtades."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had a wide grin on her face as she continued."
msgstr "Tenía una amplia sonrisa en su rostro mientras seguía hablando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had a wide smile on her face as she said it."
msgstr "Tenía una amplia sonrisa en el rostro cuando lo dijo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had accepted it when she crossed the sea. Now she had to remain true in her resolve."
msgstr "Lo había aceptado al cruzar el mar. Ahora debía mantener firme su determinación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had accepted that this humiliation was what she would take...for her nation..."
msgstr "Había aceptado que esta humillación era lo que tendría que soportar... por su nación..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had allowed herself to be so foolish that she would meet with Lily. To promise her...to invite her to her room."
msgstr "Se había dejado llevar por la estupidez hasta el punto de encontrarse con Lily y prometerle...invitarla a su habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had already fooled herself once, believing that being born to a safe life meant she would remain safe."
msgstr "Ya se había engañado a sí misma una vez, creyendo que nacer en una vida segura significaba permanecer a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had already lost her dignity, and would then lose the votes as well."
msgstr "Ya había perdido su dignidad y también perdería los votos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had already pushed herself as far as she thought herself comfortable."
msgstr "Ya se había empujado a sí misma hasta el límite de lo que creía cómodo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had already suffered the humiliation, and here at the edge of the world, nobody would know anyway."
msgstr "Ya había sufrido la humillación y, aquí al borde del mundo, nadie lo sabría de todos modos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had always been in control of her own mind, but now she found it often wandering, whether she wanted to or not."
msgstr "Siempre había estado en control de su propia mente, pero ahora la encontraba a menudo divagando, queriendo o no."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had always found him attractive, even before marriage, but in their union she had also come to find something else."
msgstr "Siempre lo había encontrado atractivo, incluso antes del matrimonio, pero en su unión también llegó a encontrar algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had always known and lived with her betrayal to her brother. But to some degree, it had always been abstract."
msgstr "Siempre había sabido y vivido con su traición hacia su hermano. Pero, en cierto grado, siempre había sido abstracta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had always loved this view, but now, it made her feel like ice ran through her chest."
msgstr "Siempre había amado esta vista, pero ahora le parecía que el hielo corría por su pecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had always thought the world was a mostly fair place, where everyone got what they deserved."
msgstr "Siempre había pensado que el mundo era un lugar mayormente justo, donde todos recibían lo que merecían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had arrived here. She had nothing left to her name. No direction to move towards."
msgstr "Había llegado aquí. No le quedaba nada a su nombre. No sabía hacia dónde ir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had attacked the soldiers, her soldiers, and the girl even proudly admitted it."
msgstr "Ella había atacado a los soldados, sus propios soldados, y la muchacha lo admitió incluso con orgullo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had barely arived in the city, not even a minute, and already someone was waiting for her."
msgstr "Apenas había llegado a la ciudad, ni siquiera un minuto, y ya alguien la esperaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had barely gathered a few items from the pantry when she heard a voice."
msgstr "Había recogido apenas unos cuantos objetos de la despensa cuando oyó una voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had barely spoken to Hugh, but it was clear first impressions could be deceiving."
msgstr "Sarah apenas había hablado con Hugh, pero ya era claro que las primeras impresiones podían ser engañosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had become Queen."
msgstr "Se había convertido en reina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had become desperate for him to finish. So this could be over."
msgstr "Había llegado a la desesperación de que él terminara. Así podría acabar esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had become herself surprised by how quickly she had learned to wear the slave outfit without thinking about it."
msgstr "Se había sorprendido a sí misma por lo rápido que había aprendido a llevar el atuendo de esclava sin pensarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a fool to trust anyone, let alone such a lowly creature that she barely knew."
msgstr "Ha sido tonta al confiar en cualquiera, ¡menos aún en una criatura tan miserable que apenas conocía!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a fool to trust this creature, and now she'd pay the price."
msgstr "Había sido una tonta de confiar en esta criatura, y ahora pagaría el precio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a fool, she now realized."
msgstr "Ella había sido una tonta, ahora lo comprendía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a fool. She and Nick both, she now realized."
msgstr "Ella había sido una tonta. Ella y Nick también, ahora lo comprendía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a mage once, she could recall. But that was more dream than memory."
msgstr "Era maga alguna vez, lo recordaba. Pero eso era más sueño que memoria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been a princess, she could recall."
msgstr "Era una princesa, lo recordaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been able to carry the shame of it inside herself. Her own private secret"
msgstr "Podía llevar la vergüenza dentro de sí misma. Su propio secreto privado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been bored at the time, but now she was grateful for his lessons."
msgstr "En aquel entonces estaba aburrida, pero ahora le estoy agradecida por sus lecciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been carrying it on her back all her life."
msgstr "La había cargado en su espalda toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been casually sunbathing in the nude near the front of the ship, and it hadn't taken long for Belmont to take the hint."
msgstr "Había estado tomando el sol despreocupadamente desnuda cerca de la proa del barco, y no tardó en que Belmont entendiera la señal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been embarased for a brief moment, having to learn how to cook, but over time she had oddly learned to enjoy it."
msgstr "Sintió una breve vergüenza al tener que aprender a cocinar, pero con el tiempo descubrió de forma extraña que le gustaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been following and rushing from one point to the next for so long, that a chance to just sit and be useful seemed all she could want."
msgstr "Había estado siguiendo y corriendo de un punto a otro durante tanto tiempo, que la oportunidad de simplemente sentarse y ser útil parecía todo lo que podía desear."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been here before, she realized."
msgstr "Se había estado aquí antes, se dio cuenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been here only a few times before, whenever Xan tasked her to run some errands for her."
msgstr "Solo había estado aquí unas pocas veces antes, cada vez que Xan la encargaba de hacerle unos recados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been here with Xan, many years ago, and he had shown her about."
msgstr "La había estado aquí con Xan, hace muchos años, y él le había mostrado todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been hoping he'd come by."
msgstr "Ella había estado esperando que él viniera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been in Samayra's place before."
msgstr "Ya había estado en el lugar de Samayra antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been in that room for so long, plagued by so much noise that the sudden silence felt like a blessing."
msgstr "Había estado en esa habitación durante tanto tiempo, acosada por tanto ruido que el repentino silencio se sintió como una bendición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been no stranger to being the center of attention, but this was nearly too much, even for her."
msgstr "No era ajena a ser el centro de atención, pero esto era casi demasiado, incluso para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been on a ship for days. She yearned to feel warm again."
msgstr "Había estado en un barco durante días. Anhelaba sentir el calor de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been on the run for so long, Sarah had all but imagined she had no friends left in the world."
msgstr "Sarah había huido tanto tiempo que casi imaginaba no tener amigos en el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been out on her own in this city for a single day and she had nearly been attacked."
msgstr "Había estado sola en esta ciudad durante un solo día y casi la habían atacado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been playing in the castle gardens by herself. Her mother had passed away only a year or so before."
msgstr "Había estado jugando sola en los jardines del castillo. Su madre había fallecido hace apenas un año."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been raised to be proper and follow the protocols of court, enough rules to drive anyone mad."
msgstr "Fue educada para ser correcta y seguir los protocolos de la corte, suficientes reglas como para enloquecer a cualquiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been raised to possibly one day lead a nation, so the idea of ordering commands was not so unnatural to her as it was to Ephraim."
msgstr "Fue educada para liderar un reino algún día, por lo que la idea de dar órdenes no le resultaba tan extraña como a Ephraim."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been sitting in the dark long enough that her sight had grown used to it."
msgstr "Había estado sentada en la oscuridad lo suficiente para que su vista se hubiera acostumbrado a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been staring at it for a while, working up the courage to read it."
msgstr "La había estado observando por un tiempo, acumulando la valentía necesaria para leerla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been stressed, she couldn't deny that, but she never knew that could keep someone from solving a problem."
msgstr "Estaba estresada, no podía negarlo, pero nunca supo que eso pudiera impedirle a alguien resolver un problema."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been stripped of everything, title, money, respect."
msgstr "Había sido despojada de todo: título, dinero y respeto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been used by him, and no proper man would be mad enough to have her now."
msgstr "Él la había usado, y ningún hombre decente estaría loco por tenerla ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been used by them, used them in return."
msgstr "Fue usada por ellos y, a cambio, los usó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been warned a great many times by now about the dangers of the old road, but it was different to experience it."
msgstr "Ya le habían advertido muchas veces sobre los peligros del viejo camino, pero era diferente experimentarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had been weak then. She was strong now."
msgstr "Era débil entonces. Era fuerte ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had begun to form the body of a soldier."
msgstr "Ya había comenzado a formar el cuerpo de un soldado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had betrayed Xan, but there was nothing to be gained from endlessly reflecting on it."
msgstr "Traicionó a Xan, pero no había nada que ganar en reflexionar sobre ello sin fin."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had betrayed him when she confessed the truth to his son Marius."
msgstr "Traicionólo cuando confesó la verdad a su hijo Marius."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had betrayed his trust, just to save his father Alfred's reputation."
msgstr "Traicionó su confianza, solo para salvar la reputación de su padre, Alfred."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had broken that city. She would break this one all the same."
msgstr "Ella había roto esa ciudad. Rompería esta otra de igual forma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had carelessly crossed into this sacred space, violating it by her presence alone."
msgstr "Había cruzado descuidadamente este espacio sagrado, violándolo con su mera presencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had caught him by surprise, but she could feel him slowly warm to her."
msgstr "Lo había pillado por sorpresa, pero podía sentir cómo él se iba acostumbrando a ella poco a poco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had caught the blow with her shield, but it was as if the force of the strike was now reverberating through her arm, and into the rest of her body."
msgstr "Hirió el golpe con su escudo, pero era como si la fuerza del impacto resonara ahora por su brazo y se extendiera al resto de su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had caused too much commotion and before long, more soldiers would come. Fools who might hope to kill a mage."
msgstr "Había causado demasiado alboroto y antes de que pasara mucho tiempo vendrían más soldados. Tontos que podrían querer matar a un mago."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had ceased to count, but somewhere in the slaughter, she finally regained her senses."
msgstr "Ella había dejado de contar, pero en medio del masacre, finalmente recuperó el sentido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had chosen the captain, and whatever else he had in store, surely he would reward her loyalty to him."
msgstr "Ella había elegido al capitán, y por lo que tuviera en mente, sin duda le recompensaría su lealtad hacia él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had chosen to believe him and given up her body in return for information. She wanted to make good on that bargain."
msgstr "Había elegido creerle y entregado su cuerpo a cambio de información. Quería honrar ese acuerdo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come aboard to give him a piece of her mind. To shame him for what he had made her do on the voyage over. Instead, she now had his cum leaking down her legs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come here for peace and quiet, not to start a family feud only one day in."
msgstr "Vino aquí buscando paz y tranquilidad, no para iniciar una disputa familiar apenas un día después de llegar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come here to be safe. Safe from all the madness out there."
msgstr "Ha venido aquí para estar a salvo. A salvo de toda la locura que hay fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come this far."
msgstr "Llegó tan lejos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to accept her new role, not just as pretend, but in truth."
msgstr "Había llegado a aceptar su nuevo rol, no solo como fingimiento, sino en verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to know him in ways nobody else did."
msgstr "Ella había llegado a conocerlo de una manera que nadie más jamás conoció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to learn what he expected of her, and to obey before even commanded. She feared that for as much as she denied her new role, she was in many ways settling into it."
msgstr "Había llegado a aprender qué esperaba de ella y a obedecer antes incluso de ser comandada. Temía que, por mucho que negara su nuevo papel, en muchos aspectos estuviera acomodándose a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to power years before Sarah's father had died."
msgstr "Llegó al poder años antes de que muriera el padre de Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to see so much of it by now."
msgstr "Ya había visto tanto de ello por entonces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had come to stop them. Kill them."
msgstr "Ella había venido para detenerlos. Para matarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had committed herself to this path...decided on it...she would see it through..."
msgstr "Se había comprometido con este camino...había decidido por él...lo vería hasta el final..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had crossed something, though she could not tell what."
msgstr "Había cruzado algo, aunque no podía decir qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had debased herself this much, given in to him, what did more matter?"
msgstr "Se había degradado hasta ese punto, entregada a él, ¿qué importaba más?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had decided to leave Samayra behind."
msgstr "Había decidido dejar a Samayra atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had denied the possibility for so long, but given how often he took her, this outcome had always been obvious."
msgstr "La había negado durante tanto tiempo, pero dado lo a menudo que él la tomaba, este resultado siempre había sido obvio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had done it. Killed one of the blasted things."
msgstr "Lo había hecho. Había matado a uno de esos malditos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had done this."
msgstr "Lo había hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had earned a day of rest, and she was eager to take it."
msgstr "Se había ganado un día de descanso, y estaba ansiosa por tomarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had eaten about half her plate of food when she heard soft sounds coming down the hall."
msgstr "Sarah había comido aproximadamente la mitad de su plato cuando escuchó sonidos suaves provenir del pasillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had endured all of this so far...was she to stop it now? Waste all that she had sacrificed?"
msgstr "Hasta ahora había soportado todo esto... ¿debía detenerlo ahora? ¿Derrochar todo lo que había sacrificado?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had endured every humiliation."
msgstr "Había soportado cada humillación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had endured him so far. She could endure this too."
msgstr "Hasta ahora la había aguantado. Podía aguantar esto también."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had enjoyed the simplicity that came with housekeeping, but now she once again found her world filling with complexities."
msgstr "Había disfrutado de la simplicidad que conllevaba el aseo del hogar, pero ahora volvía a encontrar que su mundo se llenaba de complejidades."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had enough troubles in her life as it was, she didn't need to spend more worrying about magics and spirits."
msgstr "Ya tenía de sobra problemas en su vida, no necesitaba pasar más tiempo preocupándose por la magia y la brujería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had enough troubles, no need to add the troubles of others to her conscience."
msgstr "Tenía suficiente con sus problemas; no hacía falta añadir los ajenos a su conciencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had even been the one that betrayed him in the first place."
msgstr "Ella misma había sido la que lo traicionó en primer lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had expected Kate to be cynical, but she couldn't deny there was some truth to it."
msgstr "Había esperado que Kate fuera cínica, pero no podía negar que había algo de verdad en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had expected a ritual with more violence."
msgstr "Había esperado un ritual con más violencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had expected any manner of things, but this place was not one of them."
msgstr "Esperaba cualquier cosa, pero este lugar no era una de ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had expected that it would move her, but she had not expected to feel everything that she was now feeling."
msgstr "Había esperado que la afectara, pero no esperaba sentir todo lo que ahora sentía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had expected water, but instead, she found something surprising."
msgstr "Había esperado agua, pero en su lugar encontró algo sorprendente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had failed to gain her support. She would have to make sure the other votes were secured."
msgstr "No logró obtener su apoyo. Tendrá que asegurarse de que los demás votos estén garantizados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had failed to secure the support for her position."
msgstr "No había logrado conseguir el apoyo para su puesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had failed to secure the vote for her position."
msgstr "Falló en conseguir el voto para su cargo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had faith in her companions."
msgstr "Tenía fe en sus compañeros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had far more questions, but those would have to wait for another time."
msgstr "Tenía muchas más preguntas, pero aquellas tendrían que esperar para otra ocasión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had feared that he might learn or know of what had transpired before. That this might ruin her in his eyes."
msgstr "Tenía miedo de que él pudiera enterarse o saber lo que había sucedido antes, y eso podría arruinarla ante sus ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had feared that one of her soldiers might have been the cause of all this carnage."
msgstr "Temía que uno de sus soldados hubiera sido la causa de toda esa masacre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had feared this had been ruined to her by the violence of her own people, but she found in him all things inversed."
msgstr "Le había temido que esto le fuera arruinado por la violencia de su propio pueblo, pero en él halló todo lo opuesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had felt him inside of her enough to know that this was barely any of him. Already, the pain was too much."
msgstr "Ya había sentido su polla dentro de ella lo suficiente para saber que apenas era una fracción de él. El dolor ya era demasiado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had fought the cold for so long, she hardly realized just how close to death she had come."
msgstr "Luchó contra el frío durante tanto tiempo que apenas se dio cuenta de lo cerca del fin había estado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had found herself ever more protective of the girl ever since deciding on her course."
msgstr "Se había vuelto cada vez más protectora con la muchacha desde que decidió su camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had found the door that supposedly lead to the city. Nauyziri."
msgstr "Había encontrado la puerta que supuestamente conducía a la ciudad. Nauyziri."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had found the spirit to be a useful ally, but she was quickly losing her patience with the creature."
msgstr "Había encontrado al espíritu como una aliada útil, pero pronto estaba perdiendo la paciencia con la criatura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gained the votes, but was the price worth it?"
msgstr "¿Había conseguido los votos, pero valía la pena el precio?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given her body to him, even kissing him back."
msgstr "Le había entregado su cuerpo, e incluso lo había besado de vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given him a son."
msgstr "Le había dado un hijo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given him her body in turn, but she still felt constantly as though she fell short of what he gave her."
msgstr "A cambio, le había entregado su cuerpo, pero seguía sintiendo constantemente que no alcanzaba a lo que él le daba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given them a proper scare."
msgstr "Les habían dado un susto bien merecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given up any illusions that she was the first girl to find herself between his legs."
msgstr "Había abandonado cualquier ilusión de ser la primera chica en encontrarse entre sus piernas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had given up so much to gain it, made it her goal in life, and yet it never made her happy."
msgstr "Había sacrificado tanto para conseguirla, se había hecho su objetivo en la vida, y sin embargo nunca le trajo felicidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gone from sunbathing, enjoying the open seas, to letting herself be railed by the captain, and now she was tasked with deck scrubbing duty."
msgstr "Había pasado de tomar el sol y disfrutar del mar abierto a dejarse montar por el capitán, y ahora tenía asignada la tarea de limpiar el muelle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gone into town to take her mind off things, and the Captain was nothing if not a distraction."
msgstr "Sarah salió a la ciudad para distraerse de las cosas, y el Capitán no era más que una distracción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten more comfortable with being naked before others than she could have ever believed."
msgstr "Había logrado sentirse más cómoda desnuda ante los demás de lo que jamás habría creído posible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten most of the work done, but her encounter with Gilead still haunted her."
msgstr "Había terminado la mayor parte del trabajo, pero el encuentro con Gilead aún la atormentaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten the city, but at the expense of her dignity."
msgstr "Había conseguido la ciudad, pero a costa de su dignidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten the vote she came for, but she seemed hardly happy at that fact."
msgstr "Había conseguido el voto que había ido a buscar, pero parecía estar apenas contenta con ese hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten the vote she came for, though she was unsure of the cost."
msgstr "Había conseguido el voto que había buscado, aunque no estaba segura del precio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten wet, but there was only so much that could be done to accomodate orc's and their sizes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten what she came for, and paid little of a price for it."
msgstr "Obtuvo lo que vino a buscar y pagó muy poco precio por ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had gotten what she came for."
msgstr "Había conseguido lo que venía a buscar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had grown to fear this moment. The coming end of their training. Without this excuse to keep them together, would they be able to?"
msgstr "Había llegado a temer este momento. El final de su entrenamiento. Sin esta excusa para mantenerlos juntos, ¿serían capaces?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had grown up as the daughter of the King, and so every noble that ever came to castle Reinmeer was always polite and kind."
msgstr "Creció como la hija del Rey, y por ello cada noble que alguna vez llegó al castillo Reinmeer siempre fue cortés y amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had grown up in court, pretending the part of Princess until it came as second nature to her."
msgstr "Creció en la corte, fingiendo el papel de Princesa hasta que se convirtió en segunda naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had heard the wailing of those confided to the medical sleds. Thinking of putting Samayra among them, made her fearful."
msgstr "Había oído los lamentos de aquellos que habían sido entregados a las camillas médicas. El pensamiento de colocar a Samayra entre ellos la llenó de un terror abrumador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had held back, but at hearing Kate's order, Sarah relented."
msgstr "Sarah cedió al oír la orden de Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had her arms wrapped around his neck for balance, her head cocked back letting out repressed moans."
msgstr "Tenía los brazos enroscados alrededor de su cuello para mantener el equilibrio, la cabeza echada hacia atrás, dejando escapar gemidos reprimidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had her own fair share of trauma, but she never showed it."
msgstr "Tenía su propia cuota de trauma, pero nunca lo mostraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had her sword...she could fight the thing...but what would victory even look like?"
msgstr "Tenía su espada...podía luchar contra la cosa...¿pero qué aspecto tendría incluso la victoria?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had him where she wanted."
msgstr "Lo tenía donde quería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped a night's rest might give her some peace of mind, but his proposal was still all she could think about."
msgstr "Ella había esperado que una noche de descanso le otorgara cierta paz mental, pero su propuesta seguía siendo todo lo que podía pensar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped she could have been more subtle, but she had clearly worn her intentions on her face."
msgstr "Había esperado poder ser más sutil, pero claramente había dejado que sus intenciones se notaran en su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped the campire would make her feel warm."
msgstr "Había esperado que el campirano la hiciera sentir cálida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped to find an ally, but she should have known better than to expect to find one in a place like this."
msgstr "Había esperado encontrar un aliado, pero debería haber sabido mejor que esperar hallar uno en un lugar como este."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped to read the books on his behalf and give Thomas a summary so he could at least learn something."
msgstr "Esperaba leer los libros en su nombre y darle a Thomas un resumen para que al menos aprendiera algo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had hoped to sound strong, confident. Instead, her voice came out soft."
msgstr "Había esperado sonar fuerte, segura. En cambio, su voz salió suave."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had humiliated him, and now he enjoyed doing it back to her."
msgstr "Lo había humillado, y ahora disfrutaba humillándola a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had imagined she was alone, all her allies abandoned her, her family lost to her, but she now realized there were still those who cared for her..."
msgstr "Ella había imaginado estar sola, con todos sus aliados abandonándola y a su familia perdida para siempre, pero ahora comprendía que aún existían quienes la cuidaban..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had imagined to look up and find herself the center of some kind of attention."
msgstr "Ella había imaginado levantar la vista y encontrarse en el centro de algún tipo de atención."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had imagined, even during their brief affair, that she stood above him."
msgstr "Incluso durante su breve aventura, había imaginado que se situaba por encima de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had inherited Vaelen's fortune. Carolyn likely had more money still. She could spare such an expense."
msgstr "Había heredado la fortuna de Vaelen. Carolyn probablemente tenía aún más dinero. Podía permitirse tal gasto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had just begun her rounds when she noticed a man stride across the square towards her."
msgstr "Acababa de comenzar sus rondas cuando notó a un hombre cruzar la plaza hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had kept the bottle behind her back, but with her arms now crossed over her breasts, the bottle was exposed."
msgstr "Había mantenido la botella oculta tras su espalda, pero con los brazos ahora cruzados sobre sus pechos, el frasco quedaba expuesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had kept watch for most of the night, but she had failed to stay awake entirely."
msgstr "Ha vigilado la mayor parte de la noche, pero no ha logrado mantenerse despierta del todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had killed more, for lesser reasons."
msgstr "Había matado a más gente por razones menores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had killed the Beast."
msgstr "Ella había matado a la Bestia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known Vaelen for years, and he had always proven true. Promoted her, supported her."
msgstr "La conocía a Vaelen desde hacía años, y siempre había demostrado ser fiel. La promovió, la apoyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known Xan was old. Like all mages, he lived a long life, centuries she had imagined..."
msgstr "Sabía que Xan era viejo. Como todos los magos, vivía una larga vida, siglos que había imaginado..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known for a while that they had been drawing closer to Al'Gahaem, the sounds of the city had been carried on the wind, meeting them as they neared the city."
msgstr "Ya lo sabía desde hace un tiempo: estaban acercándose a Al'Gahaem, los sonidos de la ciudad llegaban arrastrados por el viento y les recibían conforme se aproximaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known him for hardly any time at all. To be speaking of marriage felt absurd."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known him long enough. His family was one of the oldest and most important families on Rosanna."
msgstr "La había conocido lo suficiente. Su familia era una de las más antiguas e importantes de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known the girl for barely a moment, and to her surprise, began to see so much of herself in her."
msgstr "La conocía apenas un instante y, para su sorpresa, comenzó a ver en ella tanto de sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known the killing that would come, and she had accepted that bargain long ago."
msgstr "Ella había conocido el asesinato que vendría y había aceptado ese pacto hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had known they were something other than human, but she had never exactly known their nature."
msgstr "Había sabido que eran algo más que humanos, pero nunca había conocido exactamente su naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had learned by watching, now she would have to show him was she had learned."
msgstr "Ahora tendría que mostrárselo a él, todo lo que había aprendido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had learned her lesson when it came to asking the Daemon anything."
msgstr "Había aprendido su lección cuando se trataba de preguntar al Daemon cualquier cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had learned only enough to begin to understand how little she really knew."
msgstr "Solo había aprendido lo suficiente para empezar a comprender cuánto ignoraba realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had learned the ways of his body, as he had learned hers."
msgstr "Había aprendido las formas de su cuerpo, así como él había aprendido las suyas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had let everyone down, including herself."
msgstr "Había decepcionado a todos, incluso a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had let him fuck her in her dreams, the least she could do was deny him hearing her in reality."
msgstr "Hacía que él la follara en sus sueños, y lo menos que podía hacer era negarle oírla en la realidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had let the bottle slip in a moment of panic, and Belmont had caught it again."
msgstr "Había dejado caer la botella en un momento de pánico, y Belmont la había atrapado nuevamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lived for herself for so long, and lost so much, that she had come to believe that love would forever lost to her."
msgstr "Había vivido por sí misma durante tanto tiempo y perdido tanto, que llegó a creer que el amor le había sido arrebatado para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lived most of her life in the capital of Rosanna, which to her had appeared a large city."
msgstr "Había vivido la mayor parte de su vida en la capital de Rosanna, que para ella había parecido una gran ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had long ceased to be a Princess, but only now did she truly kill that part of herself."
msgstr "Hace mucho tiempo dejó de ser una Princesa, pero solo ahora es cuando realmente mató esa parte de sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had long lost track of time when they finally came upon the camp."
msgstr "Había perdido la noción del tiempo desde hacía mucho cuando finalmente encontraron el campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lost any sense of direction when the orcs captured them, now, she was entirely lost."
msgstr "Perdió la orientación cuando los orcos la capturaron; ahora, estaba completamente perdida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lost consciousness at some point, though she couldn't recall when."
msgstr "En algún momento había perdido el conocimiento, aunque no recordaba cuándo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lost everything, she concluded."
msgstr "Todo lo había perdido, concluyó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lost so much blood, her gown was nearly all red, sticking to her body."
msgstr "Había perdido tanta sangre que su vestido estaba casi todo rojo, pegado a su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had lost the bet. All this had been for nothing…you’re an idiot, she thought to herself. The captain disgusted her, and yet, she had still found herself right back here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had loved today. Meeting someone like Nick had made her believe that her life wouldn't be an endless tragedy."
msgstr "La había amado hoy. Conocer a alguien como Nick le hizo creer que su vida no sería una tragedia interminable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made a small mistake, and now, she had found herself here."
msgstr "Hizo un pequeño error y ahora se encontró aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made fun of him for it. She had even thought to make fun of the silly girls that fell for his charm."
msgstr "Se había burlado de él por ello. Incluso había pensado burlarse de las niñas tontas que se dejaban engañar por su encanto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made her decisison to attend the Union Council, but there was so much more to do."
msgstr "Había tomado la decisión de asistir al Consejo de la Unión, pero había mucho más por hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made it."
msgstr "Lo logró."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made peace because in her heart she knew this was but a moment in her life. There would be a next phase to her life, she just knew it..."
msgstr "Había hecho la paz porque en su corazón sabía que esto era solo un momento en su vida. Habría una siguiente fase en su vida, lo sabía..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made peace, as far she could, with her condition."
msgstr "Había hecho las paces, tanto como podía, con su condición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made the food, didn't that mean she deserved to at least eat some of it? How long could they make her live off that disgusting gruel?"
msgstr "¿Había preparado la comida, ¿no significaba eso que merecía al menos comer algo de ella? ¿Cuánto tiempo podían hacerla vivir de ese repugnante puré?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made this choice, for herself and her friends. She would see it through."
msgstr "Ella había tomado esta decisión, por sí misma y por sus amigas. La vería a través."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had magic. Resources. Power."
msgstr "Tenía magia. Recursos. Poder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to avoid the Khan's grasp only days earlier...was it all for nothing?"
msgstr "¿Había logrado esquivar el agarre del Khan apenas días antes... ¿había sido todo en vano?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to eat no more than two spoonfuls when she felt a small rock hitting her body."
msgstr "Solo había logrado comer dos cucharadas cuando sintió que una pequeña piedra impactaba su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to escape him in the alley all those years ago, only for her to now end up down on her knees in front of him, as if it had made no difference."
msgstr "Logró escapar de él en el callejón hace tantos años, solo para terminar ahora arrodillada frente a él, como si nada hubiera cambiado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to secure her first victory by securing the support for her position."
msgstr "Logró asegurar su primera victoria al conseguir el apoyo para su puesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to secure her victory by securing the votes for her position."
msgstr "Logró asegurar su victoria al conseguir los votos para su posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to secure the most important victory of all."
msgstr "Logró asegurar la victoria más importante de todas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had managed to stifle her moans earlier by using Sakar's cock, but as she came, there was no hiding it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had many teachers growing up, experts in all fields. A princess was expected to be well educated."
msgstr "Tenía muchas maestras desde niña, expertas en todas las disciplinas. Se esperaba que una princesa estuviera bien educada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had met Sarah was a princess, and they had managed to forge a bond despite that fact. True friends."
msgstr "Ella había conocido a Sarah, que era una princesa, y lograron forjar un lazo a pesar de ese hecho. Verdaderas amigas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had miscalculated Maeiv's interests."
msgstr "Sarah había calculado mal los intereses de Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had moaned for him like a whore. She could hardly play the maiden now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had mocked him at times, for his low birth and low learning."
msgstr "A veces lo había burlado por su baja cuna y su escasa instrucción."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never been cruel or even mean to the servants, not in the way that some nobles did."
msgstr "Nunca había sido cruel ni siquiera maledicente con los sirvientes, no como lo hacían algunos nobles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never been raised for anything other than the life of a princess."
msgstr "Nunca había sido criada para nada más que la vida de una princesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never been the best at this, and the result showed."
msgstr "Nunca había sido la mejor en esto, y el resultado lo demostraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never been this naked in front of a man in all her life."
msgstr "Nunca había estado tan desnuda frente a un hombre en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never been to this place before, and yet every step she took felt obvious."
msgstr "Nunca había estado en este lugar antes, y sin embargo cada paso que daba parecía obvio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never before experienced him, or anyone, so utterly."
msgstr "Nunca antes había experimentado a él, o a nadie, de tal manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never considered that there were people out there for whom slavery could be seen as an improvement in their life."
msgstr "Nunca había considerado que existieran personas para quienes la esclavitud pudiera ser vista como una mejora en su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never considered the basic fact that there might be other keys in the world."
msgstr "Nunca había considerado el hecho básico de que podrían existir otras llaves en el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never contemplated that they'd do the same with the males."
msgstr "Nunca había contemplado que hicieran lo mismo con los hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never dared to dream that delivering this carnage to her enemies, could feel so good."
msgstr "Nunca se había atrevido a soñar que entregar esta carnicería a sus enemigos pudiera sentirse tan bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never felt anything like this."
msgstr "Nunca había sentido nada así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never felt closer to herself, nor to anyone other than Alaric."
msgstr "Nunca se había sentido tan cerca de sí misma, ni de nadie más que de Alaric."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never fully realized just how trivial her homeland had been in the grand design of the world."
msgstr "Nunca había comprendido realmente cuán trivial era su tierra natal en el gran diseño del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never given this part of herself up to him, nor had she planned too..."
msgstr "Ella nunca había cedido esta parte de sí misma a él, ni tampoco lo había planeado demasiado..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never gone hungry in her life."
msgstr "Nunca había conocido la hambruna en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never had friends to talk about this sort of stuff before."
msgstr "Nunca había tenido amigas con las que hablar de este tipo de cosas antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never held a sword in all her life."
msgstr "Nunca había sostenido una espada en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never imagined that operating a sewing machine would be so complicated."
msgstr "Nunca había imaginado que operar una máquina de coser fuera tan complicado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never known the meaning of the word busy before now."
msgstr "Nunca había conocido el significado de la palabra ocupada hasta ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never known this city before. Never known its people. And still, there was a kind of universal sadness in this place."
msgstr "Nunca había conocido esta ciudad antes. Nunca había conocido a su gente. Y aún así, había una especie de tristeza universal en este lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never met a Noctori before, a member of the Eternal Court."
msgstr "Nunca había conocido a un Noctori antes, miembro de la Corte Eterna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never met either before, though she had exchanged the occasional letter in manners of state."
msgstr "Nunca había conocido a ninguno de ellos antes, aunque habían intercambiado cartas ocasionales por cortesía de estado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never much cared for this city, but even this place could be beautiful."
msgstr "Nunca le había importado mucho esta ciudad, pero incluso aquí se podía encontrar belleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never quite managed to figure out what they were to each other."
msgstr "Nunca había logrado del todo entender qué eran para sí mismos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never run so fast in all her life."
msgstr "Nunca había corrido tan rápido en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never said it aloud, but it was the truth."
msgstr "Nunca lo había dicho en voz alta, pero era la verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never seen a room this vast in all of her life."
msgstr "Nunca había visto una habitación tan vasta en toda su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never seen anything like this in her life, and imagined she never would again if she ever left this place."
msgstr "Nunca había visto nada como esto en toda su vida, y temía que jamás volvería a ver algo así si alguna vez abandonaba aquel lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never seen the orc so vulnerable."
msgstr "Nunca había visto al orco tan vulnerable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never seen this room before, but she instantly recognized it from her youth."
msgstr "Nunca había visto esta habitación antes, pero la reconoció al instante de su juventud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never tasted anything quite like this."
msgstr "Nunca había probado nada igual."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never thought that perhaps her plans could change."
msgstr "Nunca había pensado que quizás sus planes podrían cambiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had never wanted his role, had always served faithfully and given her honest advice."
msgstr "Nunca había deseado su papel; siempre le había servido fielmente y ofrecido sus consejos sinceros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no allies left in this city, thrown out by the mercenary company."
msgstr "No tenía aliados en esta ciudad, expulsada por la compañía mercenaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no cause to know one way or another, and yet, one some level she could not imagine he wasn't still out there."
msgstr "No tenía motivo para saberlo de una u otra manera, y sin embargo, en algún nivel que no podía imaginar, seguía estando ahí fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no choice but to follow him or be left naked on the streets."
msgstr "No tenía más remedio que seguirlo o quedarse desnuda en las calles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubt she could siege Calshure. Take the city by force."
msgstr "No tenía la menor duda de que podía asediar Calshure. Tomar la ciudad por la fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubt someone could hear them, but she was beyond caring."
msgstr "No dudaba de que alguien pudiera oírlos, pero ya no importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubt that he had fostered some affection for her."
msgstr "No tenía la menor duda de que él había cultivado algún afecto por ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubt that if Marion had won, Maeiv would have called him a dear and loyal friend."
msgstr "No tenía duda de que, si Marion hubiera ganado, Maeiv lo habría llamado un querido y leal amigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubt that the others would all be eager to put themselves up first."
msgstr "No tenía duda de que los demás estarían ansiosos por colocarse primero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubts of their intentions."
msgstr "No tenía dudas de sus intenciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no doubts that she could never do it. But Marius seemed unfazed by it."
msgstr "No tenía la menor duda de que nunca podría hacerlo, pero Marius parecía estar completamente tranquilo ante ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no idea how big this place was, and she wanted to be sure she could find her way back."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea de qué tan grande era ese lugar, y quería estar segura de poder encontrar el camino de vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no idea how long they had been there in that alley."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea de cuánto tiempo habían estado allí en ese callejón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no idea of the strength of the weapon, but she was certain that she didn't want to be near it when it went off."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea de la potencia del arma, pero estaba segura de que no quería estar cerca cuando explotara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no idea what this was about, yet she could not help but feel as if there was danger, somewhere."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea de qué se trataba todo esto, sin embargo no podía evitar sentir que había peligro, por algún lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no idea where it would be safe or not."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea de dónde sería seguro o no."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no illusions about the Beast's desires."
msgstr "No tenía ilusiones sobre los deseos de la Bestia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no illusions he'd be content to just sleep."
msgstr "No tenía ilusiones de que se conformara con solo dormir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no illusions that this was a first time for Atilla."
msgstr "Narradora: No tenía la menor duda de que esto no era su primera vez con Atilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no illusions what would happen if she fell into the hands of an orc warband."
msgstr "No tenía ilusiones sobre lo que le ocurriría si caía en manos de una banda de orcos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no money to speak of. Only a few skills to work a ship, but she was far from an experienced deck hand."
msgstr "No tenía dinero que valiera la pena. Solo unas pocas habilidades para trabajar en un barco, pero estaba lejos de ser marinera experimentada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no money. No allies to take her away. Not even a home that belonged to her."
msgstr "No tenía dinero. No tenía aliados que la llevaran lejos. Ni siquiera un hogar que le perteneciera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no shame left to her. Not with him."
msgstr "No tenía nada de vergüenza con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had no way of truly knowing if she was pregnant, but she found herself wishing profoundly that she was."
msgstr "No tenía forma de saber realmente si estaba embarazada, pero se encontró deseando profundamente que lo estuviera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been able to put off opening it much longer."
msgstr "No había podido posponer más tiempo abrirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been beaten like this in...perhaps ever."
msgstr "Nunca la habían golpeado así... tal vez nunca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been here before yet, and she didn’t know what came next. The man holding her chain made no impression to care for her, neither kindly nor cruelly."
msgstr "Nunca había estado aquí antes y no sabía qué vendría después. El hombre que sostenía su cadena no daba señales de importarse por ella, ni con amabilidad ni con crueldad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been prepared for him, much less his skill."
msgstr "No había estado preparada para él, ni mucho menos para su destreza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been the only one to realize this was one of the last ships to depart."
msgstr "No había sido la única en darse cuenta de que este era uno de los últimos barcos a partir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been this close to him since the uprising began, and yet, when she saw the fortress, she lost all hope that she would ever see him again."
msgstr "No había estado tan cerca de él desde que comenzó la rebelión, y sin embargo, al ver la fortaleza, perdió toda esperanza de volver a verlo jamás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not been whipped in some of these places, but Sarah was eager for the relief and not about to object."
msgstr "No había sido azotada en algunos de esos lugares, pero Sarah ansiaba el alivio y no iba a oponerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not cried out as she knew Belmont would have wanted her to."
msgstr "No había gritado como Belmont habría deseado que lo hiciera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not fled, not intentionally, but people might very well read her actions as such."
msgstr "No huyó, no intencionalmente, pero la gente podría interpretar sus acciones de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not imagined it would come down to this."
msgstr "No había imaginado que llegara a esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not moved at all."
msgstr "No se había movido en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not seen the actual fall of her beloved homeland, but she imagined that experiencing it as Samayra had was likely even more traumatic."
msgstr "No había visto la caída real de su amada patria, pero imaginaba que experimentarla como Samayra debía ser aún más traumático."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not the energy to speak words, nor the mind to formulate any."
msgstr "No tenía la energía para articular palabras, ni la mente para formular ninguna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had noticed that Kate was likely drunk, given her disheveled appearance, but if her looks didn't give it away, the smell did."
msgstr "Había notado que Kate probablemente estaba borracha, dado su aspecto desaliñado, pero si su apariencia no lo delataba, el olor sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had offended him with her offer of a handout, she understood that now. His bruised ego demanded repayment."
msgstr "Ahora comprendía que lo había ofendido con su oferta de ayuda; su ego herido exigía una compensación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had offered herself up. She would have to follow through."
msgstr "Se había ofrecido a sí misma. Tendría que cumplir su palabra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had offered it to him, sure enough, but now the promise suddenly felt very real."
msgstr "Se lo había ofrecido a él, efectivamente, pero ahora la promesa de repente se sentía muy real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had offered the man help, but she had imagined something more limited than this."
msgstr "Había ofrecido al hombre ayuda, pero había imaginado algo más limitado que esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had often prayed that her father might look down on her and be proud of who she had become, but now she prayed that he would look away from her. She could not bear the idea of him watching her do this."
msgstr "A menudo había orado porque su padre la mirara desde arriba y se enorgulleciera de quien había llegado a ser, pero ahora rezaba para que apartara la vista de ella. No podía soportar la idea de que él la observara mientras lo hacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had often taken Sarah along to the chapel when she was still small, teaching her all the names of the Pantheon."
msgstr "Suelo llevar a Sarah a la capilla cuando aún era pequeña, enseñándole todos los nombres del Panteón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only her own support. Edmond held two votes. Antonio was not the kind of man she wanted to be begging for support."
msgstr "Solo contaba con su propio apoyo. Edmond tenía dos votos. Antonio no era el tipo de hombre al que ella quisiera suplicar apoyo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just adjusted her position when Belmont hooked his foot around her ankle."
msgstr "Acababa de ajustar su posición cuando Belmont encajó el pie alrededor de su tobillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just arrived in the city, but it seemed this Gilead knew nearly everything."
msgstr "Acababa de llegar a la ciudad, pero parecía que este Gilead sabía casi todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just begun."
msgstr "Solo acababa de comenzar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just finished when she now found herself close to the edge again."
msgstr "Solo acababa de terminar cuando se encontró nuevamente cerca del borde."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just managed to find the courage to leave Lethram, and now this stranger was all but forcing her back."
msgstr "Acababa apenas de encontrar el valor para abandonar Lethram, y ahora este extraño la empujaba de vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just stumbled inside when she felt his hands on her hips."
msgstr "Acababa de tropezar al entrar cuando sintió sus manos en su cintura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had only just thrown the letter back when she heard a noise."
msgstr "Acababa de lanzar la carta cuando escuchó un ruido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had packed up her things more quickly than Sarah had expected."
msgstr "Sarah había recogido sus cosas con más rapidez de lo que ella esperaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had promised to meet with him in the royal forest after the battle."
msgstr "Había prometido encontrarse con él en el bosque real después de la batalla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had punished herself plenty in her life for her desires as she grew older."
msgstr "Se había castigado a sí misma con frecuencia en su vida por sus deseos mientras crecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had pushed it too far."
msgstr "Llevó las cosas demasiado lejos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had put herself upon this path to forget the painful memories of her home, but she now found her mind drifting to Rosanna more than ever."
msgstr "Se había puesto en este camino para olvidar los recuerdos dolorosos de su hogar, pero ahora sentía que su mente se desviaba hacia Rosanna más que nunca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had put it all off as long as she could."
msgstr "Lo había pospuesto todo lo que pudo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had quietly sneaked out of bed, leaving Samayra to get a few extra hours of sleep."
msgstr "Se había colado silenciosamente de la cama, dejando a Samayra para que durmiera unas horas extra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had read enough books and other texts by now, but nothing compared to the real practice of it."
msgstr "Ya había leído suficientes libros y otros textos hasta ahora, pero nada se compara con la práctica real de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had read enough history, and been lectured enough by her father on what happened to cities that were looted. And to the women in them."
msgstr "Había leído bastante historia y había recibido suficientes lecciones de su padre sobre lo que sucede a las ciudades saqueadas y a las mujeres que habitan en ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had read the reports, but to see the fortress was something else. Its vast size made her feel small."
msgstr "Había leído los informes, pero ver la fortaleza era otra cosa. Su vasta magnitud la hacía sentirse pequeña."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had remembered nearly nothing, and still fumbled with every swing of her blade. The truth was that she couldn't focus."
msgstr "Había recordado casi nada y aún torpeaba con cada estocada de su espada. La verdad es que no podía concentrarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had resisted him by staying quiet, she could not resist the captain too much. She still relied on him for work, shelter, a chance to learn how to sail the world."
msgstr "La había resistido callándose, pero no podía resistir al capitán demasiado tiempo. Todavía dependía de él para el trabajo, el refugio y la oportunidad de aprender a navegar el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had resisted him."
msgstr "Se había resistido a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had revealed a weakness to him, and now he pounced on it."
msgstr "Reveló una debilidad ante él, y ahora él se lanzó sobre ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had run away for a reason, and that meant never looking back."
msgstr "Huyó por una razón, y eso significaba nunca mirar atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had sacrificed her dignity the moment she had proposed them...she would not stop now."
msgstr "Había sacrificado su dignidad en el momento en que se lo propuso... no iba a detenerse ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had said it without even really thinking about it."
msgstr "Lo había dicho sin ni siquiera pensarlo realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had saved the girl from the hordes of soldiers, or at least she had told herself that's what she had done."
msgstr "Había salvado a la chica de las hordas de soldados, o al menos se había dicho que eso era lo que había hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had secured his support, that was all she needed from him."
msgstr "Había asegurado su apoyo, eso era todo lo que necesitaba de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had secured his vote, and she had not even had to compromise herself."
msgstr "Había asegurado su voto, y ni siquiera tuvo que comprometerse a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had secured the vote for her position."
msgstr "Había asegurado el voto para su puesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen desire. Contempt. Now she saw something new in there."
msgstr "Había visto deseo. Desdén. Ahora veía algo nuevo en su interior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen far more than she wanted to already."
msgstr "Ya había visto mucho más de lo que deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen her brother shortly before he left for the battlefield. He had looked more like a child playing at being a soldier than a real soldier. Then again, perhaps that was what he was."
msgstr "La había visto poco antes de que partiera para el campo de batalla. Parecía más un niño jugando a ser soldado que un soldado de verdad. Sin embargo, quizás eso era lo que realmente era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen him look at her before."
msgstr "Ya lo había visto mirar antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen it before, but feeling him inside of her mouth was another."
msgstr "Ya lo había visto antes, pero sentirlo dentro de su boca era otra cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen many sides of Belmont since the day she first met him, but despite everything, he could still surprise her."
msgstr "Ha visto muchas facetas de Belmont desde que lo conoció por primera vez, pero a pesar de todo, aún puede sorprenderla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen plenty of the world and the cruel men in it."
msgstr "Había visto bastante del mundo y de los hombres crueles que lo habitan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen the damage that even Sigmund alone could inflict."
msgstr "Había visto el daño que incluso Sigmund solo podía infligir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen the orc, only for a moment, but he had made an impression on her."
msgstr "La había visto al orco, solo por un momento, pero él había dejado una impresión en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen this one up on the hill with the others..."
msgstr "La había visto a ella en la colina con los demás..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had seen what these creatures could do at Lethram, and she knew that she alone couldn't stop them."
msgstr "Había visto qué podían hacer estas criaturas en Lethram, y sabía que ella sola no podía detenerlas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had served him, more than once by now."
msgstr "Ya le había servido, más de una vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had set he sights on Rahayal. The city had sat at the end of the road for so long, her final destination."
msgstr "Había puesto su mira en Rahayal. La ciudad había permanecido al final del camino durante tanto tiempo, su destino final."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had simply done as he had instructed her."
msgstr "Hacía exactamente lo que él le había ordenado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had slept as well as could be hoped on a mattress, naked, out on the streets of a city she barely knew."
msgstr "Ha dormido tan bien como se podía esperar sobre un colchón, desnuda, al aire libre en las calles de una ciudad que apenas conocía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had slung a shield along the side of her horse in case anyone would try to fire an arrow at her, though she doubted anyone would be that dishonorable."
msgstr "Había colgado un escudo a lo largo del costado de su caballo por si alguien intentaba dispararle una flecha, aunque dudaba que alguien fuera tan deshonesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had smelled this before."
msgstr "La había olido antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had so many questions for him. So many things she wanted to ask him."
msgstr "Tenía tantas preguntas para él. Había tantas cosas que quería preguntarle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had so nearly given herself to the soldiers, but he had risked his life to save her."
msgstr "Casi se entregaba a los soldados, pero él arriesgó su vida para salvarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had sold her body to him, but now realized she had sold all the rest of herself along with it."
msgstr "Vendió su cuerpo a él, pero ahora comprendía que había vendido también todo lo demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had some money, and now a place to stay, but she knew she didn't really have all that much."
msgstr "Tenía algo de dinero y ahora un lugar donde quedarse, pero sabía que no tenía realmente tanto como creía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had sought out a distraction from her work."
msgstr "Buscó una distracción para su trabajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spend most the day studying."
msgstr "Sarah había pasado la mayor parte del día estudiando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spend quite number of days on the ship when she first made the crossing to Lethram."
msgstr "Había pasado bastantes días en el barco cuando hizo por primera vez la travesía hacia Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spend so much time doubting herself, questioning if this was the right thing to do."
msgstr "Pasó tanto tiempo dudando de sí misma, preguntándose si esto era lo correcto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spend years in this house, and over the course of it, she had come to know it like a maze."
msgstr "Pasó años en esta casa y, con el paso del tiempo, llegó a conocerla como un laberinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spoken of those with nobody, not even Thomas."
msgstr "Había hablado de aquellos sin nadie, ni siquiera con Thomas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spoken to Lily, but no reply would come."
msgstr "Había hablado con Lily, pero no recibiría respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spoken to Naydeen a few times now, but suddenly the energy in the room appeared very different. Charged."
msgstr "Había hablado con Naydeen unas cuantas veces, pero de repente la energía en la habitación parecía muy diferente. Cargada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had spoken with seasoned soldiers who had never seen a mage in more than a decade of soldiering."
msgstr "Había hablado con soldados veteranos que nunca habían visto a una maga en más de una década de servicio militar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had started in the corner, working her way towards the end of the room, when she slid her duster across a series of glass containers at the back."
msgstr "Comenzó en la esquina, avanzando hacia el fondo de la habitación, hasta que deslizó su gabardina sobre una serie de recipientes de vidrio situados al final."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stayed, and now she would have to carry this with her."
msgstr "Se quedó allí, y ahora tendría que cargar con esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stepped into his bed, simply because she wanted to."
msgstr "Había entrado en su cama, simplemente porque lo deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had still been half dreaming from her encounter with Sigmund the night before."
msgstr "Aún estaba medio dormida por el encuentro con Sigmund la noche anterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stood off to the side, watching recruit after recruit apply."
msgstr "Se había mantenido al margen, observando cómo uno tras otro solicitaban la admisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stood up for herself, and more importantly, Nick. For the first time she hadn't let the captain walk all over her."
msgstr "Se había defendido a sí misma, y, más importante aún, a Nick. Por primera vez, no había permitido que el capitán la pisoteara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stumbled on some small intersection in the maze of streets."
msgstr "Se había topado con una pequeña intersección en el laberinto de calles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had stumbled to the ground, tears forming in her eyes."
msgstr "Se había deslizado hasta el suelo, y las lágrimas comenzaban a formarse en sus ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had submitted herself to Atilla's excercises and training regiments. In turn, her body had transformed itself in the months since."
msgstr "Se había sometido a los ejercicios y regímenes de entrenamiento de Atilla. A cambio, su cuerpo se había transformado durante los meses siguientes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had suspected that the appetites of men receded in age, but that had proven very wrong."
msgstr "Había sospechado que los apetitos de los hombres menguaban con la edad, pero eso había resultado ser muy falso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had swung the blade, and still, she wondered at what she had done."
msgstr "Lanzó el cuchillo y, aun así, dudaba de lo que había hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had taken a small sip at first, but now, she was eager to relieve her thirst, and the drink wasn't unpleasant."
msgstr "Al principio solo tomó un pequeño sorbo, pero ahora ansiaba saciar su sed y la bebida no era desagradable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had taken him has far as she could manage, and still, she knew there were inches of him left."
msgstr "Lo había tomado tan lejos como pudo, y aún así sabía que quedaban pulgadas de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had taken no more than a few steps before she could hear gravel cracking against metal boots."
msgstr "No había dado más de unos pocos pasos cuando escuchó el crujir del gravillero contra sus botas metálicas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had tasted him so much...had him inside of her...moaned for him..."
msgstr "Lo había saboreado tanto... lo tenía dentro de ella... gemía por él..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had teased him in the desert, serviced him with her mouth at the auction house, but now he would have this part of her too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had the benefit of the House."
msgstr "Tenía la ventaja de la Casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had the duke's vote, but the price of it, she might forever regret."
msgstr "Tenía el voto del duque, pero el precio de ello podría lamentarlo para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had the heart of a conqueror, but that did not mean she was fit for a throne. Fit to rule."
msgstr "Tenía el corazón de un conquistador, pero eso no significaba que fuera apta para un trono. Apta para gobernar."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "She had the money that he left us, but looking back, I think she would have gladly given it all away if it meant never meeting the bastard in the first place."
msgstr "Tenía el dinero que él nos dejó, pero mirando hacia atrás, creo que habría dado todo con gusto si eso significara nunca haber conocido al bastardo en primer lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had the strongest army out of all of them, and she would be a fool to give up such an advantage."
msgstr "Tenía el ejército más fuerte de todos ellos, y sería una tonta si abandonara tal ventaja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought Sakar's only intentions were with her and her body, but unexpectedly, he seemed to be honouring his previous obligation."
msgstr "Ella había pensado que las únicas intenciones de Sakar eran con ella y su cuerpo, pero inesperadamente, parecía estar honrando su obligación anterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought before that the creature violated all of her, but only now did she understand what that really meant."
msgstr "Antes había pensado que la criatura violaba a todas, pero solo ahora entendió lo que eso realmente significaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought herself above Nick in the hierarchy of the ship, but the truth was that his torment would pass."
msgstr "Creía estar por encima de Nick en la jerarquía del barco, pero la verdad es que su tortura pasaría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought it many times, this was the first time anyone said it out loud. Even herself."
msgstr "Lo había pensado muchas veces; esta fue la primera vez que alguien lo dijo en voz alta. Incluso ella misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought of Alfred as a harmless old man, kindly even."
msgstr "La había pensado como un anciano inocente, incluso amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought of all the things she would have done to this man all those years ago."
msgstr "Había pensado en todas las cosas que habría hecho con este hombre hace tantos años."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought of escaping this world, back to her own."
msgstr "Había pensado en escapar de este mundo, volver a la suya propia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought she was willing to do anything for his aid, but this..."
msgstr "Había pensado que estaba dispuesta a hacer cualquier cosa por su ayuda, pero esto..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had thought they had made it down the mountain at least."
msgstr "Había pensado que al menos habían logrado bajar de la montaña."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to be careful. Not too eager."
msgstr "Tenía que tener cuidado. No demasiado ansiosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to do so much, in a way, it spared her from dealing with her grief."
msgstr "Tenía que hacer tanto, de cierto modo, lo cual le ahorraba enfrentar su dolor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to escape from this place. But how..."
msgstr "Tenía que escapar de este lugar. Pero cómo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to escape, but in the midsts of this madness, it had become hard to tell which direction was even safe."
msgstr "Tenía que huir, pero en medio de esta locura, había dejado de ser posible discernir siquiera qué dirección era segura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to escape. Use her magic."
msgstr "Tenía que huir. Usar su magia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to get back to them. She had to help them. Help them before-"
msgstr "Tenía que volver con ellos. Tenía que ayudarlos. Ayudarlos antes de—"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to get off the streets..."
msgstr "Tenía que salir de la calle..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to get out of here."
msgstr "Tenía que salir de aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to go outside. Lower the bucket, raise it with the winch. Carry it back, full of water, making sure not to spill any."
msgstr "Tenía que salir al exterior. Bajar el cubo, subirlo con la grúa. Llevárselo de vuelta, lleno de agua, asegurándose de no derramar ni una gota."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to half laugh as she said it."
msgstr "Tuvía que reír a medias al decirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to help him, if only to make sure he would not get hurt."
msgstr "Tenía que ayudarlo, aunque fuera solo para asegurarse de que no se hiciera daño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to keep her momentum. Continue to march on the Capital as soon as possible."
msgstr "Tenía que mantener su impulso. Marchar sobre la Capital lo antes posible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to keep herself from thinking of this as her room, rather than her prison, lest she forget what it was."
msgstr "Tenía que evitar pensar en esto como su habitación y no como su prisión, por si acaso olvidaba de qué se trataba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to laugh as she walked through it."
msgstr "Tuvo que reír mientras caminaba por ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to make a decision."
msgstr "Tenía que tomar una decisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to make her next moves carefully, but equally knew she could not lean back and wait things out."
msgstr "Tuvo que planear sus siguientes movimientos con cuidado, pero también sabía que no podía quedarse quieta esperando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to make the most of her time here, and Sarah was eager not to waste a moment of it."
msgstr "Tenía que aprovechar al máximo su tiempo aquí, y Sarah estaba ansiosa por no perder ni un instante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to open it. To know...to understand..."
msgstr "Tenía que abrirla. Para saber... para comprender..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to pace herself to keep herself from gagging on it."
msgstr "Tenía que moderar su propio ritmo para no vomitárselo todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to push back, not let her get the better of her."
msgstr "Tenía que resistirse, no dejar que ella la ganara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to remind herself of the dangers that this place posed. Even behind the smiling faces."
msgstr "Tenía que recordarse de los peligros que este lugar encerraba. Incluso detrás de las sonrisas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to remind herself, because the object seemed to almost reach out to her, begging to be seized."
msgstr "Tenía que recordárselo a sí misma, porque el objeto parecía casi alcanzarla, suplicando ser agarrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to squint her eyes to block out the stinging sunlight."
msgstr "Tenía que entrecerrar los ojos para bloquear el sol punzante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had to wrestle her way through the masses of people."
msgstr "Tenía que abrirse paso entre la multitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had told them the story a hundred times, if not more, and by now they could all dream every letter of it."
msgstr "Ya les había contado la historia cien veces, si no más, y ahora todos podían soñar con cada letra de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had too many thoughts running through her mind to sleep."
msgstr "Tenía demasiados pensamientos dando vueltas por su cabeza para poder dormir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had tricked him, or tried to at least, and he had done nothing to deserve such dishonesty from her."
msgstr "La había engañado, o al menos había intentado hacerlo, y él no merecía tal deshonestidad por su parte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had tried on nearly fifty plants."
msgstr "Había probado casi cincuenta plantas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had tried to play it confident. Act as though she had any power, but she had none."
msgstr "Había intentado aparentar confianza. Actuar como si tuviera algún poder, pero no lo tenía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had trouble seeing Marius that way. His father though..."
msgstr "Le resultaba difícil ver a Marius de esa manera. Su padre, sin embargo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had truly never seen anything like the raw nature of this place."
msgstr "Nunca había visto nada tan crudo como la naturaleza de este lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had trusted him, and instead, she had now been given to him as some prized livestock, his slave."
msgstr "Había confiado en él, y ahora, en su lugar, se le había entregado a él como ganado precioso, su esclava."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had underestimated just how heavy a burden Thomas had carried, and how heavy that burden now weighed on her."
msgstr "Había subestimado cuánto peso cargaba Thomas y cuán pesado era ese mismo peso ahora sobre ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had waited a lifetime for someone she never knew to expect."
msgstr "Ella había esperado toda una vida a alguien que nunca imaginó que esperaría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had walked for a few minutes down the road."
msgstr "Había caminado por el camino durante unos minutos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had wanted a new life, and against all odds, had gotten a chance at it. She had to forget the past. Learn to let it go."
msgstr "Quería una nueva vida y, contra toda probabilidad, había conseguido la oportunidad de tenerla. Tenía que olvidar el pasado. Aprender a dejarlo ir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had wanted more, but she was too fearful that she might lose it, and give away the fact that she had been watching."
msgstr "Quería más, pero el miedo a perderlo y a delatar que había estado vigilando la paralizaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had wanted to go fast, learn as much as she could, and that would demand more of her than she had ever been asked to offer up."
msgstr "Ella había deseado avanzar con rapidez, aprender todo lo posible, y eso exigía de ella mucho más de lo que jamás se le hubiera pedido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had wanted to go out into the forest with Kate."
msgstr "Había querido ir al bosque con Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had watched him spar with each of the previous participants. He didn't seem to have even begun to break a sweat."
msgstr "La había visto esgrimirse con cada uno de los participantes anteriores. No parecía haber empezado a sudar siquiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had won Maeiv's support, yes she found herself oddly confused by how easy it had been."
msgstr "Había ganado el apoyo de Maeiv, sí, y se sentía extrañamente confundida por lo fácil que había sido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had won her first true victory in the war."
msgstr "Había logrado su primera verdadera victoria en la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had won her war. Subdued a rebellion."
msgstr "Había ganado su guerra. Había aplastado una rebelión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had won the day, but it had come at a great price."
msgstr "Había ganado el día, pero había llegado a un gran precio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had work to do, and this distraction had already cost her more time than she was willing to waste."
msgstr "Tenía trabajo que hacer, y esta distracción ya le había costado más tiempo del que estaba dispuesta a desperdiciar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had worked so hard to break free, make her own path, only for him to threaten to take it all away again."
msgstr "Había trabajado tan duro para liberarse, para trazar su propio camino, solo para que él amenazara con arrebatárselo todo de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had worked so hard to convince him that she was strong. She wasn't going to throw that away by begging him now."
msgstr "Había trabajado tan duro para convencerlo de que era fuerte. No iba a tirar eso por el desagüe suplicándole ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't been sitting for more than a minute when she heard a voice."
msgstr "No había pasado de un minuto sentada cuando oyó una voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't even realized she was staring...but it was impossible to look away."
msgstr "Ni siquiera se había dado cuenta de que lo miraba... pero era imposible apartar la vista."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't expected he'd be so crass about it, neither was she too surprised."
msgstr "No esperaba que fuera tan grosero al respecto, ni tampoco me sorprendió demasiado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't felt this way in a long time."
msgstr "No había sentido esto en mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't long begun when she suddenly heard a noise."
msgstr "No había pasado mucho tiempo cuando de repente escuchó un ruido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't much choice. She'd taken the bet, even if he had hustled her."
msgstr "No tenía mucha opción. Aceptó la apuesta, aunque él la hubiera presionado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't seen fit to put on any clothes so far."
msgstr "No se había puesto ninguna prenda hasta ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't seen him since she stepped through the portal..."
msgstr "No lo había visto desde que cruzó el portal..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't thought about the fact that life might be safe, but that this might also be all there was."
msgstr "No había pensado en el hecho de que la vida pudiera ser segura, pero también de que esto podría ser todo lo que quedaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't thought of the man like this all night."
msgstr "No había pensado en él de esta manera toda la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't told him anything of her origins, nor would she."
msgstr "No le había contado nada de sus orígenes, ni lo haría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't used this room...not since Xan."
msgstr "No había usado esta habitación... no desde Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't worked in a kitchen for a day in her life, but Sarah caught on fast enough."
msgstr "Nunca había trabajado en una cocina ni un solo día en su vida, pero Sarah lo entendió rápido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't yet spoken the words, but she could see the pain in his face."
msgstr "Aunque aún no había pronunciado las palabras, ya podía ver el dolor en su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn’t fought him, or protested, nor would she have wanted to do."
msgstr "No se había opuesto a él, ni protestado, y de todas formas no habría querido hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She half wanted to beat him herself. She half wanted to let Marius do it for her."
msgstr "Casi quería golpearlo yo misma. Casi quería dejar que Marius lo hiciera por mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She handed Sarah a pile of documents."
msgstr "Ella entregó a Sarah un montón de documentos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She handed him the bowl of stew."
msgstr "Le entregó el cuenco de estofado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She handed it back to Samayra."
msgstr "Se lo devolvió a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She handed the flagon back to Varga."
msgstr "Se lo devolvió al Varga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hardly knew what it was, and still, the object seemed to linger on her mind."
msgstr "Apenas sabía qué era, y aun así, el objeto parecía persistir en su mente."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "She has a way of turning events to her hand."
msgstr "Sabe manejar los acontecimientos a su antojo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "She has been a real pleasure."
msgstr "Ha sido un verdadero placer."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "She has developped a nasty cough..."
msgstr "Se le ha pegado una tos horrible..."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "She has no idea, but she knows the Khan favors sons and so she simply hopes that by pretending, the world will follow."
msgstr "No lo sabe, pero conoce que el Kan prefiere los hijos varones, así que simplemente espera que, al fingir, el mundo le siga."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "She has spoken to me that she will soon part our contract onto you."
msgstr "Ella me ha dicho que pronto transferirá nuestro contrato a ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "She has the experience and the character to perform the duties expected of such a high office."
msgstr "Tiene la experiencia y el carácter para desempeñar las funciones que exige tal alto cargo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated being ordered around."
msgstr "Odía recibir órdenes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated even having to apologize to a lowly creature like that, but until she had her magic back, she would have to careful."
msgstr "Odiaba incluso tener que disculparse con una criatura tan insignificante, pero hasta recuperar su magia, tendría que ser cuidadosa..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated having to lie to the one person that was actually decent."
msgstr "Odía tener que mentir a la única persona decente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated her body for betraying her mind, and still, she couldn't control those parts of herself."
msgstr "Odía a su cuerpo por traicionarle la mente, y aun así, no podía controlar esas partes de sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated her own body for betraying her like this."
msgstr "Odio su propio cuerpo por traicionarla de esta manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated her own body, and how it betrayed herself."
msgstr "Odía su propio cuerpo y la forma en que lo traicionaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated her own body. Wasn't she in charge of what she did and didn't do? Then why did her body want these things?"
msgstr "¿No estaba ella al mando de lo que hacía y no hacía? Entonces, ¿por qué su cuerpo deseaba esas cosas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated herself for not feeling more pain..."
msgstr "La odiaba a sí misma por no sentir más dolor..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated herself for wanting him."
msgstr "La odiaba a sí misma por quererlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated herself more for knowing she would give herself to him again and again."
msgstr "La odiaba más por saber que se le entregaría a él una y otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated him calling her that, and loved him for calling her that anyway."
msgstr "Lo odiaba que la llamara así, y lo amaba por llamarla así de todas formas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated him so much in her mind, and yet, who else in this wretched world had even cared to look at her?"
msgstr "La odiaba tanto en su mente, y sin embargo, ¿quién más en este maldito mundo se había tomado el tiempo de mirarla?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated him, in the moment, almost as much as the orcs."
msgstr "Lo odiaba, en ese momento, casi tanto como a los orcos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated him, that much she knew."
msgstr "Ella lo odiaba, eso sí que sabía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated him. But more than that, she hated how her body enjoyed all of it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how by now she had experience with this."
msgstr "La odiaba por tener experiencia con esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how happy and content the creature looked."
msgstr "La odiaba por lo feliz y satisfecha que parecía la criatura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how he talked down to her, and hated herself more for how it turned her on."
msgstr "La odiaba por cómo hablaba con ella como si fuera inferior, y la odiaba más aún por cómo eso la excitaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how her body always betrayed her."
msgstr "Odía cómo su cuerpo siempre la traicionaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how much she liked it."
msgstr "Odía lo mucho que le gustaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how quiet her voice was around him. How she couldn't find it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how she had to apologize to him, even as he greedily leered at her exposed body."
msgstr "Odiaba cómo tenía que disculparse con él, incluso mientras él la escrutaba con lascivia devorando su cuerpo desnudo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated how she had to repress herself, she wanted to wildly flail around, let the pleasure roar through her, but she knew she had to contain herself, lest they noticed her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated it as much as she loved it."
msgstr "La odiaba tanto como la amaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated that most of all, how her body betrayed her."
msgstr "Eso le disgustaba sobre todo, cómo su cuerpo la traicionaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated that she got wet for him, but right now, she was grateful."
msgstr "Odía que se empapara por él, pero ahora mismo, está agradecida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated the loneliness that gripped her heart, and yet she equally feared it fading."
msgstr "Odio la soledad que le aprieta el corazón, y sin embargo, teme tanto lo mismo: que desaparezca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated the weakness of her body, but in a cold and lonely place like this, the spirit had been a rare companion."
msgstr "Aborrecía la debilidad de su cuerpo, pero en un lugar frío y solitario como este, el espíritu había sido un raro consuelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hated to dissapoint the girl."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She headed back into the yard and began to walk the perimeter, marked by the ramshackle fence."
msgstr "Salió de nuevo al patio y comenzó a recorrer el perímetro, delimitado por la valla precaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She headed out through the hallway and made her way to the kitchen."
msgstr "Salió por el pasillo y se dirigió a la cocina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heads back inside and presents the bottle."
msgstr "Regresa al interior y presenta la botella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Alaric grunt."
msgstr "Sarah escuchó el gruñido de Alaric."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Alaric's mocking laughter."
msgstr "Escuchó la risa burlona de Alaric."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Belmont slap Nick."
msgstr "Escuché a Belmont dar una bofetada a Nick."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Caleb laugh."
msgstr "Escuchó la risa de Caleb."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Dalia's soft and distant voice."
msgstr "Escuchó la voz suave y lejana de Dalia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Ephraim moan with pleasure."
msgstr "Escuchó a Efraín gemir de placer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Garret laugh as she walked up the road ahead of him."
msgstr "Oyó reír a Garret mientras caminaba por el camino que tenía delante de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Hugh laugh."
msgstr "Escuchó a Hugh reír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Kate laugh."
msgstr "Ella escuchó a Kate reír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Kate sigh."
msgstr "Ella escuchó el suspiro de Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Lady Carolyn approach."
msgstr "Oyó el acercamiento de la Dama Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Lady Carolyn rummaging through something."
msgstr "Oyó a Lady Carolyn revolvendo algo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Lily mumble something under her breath."
msgstr "Escuchó a Lily murmurar algo con los labios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Naydeen softly chuckle."
msgstr "Escuchó a Naydeen reírse suavemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Nick's repressed grunting as the orc continued to fuck him."
msgstr "Escuchó los gemidos reprimidos de Nick mientras la orca continuaba follando con él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Samayra follow her."
msgstr "Escuché que Samayra la seguía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Samayra loudly puffing, like a scolded child that didn't agree."
msgstr "Escuchó cómo Samayra jadeaba con fuerza, como un niño regañado que no estaba de acuerdo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Samayra sigh."
msgstr "Escuchó cómo Samayra suspiraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Samayra softly laugh."
msgstr "Oyó a Samayra reír suavemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Samayra walking close to her, equally struck silent by the majesty of the place."
msgstr "Escuché cómo Samayra caminaba cerca de mí, igualmente aturdida por la majestuosidad del lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Sigmund grunt."
msgstr "Escuché un gruñido de Sigmund."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard Sigmund only growl."
msgstr "Solo escuchó un gruñido de Sigmund."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard a loud crack rang out and felt a burning sensation on her ass."
msgstr "Escuchó un estruendo seco y sintió una sensación ardiente en su culo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard a man, bound in iron, call out."
msgstr "Escuchó cómo un hombre, atado de hierro, gritaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard a woman, howling like she had gone mad."
msgstr "Escuchó a una mujer aullando como si hubiera perdido la cordura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard and approving groan from the chieftain."
msgstr "Escuchó un gruñido de aprobación del jefe tribal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard and felt his face crack beneath the force of her punch."
msgstr "Oyó y sintió cómo su rostro se reventaba bajo la fuerza de tu puño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard every sound, but heard within every sound, the infinite complexities that she had otherwise never heard."
msgstr "Escuchó cada sonido, pero dentro de cada sonido, percibió las infinitas complejidades que jamás había oído antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard her husband grunting beneath her, his member swelling inside of her."
msgstr "Escuché a mi esposo gemir bajo mí, sintiendo cómo su polla se hincha dentro de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard her name called out, and she strode onto the open arena."
msgstr "Escuchó que la llamaban y se dirigió al amplio recinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard her own voice ring out."
msgstr "Escuchó su propia voz resonar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard herself continue to cry out, but something else had entered her voice."
msgstr "Escuchó cómo seguía gritando, pero algo más había entrado en su voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him finish before she felt it."
msgstr "Ella escuchó que él terminaba antes de sentirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him fumbling over his words."
msgstr "Escuché cómo tartamudeaba con las palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him gargle a sound, but only blood poured from his mouth."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him get dressed."
msgstr "Escuché cómo se vestía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him groan loudly as he finished."
msgstr "Oyó cómo gemía con fuerza al terminar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him groan, and hated him even more for it."
msgstr "Escuché su gemido y lo odié aún más por ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him groan, deep."
msgstr "Escuché su gemido, profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him groan, his body tensing to our touch."
msgstr "Escuché su gemido, su cuerpo tensándose ante nuestro contacto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him groaning approvingly."
msgstr "Escuché cómo gruñía aprobadoramente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him grunt in his goblin language, something to the other goblin."
msgstr "Escuché como gruñía en su lengua de goblin, algo para el otro goblin."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him grunt some words, perhaps only half believing her."
msgstr "Escuché cómo gruñía algunas palabras, quizás creyéndola apenas a la mitad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him gutter out a few last breaths."
msgstr "Escuchó cómo exhalaba sus últimos alientos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him laugh at her efforts."
msgstr "Escuché cómo reía a mis esfuerzos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him laugh."
msgstr "Ella escuchó su risa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him laughing."
msgstr "Escuché su risa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him scream at the injury, too grievous to suppress."
msgstr "Ella escuchó cómo él gritaba por la herida, demasiado grave para contenerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him softly groan."
msgstr "Ella escuchó su gemido suave."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him softly laugh."
msgstr "Ella escuchó su risa suave."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him spit loudly."
msgstr "Ella escuchó cómo escupía con fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him spit, then felt the spit hit between the cheeks of her ass."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She heard him utter a cruel laugh."
