msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell me."
msgstr "Cuéntame."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Tell me. Tell me all of it and I'll still be here."
msgstr "Dímelo. Dime todo y seguiré aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Tell me..."
msgstr "Cuéntame..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Tell me..."
msgstr "Cuéntame..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell me..."
msgstr "Dime..."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "Tell me...was it Rosanna?"
msgstr "Dime... ¿fue Rosanna?"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Tell the mob to disband"
msgstr "Diles a la muchedumbre que se disuelvan"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell the scouts to remain close to camp."
msgstr "Diles a los exploradores que se mantengan cerca del campamento."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Tell the scouts to stay near camp"
msgstr "Diles que se queden cerca del campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell them to close up the gap, prevent the Tribesman from falling back!"
msgstr "¡Diles que cierren la brecha y impidan que el Tribusmano se repliegue!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell them to leave their armor and sigils here, move undercover, then report back what they find."
msgstr "Diles que dejen sus armaduras y sigilos aquí, se muevan ocultos y luego cuenten lo que hallen."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Tell them what they want to hear."
msgstr "Diles lo que quieren oír."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell who?"
msgstr "¿A quién?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Tell ya what kid, I heard your terms now how about you hear mine?"
msgstr "Dime qué quieres que oiga, ¿eh? He escuchado tus condiciones, ahora toca que tú escuches las mías."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "Tell you what though, I'm a bit busy opening up here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Tell you what though, why don't you give me a show?"
msgstr "Dime, ¿por qué no me das un espectáculo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Tell you what, Blondie."
msgstr "Dime algo, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tell you what, I'm gonna go in first, then you come up after on the same stall, ok?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Tell you what, Sarah. I'll tell you where I'm from, if you tell me where you're from, deal?"
msgstr "Déjame decirte algo, Sarah. Te diré de dónde soy si me dices de dónde eres, ¿vale?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Tell you what, blondie, I’ll make you a bet. I just earned a big payout from a ship run I did, 20.000 pieces of gold."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "Tell you what, how bout you take the night to sleep it over?"
msgstr "Dime, ¿por qué no te quedas a pasarla toda la noche?"

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Tell you what, if I get back we can pick up on the lessons. In between, keep studying and practice. But don't go pushing yourself."
msgstr "Escucha, si regreso podemos retomar las lecciones. Mientras tanto, sigue estudiando y practica, pero no te empujes demasiado."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Tell you what, let's retire to my room, we'll have the servants bring up our food and we can work over dinner."
msgstr "Déjame decirte algo, vámonos a mi habitación, haremos que los sirvientes traigan nuestra comida y podremos trabajar sobre la cena."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Tell you what, pretty-boy, I ain't looking for a coach."
msgstr "Dime, guapo, que no busco un cochero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Telling Marius would surely cause a scene."
msgstr "Contárselo a Marius sin duda causaría escándalo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Telling him about the voice would surely do her no favors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Telling him would surely cause a scene."
msgstr "Contárselo le causaría un escándalo."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Telling love stories that belonged only in books."
msgstr "Contar historias de amor que solo pertenecían en los libros."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Tells me, we're gonna make a family, and he'll buy me my own big house on the countryside."
msgstr "Me dice que vamos a formar una familia y que él me comprará mi propia casa grande en el campo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Template."
msgstr "Plantilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Temporary placeholder."
msgstr "Oferta tentadora, pero creo que me quedaré con mi decisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Tempting offer, but I think I'll pass."
msgstr "Oferta tentadora, pero creo que me quedaré con la mía."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Ten-thousand Lethram shillings."
msgstr "Diez mil shillings lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Tenderly, the spirit's limb ran further up her legs until, finally, it found purchase."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Tenderness gave way to a more primal desire."
msgstr "La ternura dio paso a un deseo más primitivo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Tendrils of raw magical energy came into focus, wrapping around her body and lifting her up into the air."
msgstr "Se hicieron visibles hilos de energía mágica pura que se enrollaron alrededor de su cuerpo y la levantaron hacia el aire."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Tensing her grip on the handle..."
msgstr "Aprieta la empuñadura con cautela..."

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Terrible with money though, so I hope you're not used to livin in luxury, cause he ain't givin you none."
msgstr "Terrible con el dinero, así que espero que no estés acostumbrada a vivir en lujo, porque él no te está dando ninguno."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Terrible with money?"
msgstr "¿Terrible con el dinero?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Terrified, Sarah allowed her hand to slide down her body."
msgstr "Con terror, Sarah dejó que su mano deslizara por su cuerpo."

msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Test"
msgstr "¿Prueba?"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Testify against Alaric"
msgstr "Deponer contra Alaric"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Testify against Alaric and she would be spared..."
msgstr "Testificar contra Alaric y sería perdonada..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Testing, first carefully, then boldly, what parts of her she would let him."
msgstr "Probando, primero con cuidado y luego con atrevimiento, qué partes de ella le dejaría."

msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Text Speed"
msgstr "Velocidad del texto"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Thank fuck he let us in."
msgstr "¡Por fin nos dejó entrar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Thank god that you screamed, I got here just in time."
msgstr "¡Gracias a los dioses que gritaste; llegué justo a tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank the Gods it's you."
msgstr "¡Gracias a los dioses eres tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thank the Gods she at least had her underwear between them, she thought."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses, al menos tenía su ropa interior entre sus piernas, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thank the Gods she was drenched, she thought as she felt him massive cock press into her."
msgstr "Agradeciendo a los dioses por estar empapada, pensó mientras sentía cómo su verga masiva la presionaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thank the Gods the girl was safe."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses, la muchacha estaba a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Thank the Gods you made it out!"
msgstr "¡Gracias a los dioses que lograste escapar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thank the Gods."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank the Gods."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Thank the Gods..."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank the Gods..."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses..."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Thank the god that I arrived when I did."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses por haber llegado cuando llegué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thank the gods she was wet, she thought to herself."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses que estaba mojada, pensó para sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank the gods we managed to reach this place before it all broke down."
msgstr "¡Gracias a los dioses logramos llegar a este lugar antes de que todo se derrumbara!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Thank the gods, I was so worried that he would hurt you."
msgstr "Gracias a los dioses, estaba tan preocupada de que te hiciera daño."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Thank ya boy, you can leave us now."
msgstr "Gracias, muchacho; ya puedes irte."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "Thank you Jaeid. Had I but a thousand men like you, this great war of mine would have been won years ago."
msgstr "Gracias, Jaeid. Si hubiera tenido mil hombres como tú, esta gran guerra mía habría sido ganada años atrás."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you Marion, that means a lot to us. Both of us."
msgstr "Gracias, Marion, eso significa mucho para nosotros. Para los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "Thank you Sarah."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "Thank you Sarah. It means a lot to hear you say that."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah. Es muy gratificante oírte decir eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you Sarah. You're very kind for a soldier."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah. Eres muy amable para una soldada."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you Vaelen."
msgstr "Gracias, Vaelen."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you again for listening, it really helps."
msgstr "Gracias otra vez por escucharme, realmente me ayuda."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you again, for buying me one."
msgstr "Gracias otra vez por comprármela."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you again, truly Marion. You've been a steadfast friend to our family in these trying times."
msgstr "Gracias de nuevo, verdaderamente Marion. Has sido una fiel amiga para nuestra familia en estos tiempos difíciles."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you again. You've been so kind."
msgstr "Gracias otra vez. Has sido tan amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you all for gathering here so swiftly."
msgstr "Gracias a todos por reunirse aquí con tanta rapidez."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you all for your votes of support."
msgstr "Gracias a todos por sus votos de apoyo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you all...for receiving me here."
msgstr "Gracias a todos... por recibirme aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Thank you captain Belmont!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, capitán Belmont!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you captain Belmont!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, capitán Belmont!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for briefing me."
msgstr "Gracias por explicármelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for bringing me this..."
msgstr "Gracias por traérmelo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for coming."
msgstr "Gracias por venir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for delivering this message. Consider your oath fulfilled."
msgstr "Gracias por entregar este mensaje. Considera cumplido tu juramento."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Thank you for doing that for me."
msgstr "Gracias por haber hecho eso por mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for escorting me. I'll find my way in myself."
msgstr "Gracias por acompañarme. Encontraré mi camino por mí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for everything you've done in supporting me."
msgstr "Gracias por todo lo que has hecho por apoyarme."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for forgiving me, and I promise I won't pry anymore."
msgstr "Gracias por perdonarme, y te prometo que no seguiré insistiendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for having us."
msgstr "Gracias por recibirnos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for keeping me safe for yet another day. I'm going to try and get some sleep."
msgstr "Gracias por mantenerme a salvo otro día más. Voy a intentar dormir un poco."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you for listening to me."
msgstr "Gracias por escucharme."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for offering them, you didn't need to do that."
msgstr "Gracias por ofrecérselo, no necesitabas hacerlo así."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for receiving me at this late hour."
msgstr "Gracias por recibirme en esta hora tan tarde."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you for receiving us, we were humbled to hear of your invitation."
msgstr "Gracias por recibirnos; nos sentimos honrados de haber recibido su invitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for saving me."
msgstr "Gracias por salvarme."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for saving me. Really, I don't want to think about what he would have done to me."
msgstr "Gracias por salvarme. De verdad, no quiero pensar en lo que él habría hecho conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you for saying that, it means a lot to me."
msgstr "Gracias por decir eso, significa mucho para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for showing me this."
msgstr "Gracias por mostrármelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for standing up for me, Thomas. I know it isn't easy."
msgstr "Gracias por defenderme, Thomas. Sé que no es fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for stopping by and checking in on me."
msgstr "Gracias por pasar y comprobar cómo estoy."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for telling me about her."
msgstr "Gracias por contármelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for that offer. King Thomas and myself will certainly call on you, should we need your aid."
msgstr "Gracias por esa propuesta, mi rey Thomas y yo nos pondremos a su disposición si necesitamos tu ayuda."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for that too."
msgstr "Gracias por eso también."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for the blankets."
msgstr "Gracias por las mantas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for the kind advice."
msgstr "Gracias por el buen consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for the kind offer, but I must refuse."
msgstr "Gracias por la amable oferta, pero debo rechazarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for the report, go back to your station."
msgstr "Gracias por el informe, regresa a tu puesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for those kind words."
msgstr "Gracias por esas palabras amables."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Thank you for you council, sister."
msgstr "Gracias por tu consejo, hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for your consideration. It really means more than you can know."
msgstr "Gracias por tu consideración. Significa más de lo que puedes imaginar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for your counsel, Brother."
msgstr "Gracias por su consejo, hermano."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for your kind words, but I was hoping we could speak of more serious matters than dressed and balls."
msgstr "Gracias por tus amables palabras, pero esperaba que pudiéramos hablar de asuntos más serios que la ropa y los cojones."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for your offer, it's very kind."
msgstr "Gracias por tu propuesta, es muy amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for your time, Lord Edmond."
msgstr "Gracias por tu tiempo, señor Edmond."

msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "Thank you for your trust, Lady Rose."
msgstr "¡Gracias por confiar en mí, Lady Rose!"

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "Thank you kindly for the compliment, but I'll have to share some of that credit."
msgstr "Gracias por el cumplido, pero tendré que compartir un poco de ese crédito."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Thank you kindly, Blondie, I promise I'll pay back every cent. Captain's honor."
msgstr "Gracias, rubia, te lo prometo: pagaré cada centavo. Honor de capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "Thank you kindly."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Thank you princess, your concern means a lot to me. To all of us."
msgstr "Gracias, princesa, tu preocupación significa todo para mí... para todos nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you sir!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, señor!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you so much!"
msgstr "¡Muchas gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you! I will!"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¡Lo haré!"

msgctxt "speaker:Woman"
msgid "Thank you! Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¡Muchas gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¡Gracias! ¡Gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Captain."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Carolyn."
msgstr "Gracias, Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Duke Antonio."
msgstr "Gracias, duque Antonio."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Edmond then."
msgstr "Gracias, Edmond."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Elder Tirion. You are a true friend."
msgstr "Gracias, anciano Tirion. Eres un verdadero amigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Eula. You're maybe the one nice person I've met today."
msgstr "Gracias, Eula. Quizás seas la única persona amable que he conocido hoy."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Garret."
msgstr "Gracias, Garret."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Thank you, Great Khan, for respecting my refusal."
msgstr "Gracias, Gran Kan, por respetar mi negativa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, I mean, uhm, I'll think about it."
msgstr "Gracias, quiero decir, uh, lo pensaré."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, I needed to hear some kind words."
msgstr "Gracias, necesitaba escuchar unas palabras amables."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "Thank you, I suppose."
msgstr "Gracias, supongo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, I will."
msgstr "Gracias, lo haré."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, I'll go speak with him and see about resolving this matter."
msgstr "Gracias, iré a hablar con él y veré cómo resolver este asunto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Kate..."
msgstr "Gracias, Kate..."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Thank you, Khan Hassar, for granting me my request."
msgstr "Gracias, Khan Hassar, por concederme mi petición."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Khan Hassar."
msgstr "Gracias, Khán Hassar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Gracias, Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Lord Edmond, for your trust."
msgstr "Gracias, señor Edmond, por su confianza."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Lord Edmond."
msgstr "Gracias, mi señor."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Thank you, Lord Gilead."
msgstr "Gracias, señor Gilead."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Marion, my brother and I were very happy when we heard you would attend."
msgstr "Gracias, Marion; mi hermano y yo estuvimos muy contentos al saber que asistirías."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Marius."
msgstr "Gracias, Marius."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Marius. You've really been so kind to me."
msgstr "Gracias, Marius. Has sido tan amable conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Thank you, Master!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, señor!"

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Thank you, Master."
msgstr "Gracias, Maestro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Metis."
msgstr "Gracias, Metis."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Nick. I think I've learned more today than I did in all the weeks before."
msgstr "Gracias, Nick. Creo que he aprendido más hoy de lo que aprendí en todas las semanas anteriores."

msgctxt "speaker:Young woman"
msgid "Thank you, Princess! Thank you for your mercy!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, ¡Princesa! ¡Gracias por tu clemencia!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Queen Maeiv, for your kind offer of a feast. I shall attend, as shall the most important members of my household."
msgstr "Gracias, Reina Maeiv, por tu amable oferta de un banquete. Asistiré yo, así como los miembros más importantes de mi hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Razaphel."
msgstr "Gracias, Razafael."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Samayra, for saying that."
msgstr "Gracias, Samayra, por decir eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Samayra. That means more to me than you might think."
msgstr "Gracias, Samayra. Eso significa más para mí de lo que podrías imaginar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Samayra..."
msgstr "Gracias, Samayra..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah, that means a lot to me."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah, eso significa mucho para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah. There is a girl with a smart head on her shoulders."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah. Hay una chica con gran ingenio en su cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Thank you, Sarah. Yours is an offer I would gladly accept."
msgstr "Gracias, Sarah. Tu oferta es algo que aceptaría con gusto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Sigmund."
msgstr "Gracias, Sigmund."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Sigmund. I really don't know what else to say."
msgstr "Gracias, Sigmund. No sé realmente qué más decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Thomas. It's kind of you."
msgstr "Gracias, Thomas. Eres muy amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Thomas. It's very kind."
msgstr "Gracias, Thomas. Es muy amable de ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Varga."
msgstr "Gracias, Varga."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, and I will."
msgstr "Gracias, y lo haré."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, anyway."
msgstr "De todos modos, gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Thank you, by the way."
msgstr "Por cierto, gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain Belmont! I promise I'll earn my keep."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán Belmont! Prometo ganarme el pan."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain Belmont, I promise you won't regret it."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán Belmont; prometo que no lo lamentará."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain Belmont, for sparing his life."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán Belmont, por haberle perdonado la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain Belmont, that means a lot."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán Belmont, eso significa mucho para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, captain. This dress means a lot to me."
msgstr "Gracias, capitán. Este vestido significa mucho para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, for the book. It's proving to be very enlightening."
msgstr "Gracias por el libro. Está resultando muy esclarecedor."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, for the clothes."
msgstr "Gracias por la ropa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, is she ready to receive me?"
msgstr "Gracias, ¿está lista para recibirme?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, it is a most kind offer."
msgstr "Gracias, es una oferta muy amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, it means more to me than you might think."
msgstr "Gracias, significa más para mí de lo que podrías imaginar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, it's really beautiful."
msgstr "Gracias, es realmente hermoso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, kind sir."
msgstr "Gracias, buen hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Peasant girl"
msgid "Thank you, lady Rose, I will remember your mercy for as long as I live!"
msgstr "Gracias, señora Rose, recordaré su misericordia por el resto de mi vida!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, master..."
msgstr "Gracias, mi señor..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Thank you, missy."
msgstr "Gracias, cariño."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, really, it does make me feel better to hear that."
msgstr "Gracias, de verdad; me hace sentir mejor saber eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, really. It's been nice to talk to someone for a while and not have it be about...well, you know."
msgstr "Gracias, de verdad. Ha sido agradable hablar con alguien durante un rato y que no fuera sobre... bueno, sabes."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, sir! I will!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, señor! Lo haré!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, sir."
msgstr "Gracias, señor."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Thank you, so much!"
msgstr "¡Muchas gracias!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, thank you, thank you..."
msgstr "Gracias, gracias, gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, thank you."
msgstr "Gracias, gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Thank you, that will be all."
msgstr "Gracias, eso es todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, that's all. Good work."
msgstr "Gracias, eso es todo. Buen trabajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, though most of the credit goes to the servants that did all the work."
msgstr "Gracias, aunque la mayor parte del crédito corresponde a los sirvientes que hicieron todo el trabajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "Thank you, you're very kind. But I fear that will make little difference."
msgstr "Gracias, es muy amable. Pero temo que no hará mucha diferencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Merchant"
msgid "Thank you, your Highness, you have saved my business!"
msgstr "Gracias, Su Alteza, ¡ha salvado mi negocio!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. Both of you."
msgstr "Gracias. A los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. I forget sometimes how long it's been."
msgstr "Gracias. A veces olvido cuánto tiempo ha pasado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. I promise I won't be a burden."
msgstr "Gracias. Prometo que no seré una carga."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. I'll be sure to check it out."
msgstr "Gracias. Me aseguraré de echar un vistazo."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you. I'll finish these and bring them back for final approval."
msgstr "Gracias. Terminaré estas y las traeré de vuelta para la aprobación final."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. I'm just glad I can be useful around here."
msgstr "Gracias. Solo estoy contenta de poder ser útil por aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. It makes me feel a little better hearing that from you."
msgstr "Gracias. Me siento un poco mejor al escuchar eso de ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. It means a lot to hear that from someone like you. Someone who knew my father better than most."
msgstr "Gracias. Significa mucho oír eso de alguien como tú. Alguien que conocía a mi padre mejor que la mayoría."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. It might sound silly, but it means a lot coming from you."
msgstr "Gracias. Puede sonar tonto, pero significa mucho que lo digas tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. Really, you saved me."
msgstr "Gracias. De verdad, me has salvado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. Thank you."
msgstr "Gracias. Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. That's all I want."
msgstr "Gracias. Eso es todo lo que quiero."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Thank you. That's all I wanted to hear."
msgstr "Gracias. Eso es todo lo que quería oír."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Thank you. You really are a good friend."
msgstr "Gracias. Eres realmente una buena amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you. You really didn't have to do any of this."
msgstr "Gracias. De verdad no necesitabas hacer todo esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank you..."
msgstr "Gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you..."
msgstr "Gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Slave Woman"
msgid "Thank you..."
msgstr "Gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you...Jaeid. I think I need to be alone now for a moment."
msgstr "Gracias... Jaeid. Creo que necesito estar sola un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you...a lot of servants put a lot of time and effort into this."
msgstr "Gracias... muchos sirvientes dedicaron mucho tiempo y esfuerzo a esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you...for inviting me."
msgstr "Gracias... por invitarme."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you...sir."
msgstr "Gracias... señor."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "Thank you...truly."
msgstr "Gracias... de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank..."
msgstr "...dame..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank...me?"
msgstr "¿Gracias... a mí?"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thank...thank you..."
msgstr "Gracias... gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thankfully, and partly to her own shame, she knew she was wet between her legs."
msgstr "Afortunadamente, y en parte por su propia vergüenza, sabía que estaba mojada entre sus piernas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thankfully, for now, he was kind, and Sarah was happy. Genuinely happy in her heart."
msgstr "Afortunadamente, por ahora, era amable y Sarah estaba feliz. De verdad feliz en el corazón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thankfully, there had also been a bed there. Old to be sure, but functional."
msgstr "Afortunadamente, también había una cama allí. Antigua, es cierto, pero funcional."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thanking him felt like going a step too far, even if he could deliver her the alliance she desperately needed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Thanks again for letting us stay here."
msgstr "Gracias otra vez por permitirnos quedarnos aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Thanks for helping me with that."
msgstr "Gracias por ayudarme con eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thanks! And your name is?"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¿Y cuál es tu nombre?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thanks, I didn't have enough on my shoulders."
msgstr "Gracias, no tenía suficientes en los hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Thanks, I'm starving."
msgstr "Gracias, estoy muerto de hambre."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Thanks, boss!"
msgstr "¡Gracias, jefe!"

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Thanks."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thanks."
msgstr "Gracias."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thanks. I'll be down in just a bit."
msgstr "Gracias. Estaré abajo en un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thanks..."
msgstr "Gracias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That I do."
msgstr "Eso es."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That I know how to make a campfire? You live on the road for long enough, you learn it sooner or later."
msgstr "¿Sabes hacer fuego de campamento? Si pasas tanto tiempo en la carretera, lo aprendes antes o después."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That I only end up fucking you when we're almost in Rahayal."
msgstr "Que solo acabo follando contigo cuando estamos casi en Rahayal."

msgctxt "speaker:Caleb"
msgid "That I thought we should invite you to join us."
msgstr "Que pensé que deberíamos invitarte a unirse."

msgctxt "speaker:Young woman"
msgid "That I threw a rock? Pff, it wasn't a rock, a pebble, maybe."
msgstr "¿Que lancé una piedra? Pff, no era una piedra, un guijarro, quizás."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "That I was attracted to you?"
msgstr "¿Que me sentía atraída por ti?"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That I was coming over tonight."
msgstr "Que iba a venir esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That I...I vow..."
msgstr "Que yo... yo juro..."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "That a God, can deceive a God."
msgstr "Que un Dios pueda engañar a otro Dios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That a world like this could have been out here..."
msgstr "Que un mundo como este pudiera existir fuera de aquí..."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "That actually doesn't sound as bad as you make it out to be."
msgstr "Eso en realidad no suena tan mal como lo estás pintando."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "That ain't no kindness little lady."
msgstr "Ese no es ningún gesto de bondad, chica."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That ain't supposed to be impressive, but in this business, you meet a lot of shady folks."
msgstr "Eso no está pensado para impresionar, pero en este negocio se conoce a mucha gente sospechosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "That ain't used to be there."
msgstr "Eso no estaba ahí antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That ain't you blondie."
msgstr "Eso no eres tú, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That almost made it worse, she realized."
msgstr "Eso casi lo empeoró, se dio cuenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That alone gave her cause to wonder."
msgstr "Eso solo le dio motivo para preguntarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That alone made her stand out. Her mage outfit, twice over."
msgstr "Eso la hacía destacar por sí solo. Su atuendo de maga, el doble."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That and other things."
msgstr "Y otras cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That arrogant grin of his."
msgstr "Esa sonrisa arrogante suya."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That ass of yours..."
msgstr "Ese culo tuyo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That attentive gaze he used on her was now reserved for the map, and Sarah found herself oddly jealous of it."
msgstr "Esa mirada atenta que él le dedicaba a ella ahora se la reservaba para el mapa, y Sarah se sentía extrañamente celosa de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That awkwardness. It might be cute in Rosanna, but here, it just signals weakness. And weakness invites troublemakers."
msgstr "Esa torpeza. Podría ser tierna en Rosanna, pero aquí solo denota debilidad. Y la debilidad atrae a los que buscan problemas."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "That barely pays for me, let alone my men. How am I supposed to feed them if I let you and every other miserable son-of-a-bitch pass for a price like that?"
msgstr "Eso apenas paga por mí, ¡hace mucho menos para mis hombres! ¿Cómo debo alimentarlos si les dejo pasar a ti y a cada miserable hijo de perra por ese precio?"

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That bastard! I just thought he was some pervert who'd pay me extra for putting it on."
msgstr "¡Ese maldito! Solo pensé que era algún perverso que me pagaría extra por meterla."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That bastard."
msgstr "Ese maldito."

msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Officer"
msgid "That big old horde that had been gathered under...what was that fella's name, Khan...something."
msgstr "Esa gran horda que había reunido bajo... ¿cómo se llamaba ese tipo, Khan...algo así."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "That can be a problem of a restless mind."
msgstr "Eso puede ser un problema de una mente inquieta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That city had struck her with its grandness, this city seemed to do the opposite."
msgstr "Esa ciudad le había impactado con su grandeza; esta parecía hacer exactamente lo contrario."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That city...the Mythran army there, they are our only real way out of this mess."
msgstr "Esa ciudad... el ejército Mythran allí, son nuestra única salida real de este lío."

msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "That comes out to a big bundle."
msgstr "Eso suma un gran paquete."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That concludes the very first council meeting."
msgstr "Eso concluye la primera reunión del consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That could be you."
msgstr "Eso podría ser tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That could look past all the bullshit about titles and ranks, and see who I really was!"
msgstr "¡Eso podría mirar más allá de toda la basura sobre títulos y rangos, y ver quién realmente era yo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That cruelty that she oddly enjoyed."
msgstr "Esa crueldad que extrañamente disfrutaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That cruelty was at the root of the problem."
msgstr "Esa crueldad era la raíz del problema."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That cunt of yours."
msgstr "Esa zorra de la tuya."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That deep down, there's something else there."
msgstr "Allí, en lo más profundo de ti, hay algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That doesn't count!"
msgstr "¡No cuenta!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That doesn't mean I wanna eat rancid food."
msgstr "Eso no significa que quiera comer comida agria."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That doesn't mean I'm not right."
msgstr "Eso no significa que no tenga razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That doesn't mean we have to just get married out of nowhere."
msgstr "Eso no significa que tengamos que casarnos de la nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "That doesn't mean you'll accept my offer."
msgstr "Eso no significa que aceptes mi propuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That doesn't surprise me."
msgstr "Eso no me sorprende."

msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "That dress of yours is worth a decent penny."
msgstr "Ese vestido tuyo vale un buen dinero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That easy time, before Nick and his troubles had interrupted her relationship with the captain, which had been so easy and simple."
msgstr "Ese momento de calma, antes de que Nick y sus problemas interrumpieran su relación con el capitán, la cual había sido tan fácil y sencilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That energy had never been in the air back home. Her home was a place of tradition and routine."
msgstr "Esa energía nunca había estado en el aire allí de casa. Su hogar era un lugar de tradición y rutina."

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "That explains why we got so many of our kind showing up here, I guess."
msgstr "Eso explica por qué aparecemos tantas de nuestra especie aquí, supongo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That face of his, seemingly unmarked by any adversity, beautiful. So beautiful he seemed almost radiant, crowned by his golden blonde hair."
msgstr "Ese rostro suyo parecía no estar marcado por ninguna adversidad, hermoso. Tan hermoso que parecía casi radiante, coronado por su cabello rubio dorado."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That far out, it was vague, but noticeable to a Witch of my talents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That fast?"
msgstr "¿Tan rápido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That fatso runs a solid hideout, but he doesn't know when to shut it."
msgstr "Ese gordito tiene un refugio sólido, pero no sabe cuándo cerrarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That flickering flame in a blizzard."
msgstr "Esa llama titilante en una tormenta de nieve."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That for a brief moment, he lived out an eternity in the pit of the earth, tortured by demons and flames, punished for the countless sins he had carried out."
msgstr "Por un breve instante, vivió una eternidad en el abismo de la tierra, atormentado por demonios y llamas, castigado por los innumerables pecados que había cometido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That for all of her magical training, she never had the kind of community that she saw here."
msgstr "Por todo su entrenamiento mágico, nunca había tenido el tipo de comunidad que veía aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That fucking asshole! I should...I should..."
msgstr "¡Ese maldito cabrón! Debería... debería..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That fucking pervert."
msgstr "¡Ese puto pervertido!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That fucking snake!"
msgstr "¡Esa puta víbora!"

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That garden...it's like nature...but not really."
msgstr "Ese jardín... es como la naturaleza... pero no del todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That gave her time. Space. To think."
msgstr "Eso le dio tiempo. Espacio. Para pensar."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That girl used to have more stuff propped into one dresser than what you carry around in that bag."
msgstr "Esa chica solía tener más cosas amontonadas en un mueble que las que llevas tú en esa bolsa."

msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "That goes for both of you."
msgstr "Eso aplica a los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That good huh?"
msgstr "¿Tan bueno, eh?"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That good,huh?"
msgstr "¿Tan bien, eh?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That had also been the danger of it, she remembered."
msgstr "Eso también había sido el peligro de ello, recordó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That had always been what made him so dangerous to her. The way he held sway over her."
msgstr "Eso había sido siempre lo que le hacía tan peligroso para ella. La manera en que ejercía dominio sobre ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That had been here, but a moment ago, and now all she felt was jealousy. Ephraim had stolen that dick from her."
msgstr "Aquí había estado, pero hace un momento, y ahora todo lo que sentía era celos. Ephraim se había llevado esa polla de mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That had been just one night."
msgstr "Eso había sido solo una noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That he had ever dared to show her that side of himself was something Sarah cherished more than any material wealth."
msgstr "Que él hubiera osado mostrársela ese lado de sí mismo era algo que Sarah valoraba más que cualquier riqueza material."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That he had reached such an age at all, was a testament to either his martial skill or his luck."
msgstr "Que haya llegado a tal edad, es testimonio de su habilidad marcial o de la suerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That he knew the risk about me? What...are you talking about?"
msgstr "¿Que sabía del riesgo que corría? ¿Qué... qué estás diciendo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That he will die by your blade in the sands of a forgotten city."
msgstr "Que morirá bajo tu espada en las arenas de una ciudad olvidada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That her old life had been a fading memory, and that she could live like this forever."
msgstr "Que su vida anterior había sido un recuerdo desvaneciéndose, y que podía vivir así para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That high?"
msgstr "¡Tan alta?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That hissing laughter again."
msgstr "¡Esa risa sibilante otra vez!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That idiot!"
msgstr "¡Idiota!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That idiot...Marion, what he did today..."
msgstr "¿Qué idiota... Marion, lo que hizo hoy..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That in a world of chaos, this might be the smallest island of security?"
msgstr "¿Acaso en un mundo de caos, esto podría ser la más pequeña isla de seguridad?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That in all of the world, their souls had been made to fit one another."
msgstr "Que en todo el mundo, sus almas habían sido hechas para encajar una con la otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That instead, she might yet live anew."
msgstr "Que, en su lugar, podría aún renacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "That is a different topic."
msgstr "Ese es otro tema."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "That is a fair point."
msgstr "Ese es un punto justo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is actually the matter which I have come to discuss."
msgstr "Eso es en realidad el asunto por el que he venido a hablar."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "That is actually why I came to see you."
msgstr "Eso es exactamente por qué vine a verte."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That is all I have ever offered you. The freedom to do as you please."
msgstr "Eso es todo lo que jamás te he ofrecido. La libertad de hacer como quieras."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That is how we move the support towards your cause. That is how you get your legions."
msgstr "Así es como movemos el apoyo hacia tu causa. Así es como consigues tus legiones."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is it then? Bloodshed, all for your people's pride?"
msgstr "¿Eso es todo entonces? Sangre derramada, todo por el orgullo de tu pueblo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "That is most likely true."
msgstr "Eso es muy probable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is not an answer to my question."
msgstr "Eso no es una respuesta a mi pregunta."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "That is not what happened. Allow your father to tell you the full story."
msgstr "Eso no es lo que sucedió. Deja que tu padre te cuente la historia completa."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That is one of the Ink merchants, let's go ahead and see if he as what I need."
msgstr "Ese es uno de los comerciantes de tinta; vamos a ver si tiene lo que necesito."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "That is right."
msgstr "Eso es correcto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is the Art that caused the Ruin, no? Surely the Gods would have cared to prevent that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That is the first place they put her to work."
msgstr "Ese fue el primer lugar donde la pusieron a trabajar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is the flower of the royal Normandi family."
msgstr "Esa es la flor de la familia real Normandi."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "That is treason!"
msgstr "¡Eso es traición!"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That is true, but this particular creature is not from your world or mine. Some other place altogether."
msgstr "Eso es cierto, pero esta criatura en particular no es de tu mundo ni del mío. De algún lugar totalmente distinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "That is true, but unusual times can require unusual responses."
msgstr "Eso es cierto, pero los tiempos inusuales pueden requerir respuestas inusuales."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "That is true..."
msgstr "Eso es cierto..."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That is what Daemonology is, the magic of the space between the worlds. The essential magic that operates the Cosmos."
msgstr "Eso es lo que es la Daemonología, la magia del espacio entre los mundos. La magia esencial que hace funcionar el Cosmos."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "That is what I thought."
msgstr "Eso es lo que pensé."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "That is what this is about?"
msgstr "¿De eso se trata esto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That is what we offer. A steady hand. And that is what I do, and some others. We are agents of that steady hand, seeking to implement this project of peace."
msgstr "Eso es lo que ofrecemos. Una mano firme. Y eso es lo que hago yo, y algunos otros. Somos agentes de esa mano firme, buscando implementar este proyecto de paz."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is what you are, no?"
msgstr "¿Eso es lo que eres, no?"

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "That is why I issued an order to replace the current Governor for the Eastern Provinces."
msgstr "Esa es la razón por la que emití una orden para reemplazar al actual Gobernador de las Provincias Orientales."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "That is why I say that we can make this work...for the both of us."
msgstr "Eso es por lo que digo que podemos hacer que esto funcione... para ambos de nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That is why I wanted to talk to you."
msgstr "Esa es la razón por la que quería hablar contigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is why I'm still here, Duke Antonio."
msgstr "Esa es la razón por la que aún estoy aquí, Duque Antonio."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "That is why our world has remained in such a state of decline."
msgstr "Esa es la razón por la cual nuestro mundo ha permanecido en tal estado de decadencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That is why we leave the totems, to remind them of their old lives."
msgstr "Por eso dejamos los tótems, para recordarle a ellos sus vidas pasadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That is, supposing you are still interested in learning more of the book."
msgstr "Es decir, suponiendo que sigas interesada en aprender más del libro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That is...you speak the language of the Tribes?"
msgstr "Eso es... ¿hablas el idioma de las Tribus?"

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "That isn't why I called you over."
msgstr "No es por eso que te llamé."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That it might just be. Still, you should be celebrating."
msgstr "Tal vez lo sea. Aún así, deberías celebrar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That it was Xan who was doing it."
msgstr "Que fuera Xan quien lo hacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That it's you! Xan had told me so much about you, his new apprentice."
msgstr "¡Que eres tú! Xan me había contado tanto sobre ti, su nuevo aprendiz."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That just cost you."
msgstr "Eso te ha costado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That just happened to be yours."
msgstr "Esa era la tuya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That kind of softness was something she couldn't afford in her current life."
msgstr "Ese tipo de suavidad era algo que ella no podía permitirse en su vida actual."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That kinda connection...that's always gonna cost ya."
msgstr "Esa clase de conexión... eso siempre te va a costar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That knowledge had lost its use when her homeland fell, and most houses she could name were now either snuffed out or living as refugees."
msgstr "Ese conocimiento había perdido su utilidad cuando cayó su patria, y la mayoría de las casas que podía nombrar ya habían sido extinguidas o vivían como refugiadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That leaves the palace almost entirely undefended. There will be a handful of guards left, but that's it."
msgstr "Eso deja el palacio casi totalmente indefenso. Habrá un puñado de guardias que queden, pero nada más."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That leaves you with only your own."
msgstr "Eso te deja solo con la tuya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That lithe frame, mixed with the strong muscles, hers was truly a body in its prime."
msgstr "Esa esbelta figura, combinada con sus fuertes músculos, era verdaderamente un cuerpo en su plenitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That little?"
msgstr "¿Tan poco?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That long, without food?"
msgstr "¿Tan largo, sin comer?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That long?"
msgstr "¿Tan largo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "That looked like a nasty fall."
msgstr "Eso pareció una caída fea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That looked more natural on him than the nervousness."
msgstr "Eso le quedaba más natural que la nerviosidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "That looks decent enough."
msgstr "Eso se ve bastante bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That magical pulse. Don't tell me you can't feel it?"
msgstr "Ese pulso mágico. No me digas que no puedes sentirlo."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That makes sense"
msgstr "Eso tiene sentido"

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That makes sense. I really should have figured that out myself."
msgstr "Tiene sentido. Debería haberlo descubierto yo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That makes sense...I think."
msgstr "- Tiene sentido... creo que sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "That man...that man that served you your drink, and your food, he used to be little more than a farmhand and a thief."
msgstr "Ese hombre... ese hombre que te sirvió la bebida y la comida, solía ser poco más que un jornalero y un ladrón."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That many."
msgstr "Tantas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That many?"
msgstr "¿Tan muchos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That maybe if we picked up on where we left off years ago, I could be all quiet like about it."
msgstr "Tal vez si retomamos donde nos dejamos hace años, podría hablar de ello con absoluta tranquilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That means I'll take you on as an apprentice."
msgstr "Eso significa que te tomaré como aprendiz."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "That means leaving everyone except the capital, defenseless. If Hassar avoids the capital, and attacks another district, they'll only have women and children to defend themselves."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "That means no fights. No drugs. No trouble."
msgstr "Eso significa sin peleas. Sin drogas. Sin problemas."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That means they were there when the old Empire fell."
msgstr "Eso significa que estaban allí cuando el antiguo Imperio cayó."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That means you must govern not just from your heart, but also from what is right for the country."
msgstr "Eso significa que debes gobernar no solo desde tu corazón, sino también desde lo que es correcto para el país."

msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Prince"
msgid "That means you're free to leave. Even if I suspect you probably killed more than a few of my men."
msgstr "Eso significa que estás libre de irte. Incluso si sospecho que probablemente hayas matado a más de unos cuantos de mis hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That meant bringing them over to her side. For some that was inspiring their hearts, but for many more it was simply filling their greed and urges."
msgstr "Eso significaba atraerlos a su lado. Para algunos, eso era inspirar sus corazones; pero para muchos más, simplemente llenar su codicia y sus impulsos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That men were of such nature, and women of another nature, and this justified all the ways in which they were treated differently."
msgstr "Que los hombres eran de tal naturaleza y las mujeres de otra, lo cual justificaba todas las formas en que eran tratados de manera distinta."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "That might last you longer than you think."
msgstr "Eso podría durarte más de lo que crees."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That might not mean anything to you, but it does to me."
msgstr "Eso quizás no tenga ningún significado para ti, pero sí para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That moment is now, in this place..."
msgstr "Ese momento es ahora, en este lugar..."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That moment on the balcony just keeps haunting me and I can't do anything about it!"
msgstr "¡Ese momento en la terraza simplemente me persigue y no puedo hacer nada al respecto!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That moment when all she needed to do was be present, for him."
msgstr "Ese momento en el que todo lo que necesitaba era estar presente por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That money would be far better spend on the needy."
msgstr "Ese dinero se gastaría mucho mejor en los necesitados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That morning she had awoken as a princess, and before the sun had fully set, she was now a slave."
msgstr "Esa mañana despertó como una princesa, y antes de que el sol se hubiera puesto del todo, ya era una puta esclava."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That moron!"
msgstr "¡Ese imbécil!"

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "That much is clear, but why did you lose? Why are you now offering your body to the man that destroyed your nation?"
msgstr "Eso está claro, pero ¿por qué perdiste? ¿Por qué ahora ofreces tu cuerpo al hombre que destruyó tu nación?"

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That much is probably true. I'll go and see about uniform, give me a moment."
msgstr "Eso probablemente sea cierto. Iré a ver por el uniforme, dame un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That much is true."
msgstr "Eso es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That much was the truth."
msgstr "Eso era la verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That much, Sarah knew to be true. For every king and emperor in her world, there were millions who simply toiled away their lives."
msgstr "Eso, Sarah, lo sabía con certeza. Por cada rey y emperador en su mundo, había millones que simplemente vivían esclavizados."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "That nobody really knows what they're doing. No truly."
msgstr "Nadie realmente sabe lo que hace. Ni siquiera eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That nobody would ever know how she had given in to him."
msgstr "Nadie jamás sabría cómo se entregó a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That obnoxious booming laugh of his."
msgstr "Esa risa estruendosa y molesta de él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That once, rivers flowed and carried with them life. Fields of grass and grain, spoiling the citizens of the nation with plenty."
msgstr "Que una vez, los ríos fluían y llevaban consigo la vida. Campos de hierba y grano, que abastecían a los ciudadanos de la nación con abundancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That one over, not under. The rope gets pulled up this way, and leans across that part. You wrap them up, you risk it snapping at high winds."
msgstr "Esa, no aquella. La cuerda se tira hacia este lado y se apoya sobre esa parte. Si la ajustas mal, corre el riesgo de romperse con el viento fuerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "That one was a deviant as well. I got rid of it."
msgstr "Ese también era un deviante. Lo eliminé."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That over there was the town square, but you might a figured that out."
msgstr "Aquella era la plaza del pueblo, pero probablemente ya lo habías deducido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That part also belonged to him."
msgstr "Esa parte también le pertenecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That part was clearly virile."
msgstr "Esa parte era claramente viril."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That people could live so freely...and confusingly...it was a lot for her to make sense of."
msgstr "Que la gente pudiera vivir tan libremente... y de manera tan confusa... era mucho para ella intentar comprender."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That perhaps it was as simple as the fact that she wanted him, no other conditions."
msgstr "Tal vez fuera tan sencillo como el hecho de que lo deseaba, sin más condiciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That place had nothing left for me."
msgstr "Ese lugar ya no tenía nada para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That place was no doubt dangerous. Going in at dark was not something she was planning for."
msgstr "Ese lugar era sin duda peligroso. Meterse en la oscuridad no era algo que estuviera planeando hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That poor peasant girl, whipped on your command."
msgstr "¡Esa pobre muchacha campesina, azotada por tu orden!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That power, his iron muscles, the way he could so easily throw her around, thinking about it, Sarah felt herself get wet."
msgstr "Ese poder, sus músculos de hierro, la forma en que podía lanzarla alrededor con tanta facilidad; pensándolo bien, Sarah sintió cómo se le mojaba el coño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That promise, of war, then comfort, had now been crudely violated by Vaelen."
msgstr "Esa promesa de guerra, luego de consuelo, había sido ahora crudamente violada por Vaelen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That reminded her. She had been so busy lately, she had let her prayers slip."
msgstr "Eso la recordó. Llevaba tanto ocupada últimamente que había dejado de rezar."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That reminds me, I need to get one of my tools from the cabin, that will make it easier to show you."
msgstr "Eso me recuerda; necesito ir a la cabina por una de mis herramientas, que facilitará mostrártelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That rough and violent desire, mixed with that arrogant disregard that he had for her."
msgstr "Ese deseo rudo y violento, mezclado con ese desprecio arrogante que él tenía para con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same brutal winter landscape that had ruined her last time."
msgstr "Ese mismo brutal paisaje invernal que la arruinó la última vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same false smile. Those same cruel eyes."
msgstr "Esa misma falsa sonrisa. Esos mismos ojos crueles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That same night, they also murdered every remote branch of that family."
msgstr "Esa misma noche, también exterminaron cada rama distante de esa familia."

msgctxt "speaker:Shah Mahda"
msgid "That seems to be about all I ever purchased from you, despite everything."
msgstr "Parece que eso es todo lo que he comprado de ti, a pesar de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That seems to fit."
msgstr "Eso parece adecuado."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "That settles the matter of Hassar and the desert tribes. What is left on the agenda for today?"
msgstr "Eso resuelve el asunto de Hassar y las tribus del desierto. ¿Qué queda en la agenda para hoy?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That sex between a husband and a wife, like all skills, was one honed over time."
msgstr "Ese sexo entre un marido y una mujer, como todas las habilidades, se perfeccionaba con el tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That shame will follow your family's name until the end of times."
msgstr "Esa vergüenza perseguirá el nombre de tu familia hasta el fin de los tiempos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she could manipulate him."
msgstr "Que pudiera manipularlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she had lost something that had never been hers to begin with?"
msgstr "¿Que había perdido algo que nunca le había pertenecido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she had permission."
msgstr "Que tenía permiso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she would do anything, literally anything, if it meant that he might call her that again."
msgstr "Que haría cualquier cosa, literalmente cualquier cosa, si eso significaba que él pudiera volver a llamarla así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she would take off her clothes and reveal nothing other than her ordinary body."
msgstr "que se quitara la ropa y no revelara nada más que su cuerpo ordinario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That she, the young and beautiful woman, was like a gift to the old man, for which he should be grateful."
msgstr "que ella, la joven y hermosa mujer, era como un regalo para el viejo, por lo que debería estar agradecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That smells amazing!"
msgstr "¡Qué huele increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That somehow sounds even worse."
msgstr "Eso suena incluso peor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That somehow, despite everything she knew about him, he would prove a hero."
msgstr "De alguna manera, a pesar de todo lo que sabía sobre él, se demostraría un héroe."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds awful."
msgstr "Eso suena terrible."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That sounds familiar."
msgstr "Eso suena familiar."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That sounds horrible."
msgstr "Suena terrible."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds horrible."
msgstr "Suena horrible."

msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "That sounds like a problem for the two of you."
msgstr "Suena como un problema para los dos."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "That sounds nice."
msgstr "Suena bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That sounds nice."
msgstr "Suena bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That sounds pretty bleak."
msgstr "Suena bastante sombrío."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That stuf...was..."
msgstr "Esa cosa... fue..."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That such a flower should belong to another family, when it looks so good on you."
msgstr "Que una flor tan hermosa pertenezca a otra familia, cuando te queda tan bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That summer, shipment after shipment of grain arrived in the nearby town, collapsing the price."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the death of their Khan had caused them to fall back to infighting."
msgstr "Que la muerte de su Kan les hubiera llevado a caer en una lucha interna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the one true ambition of Maeiv had been this last and final proposal."
msgstr "Que la única verdadera ambición de Maeiv había sido esta última y definitiva propuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That the real work was done in the shadows."
msgstr "que el verdadero trabajo se realiza en las sombras."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "That there is Edgar."
msgstr "Que ahí está Edgar."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "That there is Pale Eclips, what I use for my cartography."
msgstr "Ahí está Pale Eclips, lo que uso para mi cartografía."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "That there is a proper glass of wine. Or at least as proper as you're going to find in these here slums."
msgstr "Eso es un buen vaso de vino. O al menos tan bueno como podrás encontrar en estos barrios bajos."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That there is shoreline."
msgstr "Ahí está la costa."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That there is the last housing block that is still standing."
msgstr "Que allí se alzaba el último bloque de viviendas que aún estaba en pie."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That there was some part of herself that didn't fully live in this world."
msgstr "Que había una parte de sí misma que no vivía completamente en este mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That there would be more here than mere lust."
msgstr "Que aquí hubiera más que mera lujuria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they could make so much money off just one cart seemed absurd to Sarah."
msgstr "Que pudieran ganar tanto dinero con solo un carrito parecía absurdo para Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they were not all so different, and that they likewise lived upon the edge between surviving and ruin."
msgstr "Que no eran todos tan diferentes, y que también vivían al borde de la supervivencia y la ruina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That they were somehow the same."
msgstr "Que de alguna manera eran los mismos."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "That time it was one of the carpenter's apprentices. Boy lost his entire left hand but at least he lived to tell about it."
msgstr "Esa vez fue uno de los aprendices del carpintero. El muchacho perdió toda la mano izquierda, pero al menos sobrevivió para contarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That time passed, she could only faintly tell because the light of the sun slowly turned and then darkened."
msgstr "Ese momento pasó, y ella apenas pudo percibirlo porque la luz del sol giró lentamente y luego se oscureció."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That time will come."
msgstr "Ese momento llegará."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That title of yours...the Silent Queen...I don't think it fits."
msgstr "Ese título tuyo... la Reina Silenciosa... no creo que te quede bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That too, but I also think you got potential."
msgstr "Eso también, pero creo que tienes potencial."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "That trade official was a big softy, but plenty of those people up there are ruthless."
msgstr "Ese funcionario de comercio era un tierno, pero muchos de los que están arriba son implacables."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That type of stuff should be between people that love each other. I don't love you."
msgstr "Ese tipo de cosas debería estar entre personas que se aman. No te amo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That underneath all the pretense and protocol, the world, and the people in it, are reduced to their nature."
msgstr "Bajo toda la pretensión y el protocolo, el mundo y sus habitantes se reducen a su verdadera naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "That understanding ultimately led me to...well, you know our history."
msgstr "Esa comprensión finalmente me llevó a... bueno, conoces nuestra historia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That use also no longer mattered."
msgstr "Que usar ya no importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was Atilla to her. The surface, and the deeper version of him. The real truth that only she knew about."
msgstr "Eso era Atilla para ella. La superficie y la versión más profunda de él. La verdad real que solo ella conocía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was a dangerous thing in a place like this."
msgstr "Eso era peligroso en un lugar como este."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was a lifetime ago."
msgstr "Eso fue hace una eternidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was about all that she could say for it. No luxury. Nothing that made it seem like there was any personal touch to it."
msgstr "Eso era todo lo que se podía decir al respecto. Sin lujos, nada que hiciera parecer que había algún toque personal en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was about all there was to the sparsely decorated room."
msgstr "Eso era todo lo que había en la habitación, escasamente decorada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was all it took. And in return he would give her so much more."
msgstr "Eso era todo lo que necesitaba. Y a cambio, él le daría mucho más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was an idea that did seem to appeal to her."
msgstr "Esa era una idea que parecía gustarle."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was an insane amount of money for anything, let alone a drink."
msgstr "Ese era un monto de dinero insano para cualquier cosa, y mucho menos para una bebida."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That was back then. We ain't doin nothing you don't wanna do now."
msgstr "Eso fue entonces. Ahora no hacemos nada que tú no quieras hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was before they went to war with the Mythran empire, centuries ago."
msgstr "Antes de que se declarara la guerra contra el imperio Mythran, hace siglos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was enough for her."
msgstr "Eso fue suficiente para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was essentially all of it. From a princess, down to this."
msgstr "Eso era esencialmente todo. Desde una princesa, hasta esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was far from how the people of Rosanna lived."
msgstr "Eso estaba lejos de cómo vivían las personas de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was her weapon, she realized. The means by which she could bend a man like him to her own will."
msgstr "Eso era su arma, se dio cuenta. El medio por el cual podía doblar a un hombre como él a su propia voluntad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was him, she thought. Those two parts, the desire mixed in with his hesitant tenderness."
msgstr "Eso era él, pensó. Aquellas dos partes: el deseo mezclado con su tierna vacilación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was his curse, Sarah thought. If her brother had simply not cared, or been lazier, he wouldn't have demanded so much from himself. He wouldn't push himself this hard."
msgstr "Eso era su maldición, pensó Sarah. Si su hermano no le hubiera importado o se hubiera mostrado más perezoso, no habría exigido tanto de sí mismo. No se habría empujado tan fuerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Eso era todo, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it, she realized."
msgstr "Eso era todo, lo comprendió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was it. Her one ally. Her one resource."
msgstr "Eso era todo. Su única aliada. Su único recurso."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That was it. That abominable mage..."
msgstr "Eso era todo. Ese abominable mago..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That was just...foolishness, captain."
msgstr "Eso fue simplemente... locura, capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That was more than five years ago. I thought they had killed the entire royal family."
msgstr "Eso fue hace más de cinco años. Creí que habían matado a toda la familia real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was one thing about soldiers, Sarah thought, at least they knew to keep to themselves."
msgstr "Eso era una de las cosas que tenían los soldados, pensó Sarah: al menos sabían callarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was something she could give him, she had decided."
msgstr "Eso era algo que podía darle a él, había decidido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That was something..."
msgstr "Eso era algo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the life she had been preparing for back then. The game of politics."
msgstr "Eso era la vida para la que había estado preparándose en aquel entonces. El juego de las políticas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the not the wound that a soldier might have given her. It was more like something a wild animal might do."
msgstr "Eso no era la herida que un soldado podría haberle infligido. Era más bien algo que haría una bestia salvaje."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was the only fraction of comfort she had. The knowledge that the creature would pay, in time."
msgstr "Esa fue la única fracción de consuelo que tenía. El conocimiento de que la criatura pagaría, con el tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was their biggest difference, Sarah knew."
msgstr "Esa era su mayor diferencia, lo sabía Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That was true when you found me in the alley too."
msgstr "Eso era cierto cuando me encontraste en el callejón también."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was true, but Sarah also knew what Samayra likely hinted at."
msgstr "Eso era cierto, pero Sarah también sabía lo que Samayra probablemente insinuaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was until its ruler, Shah Mahda, had accidentally caused the death of a Mythran prince during a fight at a party."
msgstr "Eso fue hasta que su gobernante, Shah Mahda, causó accidentalmente la muerte de un príncipe Mythran durante una pelea en una fiesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was what all these nights had done to her. He had trained her, and unknowingly, she had allowed herself to be trained to his desires."
msgstr "Eso fue lo que todas esas noches hicieron con ella. Él la entrenó, e inconscientemente, ella permitió ser moldeada a sus deseos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was what passed for privacy and politeness."
msgstr "Eso es lo que se entendía por privacidad y cortesía."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "That was why I could never bring myself to ask you."
msgstr "Eso es por lo que nunca pude obligarme a preguntártelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was worse."
msgstr "Eso fue peor."

msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "That was years ago."
msgstr "Eso fue hace años."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That was, until Xan told Sarah that they were going to offer the city their protection."
msgstr "Eso fue, hasta que Xan le dijo a Sarah que iban a ofrecer a la ciudad su protección."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That was, until a thought came to her."
msgstr "Eso fue, hasta que le vino un pensamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That was...how did you do that?"
msgstr "Eso fue... ¿cómo lo hiciste?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That was...something else."
msgstr "Eso fue... otra cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That wasn't funny!"
msgstr "¡Eso no era gracioso!"

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That wasn't my fault!"
msgstr "¡No fue mi culpa!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That way that only he could make her feel."
msgstr "De esa manera que solo él podía hacerla sentir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That way, no matter what, I will be safe."
msgstr "De esa manera, sin importar qué, estaré segura."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "That we as leaders of our respective nations are bound to uphold a duty to our people."
msgstr "Que como líderes de nuestras respectivas naciones tenemos el deber de cumplir con nuestro pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That we can do."
msgstr "Eso podemos lograr."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "That we do. A few open actually, there is a nice one that has a view of the plaza outside."
msgstr "Eso haremos. Hay algunas abiertas, de hecho; hay una bonita con vista a la plaza exterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That whatever this latest act is, it comes only after a long series of debasements."
msgstr "Sea cual sea este último acto, solo llega tras una larga serie de humillaciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That whole attitude. Acting like I can't fuck you whenever and whatever way I want."
msgstr "Esa actitud de todo. Actuar como si no pudiera follarte cuando y como quiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "That will bring a child of whose claim to power is legitimate in strength, as well as in blood."
msgstr "Eso traerá un hijo cuya reclamación al poder sea legítima tanto en fuerza como en sangre."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That will give me enough votes to secure what I wanted regardless."
msgstr "Eso me dará suficientes votos para asegurar lo que deseaba de todos modos."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That will keep him in check. Make sure he gets no ideas. So he remembers whose in charge on this ship."
msgstr "Eso lo mantendrá a raya. Asegúrate de que no se le ocurran ideas. Así recordará quién manda en este barco."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That will likely slow us down."
msgstr "Eso probablemente nos retrasará."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "That will take us into the inner palace grounds."
msgstr "Eso nos llevará a las tierras del palacio interior."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That won't be enough!"
msgstr "¡Eso no será suficiente!"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That won't be necessary blondie."
msgstr "No será necesario, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "That won't do."
msgstr "Eso no funcionará."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That won't work. My nature is not quite so similar."
msgstr "No funcionará. Mi naturaleza no es tan parecida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "That would be Gallow's Creek."
msgstr "Eso sería el Arroyo de los Cadáveres."

msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "That would be a good start."
msgstr "Eso sería un buen comienzo."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "That would be much appreciated."
msgstr "Eso sería muy apreciado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That wouldn't have been a problem if we had reached our destination by now."
msgstr "Eso no habría sido un problema si ya hubiéramos llegado a nuestro destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That ya did, blondie."
msgstr "Eso sí que hiciste, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That you are hurting them. Is it on purpose?"
msgstr "Que los estás lastimando. ¿Es a propósito?"

msgctxt "speaker:Kamal"
msgid "That you are just! You are rightious and kind! You will do what is right!"
msgstr "¡Eres justo! ¡Tienes razón y eres bondadosa! ¡Harás lo que es justo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "That you are your father's daughter."
msgstr "Eres la hija de tu padre."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That you are."
msgstr "Eso eres tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "That you murdered Xan."
msgstr "Que has matado a Xan."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That you were always going to be like this."
msgstr "Que siempre lo fuiste, maldita sea."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That you were dangerous."
msgstr "Que eras peligrosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That you're disgusting. Fat. Old. A pervert."
msgstr "Que eres repugnante. Gorda. Vieja. Pervertida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That you're not as prim and proper as you like to pretend."
msgstr "Que no eres tan casta y correcta como te gusta fingir."

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "That you, Marius?"
msgstr "¿Tú, Marius?"

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "That young man was no warrior. He would have died regardless. Now he lives."
msgstr "Ese joven no era un guerrero. Habría muerto de todos modos. Ahora vive."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "That's Synara and her cronies."
msgstr "Eso son Synara y sus secuaces."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's Thomas."
msgstr "Ese es Thomas."

msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "That's a decent start."
msgstr "Eso es un buen comienzo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's a good girl."
msgstr "Eres una buena chica."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That's a good thing."
msgstr "Eso es algo bueno."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's a lie, and you know it."
msgstr "Mentira, y lo sabes."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "That's a new look for you."
msgstr "Eso es un nuevo aspecto para ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "That's a nice phrase, but it doesn't change reality."
msgstr "Esa es una frase bonita, pero no cambia la realidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's a nice thought."
msgstr "Esa es una idea bonita."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That's a promise."
msgstr "Eso es una promesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That's a side branch to the main road."
msgstr "Ese es un ramal de la carretera principal."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's a storage room."
msgstr "Es un almacén."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That's a strong name."
msgstr "Ese es un nombre potente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's a very kind offer. I'd be happy to accept."
msgstr "Eso es una oferta muy amable. Con gusto la acepto."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's about it."
msgstr "Eso es todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "That's about when the food stores will be running low, and I don't want to be here when this city starts starving."
msgstr "Eso es justo cuando los suministros de comida empezarán a escasear, y no quiero estar aquí cuando esta ciudad comience a pasar hambre."

msgctxt "speaker:Male Soldier"
msgid "That's all I wanted to hear from you."
msgstr "Eso es todo lo que quería oír de ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's all we can do really, Ephraim. Promise to do for each other what we wish we could do for ourselves."
msgstr "Eso es todo lo que podemos hacer realmente, Efraim. Promete hacer por el otro lo que anhelamos no poder hacer por nosotros mismos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That's alright, I was only offering."
msgstr "Está bien, solo lo ofrecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That's alright. I'm sure you're a fast learner, the captain speaks highly of you."
msgstr "No te preocupes. Estoy seguro de que aprendes rápido, el capitán está encantado contigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "That's also why I don't really like to talk about it."
msgstr "Eso es también por lo que no me gusta hablar de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's always your answer to everything."
msgstr "Siempre es tu respuesta a todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "That's an interesting choice. But I'm not sure that Xan would approve."
msgstr "Esa es una elección interesante. Pero no estoy segura de que Xan apruebe."

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "That's better."
msgstr "Eso es mejor."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's bullshit."
msgstr "¡Eso es una puta mierda!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "That's cause they see me talkin to ya."
msgstr "Eso es porque ven que hablo contigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That's definitely true."
msgstr "Eso es absolutamente cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That's enough for today. Don't want to fry your brain."
msgstr "Eso es suficiente por hoy. No quiero que te queme el cerebro."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That's exactly it..."
msgstr "Eso es exactamente lo que quería decir..."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That's fair."
msgstr "Eso es justo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "That's fair. Any other?"
msgstr "Eso es justo. ¿Algún otro?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's fast."
msgstr "Eso es rápido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's fine, I was really hoping to talk to you."
msgstr "Eso está bien, de verdad esperaba poder hablar contigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That's fine, I'll lead!"
msgstr "¡Eso está bien, yo iré adelante!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's fine, I'm not a difficult eater."
msgstr "Eso está bien, no soy una glotona difícil."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's fine, Xan. Thank you for telling me all this. I've never heard of it before."
msgstr "Eso está bien, Xan. Gracias por contármelo todo. Nunca había oído hablar de eso antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "That's fine, it took quite a while for all of us to settle here, but in time we made it work."
msgstr "Eso está bien, tardó un buen tiempo en que todos nos acomodáramos aquí, pero con el tiempo logramos hacerlo funcionar."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That's fine, you can let me know how you want them handled and I can finish them up."
msgstr "Está bien, puedes decirme cómo quieres que los maneje y yo terminaré con ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's fine."
msgstr "Eso está bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "That's for spinning up the back valve, it can let the ship load on water in the lower hull. Slows the speed, but when the ocean gets rowdy, it makes the ship more stable."
msgstr "Eso es para activar la válvula trasera; permite que el barco cargue agua en la parte inferior de la quilla. Reduce la velocidad, pero cuando el océano se pone revuelto, hace que el barco sea más estable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's gonna go on your review. Does poorly with authority and doesn't know when to keep his mouth closed."
msgstr "Eso irá en tu evaluación. Le va mal con la autoridad y no sabe cuándo cerrar la boca."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's good, right?"
msgstr "Eso es bueno, ¿verdad?"

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "That's good."
msgstr "Eso es bueno."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's good."
msgstr "Eso es bueno."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That's good...but it's also..."
msgstr "Eso es bueno... pero también es..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's gotta be at least a few days worth."
msgstr "Eso tiene que ser al menos unos días."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "That's great news!"
msgstr "¡Qué gran noticia!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's great. About all I was used to drinking back in Rosanna."
msgstr "Eso es genial. Lo único a lo que estaba acostumbrada al beber en Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's home. Yeah, for me that's what I think of when I remembered Rosanna all those years."
msgstr "Eso es mi hogar. Sí, para mí eso es lo que pienso cuando recuerdo Rosanna todos esos años."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That's horrible."
msgstr "Eso es horrible."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's horrible."
msgstr "Eso es horrible."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's how I go through life, I don't make excuses and I don't lie. I am who I am, simple as that."
msgstr "Así es como vivo, no hago excusas y no miento. Soy quien soy, tan sencillo como eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's how it usually goes though."
msgstr "Pero eso es lo que suele ocurrir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's insane..."
msgstr "Eso es insano..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That's it, keep going!"
msgstr "¡Eso es, sigue así!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That's it."
msgstr "Eso es."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's it?"
msgstr "¿Eso es todo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's it? So simple?"
msgstr "¿Eso es todo? ¿Tan sencillo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's it? That's the story you want to go with?"
msgstr "¿Es eso todo? ¿Esa es la historia con la que quieres quedarte?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's it? This everything you earn in a day?"
msgstr "¿Eso es todo? ¿Todo lo que ganas en un día?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's just a polite way of saying morose."
msgstr "¿Eso es solo una forma educada de decir que estás deprimido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That's just about the only time he ever talks about himself."
msgstr "Esa es la única vez que habla de sí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's just called gettin hustled, Blondie."
msgstr "Eso se llama ser estafado, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That's just like the door from my family vault!"
msgstr "¡Eso es igual que la puerta de mi bóveda familiar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That's low."
msgstr "Eso es sucio."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's my Blondie, always such a smart head on her shoulders."
msgstr "¡Esa es mi rubia, siempre tan lista con esa cabeza en sus hombros!"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's my Blondie, now get on all fours."
msgstr "Esa es mi rubia, ahora ponete a cuatro patas."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That's my fault for depressing you with my stories. I always drink too much when I'm sad."
msgstr "Es mi culpa por entristecerte con mis historias. Siempre bebo demasiado cuando estoy triste."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "That's my girl."
msgstr "Eres mi niña."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's my girl."
msgstr "Eres mi niña."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "That's my home, right over there."
msgstr "Eso es mi hogar, justo allí al fondo."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's my kind heart."
msgstr "Eso es mi corazón ardiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's my problem, I guess. Still figuring that out."
msgstr "Eso es mi problema, supongo. Todavía lo estoy resolviendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's nice of you to say, but you're going to have to do better than flattery if you want to repay me."
msgstr "Eso es muy amable de tu parte, pero tendrás que hacer más que halagos si quieres pagarme."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's no way to greet an old friend."
msgstr "No es así como se saluda a un viejo amigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Merchant"
msgid "That's not a serious price, come on lady!"
msgstr "Eso no es un precio serio, ¡venga, señora!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not fair, you didn't-"
msgstr "¡Eso no es justo, tú no..."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "That's not funny Sarah, they'd whip me if anyone heard you."
msgstr "Eso no es gracioso, Sarah; si alguien lo oyera, me azotarán."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "That's not funny."
msgstr "No es gracioso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not happening."
msgstr "Eso no va a pasar."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "That's not how I meant it."
msgstr "No es así como lo quise decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not how I recall it. Wasn't it the other way around?"
msgstr "No es así como lo recuerdo. ¿No fue al revés?"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's not how I remember it."
msgstr "Eso no es como lo recuerdo."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That's not luck, that's fate. Fate brought you right to my doorstep."
msgstr "Eso no es suerte, eso es destino. El destino te trajo directamente a mi puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "That's not my story to tell, Sarah. If I did, he'd kill me."
msgstr "Esa no es mi historia para contarla, Sarah. Si lo hiciera, me mataría."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "That's not possible, commander."
msgstr "Eso no es posible, comandante."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not true, he's lying!"
msgstr "¡No es cierto, ¡está mintiendo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not true."
msgstr "No es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's not true. He told me how difficult it was, growing up under his father. How nothing he ever did was good enough."
msgstr "No es cierto. Me contó lo difícil que fue crecer bajo la tutela de su padre. Cómo nada de lo que hacía jamás era suficiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "That's not what I meant!"
msgstr "¡Eso no es lo que quise decir!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That's not why I'm here Sarah."
msgstr "Eso no es por qué estoy aquí, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Barion"
msgid "That's not your concern, my lady. Please, allow these men to escort you back to your room. I promise no harm will come to you."
msgstr "No es de su incumbencia, mi señora. Por favor, permita que estos hombres la escolten de vuelta a su habitación. Prometo que no le ocurrirá ningún daño."

msgctxt "speaker:Robber"
msgid "That's one way of resolving this. How about I tell you my way, grandpa?"
msgstr "Eso es una forma de resolver esto. ¿Qué te parece si te cuento mi manera, abuelo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That's perhaps a story best left for another time."
msgstr "Eso es quizás una historia mejor dejada para otra ocasión."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "That's politics, and I don't know anything about that."
msgstr "Esa es política, y no sé nada de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's pretty impressive, but I already know how to levitate."
msgstr "¡Eso es realmente impresionante, pero ya sé cómo elevarme!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's really your question?"
msgstr "¿Eso es realmente tu pregunta?"

msgctxt "speaker:Damian"
msgid "That's rich."
msgstr "Qué gracioso."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That's right my dear. It's a man's world we're forced to live in, but where would they really be without us."
msgstr "¡Así es, mi amor! Es un mundo de hombres en el que estamos obligadas a vivir, pero ¿dónde estarían ellos sin nosotras?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "That's right, and I promised I was gonna fuck that attitude out of you. Didn't I?"
msgstr "Eso es cierto, y te prometí que iba a follarte esa actitud hasta sacártela. ¿No lo hice?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right, now stop hovering. Day's work only just started."
msgstr "¡Exacto! Ahora deja de acechar. El trabajo del día apenas ha comenzado."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right, so go above deck to the helm and bring me back my map, hurry up!"
msgstr "¡Exacto! ¡Ve al puente de mando y tráeme mi mapa, ¡prisa!"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right, so go above deck to the helm and bring me back my map, now!"
msgstr "¡Exacto! Sube al puente de mando y tráeme mi mapa, ¡ya mismo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "That's right, you get on now lad. Ain't nothin worse than someone whose late or lazy."
msgstr "Eso es, sube ahora, muchacho. No hay nada peor que alguien que llega tarde o que se hace el vago."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "That's right, you have never been here. Such a shame, I really should have invited you sooner."
msgstr "Eso es cierto, nunca has estado aquí. Qué pena, realmente debí haberte invitado antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Eso es."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Eso es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Exacto."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Eso es correcto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Eso es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Eso es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right. A whore would be gettin paid to fuck me. You just do it for free."
msgstr "¡Exacto! Una puta se cobraría por follarme, pero tú lo haces gratis."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right. And I am?"
msgstr "Eso es cierto. Y yo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "That's right. And captain Belmont doesn't share."
msgstr "Eso es cierto. Y el capitán Belmont no comparte."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's right. It's going to be just as before, when I would read father's books, and tell you the important parts. Working together, as a brother and sister should."
msgstr "Eso es cierto. Será exactamente como antes, cuando leía los libros de mi padre y te contaba las partes importantes. Trabajando juntos, como lo harían un hermano y una hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "That's right. Proud owner of this fine establishment."
msgstr "¡Exacto! Dueña orgullosa de este famoso local."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "That's right. So you think making me queen is your final punishment?"
msgstr "Es cierto. ¿Entonces crees que hacerme reina es tu castigo final?"

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "That's right. You don't got any talents or skills."
msgstr "Eso es cierto. No tienes ningún talento ni habilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
