msgstr "Entonces, el súbito y rápido gemido, la creciente presión en sus manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, the thing's tail sprung like a coil, launching itself towards her."
msgstr "Entonces, la cola de la cosa se soltó como un resorte y se lanzó hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, the trumpets blared and the servants pulled open the door."
msgstr "Entonces, sonaron estruendosamente las trompetas y los sirvientes abrieron la puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Then, the truth of the situation will be brought to light, and he can receive a fitting punishment."
msgstr "Entonces, la verdad de la situación será revelada y él recibirá un castigo merecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, the very earth beneath her feet began to twist and move."
msgstr "Entonces, la tierra misma bajo sus pies comenzó a torcerse y moverse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, the world went dark."
msgstr "Entonces, el mundo se sumió en la oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, their horses broke course."
msgstr "Entonces, sus caballos desviaron el curso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, they struck her like lightining."
msgstr "Entonces, la golpearon como un rayo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, to Sarah's surprise, he fell down to his knees."
msgstr "Entonces, para sorpresa de Sarah, él se arrodilló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, to her own surprise, she saw a familiar face in the crowd."
msgstr "Entonces, para su propia sorpresa, vio un rostro familiar en la multitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, upon the reshaped essence, imprint a will or a meaning, expressed in word, thought and movement."
msgstr "Entonces, sobre la esencia reconfigurada, imprime una voluntad o un significado, expresado en palabra, pensamiento y movimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, uttering her last command to fire the trebuchets, Sarah saw the wall break."
msgstr "Entonces, con creciente entusiasmo, al pronunciar su última orden para disparar los trabucos, Sarah vio cómo la pared se rompía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, very slowly, his body drifted back down to the floor."
msgstr "Entonces, muy lentamente, su cuerpo se deslizó de nuevo hacia el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Then, when I saw you jump onto this one, I realized that it was one of the last ships to depart."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando te vi saltar en esta, me di cuenta de que era uno de los últimos barcos que partían."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "Then, when both sides have weakened one another, we shall end the both of them."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando ambas partes se hayan debilitado mutuamente, acabaremos con ambos."

msgctxt "speaker:Ayaka"
msgid "Then, when the first frontier unit was wiped out, they suddenly claimed they needed to perform a tactical retreat beyond the mountain pass."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando la primera unidad fronteriza fue aniquilada, de repente afirmaron que necesitaban ejecutar una retirada táctica más allá del paso de montaña."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, when the last group moved out, she saw the perfect opportunity."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando el último grupo se retiró, ella vio la oportunidad perfecta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, when the years turned, she had instead imagined that it was forever lost to her, and she would never see her homeland again."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando los años se convirtieron en un recuerdo, ella había imaginado que lo había perdido para siempre y jamás volvería a ver su tierra natal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, when they were both spend, they would fall into deep sleep."
msgstr "Entonces, cuando ambos estuvieran exhaustos, caerían en un sueño profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with a final push, she felt her mouth part."
msgstr "Entonces, con un último empujón, sintió cómo se le abría la boca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with a loud clicking noise, he unbound the chains that had kept her."
msgstr "Entonces, con un estruendoso ruido de clic, él desató las cadenas que la habían retenido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with a swift motion, brought her body down on him."
msgstr "Entonces, con un movimiento rápido, la hizo bajar su cuerpo sobre él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with creaking metal, the door slowly swung open."
msgstr "Entonces, con un crujido de metal, la puerta se abrió lentamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with little resistance, pressed deeper down into her throat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then, with that same ease, she released the energy."
msgstr "Entonces, con la misma facilidad, liberó la energía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then. The impact."
msgstr "Entonces. El impacto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Then..."
msgstr "Entonces..."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Then...I would join you."
msgstr "Entonces... me uniré a ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Then...I'll trust you."
msgstr "Entonces... confiaré en ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Then...all our lives...are already determined?"
msgstr "Entonces... ¿nuestras vidas... ya están determinadas?"

msgctxt "speaker:High Priest"
msgid "Then...by all the Gods...I crown you...Queen Sarah Rose."
msgstr "Entonces... por todos los dioses... te corono... Reina Sarah Rose."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Then...one night, someone told me that there was a branch of magic called Daemonology."
msgstr "Entonces... una noche, alguien me dijo que existía una rama de la magia llamada demonología."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then...then just..."
msgstr "Entonces... entonces solo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Then...where are they?"
msgstr "¿Dónde están?"

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "There I found again the challenges that I had been seeking. And I felt my life bloom again."
msgstr "Allí encontré de nuevo los desafíos que había estado buscando y sentí que mi vida florecía otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There are a few bodies in the rooms, male servants that were trying to hide."
msgstr "Hay unos cuantos cuerpos en las habitaciones, sirvientes masculinos que intentaban esconderse."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are a lot of other things we could do for fun."
msgstr "Hay muchas otras cosas que podríamos hacer por diversión."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There are countless from Rosanna here, refugees. There are countless more, scattered across the world."
msgstr "Hay innumerables de Rosanna aquí, refugiadas. Hay muchísimas más, dispersas por todo el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There are different faces in the crowd, but she can know these men by their gazes."
msgstr "Hay rostros distintos en la multitud, pero ella puede reconocer a estos hombres por sus miradas."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "There are entire industries in places like Medini where one can only operate if they are from the right family."
msgstr "Hay industrias enteras en lugares como Medini donde solo se puede operar si se pertenece a la familia adecuada."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There are fates quite a degree worse than death that can be encountered in this field."
msgstr "Hay destinos mucho peores que la muerte que se pueden encontrar en este campo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are few in this world that I would put above you in military skill, or even simply as a warrior in your own right."
msgstr "Hay pocos en este mundo que pondría por encima de ti en habilidad militar, o incluso simplemente como guerrera en tu propio derecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "There are four girls here, five with you now."
msgstr "Hay cuatro chicas aquí, cinco contigo ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There are freedoms you cannot have in a place like that."
msgstr "Hay libertades que no puedes tener en un lugar así."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are going to be others, I just realized. I mean, I always knew I would have to get married, but I thought I would have more time."
msgstr "Vendrán otros, acabo de darme cuenta. Quiero decir, siempre supe que tendría que casarme, pero pensé que tendría más tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Dio"
msgid "There are many schools. Those for service. Those for war. Some slaves are trained in the carnal ways."
msgstr "Hay muchas escuelas. Aquellas para el servicio. Aquellas para la guerra. Algunos esclavos son entrenados en las formas carnales."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are more like him?"
msgstr "¿Hay más como él?"

msgctxt "speaker:Curator"
msgid "There are no more efficient means than the means utilized in this space."
msgstr "No existen medios más eficientes que los empleados en este espacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "There are no peoples nor nature that can sustain you."
msgstr "No hay pueblos ni naturalezas que puedan sustentarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "There are no words to be had!"
msgstr "¡No hay nada que decir!"

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There are none that remain."
msgstr "¡Ninguno queda!"

msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "There are other fates that I can give you."
msgstr "Hay otros destinos que puedo ofrecerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "There are other matters on the table during this council meeting."
msgstr "Hay otros asuntos en la mesa durante esta reunión del consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "There are other ways to make you speak the truth."
msgstr "Hay otras formas de hacerte hablar la verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are parts of this city that are really dangerous, and if you don't know what parts to avoid..."
msgstr "Hay partes de esta ciudad que son realmente peligrosas, y si no sabes qué zonas evitar..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There are people in there...dangerous people..."
msgstr "Hay personas allí... personas peligrosas..."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "There are people like me all over this world. Born into a fate they never asked for, told how much they're worth from the day they're born till the day they die."
msgstr "Hay personas como yo en todas partes de este mundo. Nacidas en un destino que nunca pidieron, y a las que les dicen cuánto valen desde el día que nacen hasta el día que mueren."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "There are people like my all over this world. Born into a fate they never asked for, told how much they're worth from the day they were born till the day they died."
msgstr "Hay personas como yo en todo este mundo. Nacidas para un destino que nunca pidieron, a las que se les dice cuánto valen desde el día de su nacimiento hasta el día de su muerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are people waiting for me, they are-"
msgstr "Hay personas que esperan por mí, son..."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There are reports that sicken even to read, let alone imagine."
msgstr "Hay informes que enferman solo de leerlos, mucho menos de imaginarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are rooms in the castle, private rooms where we can-"
msgstr "Hay habitaciones en el castillo, recámaras privadas donde podemos..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are so many magical barriers, wards and traps around us...nobody will get through."
msgstr "Hay tantas barreras mágicas, protecciones y trampas alrededor de nosotros... nadie podrá pasar."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "There are so many uncles, aunts, nephews and nieces between us and the real Highfield family that all we have is our name."
msgstr "Hay tantos tíos, tías, sobrinos y sobrinas entre nosotros y la verdadera familia de Highfield que todo lo que tenemos es nuestro nombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "There are so very few like you."
msgstr "Hay muy pocos como tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "There are some cleaning supplies in that closet there, you can use those."
msgstr "Hay algunos productos de limpieza en ese armario, puedes usarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are some covers here, we keep the linnens in that chest over there."
msgstr "Hay algunas cobijas aquí; guardamos la ropa de cama en ese baúl allá."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "There are some matters regarding land disputes that-"
msgstr "Hay algunos asuntos relacionados con disputas de tierras que-"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There are sounds of battle, and behind them, more screams from the throne room. Other than that, the palace is empty."
msgstr "Hay sonidos de batalla, y detrás de ellos, más gritos provenientes del salón del trono. Aparte de eso, el palacio está vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There are theories, but the truth is, we don't know how or what determines a person's apptitude for magic."
msgstr "Existen teorías, pero la verdad es que no sabemos cómo ni qué determina la aptitud de una persona para la magia."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There are things I can see, and things I cannot see. This limits me in some ways, but frees me up in others."
msgstr "Hay cosas que puedo ver y otras que no. Esto me limita en cierto modo, pero también me libera en otros."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There are those in the city that would prefer the legions of Mythra not be wasted on what they believe are, pardon the word, backwaters."
msgstr "Hay quienes en la ciudad preferirían que las legiones de Mythra no se desperdicien en lo que consideran, perdone la expresión, tierras de provincia."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "There are those that believe a signal is in order. Something to show that the Rose family stands strong, and that their loyalty still lies with the old houses."
msgstr "Hay quienes creen que es momento de enviar una señal. Algo que demuestre que la familia Rose sigue fuerte y que su lealtad aún reside con las antiguas casas."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There are those who have the potential, but who never master the basics."
msgstr "Hay quienes tienen el potencial, pero que nunca dominan lo básico."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There are those who simply can wield, and those who simply never can wield it."
msgstr "Hay quienes simplemente no pueden manejarlo, y hay quienes nunca podrán hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are three mages and a Knight here. Who could hurt us?"
msgstr "Hay tres magos y un caballero aquí. ¿Quién podría hacernos daño?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are two mages and a Knight here. Who could hurt us?"
msgstr "Hay dos magos y un Caballero aquí. ¿Quién podría hacernos daño?"

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "There are ways to free oneself. Earn the right to stop wearing...well that."
msgstr "Hay formas de liberarse. Ganar el derecho a dejar de usar... bueno, eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are worse friends to have."
msgstr "Hay peores amigos que tener."

msgctxt "speaker:Peasant girl"
msgid "There aren't nearly as many merchants coming to market as before, and many farmers have held onto their food, fearing what the future might bring."
msgstr "Ya no vienen tantos comerciantes al mercado como antes, y muchos agricultores se han aferrado a sus alimentos, temiendo lo que pueda traer el futuro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There at the end of the aisle, stood Varga. Her soon-to-be husband."
msgstr "Allí, al final del pasillo, estaba Varga. Su futuro esposo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There came no response."
msgstr "No hubo respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There could be no other but her."
msgstr "No podía haber otra que ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There could be no pretending."
msgstr "No había lugar para fingir."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There exists no simplified version that would not butcher the truth so as to make it meaningless."
msgstr "No existe una versión simplificada que no acabe mutilando la verdad hasta hacerla insignificante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There had to be a strategy here. A way to win."
msgstr "Tenía que haber una estrategia aquí. Una forma de ganar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There had to be something she could do or say."
msgstr "Tenía que haber algo que pudiera hacer o decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There had to be something that could be done. A definitive answer to the threat of the Void."
msgstr "Debería haber algo que hacer. Una respuesta definitiva a la amenaza del Vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There has always been war in this world. There will always be another."
msgstr "En este mundo siempre ha habido guerra. Siempre habrá otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There have been others over the years, too ambitious, too hungry, and they've all met the same fate."
msgstr "También hubo otros a lo largo de los años, demasiado ambiciosos y hambrientos, y todos encontraron el mismo destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "There have been rumors to the fact yes. A hunting accident, I believe his father said."
msgstr "Sí, han habido rumores al respecto, creo que su padre dijo que fue un accidente de caza."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There have been rumors. In the camp."
msgstr "Hay rumores. En el campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "There he was, same handsome boy he always been."
msgstr "Allí estaba él, el mismo muchacho guapo que siempre ha sido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There in the hands of the slave girl, the crown of her ancestors. The crown of Rosanna."
msgstr "Allí, en las manos de la esclava, la corona de sus antepasados. La corona de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There is a brief window available to us."
msgstr "Hay una breve ventana de oportunidad para nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "There is a cart waiting near the markets. We need to go now, I'll guide you."
msgstr "Hay un carro esperando cerca de los mercados. Debemos irnos ahora, te guiaré."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There is a cruelty in him that she cannot deny. And a cruelty she finds oddly appealing."
msgstr "En él hay una crueldad que no puede negar. Y una crueldad que encuentra extrañamente atractiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There is a cyclical nature to they who create, and are in turn birthed from their own creation."
msgstr "Existe una naturaleza cíclica en quienes crean y son, a su vez, engendrados por su propia creación."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There is a door in this house, and it will bring you there, same as it once brought you to Bagrad."
msgstr "Hay una puerta en esta casa que te llevará allí, igual que lo hizo cuando te trajo a Bagrad."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There is a great deal more to all of this than the climax."
msgstr "Hay mucho más en todo esto que el clímax."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "There is a lot that needs to be done. I expect from each of you, the loyalty that you showed my father."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There is a majority support for the position."
msgstr "Hay un apoyo mayoritario para la posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "There is a particular item in that room that I'm after, and I don't need an entire army of soldiers stomping around."
msgstr "Hay un objeto particular en esa sala que busco, y no necesito un ejército de soldados pisoteando por ahí."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "There is a report that entire plots of grassland have turned arid."
msgstr "Hay un informe de que amplias extensiones de pradera se han vuelto áridas."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "There is a small bush, it should offer plenty of privacy."
msgstr "Hay un arbusto pequeño, debería ofrecer bastante privacidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "There is a small farming town about a day's ride up the old road, called Gallow Creek."
msgstr "Hay un pequeño pueblo agrícola a un día de camino por el viejo camino, llamado Gallow Creek."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "There is a third one inside, you pick that one, alright?"
msgstr "Hay una tercera opción dentro, tú elige esa, ¿de acuerdo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is a way...somehow...if we can just-"
msgstr "Hay un camino... de alguna manera... si solo podemos-"

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "There is also another option..."
msgstr "También hay otra opción..."

msgctxt "speaker:Shah Mahda"
msgid "There is an army at my gate!"
msgstr "¡Hay un ejército en mi puerta!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "There is gonna be a next time."
msgstr "Habrá una próxima vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There is more blood here than she had ever seen in her life. He's choking, she realizes."
msgstr "Hay más sangre aquí de la que jamás había visto en su vida. Se está ahogando, se da cuenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There is no amount that makes you say, enough."
msgstr "No hay cantidad que te haga decir 'suficiente'."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There is no conclusive majority support for the position."
msgstr "No existe una mayoría concluyente que respalde dicha postura."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is no creature in the world that can do something like this."
msgstr "No hay criatura en el mundo que pueda hacer algo así."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There is no crime in enjoying your own success. He never wanted anything more than for his children to thrive."
msgstr "No hay delito en disfrutar de tu propio éxito. Él nunca quiso nada más que ver a sus hijos prosperar."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There is no gravity. No above nor below. And your muscles don't work here."
msgstr "No hay gravedad. No hay arriba ni abajo. Y tus músculos no funcionan aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There is no home to go back to. And all the rules that applied were gone."
msgstr "No hay hogar al que volver. Y todas las reglas que aplicaban, habían desaparecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There is no majority support for the position."
msgstr "No hay apoyo mayoritario para la posición."

msgctxt "speaker:King-On-The-Outside"
msgid "There is no other way. Least of all one made by a puppet like yourself."
msgstr "No hay otra salida, y mucho menos una tejida por un títere como tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is no place for me here, I'm sorry. Please, allow me to leave."
msgstr "No tengo lugar aquí, lo siento. Por favor, permíteme irme."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "There is no place for me here."
msgstr "No tengo lugar aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There is no point in fighting you. The stones are set in place. Fate is written."
msgstr "No tiene sentido pelear contigo. Las piedras están en su lugar. El destino está escrito."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There is no reference. No above and now below. Sarah turns her head aside."
msgstr "No hay referencia. No hay arriba ni abajo ahora. Sarah gira la cabeza hacia un lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is no road."
msgstr "No hay camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "There is no singular path of history. The choices that people make, shape the direction of history."
msgstr "No existe un único camino de la historia. Las decisiones que toman las personas dan forma a su dirección."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There is no space for two worlds, in one world."
msgstr "No hay espacio para dos mundos en un solo mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There is no space for two worlds, in one world."
msgstr "No hay espacio para dos mundos en un solo mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There is no time after which you say, I am done."
msgstr "No hay tiempo después del que digas: 'ya terminé'."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "There is no us"
msgstr "No hay nosotros"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is no us, Nick."
msgstr "No hay nosotros, Nick."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There is no way...I will transform again. Hurt again..."
msgstr "No hay manera... volveré a transformarme. Volveré a sufrir..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There is none."
msgstr "No hay ninguno."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "There is nothing for you to be forgiven for."
msgstr "No hay nada por lo que debas perdonarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is nothing left to forgive."
msgstr "No queda nada que perdonar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is nothing quite as annoying as a man who wishes to speak but holds his tongue."
msgstr "Nada hay más molesto que un hombre que desea hablar pero se calla."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "There is nothing that I want to do more right now than give in to what I'm feeling."
msgstr "No hay nada que desee hacer más en este momento que ceder a lo que siento."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "There is nothing to explain, leave me alone."
msgstr "No hay nada que explicar, déjame en paz."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "There is nothing you want that you can't get, all you need to do is ask for it and they'll deliver it as soon as they can."
msgstr "No hay nada que quieras y no puedas obtener; todo lo que necesitas hacer es pedirlo y te lo entregarán tan pronto como puedan."

msgctxt "speaker:Merchant"
msgid "There is one more matter...but I fear to even speak it, invites disaster...yet it is the truth!"
msgstr "Hay un asunto más... pero temo pronunciarlo, pues ello invita al desastre... ¡sin embargo, es la verdad!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There is only swimming. Only the strokes. One more. One more. One more."
msgstr "Solo hay natación. Solo los brazos. Uno más. Uno más. Uno más."

msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "There is salvation in submission."
msgstr "Hay salvación en la sumisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "There is so much I want to tell you, Sarah. So much since we last saw."
msgstr "Hay tanto que quiero contarte, Sarah. Tanto desde la última vez que nos vimos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is something I need to ask of you."
msgstr "Hay algo que necesito preguntarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "There is the bathhouse, yes, but there are also the private quarters."
msgstr "Hay el baño, sí, pero también hay los cuartos privados."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There is truly nothing that I can do to convince you?"
msgstr "¿Realmente no hay nada que pueda hacer para convencerte?"

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There isn't a way out. And if you try to escape, the Master will..."
msgstr "No hay salida. Y si intentas escapar, el Amo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There isn't any shame in taking a moment to yourself."
msgstr "No hay vergüenza en tomarse un momento para uno mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There isn't anyone to talk to here, other than Xan, and he makes for a poor audience."
msgstr "No hay nadie con quien hablar aquí, salvo Xan, y él es una pésima audiencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There isn't anything I can do to stop him. The laws..."
msgstr "No hay nada que pueda hacer para detenerlo. Las leyes..."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There isn't much left for me in my village. And if I ever transformed again...I would be right back where I was before."
msgstr "No queda mucho para mí en mi aldea. Y si alguna vez me transformo de nuevo... volvería exactamente a donde estaba antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There isn't much time, and so our options are limited, having said that, there is a choice that is left to us..."
msgstr "No queda mucho tiempo, y por tanto nuestras opciones son limitadas; dicho esto, nos queda una elección..."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There isn't much to discuss anyway, my position is rather settled."
msgstr "De todas formas, no hay mucho que discutir; mi posición está bastante definida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it is, Sarah thought. The ask. The demand."
msgstr "Allí está, pensó Sarah. La petición. El requerimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There it is."
msgstr "¡Ahí está!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There it is."
msgstr "¡Allí está!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, Sarah thought. The end result of all this war had brought."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, Sarah thought. What he wanted most of all."
msgstr "Allí estaba, pensó Sarah. Lo que más deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, she realized."
msgstr "Allí estaba, se dio cuenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, she thought."
msgstr "Allí estaba, pensó ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, she thought. The real reason for him asking."
msgstr "Allí estaba, pensó ella. La verdadera razón de su pregunta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was, she thought. They were really going to have it out now."
msgstr "Allí estaba, pensó ella. Por fin iban a salir las cosas a la luz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was."
msgstr "Allí estaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was. Jealousy. The hint of something untoward."
msgstr "Allí estaba. Celos. El atisbo de algo indebido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There it was. That disgusting man."
msgstr "Allí estaba. Ese hombre repugnante."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There might be another way that I could pay you..."
msgstr "Quizás haya otra forma en la que pueda pagarte..."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "There must be another way"
msgstr "Debe haber otra manera"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There must have been more than a thousand souls, she guessed."
msgstr "Debió haber habido más de mil almas, supuso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There never seemed to be enough time in a day to settle anything."
msgstr "Nunca pareció haber suficiente tiempo en un día para resolver nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There never seemed to be enough time in the day."
msgstr "Nunca parecía haber suficiente tiempo en el día."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There really is no other way?"
msgstr "¿Realmente no hay otra forma?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There seemed to be a mutual acknowledgement between the groups, but nobody really socialized with anyone else."
msgstr "Parecía haber un reconocimiento mutuo entre los grupos, pero nadie realmente socializaba con nadie más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There seemed to be a strange kind of logic to it."
msgstr "Parecía haber una lógica extraña en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There seemed to be a tension."
msgstr "Parecía haber una tensión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There seemed to be little of the tenderness from before."
msgstr "Parecía que había poca de la ternura del momento anterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There seemed to be no strategy to their movement, but their numbers were more than enough for them to be dangerous."
msgstr "Parecía que no había estrategia en su movimiento, pero su número era más que suficiente para ser peligrosos."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "There she goes!"
msgstr "¡Allá va!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There she saw Kate's face, looking up at her, smiling."
msgstr "Allí vio el rostro de Kate, mirándola hacia arriba con una sonrisa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There she saw Mary, her dress thrown to the floor, sitting on top of the old soldier's lap."
msgstr "Allí vio a Mary, con su vestido tirado al suelo, sentada sobre las rodillas del viejo soldado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There she was, she thought. Back on her knees, naked, looking up at the captain as the captain looked down on her. She’d been here many times before, but she had never thought she would be back here."
msgstr "Allí estaba ella, pensó. De nuevo a sus rodillas, desnuda, mirando al capitán mientras él la observaba desde arriba. Había estado allí muchas veces antes, pero nunca había pensado que volvería a encontrarse en aquel lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There she went again, Sarah thought. Pushing her buttons."
msgstr "Allí iba otra vez, pensó Sarah. Le estaba presionando los botones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There the wounded, exhausted and sick were dragged along, but they offered little hope."
msgstr "Allí los heridos, agotados y enfermos eran arrastrados, pero ofrecían poca esperanza."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There there, Blondie. That's enough. Don't need you givin me another hard on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "There they are, safe and alive, but they are not men."
msgstr "Allí están, a salvo y vivos, pero ya no son hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "There they told the stories of what the Orcs had done in vivid detail."
msgstr "Allí contaron las historias de lo que los orcos habían hecho con detalle vívido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a beauty to Kate, but it seemed always mixed with something else."
msgstr "Había belleza en Kate, pero parecía siempre mezclada con otra cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a brief pause."
msgstr "Hubo una breve pausa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a busy chatter, which suddenly felt silent as everyone noticed Sarah."
msgstr "Hubo un bullicioso murmullo que de repente se sintió en silencio cuando todos notaron a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a calmness to the moment, shared between only two souls, neither of which would ever betray the sacredness of the moment to another."
msgstr "Hubo una calma en el momento, compartida entre solo dos almas, ninguna de las cuales jamás traicionaría la santidad del instante ante otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a chaos here, but it was also obvious that Samayra excercised a control over it."
msgstr "Había caos aquí, pero también era obvio que Samayra ejercía un control sobre él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a deepness to the sensation, not unlike the prismatic light that was caught in the petals."
msgstr "Había una profundidad en la sensación, no muy diferente de la luz prismática atrapada en las pétalos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a depth to Atilla's eyes, Sarah had come to learn. And now she saw that he was unsure. Trust her, or close himself off again."
msgstr "Había profundidad en los ojos de Atilla, algo que Sarah había aprendido a reconocer. Y ahora veía que él estaba inseguro: confiar en ella o volver a cerrarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a distance between the two, but the Tribesmen, being the more skilled riders, were quickly closing the distance."
msgstr "Había distancia entre los dos, pero los tribales, siendo jinetes más háiles, cerraban la brecha rápidamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a hierarchy in this bed, and Kate undoubtedly sat at the top."
msgstr "En esta cama existía una jerarquía, y Kate sin duda ocupaba el lugar más alto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a hierarchy on this ship, and she most definitely sat at the bottom."
msgstr "En este barco existía una jerarquía, y ella ocupaba sin duda el puesto más bajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a kindness in her face that seemed undulled, no matter her circumstances."
msgstr "Había una bondad en su rostro que parecía intacta, sin importar sus circunstancias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a lightness between them."
msgstr "Entre ellos había una ligereza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a logic that Sarah could detect."
msgstr "Había una lógica que Sarah podía detectar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a loneliness in that house, made worse by how Xan kept her at a distance."
msgstr "Había una soledad en esa casa, agravada por cómo Xan la mantenía a distancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a long silence between them."
msgstr "Hubo un largo silencio entre ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a lot of work to be done."
msgstr "Había mucho trabajo por hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a lot that Sarah could appreciate about Kate, but when it came to this, she valued above all her experience."
msgstr "Había mucho que Sarah podía apreciar de Kate, pero cuando se trataba de esto, valoraba sobre todo su experiencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a lot you could tell about him in the way he grunted."
msgstr "Podías leer mucho de él en la forma en que gruñía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a love there, but at the same time, a mutual understanding of the absurdity of their situation."
msgstr "Había un amor allí, pero al mismo tiempo, una comprensión mutua de la absurdidad de su situación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a mattress crudely stuffed under the tarp. In this place, it almost seemed like a luxury to Sarah."
msgstr "Había un colchón rudimentariamente relleno debajo del lona. En este lugar, casi parecía un lujo para Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a mercy, she figured, that she only needed to share herself with him and not the whole tribe."
msgstr "Había un acto de misericordia, pensó ella, que solo necesitaba compartir con él y no con toda la tribu."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a moment of pause."
msgstr "Hubo un instante de pausa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a moment of silence."
msgstr "Hubo un instante de silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a pause."
msgstr "Hubo un silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a profound part of her that resented even the idea of opening up. Even to her."
msgstr "Había una parte profunda de ella que resentía incluso la idea de abrirse. Incluso con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a raw masculinity about him that she found enthralling, and felt herself slowly falling into."
msgstr "Hubo una masculinidad cruda en él que le resultaba fascinante, y se sentía caer lentamente en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a release in the solitude of it."
msgstr "Había un alivio en la soledad de ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a richness and depth to its every petal."
msgstr "Había una riqueza y profundidad en cada pétalo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a shame in his voice. Breaking a vow was no easy thing for him."
msgstr "Había vergüenza en su voz. Para él, romper una promesa no era cosa fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a silence as Sarah looked up at him."
msgstr "Un silencio cargado de tensión se hizo mientras Sarah lo miraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a soft knock at the door."
msgstr "Hubo un suave golpeteo en la puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a softness to the girl's features that always made Sarah hesitant with her."
msgstr "Había una suavidad en los rasgos de la muchacha que siempre hacía que Sarah se mostrara dubitativa con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a supply ship coming in about a month."
msgstr "Había un buque de aprovisionamiento que llegaría en aproximadamente un mes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a tenderness here."
msgstr "Aquí había ternura."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a tenderness, so soft it could not be mistaken for passion, instead it brimmed with profound love."
msgstr "Había una ternura tan suave que no podía confundirse con pasión; por el contrario, rebosaba de un amor profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There was a time I knew every tree and every branch in this place."
msgstr "Hubo un tiempo en que conocía cada árbol y cada rama de este lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a vulnerability in him, but it seemed at the same time uneasy to him."
msgstr "Había una vulnerabilidad en él, pero al mismo tiempo parecía incómodo para él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a way in how he carried himself, down to his clothes, which simply made clear to everyone he was bad news."
msgstr "Había algo en la forma de portarse, hasta en su ropa, que hacía evidente para todos que era mala noticia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was a wisdom to her words."
msgstr "Hubo sabiduría en sus palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There was a woman, years ago, that liked to walk in the forest with me. With her I felt easy..."
msgstr "Había una mujer, hace años, que gustaba de caminar por el bosque conmigo. Con ella me sentía cómodo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was almost a violence there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was always a servant, quick to serve."
msgstr "Siempre había un sirviente, listo para atender."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an abudance here that Sarah had not expected."
msgstr "Había una abundancia aquí que Sarah no había esperado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an aggressiveness to her, which Sarah found oddly comforting."
msgstr "Hubo una agresividad en ella que a Sarah le resultaba extrañamente reconfortante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an ease here."
msgstr "Había una facilidad aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an easy, amicable mood."
msgstr "Había un ambiente fácil y cordial."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an efficiency to the whole process that she had come to appreciate."
msgstr "Había una eficiencia en todo el proceso que había llegado a apreciar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an erotic element to the total domination that only two men could deliver."
msgstr "Había un elemento erótico en la dominación total que solo dos hombres podían ofrecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an excitement to her that overpowered her otherwise demure nature."
msgstr "Había una excitación en ella que desbordaba su naturaleza de por sí recatada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an honesty that didn't seem to usually be there."
msgstr "Había una honestidad que no parecía estar allí habitualmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an innocence to him."
msgstr "Había una inocencia en él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an order here."
msgstr "Aquí había un orden."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an predictable rhythm to most of her days."
msgstr "Había un ritmo predecible en la mayor parte de sus días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an serenity to the quietness that Sarah appreciated."
msgstr "Había una serenidad en el silencio que Sarah apreciaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was an unfamiliar release in that surrender."
msgstr "Hubo una liberación desconocida en esa rendición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was barely a part of her body that he had not seized yet, and no part she would deny him if he did."
msgstr "Casi no había parte de su cuerpo que él no hubiera tomado aún, y ninguna parte que ella le negaría si lo quisiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was enough rage in his voice to make Sakar actually go quiet."
msgstr "Hubo tanta rabia en su voz que Sakar realmente se quedó en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was enough to worry about that she knew. She didn't need to add to ther worries with dark thoughts."
msgstr "Había suficiente de qué preocuparse como para saberlo. No necesitaba añadir más a sus problemas con pensamientos oscuros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was food. A roof. Security. And for as old as her master was, he did not leave her entirely unsatisfied."
msgstr "Había comida. Un techo. Seguridad. Y, por viejo que fuera su amo, no la dejaba enteramente insatisfecha."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was hardly any economy to speak of. Instead, the Tribesmen simply looted and carried off their wealth back to their capital of Al'Gahaem."
msgstr "No había apenas economía que mencionar. En su lugar, los tribales simplemente saqueaban y llevaban su riqueza de vuelta a su capital, Al'Gahaem."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was hardly anything left of the human he must once have been."
msgstr "Ya no quedaba apenas nada del hombre que alguna vez fue."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was her body, engaged in all manner of acts, and then her mind, that now stood seperate and observed herself."
msgstr "Había su cuerpo, involucrado en todo tipo de actos, y luego su mente, que ahora se mantenía separada y la observaba a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was honesty here, no pretense."
msgstr "Aquí había honestidad, sin fingimientos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was little here to hold onto, but enough to slightly balance herself."
msgstr "No había mucho aquí a lo que aferrarse, pero suficiente para mantenerse ligeramente equilibrada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was little more to say."
msgstr "No había más que decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was more to it than just his appearance, or even the size of his member."
msgstr "Había más en ello que su apariencia, o incluso el tamaño de su miembro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no anger here, only a strong and strict hand that expected her to follow him. Sarah did."
msgstr "No había ira aquí, solo una mano fuerte y estricta que esperaba que la siguiera. Sarah lo siguió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no doubt here, no uncertainty. Everyone knew exactly what part they played, and what was expected of them."
msgstr "Aquí no había duda, ni incertidumbre. Todos sabían exactamente qué papel desempeñaban y qué se esperaba de ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no exchange here. She expected nothing of him in return for this performance."
msgstr "Aquí no había intercambio. No esperaba nada de él a cambio de esta actuación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no family waiting for her there."
msgstr "No había familia esperándola allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no food here, so they could not stay. The longer they did, the worse their food situation would get."
msgstr "No había comida aquí, por lo que no podían quedarse. Cuanto más permanecieran, peor sería su situación alimentaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no hestitation in Dalia, rather the opposite. She seemed nearly delirious with anticipation."
msgstr "No hubo la menor vacilación en Dalia; todo lo contrario. Parecía casi delirante de anticipación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no hint of recognition."
msgstr "No había ni rastro de reconocimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no love here, neither did either of them imagine there to be any."
msgstr "No había amor aquí, ni uno de los dos imaginaba que hubiera alguno."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no more room. No air around her. No noise."
msgstr "No quedaba más espacio. No había aire a su alrededor. No había ruido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no movement to make, no escape if she even wanted to, no sounds to produce."
msgstr "No había movimiento que hacer, ni escape si hasta quería alguno, ni sonidos para producir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no part of her body that she reserved from him, no act she wouldn't submit herself to."
msgstr "No había parte de su cuerpo que reservara para él, ningún acto al que no se entregara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no part of him that held on to any figment of pride or masculinity, instead prostrating himself completely before her."
msgstr "No había en él ningún fragmento de orgullo o masculinidad que se aferrara, sino que se prosternaba completamente ante ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no pleasure in it, none for her at least."
msgstr "No había placer en ello, ninguno para ella, al menos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no point denying the obvious."
msgstr "No había nada que negar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no point to run. She could hide nowhere in the house, and outside even less. She had no choice but to turn back."
msgstr "No había sentido de huida. No podía esconderse en ningún lugar de la casa, y mucho menos fuera de ella. No tenía más opción que dar media vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no point trying to put to words what they had seen and felt and heard."
msgstr "No había punto en intentar poner en palabras lo que habían visto, sentido y oído."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no reason for them to return to the city again. All that could be looted, had been."
msgstr "No había motivo para volver a la ciudad de nuevo. Todo lo que podía ser saqueado ya lo había sido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no reason to abandon her position."
msgstr "No había motivo para abandonar su posición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no resistance here. Only submission."
msgstr "No había resistencia aquí. Solo sumisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no resistance left in her."
msgstr "Ya no quedaba resistencia en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no rest for slaves."
msgstr "No había descanso para los esclavos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no running from these thoughts."
msgstr "No había huida de esos pensamientos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no single battalion in all of Rosanna that was more well equipped. She knew Marion was somewhere among them."
msgstr "No había ningún batallón en toda Rosanna mejor equipado que ese. Sabía que Marion estaba entre ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no time to pray. What little free time she had, she should use for herself. Get some extra sleep."
msgstr "No había tiempo para orar. El poco tiempo libre que tenía, debía usarlo para sí misma. Dormir un poco más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no time to process."
msgstr "No hubo tiempo para procesarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no time to recover."
msgstr "No había tiempo para recuperarse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no time to stop."
msgstr "No había tiempo para detenerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was no use holding back now, he would either save her, or not, this was her only chance."
msgstr "Ya no había sentido para frenar; o la salvaría, o no lo haría: esta era su única oportunidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There was no want. No famine. No disease. No age."
msgstr "No había carencia. No había hambruna. No había enfermedad. No había vejez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nobody behind her."
msgstr "No había nadie detrás de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nobody else on the training ground...but anyone could walk in on them."
msgstr "No había nadie más en el campo de entrenamiento... pero cualquiera podría entrar y verlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nobody here, other than Samayra."
msgstr "No había nadie aquí, salvo Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nobody here, other than herself. Or at least, there shouldn't be anyone else."
msgstr "No había nadie aquí, salvo ella misma. O al menos, no debería haber nadie más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nobody that would save her..."
msgstr "No había nadie que la salvara..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was none of his smirking. His arrogance. He seemed genuinely desperate."
msgstr "No había esa sonrisa burlona. No había su arrogancia. Parecía genuinamente desesperado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was none of the alcohol from last time, making this any more tolerable."
msgstr "No había rastro del alcohol de la última vez, lo que no hacía esto más tolerable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was none of the alcohol from last time. What was her excuse now, Sarah thought to herself as she continued to jerk him."
msgstr "¿Cuál era su excusa ahora, pensó Sarah para sí misma mientras seguía masturbándolo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was none."
msgstr "No había nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was not much depth to any of the particulars it touched on, but rather, it formed the context by which she could begin to understand the field."
msgstr "No había mucha profundidad en ninguno de los detalles que tocaba, sino más bien formaba el contexto por el cual podía comenzar a comprender el campo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing basic about transporting and preparing a bath, out here, on the edge of the world."
msgstr "No había nada de básico en transportar y preparar un baño, aquí, al borde del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing but heartbreak going down that road."
msgstr "No había más que el desconsuelo en ese camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing fair about this exchange, but Sarah didn't want it to stop either."
msgstr "No había nada justo en este intercambio, pero Sarah tampoco quería que terminara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing handsome about him."
msgstr "No había nada de guapo en él."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There was nothing here that you have to feel ashamed about."
msgstr "No hay nada aquí de lo que debas sentirte avergonzada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing more she wanted than to set this bastard on fire, but she also knew he was right. There were laws."
msgstr "No había nada que ella quisiera más que encender a ese bastardo, pero también sabía que tenía razón. Había leyes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing more to say."
msgstr "No había nada más que decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing she could do."
msgstr "No había nada que pudiera hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing that remained, they realized. No future that one could hope for with a Rosannan man."
msgstr "No quedaba nada más, lo comprendieron. No había futuro alguno que se pudiera esperar con un hombre rosano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing there but a dead end."
msgstr "No había nada allí más que un callejón sin salida."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There was nothing to be done about it, Sarah. You did the right thing."
msgstr "No había nada que hacer al respecto, Sarah. Has hecho lo correcto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing to be spoken that their bodies had not yet said."
msgstr "No había nada que decir que sus cuerpos no hubieran dicho ya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nowhere to escape."
msgstr "No había lugar al que huir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nowhere to go. If she made a run for it, they'd surely catch her."
msgstr "No había a dónde ir. Si intentaba huir, la atraparían con seguridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was of course the alternative, to turn around and walk back the five days to Bagrad, but that was a death sentence."
msgstr "Por supuesto, existía la alternativa: girar sobre sus talones y regresar a Bagrad, lo que habría tardado cinco días, pero eso equivalía a una sentencia de muerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There was only one great empire, and it ruled all the world. There wasn't much of a world to rule, but in a savage time, they were the only real civilization."
msgstr "Solo había un gran imperio, y gobernaba todo el mundo. No había mucho mundo que gobernar, pero en tiempos salvajes, ellos eran la única civilización verdadera."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There was only the Empire itself back then. No rivals or nations."
msgstr "Solo había el Imperio mismo en aquellos tiempos. Sin rivales ni naciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was only the growing pleasure, and his voice."
msgstr "Solo había el creciente placer y su voz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was only the run."
msgstr "Solo quedaba la huida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was only the study, and her endless lessons."
msgstr "Solo había el estudio y sus lecciones interminables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was only the total domination of her body."
msgstr "Solo quedaba la dominación total de su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was rarely a more joyous couple in all the world."
msgstr "Rara vez había un par más feliz en todo el mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was ship duty, and then there was whatever else the captain might demand."
msgstr "Había el servicio de la nave, y luego estaba lo que fuera que el capitán pudiera exigir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was so much of it, a pure white, that it at times disoriented her."
msgstr "Había tanta de ella, una pura blancura que a veces la desorientaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was so much of it."
msgstr "Había tanta de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was so much to do."
msgstr "Había tanto por hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was some truth to that, she figured."
msgstr "Eso tenía cierto fundamento, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was some truth to what Varga said. There was no true hand that forced her to attend a Union Council. Nothing that forced her to take Maeiv's invitation serious."
msgstr "Había algo de verdad en lo que Varga dijo. No había mano alguna que la obligara a asistir al Consejo de la Unión. Nada que la forzara a tomar en serio la invitación de Maeiv."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was some truth to what he said."
msgstr "Había algo de verdad en lo que dijo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was someone in the alley."
msgstr "Había alguien en el callejón."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There was something I had been hopin to ask you."
msgstr "Había algo que había estado esperando preguntarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something about being caught in between these two men, their bodies in peak form, the raw masculinity of it..."
msgstr "Había algo en estar atrapada entre estos dos hombres, sus cuerpos en plena forma, esa masculinidad cruda..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something about being on campaign. Something that was both exciting, yet also terribly draining."
msgstr "Había algo en la campaña. Algo que era a la vez excitante y terriblemente agotador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something about his smile that had always unsettled her. It had taken her years before she finally realized what it was."
msgstr "Hubo algo en su sonrisa que siempre la había inquietado. Le tomó años antes de darse cuenta de qué era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something amusing to her about the idea of this tall and confident Huntsman, now turned quiet and awkward."
msgstr "A ella le resultaba divertido imaginar a ese alto y seguro cazador, ahora convertido en alguien callado e incómodo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something comfortable in the silence too. The simple act of being naked next to him was oddly soothing."
msgstr "También había algo de comodidad en el silencio. El simple hecho de estar desnuda a su lado resultaba extrañamente reconfortante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something erotic, Sarah thought as she worked her body, about no longer having to hide this part of herself."
msgstr "Había algo erótico en ello, pensó Sarah mientras movía su cuerpo, al no tener que ocultar ya esta parte de sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something foxlike about his behavior."
msgstr "Había algo de zorro en su comportamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something in her eyes..."
msgstr "Había algo en sus ojos..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something in the hearts of men that feared magic, the way an animal feared fire."
msgstr "Hubo algo en los corazones de los hombres que temía la magia, como un animal teme al fuego."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something in their eyes."
msgstr "Había algo en sus ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something in this man's eyes. A purpose. All the others in the castle looked at her for who she was, a princess, but this man had the eyes of a predator."
msgstr "Había algo en los ojos de este hombre. Un propósito. Todos los demás del castillo la miraban por lo que era, una princesa, pero este hombre tenía los ojos de un depredador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something odd about the scene."
msgstr "Había algo extraño en la escena."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something odd about the thing."
msgstr "Había algo raro en la cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something odd in his voice, but Sarah couldn't say what."
msgstr "Había algo extraño en su voz, pero Sarah no podía decir qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something off about her."
msgstr "Había algo raro en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something raw about him."
msgstr "Había algo crudo en él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something simple about just surrendering. To just being used. To terminating any thought."
msgstr "Había algo tan simple en la rendición, en ser usada y en apagar cualquier pensamiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something so clarifying about this moment. No longer did she have to pretend to herself that this wasn't what she had wanted."
msgstr "Había algo tan esclarecedor en este momento. Ya no tenía que fingirle a sí misma que esto no era lo que había deseado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something so soothing about her words."
msgstr "Había algo tan reconfortante en sus palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something so utterly charming about him. How he just was who he appeared to be. Honest. No hidden meanings."
msgstr "Había algo tan absolutamente encantador en él. La forma en que simplemente era quien aparentaba ser. Honesto. Sin significados ocultos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something strange in his eyes, she thought."
msgstr "Había algo extraño en sus ojos, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something there."
msgstr "Había algo ahí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something to be said for each."
msgstr "Cada uno tenía algo que decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was something very serious about Kate. Sarah was confused."
msgstr "Kate tenía algo muy serio. Sarah estaba confundida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was still a light, but it turned cold and grey, and the sounds around her grew muted."
msgstr "Aún había luz, pero se volvió fría y gris, y los sonidos a su alrededor se volvieron apagados."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There was such a commotion, I entirely forgot about trying to kill myself. Instead, I focussed on organizing the first hunt for the Beast."
msgstr "Había tal alboroto que olvidé por completo mi intento de suicidio. En su lugar, me concentré en organizar la primera cacería contra la Bestia."

msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "There was the basilisk-"
msgstr "—Estaba el basilisco—"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the matter of the book, but it had only been a day and she had not heard anything from Razaphel."
msgstr "Quedaba el asunto del libro, pero solo había pasado un día y no había recibido nada de Razafael."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the occasional hoot and cheer from the crowd as performers juggled or somersaulted through the aisles. Some performers managed both at the same time."
msgstr "De vez en cuando, la multitud lanzaba gritos y aplausos mientras los artistas hacían malabares o daban saltos mortales entre las filas. Algunos lograban hacer ambas cosas al mismo tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the person she pretended to be in her head and the person she was by her actions."
msgstr "Había la persona que fingía ser en su mente y la persona que era por sus acciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the pleasure of it, that much she was familiar with, but there was more to it as well."
msgstr "Había el placer de ello, eso sí que conocía, pero había más en ello también."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the reasoned Sarah, off in the corner, waiting to get back in control, to correct what her inner slut had caused."
msgstr "Había la Sarah razonable, perdida en una esquina, esperando recuperar el control para corregir lo que su zorra interior había causado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the truth of him. Nervous. Anxious. Even when he had all he wanted."
msgstr "Había la verdad de él. Nervioso. Ansioso. Incluso cuando tenía todo lo que deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was the vastness of the hall itself, but more than that, there were the endless sights and sounds."
msgstr "Había la vastedad del salón mismo, pero más que eso, había las vistas y los sonidos interminables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was too much at stake."
msgstr "Había demasiado en juego."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was too much pain among them. Too much history that was still recent."
msgstr "Había demasiado dolor entre ellos. Demasiada historia que aún era reciente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was true awe in his voice."
msgstr "En su voz había un auténtico asombro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was what her mind wanted, and then there was what her body did."
msgstr "Había lo que su mente deseaba, y luego había lo que su cuerpo hacía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was work to be done. Every day, more and more people came to her and Thomas, the requests were endless."
msgstr "Había trabajo por hacer. Cada día, más y más gente acudía a ella y a Thomas; las peticiones eran interminables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was work to be done. Every day, more and more people came to her and Thomas. The requests were endless."
msgstr "Quedaba trabajo por hacer. Cada día, más y más gente acudía a ella y a Thomas; las peticiones eran interminables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was, among all of his desire, love."
msgstr "Había, entre todo ese deseo, amor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was, among all the passion, an anxiousness to the girl. Sarah could not deny it in her own body either."
msgstr "Entre toda esa pasión, había una inquietud en la muchacha. Sarah tampoco podía negarlo con su propio cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't a lot in this world that felt better."
msgstr "No había mucho en este mundo que se sintiera mejor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't any love here, there couldn't be, not between her and him."
msgstr "No había amor aquí, no podía haberlo, no entre ella y él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't any part of the old Sarah left."
msgstr "No quedaba nada de la vieja Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't anybody else out on the street. A few streetlights were burning, but they did little to ward off the darkness."
msgstr "No había nadie más en la calle. Unas pocas farolas estaban encendidas, pero apenas servían para alejar la oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much dignity in this, but she would not be cowed by him."
msgstr "No había mucha dignidad en esto, pero no se dejaría intimidar por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much else she could do, and so instead, she leaned in."
msgstr "No había mucho más que pudiera hacer, y así, se inclinó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much joy in it. More like a predator."
msgstr "No había mucha alegría en ello. Más bien, como un depredador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much of anything she'd wanted to talk to him about ever since they had left the road."
msgstr "No había nada de lo que quisiera hablar con él desde que abandonaron el camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much of anything that she could do."
msgstr "No había mucho que pudiera hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much time for the two to clash, for not long after, the three advisors entered the room and took their place between the men."
msgstr "No hubo mucho tiempo para que los dos chocaran, pues poco después entraron los tres consejeros y se colocaron entre los hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't time, she couldn't allow herself to be distracted."
msgstr "No había tiempo; no podía permitirse distraerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There we go, I might actually make a decent Knight after all."
msgstr "¡Ahí va! Al fin podría ser una digna caballera después de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There we go, nice and steady."
msgstr "Allá vamos, con calma y firmeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr "Ya está."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr "Ahí vamos."

msgctxt "speaker:Jacob"
msgid "There we go."
msgstr "Ya."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There we go. Nice and calm."
msgstr "Allá va. Tranquila y serena."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There we go..."
msgstr "Allá vamos..."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There we'll find the entrance to the Labyrinth."
msgstr "Allí encontraremos la entrada al Laberinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were a few patrons about, but nothing too busy. The sounds of the city were still here, but muted."
msgstr "Había algunos clientes por ahí, pero nada demasiado concurrido. Los sonidos de la ciudad seguían presentes, aunque atenuados."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There were a few things, like drugs, but above all, alcohol."
msgstr "Había algunas cosas, como las drogas, pero sobre todo, el alcohol."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were a lot of rules, tricks and strategies, and Sarah had to confess she'd never really mastered the game."
msgstr "Había muchas reglas, trucos y estrategias, y Sarah tuvo que confesar que nunca había dominado realmente el juego."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were adjustments, measurements, sail rigging, but all in all, the work had dropped off considerably."
msgstr "Había ajustes, mediciones, aparejos de velas, pero en conjunto, el trabajo había disminuido considerablemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were close to twenty soldiers, each massive in size and armed with real weapons and armor."
msgstr "Había cerca de veinte soldados, cada uno masivo en tamaño y armado con armas y armaduras reales."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There were fathers that killed sons and sons that killed fathers. Brother killing brother."
msgstr "Hubo padres que mataron a hijos e hijos que mataron a padres. Hermanos matando hermanos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were few windows, leaving the great palace feeling oddly muted in its colours, but also keeping the punishing desert heat out."
msgstr "Había pocas ventanas, lo que hacía que el gran palacio pareciera extrañamente sordo en sus colores, pero también mantenía fuera el abrasador calor del desierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were her own soldiers from the mercenary company."
msgstr "Había sus propios soldados de la compañía mercenaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were her soldiers. Her servants. Her attendants."
msgstr "Había sus soldados. Sus criados. Sus asistentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There were many chains, some more obvious and some less, that weighed on those such as us."
msgstr "Había muchas cadenas, algunas más obvias y otras menos, que pesaban sobre aquellos como nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were many women who did worse for a meal, she thought. Perhaps she wasn't so different from them as she had once imagined."
msgstr "Hubo muchas mujeres que harían cualquier cosa por una comida, pensó. Quizás no era tan diferente de ellas como alguna vez había imaginado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were men, women, working side by side, and Sarah even saw some other species."
msgstr "Había hombres y mujeres trabajando lado a lado, e incluso Sarah vio a otras especies."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were moments were she longed to be loved by him, held by him, and to hear him whisper sweet words."
msgstr "Hubo momentos en los que anhelaba ser amada por él, sostenida por él, y escucharle susurrar palabras dulces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no animal noises."
msgstr "No había sonidos de animales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no more questions to be settled of what came next. How she would survive. No more decisions to be made."
msgstr "No quedaban más preguntas por resolver sobre lo que vendría después. Cómo sobreviviría. No había más decisiones por tomar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no more words needed between them, for Sarah felt the same."
msgstr "Ya no necesitaban palabras entre ellos, pues Sarah sentía lo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no riches to be found, but they could make a life. Survive."
msgstr "No había riquezas por encontrar, pero podían construir una vida. Sobrevivir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no torches, no braziers, nothing that could ward this opressive darkness."
msgstr "No había antorchas, ni braseros, nada que pudiera alejar esa opresiva oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no words for the sight."
msgstr "No había palabras para el espectáculo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were no words that would save her."
msgstr "No había palabras que pudieran salvarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were noises outside, as there always were. Lethram was a city that rarely went truly quiet."
msgstr "Había ruidos fuera, como siempre había. Lethram era una ciudad que rara vez se quedaba verdaderamente en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were now several lines between herself and the enemy, and their progess had grinded to a halt."
msgstr "Ahora había varias líneas de separación entre ella y el enemigo, y su avance se había detenido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were only a few lights, tiny hovels each a great distance away."
msgstr "Solo había unas pocas luces, pequeñas chozas cada una a gran distancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were other things she could do. Train by herself. Study even more. But something kept her here."
msgstr "Había otras cosas que podía hacer. Entrenar sola. Estudiar aún más. Pero algo la mantenía aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were others that could steer the ship in the armada."
msgstr "Había otros que podían dirigir la nave en la armada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were people, off in the main streets, working, shopping, but nobody noticed or cared for her."
msgstr "Había gente, lejos en las calles principales, trabajando, comprando, pero nadie la notaba ni le importaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were plenty of real dangers all around her."
msgstr "Había muchos peligros reales a su alrededor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were rules and laws in Lethram...but the city guard was not without its freedom to deal with problems in their own way."
msgstr "En Lethram existían reglas y leyes... pero la guardia ciudadana no carecía de libertad para resolver los problemas a su manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were slave soldiers, craftsmen, sailors. There were even slave generals and slave diplomats."
msgstr "Había soldados esclavos, artesanos y marineros. Incluso había generales esclavos y diplomáticos esclavos."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There were those I killed that deserved everything they got and more."
msgstr "Había quienes maté y que merecían todo lo que recibieron, y mucho más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were those who build this marvel, Sarah realized, and there were those who would destroy it. She was the latter."
msgstr "Había quienes construyeron esta maravilla, Sarah comprendió, y había quienes la destruirían. Ella era de los segundos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were times she found herself missing the security of that routine. Then there were times where Sarah loved the dynamism of this city."
msgstr "Había momentos en los que sentía añoranza por la seguridad de esa rutina. Luego venían los tiempos en los que Sarah amaba el dinamismo de esta ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "There were times when mages tried to affect the world, but our magic, it's too strange for people. It's too unnatural."
msgstr "Hubo momentos en que los magos intentaban alterar el mundo, pero nuestra magia es demasiado extraña para la gente. Es demasiado innatural."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were too many."
msgstr "Había demasiadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There were wars and conflict, but nothing crazy. Nothing like what the world looks like now."
msgstr "Hubo guerras y conflictos, pero nada tan extraño. Nada como lo que el mundo parece ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were worse ways to spend her last night on earth."
msgstr "Hubo formas peores de pasar su última noche en la Tierra."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There will be a day when you wish you took my hand, and when that day comes, remember that I offered, and it was you who declined."
msgstr "Habrá un día en el que desearás haber tomado mi mano, y cuando llegue ese día, recuerda que yo ofrecí, y fue tú quien lo rechazó."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There will be a great feast tonight. It is a rare fact to have every ruler of the Union Kingdoms under one roof."
msgstr "Habrá una gran fiesta esta noche. Es un hecho raro tener a cada gobernante de los Reinos Unidos bajo el mismo techo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There will be hundreds of archers in that army, crossbowmen..."
msgstr "Habrá cientos de arqueros en ese ejército, arceros..."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "There will be more attacks. More wounded."
msgstr "Habrá más ataques. Más heridos."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "There will be no country left to defend in the capital falls. Making our stand here, means pushing Hassar's forces back into the desert. That will help everyone."
msgstr "Quedará sin país que defender cuando la capital caiga. Tomar nuestra posición aquí significa empujar las fuerzas de Hassar de vuelta al desierto, y eso ayudará a todos."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There will be plenty of days to work on the paperwork when we travel back to Mythra. No need to get it all done tonight."
msgstr "Habrá suficientes días para ocuparse de la burocracia cuando regresemos a Mythra. No hace falta hacerlo todo esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There will be time, Sarah thought, for him to grow into it."
msgstr "Habrá tiempo, pensó Sarah, para que él crezca en ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There will never be another attack, and in a few years, this will all just be an aweful story people tell."
msgstr "Nunca más habrá otro ataque, y dentro de unos años, todo esto será solo una historia terrible que la gente cuente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a battle tomorrow, and she could not afford to be distracted."
msgstr "Mañana habría una batalla, y no podía permitirse distraerse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a next chapter to her life, she knew this, and it was that belief that kept her alive."
msgstr "Hubo un siguiente capítulo en su vida, lo sabía, y era esa creencia la que le mantenía con vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be a time to make a move. Eventually. But not now. She knew too little of this place, and the mark still haunted her."
msgstr "Hubo un momento para actuar. Eventualmente. Pero no ahora. Conocía demasiado poco de este lugar, y la marca aún la atormentaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no answer."
msgstr "No habría respuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no denying that she had enjoyed it, that much she could never deny between them."
msgstr "No había duda de que lo había disfrutado, eso jamás podría negar entre los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no leader at all. A Council would rule instead."
msgstr "No habría ningún líder en absoluto. Un Consejo gobernaría en su lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be no other chance. If she wanted her freedom, she would have to seize this moment."
msgstr "No habría otra oportunidad. Si quería su libertad, tendría que aprovechar este momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There would be other times to talk to the girl, and she feared she might add more stress for no reason."
msgstr "Habrá otras ocasiones para hablar con la chica, y temía que quizás estuviera añadiendo más estrés sin razón."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "There you are!"
msgstr "¡Allí estás!"

msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "There you are."
msgstr "¡Ahí estás!"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There you go again. Pretending you don't want something you do want. That's what gets you all twisted."
msgstr "Ahí va otra vez. Haciendo como que no quieres algo que sí deseas. Eso es lo que te vuelve toda retorcida."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There you go, Blondie."
msgstr "Allá vas, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go, just like that. A little faster."
msgstr "Allá va, justo así. Un poco más rápido."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ya está."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ya lo tienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ya lo tienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Male Soldier"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ahí lo tienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ahí va."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ahí va."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ya lo tienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There you go."
msgstr "Ahí lo tienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr "Ya está..."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr "Ya lo tienes..."

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There you go..."
msgstr "Ahí lo tienes..."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "There you have it."
msgstr "Ya está."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There!"
msgstr "¡Listo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "There! Fits like a glove."
msgstr "¡Ahí! Queda como un guante."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's a chest over there. Go ahead and open it."
msgstr "Allí hay una caja. Abre la."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a lot you don't know about me."
msgstr "Hay mucho que no sabes de mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There's a reason I took your little barriers apart like they were nothing."
msgstr "Hay una razón por la que desmantelé tus pequeñas barreras como si no importaran."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a restaurant nearby that I've been wanting to try."
msgstr "Hay un restaurante cerca que he estado queriendo probar."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's a small chapel in Northam. Overlooking the sea."
msgstr "Hay una pequeña capilla en Northam. Con vistas al mar."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "There's a spot over here, in the grass."
msgstr "Hay un lugar aquí, en la hierba."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "There's a tent here!"
msgstr "¡Hay una carpa aquí!"

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There's only one question. Do you feel better?"
msgstr "Solo queda una pregunta. ¿Te sientes mejor?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There's some resentment there."
msgstr "Allí hay un poco de resentimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There's something wrong."
msgstr "Hay algo mal."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There's the real you, Blondie."
msgstr "Allí está el verdadero tú, rubio."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "There's the wench!"
msgstr "¡Ahí está la puta!"

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "There, I think you got me good and started."
msgstr "¡Ahí! Creo que me has dejado bien mojada y con ganas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, Sarah sat and wept, until after much time, her senses returned to her."
msgstr "Allí, Sarah se sentó y lloró; hasta que, tras mucho tiempo, sus sentidos volvieron a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, a black monolith waited for her, and whispered."
msgstr "Allí, un monolito negro la esperaba y susurró,"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, around the campfire, she saw the others."
msgstr "Allí, alrededor del fuego de la hoguera, vio a los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as she had already suspected, she found not her usual shape, but instead a man's one."
msgstr "Allí, como ya había sospechado, encontró no su forma habitual, sino la de un hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as the celebration proceeded without them, Sarah sat and listened as Kate held her own eulogy for him."
msgstr "Allí, mientras la celebración avanzaba sin ellos, Sarah se sentó y escuchó cómo Kate pronunciaba su propio elogio fúnebre por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, as they approached the gate of Calshure, Sarah saw an odd thing happen."
msgstr "Allí, mientras se acercaban a la puerta de Calshure, Sarah vio ocurrir algo extraño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, at the back, were mostly archers and lightly armored footmen."
msgstr "Allí, al fondo, había principalmente arqueros y soldados de infantería con armadura ligera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, atop the steps, the throne loomed large."
msgstr "Allí, en la cúspide de los escalones, el trono se alzaba imponente."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There, go read that. Maybe that will clear out your mind."
msgstr "Allá, léelo. Quizás eso aclare tu mente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, hidden, safe from the world, lost to their love."
msgstr "Allí, ocultos, a salvo del mundo, perdidos en su amor."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "There, holy man. How about you go count these outside for a bit?"
msgstr "Ahí, hombre santo. ¿Qué tal si vas a contar esos afuera por un rato?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in her bed, Sarah couldn't help but find herself staring at Samayra's body."
msgstr "Allí, en su cama, Sarah no pudo evitar encontrarse mirando el cuerpo de Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in the distance, was the city square atop which they had constructed their camp."
msgstr "Allí, en la distancia, se alzaba la plaza de la ciudad sobre la que habían construido su campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, in the midsts of the small clearing in front of the tent, Sarah found her friend."
msgstr "Allí, en medio del pequeño claro frente a la tienda, Sarah encontró a su amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, it skips from thirty-eight to forty. What about pot number thirty-nine?"
msgstr "Allí, salta de treinta y ocho a cuarenta. ¿Qué hay del número treinta y nueve?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, looking back at her, his perfect smile."
msgstr "Allí, mirándola de nuevo, su sonrisa perfecta."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "There, looking like a princess again."
msgstr "Allí, luciendo de nuevo como una princesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, now don't be too sad, alright?"
msgstr "Ahí, ahora no te sientas demasiado triste, ¿de acuerdo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, on the far side of the throne room, cowering behind the throne, Sarah could see Samayra."
msgstr "Allí, en el extremo lejano de la sala del trono, agachada detrás del trono, Sarah podía ver a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, on the table, she remained exhausted."
msgstr "Ahí, sobre la mesa, permanecía agotada."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, re-throw those."
msgstr "¡Echala allá, maldita!"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There, rest. You are spend."
msgstr "Allá, descansa. Estás agotada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, she saw him stirring again."
msgstr "Allí, lo vio moviéndose de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, somewhere in the third week or so, Hugh appeared at their door as he had many times before."
msgstr "Allí, en algún lugar de la tercera semana aproximadamente, Hugh apareció en su puerta como había hecho muchas veces antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "There, take a seat over there."
msgstr "Allá, siéntate allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "There, that should be enough of that."
msgstr "Ahí, eso debería ser suficiente de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There, the Three Sisters held court, and held sway over life and death."
msgstr "Allí, las Tres Hermanas ejercían su tribunal y dominaban la vida y la muerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, the black violation of natural space, still loomed."
msgstr "Allí, la oscura invasión del espacio natural aún se cernía sobre todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, the two women, distant as they were, finished together."
msgstr "Allí, las dos mujeres, distantes como estaban, terminaron juntas."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There, there dear."
msgstr "Ahí, ahí, cariño."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There, there."
msgstr "Allá, allá."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "There, there..."
msgstr "Allá, allá..."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "There, there..."
msgstr "Ya, ya..."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "There, trapped, the darkness reached out and spoke to me, but it did not frighten me, Sarah, rather, it soothed."
msgstr "Allá, atrapada, la oscuridad se extendió y habló conmigo, pero no me aterrorizó, Sarah; al contrario, me calmó."

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "There, try this one."
msgstr "Aquí, prueba con esta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, wailing to herself, Sarah was come upon by Kate."
msgstr "Allí, llorando por sí misma, Sarah fue encontrada por Kate."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "There, we can set up tonight's camp there."
msgstr "Allí, podemos establecer el campamento para esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There, with hands entwined, the two women lost themselves to the madness of their moment."
msgstr "Allí, con las manos entrelazadas, las dos mujeres se entregaron a la locura de su momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "There."
msgstr "Allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "There."
msgstr "Allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There."
msgstr "Ahí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There. It is done."
msgstr "Allí. Está hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Shah Mahda"
msgid "There. Those are the directions to the vault. Take them, if you promise you will negotiate our surrender and keep my daughter safe."
msgstr "Ahí. Esas son las indicaciones hacia la bóveda. Tómalas, si prometes negociar nuestra rendición y mantener a mi hija a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There...were bandits there?"
msgstr "¿Había bandidos allí?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There?"
msgstr "¿Aquí?"

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These Noctori live long lives, but only in so far as that they are granted this longevity by this source of power."
msgstr "Estos Noctori viven largas vidas, pero solo en la medida en que les es concedida esta longevidad por esta fuente de poder."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These Noctori...they are all quite selfish in the end."
msgstr "Estos Noctori...al final, todos son bastante egoístas."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "These Tribesmen are good warriors, but they're not that good."
msgstr "Estos tribus son buenos guerreros, pero no tan buenos."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These Woodland spirits...they see the world in troubled ways. Like looking through a fogged window."
msgstr "Esos espíritus del bosque... ven el mundo de formas turbadas. Como si miraran a través de una ventana empañada."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "These alleys and streets are dangerous. You'd be better off stayin with me."
msgstr "Estas calles y callejones son peligrosos. Serías mejor si te quedaras conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are all the servants?"
msgstr "¿Estos son todos los sirvientes?"

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These are called Voidrifts. They're wounds upon reality."
msgstr "Estas se llaman Rupturas del Vacío. Son heridas en la realidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are his private quarters?"
msgstr "¿Estas son sus estancias privadas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "These are rare artifacts, called fate stones."
msgstr "Estas son piezas raras llamadas piedras del destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These are the books that will make some, and break others. These numbers determine who gets to live in the big houses and who gets to live in the small ones."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Officer"
msgid "These are the current drafts of our defensive lives."
msgstr "Estos son los borradores actuales de nuestra vida defensiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These are the known places where we've had attacks. About a doze or so now."
msgstr "Estos son los lugares donde hemos sufrido ataques. Alrededor de una docena, creo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are your...?"
msgstr "¿Estos son...?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These are..."
msgstr "Estos son..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These creatures from the void were unlike anything she'd ever known."
msgstr "Estas criaturas del vacío eran algo que nunca había conocido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These dark corners of the world, where the people of lowest character dwelled."
msgstr "Estos rincones oscuros del mundo, donde habitaban la gente de peor moral."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These days she lives out on our family estate. Tending the gardens."
msgstr "Estos días vive en nuestra finca familiar. Cuidando los jardines."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These days, if I'm on the road for more than a week, I can feel it in my bones."
msgstr "Estos días, si estoy de viaje más de una semana, lo siento en los huesos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These drunkards, who likely had drank away the last of their coin, were now above her. Using her."
msgstr "Estos borrachos, que probablemente habían bebido hasta el último de sus monedas, ahora estaban por encima de ella. Usándola."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These extreme times call for extreme measures, and so with a heavy heart I will take on myself the title of old."
msgstr "Estos tiempos extremos exigen medidas extremas, y así, con el corazón pesado, asumiré yo misma el título de anciana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These four countries together covered most of the Northern side of the great ocean, flanked only by the great desert to the east and the Hyral mountains to the west."
msgstr "Estos cuatro países juntos cubrían la mayor parte del lado norte del gran océano, flanqueados solo por el gran desierto al este y las montañas Hyral al oeste."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These gardens..."
msgstr "Estos jardines..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These had come to the men of the march once as curses, now as treasured possessions to the mad few that continued to march."
msgstr "Estos fueron una vez maldiciones para los hombres de la marcha, y ahora son posesiones codiciadas por los pocos locos que siguen marchando."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "These here are all the legal work we need to get sorted before we get to Mythra."
msgstr "Aquí tenemos todo el trabajo legal que necesitamos ordenar antes de llegar a Mythra."

msgctxt "speaker:Elsa"
msgid "These here are the menu items."
msgstr "Estos son los artículos del menú."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These last few days out here have been nice, but my life is a lot busier than you might think. Usually."
msgstr "Estos últimos días aquí han sido agradables, pero mi vida es mucho más ocupada de lo que podrías imaginar. Normalmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men and women, millenia old, who walked a world so different from theirs..."
msgstr "Estos hombres y mujeres, milenios antiguos, que caminaron por un mundo tan diferente al suyo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "These men hail from the Northern province, where they worked as merchants."
msgstr "Estos hombres provienen de la provincia del Norte, donde trabajaban como comerciantes."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These men made a vow and they kept it, even if it meant giving up their lives."
msgstr "Estos hombres hicieron un juramento y lo cumplieron, incluso si significaba sacrificar sus vidas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men were dressed for battle, as best as poor men could be."
msgstr "Estos hombres vestían para la batalla, tan bien como podían hacerlo unos pobres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These men, all these men, desired her. And if she learned to trade herself for the proper price, she could make something out of nothing."
msgstr "Estos hombres, todos estos hombres, la deseaban. Y si aprendía a intercambiarse por el precio adecuado, podría hacer algo con nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These mountains, dangerous and inhospitable, could not support large armies in the way the open plains could."
msgstr "Estas montañas, peligrosas e inhóspitas, no podían sostener grandes ejércitos como lo hacían las llanuras abiertas."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "These orc mountains, only orcs live here."
msgstr "Estas montañas de orcos, aquí solo viven los orcos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These particular ones could be cultivated into a potion that would harden the skin, so much so that swords would bounce off it."
msgstr "Estas en particular podrían cultivarse para crear una poción que endureciera la piel tanto que las espadas rebotarían contra ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These parts of town were dangerous, but with a small magical flame for light, Sarah managed to find her way and kept anyone from bothering her."
msgstr "Estas zonas del pueblo eran peligrosas, pero con una pequeña llama mágica para iluminar el camino, Sarah logró orientarse y mantener a raya a cualquiera que intentara molestarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "These people are alive because of you."
msgstr "Estas personas están vivas gracias a ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These people, safe, feared the arrival of so many fleeing."
msgstr "Estas personas, seguras, temían la llegada de tantos huidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These places and the people here, they didn't matter to the historians that wrote the large tomes that detailed the lives of Kings and Queens."
msgstr "Estos lugares y la gente de aquí no importaban a los historiadores que escribieron los grandes tomos que detallaban las vidas de reyes y reinas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These places lived in a perpetual shade, Sarah realized as she followed Alaric."
msgstr "Estos lugares vivían en una sombra perpetua, Sarah se dio cuenta mientras seguía a Alaric."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These prices, I can't work with them, I'll go find a real merchant with a real price."
msgstr "Estos precios no puedo trabajar con ellos; iré a buscar un mercader de verdad que ofrezca un precio real."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "These proposals, I frankly don't care much for one way or the other."
msgstr "Estas propuestas, francamente, no me importan demasiado de una manera u otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "These ropes are fine as they are blondie, how about you go and wash the linnens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "These scars I'll bear gladly."
msgstr "Estas cicatrices las llevaré con gusto."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "These shadow things? Someone more important than me can decide what needs to be done there."
msgstr "¿Estas sombras? Alguien más importante que yo puede decidir qué hay que hacer allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These shadowy creatures ripped and murdered for seemingly no reason at all."
msgstr "Estas criaturas sombrías arrancaron y asesinaron sin motivo alguno."

msgctxt "speaker:Barion"
msgid "These soldiers will take you back to your room until further order."
msgstr "Estos soldados os llevarán a vuestras habitaciones hasta que reciban nuevas órdenes."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These things represent the ripping of that fabric."
msgstr "Estas cosas representan la ruptura de ese tejido."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "These things...nobody gets it right the first time."
msgstr "Estas cosas... nadie lo hace bien la primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "These totems will distract the Woodland spirits. For a while at least."
msgstr "Estos tótems distraerán a los espíritus del bosque, al menos por un tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "These troublemakers then! They are blocking the road!"
msgstr "¡Estos cabrones! ¡Están bloqueando el camino!"

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "These tunnels can be a bitch if you get lost."
msgstr "Estos túneles pueden ser una cabrona si te pierdes."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "These tunnels will take us deeper into the labyrinth."
msgstr "Estos túneles nos llevarán más profundo en el laberinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These two men, each in their prime, their naked bodies pressing against each other..."
msgstr "Estos dos hombres, cada uno en su mejor momento, sus cuerpos desnudos presionándose el uno contra el otro..."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "These unresolved questions...they are a weakness."
msgstr "Estas preguntas sin resolver... son una debilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were all her peers. None were obliged to show her the curtesy that most other commoners and nobles alike owed her."
msgstr "Estos eran todos sus pares. Ninguno estaba obligado a mostrarle la cortesía que la mayoría de los otros plebeyos y nobles debían a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were all the Tribesmen had brought to her people."
msgstr "Estos eran todos los que las tribus habían traído a su pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were heads, but judging by their features, they were clearly Tribesmen."
msgstr "Estas eran cabezas, pero juzgando por sus facciones, claramente eran tribales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were men with pent up urges, and they had found in her a willing release for it."
msgstr "Estos eran hombres con deseos reprimidos, y habían encontrado en ella una liberación dispuesta para ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the moments where she wished she could just stay in forever."
msgstr "Estos eran los momentos en los que deseaba poder quedarse ahí para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the only words she could muster."
msgstr "Estas fueron las únicas palabras que pudo reunir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These were the only words she managed to produce, quiet as a mouse."
msgstr "Estas fueron las únicas palabras que pudo articular, silenciosa como un ratón."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "These women are fine and proper royal ladies of the court of Bagrad."
msgstr "Estas damas son mujeres finas y nobles de la corte de Bagrad."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "These women here, my fine friends, aren't just any ladies."
msgstr "Estas mujeres aquí, mis queridas amigas, no son cualquier dama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "These words seemed to calm Samayra down."
msgstr "Estas palabras parecieron calmar a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They advanced...but not really."
msgstr "Avanzaron... pero no de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They ain't gonna let you die, but they won't lose a night sleep over you not eatin for a day either."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all passed through the castle, some so trivial they made Sarah want to scream out and remind everyone they were at war."
msgstr "Todos pasaron por el castillo; algunos tan triviales que Sarah quiso gritar y recordar a todos que estaban en guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They all said the stone was black, but it seemed so obvious that it was red."
msgstr "Todos dijeron que la piedra era negra, pero parecía tan obvio que era roja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all suffered their ends."
msgstr "Todos sufrieron su fin."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They all take place outside the village."
msgstr "Todos se llevan a cabo fuera del pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They all went quiet as they listened to him speak, loudly, boasting, in his Tribal tongue."
msgstr "Se quedaron en silencio, escuchándole hablar con voz alta, presumiendo y usando su idioma tribal."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They allow masters to set their slaves free, but they are no fools."
msgstr "Les permiten a los señores liberar a sus esclavos, pero no son tontas."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They also said it was the most advanced form of magic, and that only the greatest mages could master it."
msgstr "También dijeron que era la forma más avanzada de magia y que solo los mayores magos podían dominarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They always do, sooner or later."
msgstr "Siempre lo hacen, antes o después."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They always say that, don't they?"
msgstr "¿Siempre dicen eso, verdad?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They applied a red paint to her body, painting ritual markings that made no sense to her but seemed sacred to them."
msgstr "Les aplicaron una pintura roja sobre su cuerpo, dibujando marcas rituales que no tenían sentido para ella pero que parecían sagradas para ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are as weak husbands, demanding a reward because they were faithful to their wives."
msgstr "Son maridos tan débiles que exigen una recompensa por haber sido fieles a sus esposas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They are collected. Put to work. Returned."
msgstr "Son reunidos. Puestos a trabajar. Devueltos."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They are creatures of the void, born out of the shadows in the under realm."
msgstr "Son criaturas del vacío, nacidas de las sombras en el reino subterráneo."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "They are disciplined, strong, experienced."
msgstr "Son disciplinados, fuertes y experimentados."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are dressed little different than farmers. Merchants. Tell me how I know these to be bandits and not victims?"
msgstr "Están vestidos apenas diferente a los campesinos o a los mercaderes. ¿Cómo sé yo que son bandidos y no víctimas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are driven by a simple desire, to escape their horrid torture. And for a brief moment, they will. But they are lured into a trap. A war they cannot win."
msgstr "Son impulsados por un deseo simple: huir de su horrible tortura. Y por un breve instante lo lograrán. Pero son atraídos hacia una trampa. Una guerra que no pueden ganar."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "They are instead grown by combining the basics of growing plants, with magical infusion."
msgstr "En su lugar, se cultivan combinando los principios básicos del cultivo de plantas con una infusión mágica."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are looking for something, buried in the sands of the city. Something they have been searching for, for a long time now."
msgstr "Están buscando algo, enterrado en las arenas de la ciudad. Algo que han estado buscando desde hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are loyal to us, as the lesser lords are loyal to them, and as the peasants are loyal to them."
msgstr "Son leales a nosotros, tal como los señores menores son leales a ellos, y tal como los campesinos son leales a ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They are members of the Highfield family."
msgstr "Son miembros de la familia Highfield."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are more often a simple kind, with simple pleasures."
msgstr "Son más bien gente sencilla, con simples placeres."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are my friends, my family. Not by blood, but by choice."
msgstr "Son mis amigos, mi familia. No por sangre, sino por elección."

msgctxt "speaker:Emmissary"
msgid "They are my gift to you, Princess of Rosanna."
msgstr "Ellos son mi regalo para ti, Princesa de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are my people!"
msgstr "¡Son mi gente!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are not the way of the world."
msgstr "No son la senda del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They are the leaders of the Mythran Empire, yes, but they are in their own way enslaved."
msgstr "Son los líderes del Imperio Mythran, sí, pero están esclavizados de su propia manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They are the well from which all the laws that govern nature spring forth."
msgstr "Son la fuente de la cual brotan todas las leyes que rigen la naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They are tired, spend. Our supplies dwindle."
msgstr "Están agotados, gastados. Nuestras reservas se agotan."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They are trying to kill you, but they will not succeed."
msgstr "Ellos intentan matarte, pero no lo lograrán."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They are! Here, follow me and I'll take you there."
msgstr "¡Sí! Aquí, sígueme y te llevaré allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They argued back and forth for a while."
msgstr "Se argumentaron de ida y vuelta durante un rato."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They assigned us to work the same shift."
msgstr "Nos asignaron el mismo turno de trabajo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ate and shared stories until deep into the night, until it had become so late they were forced to go home."
msgstr "Comieron y compartieron historias hasta muy tarde, hasta que la hora había avanzado tanto que se vieron obligados a volver."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They awoke early the next day to continue their exploration of the forest."
msgstr "Se despertaron temprano al día siguiente para continuar su exploración del bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They balanced on a riot. Mutiny."
msgstr "Se equilibraban en una revuelta. Una rebelión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They been spreading that story before I was even a kid."
msgstr "Lo han contado antes de que yo fuera siquiera un niño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began in the bed."
msgstr "Comenzaron en la cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to pull and move her body like a ragdoll."
msgstr "Comenzaron a arrastrar y mover su cuerpo como si fuera un muñeco de trapo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to pull her away with such strength that she could not offer any resistance."
msgstr "Comenzaron a arrastrarla con tanta fuerza que no pudo ofrecer ninguna resistencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to speak to one another in a foul language she had no way of understanding."
msgstr "Comenzaron a hablar entre sí en un lenguaje sucio que no tenía forma de comprender."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They began to teach their followers how to wield God killing magic as well."
msgstr "Comenzaron también a enseñar a sus seguidores cómo manejar la magia capaz de matar a los dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to throw their magics at it, whipping the beast into a furious frenzy."
msgstr "Comenzaron a lanzar sus magias contra él, azotando a la bestia hasta convertirla en una locura furiosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to walk together, down one of the hallways, away from the celebrating masses."
msgstr "Comenzaron a caminar juntos por uno de los pasillos, alejándose de las masas que celebraban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They began to walk, crossing the vast Receiving Hall and entering the palace interior."
msgstr "Comenzaron a caminar, cruzando la vasta Sala de Recepción y entrando en el interior del palacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They begin to drag the men away."
msgstr "Comienzan a arrastrar a los hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They believe that they are entitled to the women they conquer, because they are the strongest."
msgstr "Ellas creen que tienen derecho a las mujeres que conquistan, porque son las más fuertes."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "They believe that together, one highly trained male soldier and female soldier, can make one perfectly rounded warrior."
msgstr "Creían que, juntos, un soldado altamente entrenado y una soldadera muy bien entrenada podían crear a un guerrero perfectamente equilibrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They believed that with you and your brother under arrest, they could take over the country with little bloodshed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They belonged to Sarah alone."
msgstr "Pertenecían únicamente a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They block the sight of the gods, making them blind to what transpires near the stone."
msgstr "Bloquean la vista de los dioses, dejándolos ciegos ante lo que ocurre cerca de la piedra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They blocked their path."
msgstr "Bloquearon su camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They bore witness."
msgstr "Ellos fueron testigos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They both look at captain Belmont and yell out in unison."
msgstr "¡Ambos miran al capitán Belmont y gritan en unísono!"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They both saw the future, and uttered it into existence, at the same time."
msgstr "Ambos vieron el futuro y lo pronunciaron en la existencia, al mismo tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They both walked towards the fire, as if drawn by instinct."
msgstr "Ambos caminaron hacia el fuego, como si fueran arrastrados por un instinto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They broke the great Orc Hordes of old, crushing them on the open fields and chasing them into the mountains where they now lived in squalor."
msgstr "Derrotaron a las grandes hordas de orcos del antiguo tiempo, aplastándolos en los campos abiertos y persiguiéndolos hasta las montañas, donde ahora viven en miseria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They broke the spirit of the people of Calshure, over and over again, praying for one of them to rise up and be a worthy fight."
msgstr "Rompieron el espíritu del pueblo de Calshure, una y otra vez, rezando porque uno de ellos se alzara para ser un digno oponente."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They broke through..."
msgstr "Atravesaron..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They brought up all the girls and they forced them to look at the stone and tell him what it looked like."
msgstr "Trajeron a todas las chicas y las obligaron a mirar la piedra y decirle qué parecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They call it Martial Arts. It's a special form of fighting in the Far Lands."
msgstr "Lo llaman Artes Marciales. Es una forma especial de combatir en las Tierras Lejanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They call me Raza. What is your name?"
msgstr "Me llaman Raza. ¿Cuál es tu nombre?"

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They call me a military prodigy, but I don't know about all that."
msgstr "Me llaman prodigio militar, pero no sé nada de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They came in all shapes, sizes and ages."
msgstr "Venían en todas las formas, tamaños y edades."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They can all go to hell if they think they get to tell me anything today."
msgstr "Pueden irse todos al infierno si piensan que hoy voy a aceptar sus órdenes."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They can cross the distance between the eastern district and the capital much faster than a regular army could. They could cut off the capital in a matter of days."
msgstr "Podrían cruzar la distancia entre el distrito oriental y la capital mucho más rápido que un ejército regular. Podrían aislar la capital en cuestión de días."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They can do the grunt work of ripping open drawers, hoping to find a necklace. Gods know I did that shit long enough."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They can even vary by the very laws that govern them."
msgstr "Incluso pueden variar según las propias leyes que los rigen."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "They can sense other creatures floating in that space."
msgstr "Pueden percibir a otras criaturas flotando en ese espacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They can't expect us to agree to that...can they?"
msgstr "No pueden esperar que aceptemos eso... ¿verdad?"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They can't respect rank."
msgstr "No pueden respetar el rango."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They can't survive in our world for very long. It will rage for a few days, then slowly collapse and die."
msgstr "No podrán sobrevivir en nuestro mundo por mucho tiempo. La tormenta se desatará durante unos días, luego colapsará lentamente y morirá."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They captured him, his wife, his four sons and two daughters."
msgstr "Los capturaron a él, a su esposa y a sus cuatro hijos varones e hijas."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They cared nothing for those who ended up here. Much less for the Arts that the Imperial family pursued."
msgstr "No les importaba quienes acabaron aquí, ni mucho menos las Artes que la familia imperial cultivaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They catch you or buy you?"
msgstr "¿Te atrapan o te compran?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They caught her staring."
msgstr "Me atraparon."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They caught me."
msgstr "Me atraparon."

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "They celebrate the year passing same time each year. Each time, I put a notch in the beam there."
msgstr "Cada año celebran el paso del tiempo de la misma manera. Cada vez, hago una muesca en la viga allí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They chanted her name, and with each chant, her name grew louder."
msgstr "Ellos gritaban su nombre, y con cada grito, su nombre se hacía más potente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They clanked their chalices together."
msgstr "Chocaron sus cálices entre sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They come and go."
msgstr "Vienen y van."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They come in all kinds of shapes, and I'll admit, this one was bigger than the usual kind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They consider loot earned without bloodshed to be...dishonorable."
msgstr "Ellos consideran que el botín ganado sin derramamiento de sangre es... deshonroso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued along the road for several more days, before finally coming upon the village of Hillstown."
msgstr "Continuaron por el camino durante varios días más, antes de finalmente llegar al pueblo de Hillstown."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued their screams as she looked out over them."
msgstr "Continuaron sus gritos mientras ella miraba sobre ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to explore the festival ground together whilst eating."
msgstr "Continuaron explorando el terreno del festival mientras comían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to play the game. Round afte round."
msgstr "Continuaron jugando al juego. Ronda tras ronda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued to walk through the vast, almost endless, gardens of the palace."
msgstr "Continuaron caminando por los vastos jardines del palacio, casi infinitos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They continued walking."
msgstr "Continuaron caminando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could be broken."
msgstr "Podrían estar rotos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could be dangerous, but there was a reason for why they acted."
msgstr "Podían ser peligrosos, pero había una razón por la que actuaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could hardly keep a bonfire going. The days of their glory had long faded."
msgstr "Apenas podían mantener encendido un fuego de leña. Sus días de gloria habían desaparecido hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could have all shouldered a great deal, knowing that their trials might soon end, but by now, nobody could be certain if they would ever end at all."
msgstr "Podrían haber soportado todo, sabiendo que sus pruebas pronto terminarían, pero ahora nadie podía estar seguro de si alguna vez acabarían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could manage a night without her."
msgstr "Podían pasar una noche sin ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could not just sit here and wait for the Tribesmen to finish them off."
msgstr "No podían simplemente sentarse aquí y esperar a que los Tribales los acabaran."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They could reach back and resume all the injustices that had slipped by in their absence."
msgstr "Podrían volver atrás y reanudar todas las injusticias que se les escaparon mientras estaban ausentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They could speak without words."
msgstr "Podían hablar sin palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "They crawl on their knees but they don't pull up their skirts properly, so they usually scrape them and tear them on a loose brick."
msgstr "Se arrastran sobre sus rodillas pero no se ajustan bien las faldas, por lo que suelen raspárselas y rasgarlas contra un ladrillo suelto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They crawl through the frenzy and find one another. Their hands link. Neither fears death as it comes for them."
msgstr "Se arrastran a través del frenesí y se encuentran entre sí. Enlazan sus manos. Ninguno teme a la muerte mientras se acerca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cried out her name, louder and louder."
msgstr "¡Gritaron su nombre, cada vez con más fuerza!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cried out their loyalty all at once."
msgstr "Lanzaron un grito de lealtad al unísono."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cross the vast throne room, each near exhaustion as they finally get back to the exit that Xan had made."
msgstr "Cruzan la vasta sala del trono, cada uno cerca del agotamiento, cuando finalmente llegan a la salida que Xan había preparado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cursed many things, but as men are prone to do, they soon found a concensus for their hatreds."
msgstr "Maldijeron muchas cosas, pero como suele ocurrir con los hombres, pronto llegaron a un consenso sobre sus odios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They cut him down, but he was already cold to the touch, long dead."
msgstr "Lo abatieron, pero ya estaba frío al tacto, muerto desde hacía mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They deeply believe in the system of slavery, and so anything done to overturn that is looked upon with suspicion."
msgstr "Ellos creen profundamente en el sistema de la esclavitud, y por eso todo lo que se hace para derrocarlo es visto con sospecha."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They delighted in knowing the pain they inflicted on them, each time another girl was married off to a tribesmen."
msgstr "Se deleitaban en saber el dolor que les infligían, cada vez que otra chica se casaba con un tribiano."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They deliver most of our coal and iron."
msgstr "Ellos suministran la mayoría de nuestro carbón y hierro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They desired a lifetime but had only a night to themselves."
msgstr "Deseaban una vida entera, pero solo tenían una noche para sí mismos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They desired only that we made use of it for as long as we pleased, and when we were finished with life, we could go to the tower of dying, and fade away."
msgstr "Solo deseaban que hiciéramos uso de ello tanto como nos plazca, y cuando hubiéramos terminado con la vida, podríamos ir a la torre del morir y desvanecernos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did as they were told, but a cold rage was growing in them."
msgstr "Obedecieron lo que se les ordenó, pero una fría rabia crecía en ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did not eat as animals did. Nor did they conquer as men did. They simply destroyed anything and everything."
msgstr "No comían como los animales ni conquistaban como los hombres; simplemente destruían todo y a todos."

msgctxt "speaker:Advisor"
msgid "They did not even care for a meeting."
msgstr "Ni siquiera se preocupaban por una reunión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They did not know war, and so they did not fear it the way they should."
msgstr "No conocían la guerra y, por tanto, no la temían como debían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't care enough to stop her. Nor enough to help."
msgstr "No les importaba lo suficiente para detenerla. Ni lo bastante como para ayudar."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They didn't give a fuck, so they simply constructed these large housing blocks."
msgstr "No les importaba nada, así que simplemente construyeron estos grandes bloques de viviendas."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They didn't have one in your size, so they had to make that one custom."
msgstr "No tenían uno de tu tamaño, así que tuvieron que fabricar ese a medida."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They didn't let me in the church, obviously, but I got to watch from my little room how he walked in there with all the others."
msgstr "No me dejaron entrar en la iglesia, por supuesto, pero pude observar desde mi pequeña habitación cómo entraba allí junto con todos los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't need words, Sarah thought to herself as she fell back into the bed, pulling the girl with her."
msgstr "No necesitaban palabras, pensó Sarah para sí misma mientras caía de nuevo en la cama, arrastrando a la chica consigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't seem intent on meeting the Rosannan army on the open field, but rather, to agitate them to attack first."
msgstr "No parecían tener intención de encontrarse con el ejército rosano en campo abierto, sino más bien de provocarlos para que atacaran primero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They didn't want to be here, and the desert didn't want them."
msgstr "No querían estar aquí, y el desierto no los quería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They died without in great numbers and with little glory."
msgstr "Murieron sin gran número y con poca gloria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They discuss strategy, organizing local militias to resist the raiding party, deploying additional scouts."
msgstr "Discuten estrategia, organizando milicias locales para resistir la partida de saqueadores y desplegando escopeteros adicionales."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "They dissapear."
msgstr "Desaparecen."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They do?"
msgstr "¿Ellos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They dominate the beginning and the end."
msgstr "Ellos dominan el principio y el fin."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They don't deserve this...she doesn't deserve this..."
msgstr "No lo merecen... ella no lo merece..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They don't force you or anything. You can just work the shift."
msgstr "No te obligan a nada. Solo tienes que trabajar el turno."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They don't see much of the captain after that."
msgstr "Después de eso, no ven mucho al capitán."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They don't understand the culture, how we fight among one another but still remain suspect of outsiders."
msgstr "No entienden nuestra cultura, cómo luchamos entre nosotros y aun así seguimos desconfiando de los forasteros."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They don't worry about hurting you. They worry about hurting his pride."
msgstr "No se preocupan por lastimarte. Se preocupan por lastimar su orgullo."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They don't. They think you are weak. Vulnerable."
msgstr "No lo hacen. Te consideran débil. Vulnerable."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They don'ts know how to be proper round a lady, too long out at sea pokin each other."
msgstr "¡No saben comportarse con decencia ante una dama, han estado demasiado tiempo en el mar follando entre sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They doubted."
msgstr "Dudaron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They drag her out of the auction house, through the busy streets, and down alleys."
msgstr "La arrastran fuera de la casa de subastas, por las calles bulliciosas y por callejones."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They dream of a violent death."
msgstr "Ellas sueñan con una muerte violenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They dresses were made of a fine silk, a rich embroidery decorating from the waist down to the skirt line."
msgstr "Sus vestidos estaban hechos de una fina seda, con un rico bordado que decoraba desde la cintura hasta la línea de la falda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They drew their cloaks as tight around themselves as they could manage."
msgstr "Apretaron sus capotes lo más posible contra sí mismas."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They drink, they feast, and that seems to be about all they do."
msgstr "Beben, se embriagan y eso parece ser todo lo que hacen."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each held a branch of dreamstalk in their hands, as if it were made of gold."
msgstr "Cada uno sostenía un tallo de planta del sueño en sus manos, como si estuviera hecho de oro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each retired to their own bedroll."
msgstr "Cada uno se retiró a su propia manta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each sat down again."
msgstr "Cada uno se sentó de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They each took one step and crossed a million."
msgstr "Cada uno dio un paso y cruzó un millón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They embrace each other, the captain's cum still on them."
msgstr "Se abrazan con ternura, la semilla del capitán aún en ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ended up in a decidedly poorer part of town. Boarded up windows, drunkards, trash heaped up."
msgstr "Acabaron en una parte decididamente más pobre del pueblo. Ventanas tapiadas, borrachos, basura amontonada."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They ended up looting the wrong city near one of the borders."
msgstr "Terminaron saqueando la ciudad equivocada, cerca de una de las fronteras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They enjoyed, more than anything, the dominance of it."
msgstr "Lo disfrutaban más que nada: la dominancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They expect it because they were fools and did not know the law of their new land."
msgstr "Esperan que así sea porque son tontos y no conocen la ley de su nueva tierra."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They extend from here, all the way up north to the mountains, and around there, they turn into swamplands."
msgstr "Se extienden desde aquí hasta el norte, hasta las montañas, y de allí giran hacia los pantanos."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They failed to see the world for what it was, and so instead they fell into despair."
msgstr "No vieron el mundo por lo que era, y así cayeron en la desesperanza."

msgctxt "speaker:Ragged Man"
msgid "They fear what all parents fear, to lose sight of their child. They urge you to turn away from this path to nothingness."
msgstr "Tienen miedo a lo que todo padre teme: perder de vista a su hija. Te instan, con urgencia, a apartarte de este camino hacia la nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They feast. All drunk. Stupid!"
msgstr "Se banquetean. Todos borrachos. ¡Estúpidos!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They featured blackmail, bribery and at times even assassinations."
msgstr "Recurren a chantas, sobornos e incluso asesinatos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fell to the earth, their bodies mixed in with the mud and snow and blood."
msgstr "Cayeron al suelo, sus cuerpos mezclados con el barro, la nieve y la sangre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They felt like treason to her own ears."
msgstr "Les pareció traición a sus propios oídos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finally arive in Lethram."
msgstr "Finalmente llegan a Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finally broke through the thick forest, coming back out on the open road."
msgstr "Finalmente atravesaron el espeso bosque y salieron al camino abierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They finished their meal together, chatting away the hours until night came."
msgstr "Terminaron su comida juntos, charlando hasta que llegó la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They fled beyond the borders of this world, hiding themselves in a space that even they themselves are blind to."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They forgettin there's all sorts of worlds out there."
msgstr "Se olvidan de que existen todo tipo de mundos fuera de aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They form the council that send people out on missions. They're the ones that send me off to the ruins, in fact."
msgstr "Ellas forman el consejo que envía chicas a misiones. Ellas son las que me mandan a los restos, de hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fought among each other. They carried out the occasional raid when they dared."
msgstr "Se pelearon entre sí. Realizaron incursiones ocasionales cuando se atrevían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fought not with knightly skill, but pure and raw strength."
msgstr "No luchaban con destreza caballeresca, sino con una fuerza pura y cruda."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "They fought the Voidlings and their three-sister demons to a stalemate."
msgstr "Lucharon contra los Voidlings y sus demonios de tres hermanas hasta llegar a un punto muerto."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They found the creature, and fearing for its life still, it threw itself on their mercy."
msgstr "Encontraron a la criatura y, aún temiendo por su vida, se arrojó a su misericordia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fucked themselves into exhaustion, the sweat dripping from their bodies, only adding to the overwhelming sensations."
msgstr "Se follaron hasta el agotamiento, con el sudor goteando por sus cuerpos, lo que solo aumentaba las sensaciones abrumadoras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They fucked until their bodies could carry them no further, and each sank and collapsed into an oblivion."
msgstr "Se follaron hasta que sus cuerpos no pudieron sostenerlos más, y cada uno se hundió y colapsó en un olvido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gathered in the council room of the castle."
msgstr "Se reunieron en la sala del consejo del castillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gathered up their plates and headed inside."
msgstr "Reunieron sus platos y entraron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gesture and yell, towards her, towards them. Nobody speaks the language, but everyone understands."
msgstr "Gesticulan y gritan hacia ella, hacia ellos. Nadie habla el idioma, pero todos entienden."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They get hard to count after a while."
msgstr "Se vuelven difíciles de contar con el tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They get paid, sure, and if they survive they'll win some glory, but for the most part it leaves the economies of these small towns in shambles."
msgstr "Sí, reciben pago y si sobreviven ganarán algún tipo de gloria, pero en gran parte dejan las economías de estos pueblos pequeños en ruinas."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They go around telling you what you can and can't do so much you start to believe it. But they have no right."
msgstr "Te dicen tanto qué puedes y qué no que acabas por creértelo. Pero no tienen derecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They gossiped about them. Insulted them. Laughed at them."
msgstr "Se burlaban de ellos. Los insultaban. Reían de ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "They got some, but they're still pouring it. Said it will be a few minutes."
msgstr "Tienen algo, pero siguen vertiéndolo. Dijeron que serán unos minutos más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They grab the leader first."
msgstr "Atrapan primero al líder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They grew up in the same town, and after it was burned down in a raid, decided to stick together."
msgstr "Crecieron en el mismo pueblo y, después de que fuera incendiado en un asalto, decidieron quedarse juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They had a whole civilization here...long before any other came along."
msgstr "Tenían toda una civilización aquí... mucho antes de que llegaran los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had barely closed the door before they were all over each other."
msgstr "Apenas habían cerrado la puerta cuando ya estaban encima el uno del otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had become only painful reminders of what she had lost."
msgstr "Solo quedaban como recordatorios dolorosos de lo que había perdido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been friends a lifetime ago, and it struck Sarah as remarkable that they had somehow found one another again."
msgstr "Habían sido amigos hace una vida, y le pareció asombroso a Sarah que de alguna manera se hubieran encontrado otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been loyal."
msgstr "Fueron leales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been marching for a long day."
msgstr "Habían estado marchando durante todo el día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been out there until their father had furiously come to collect them, warning them of the cold."
msgstr "Estaban allí afuera hasta que su padre vino furioso a recogerlos, advirtiéndoles del frío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been ready to die. Every Tribesman was trained to expect death."
msgstr "Estaban dispuestos a morir. Cada tribiano estaba entrenado para esperar la muerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been right. She wouldn't have survived for a day out here without them."
msgstr "Tenían razón. Ella no habría sobrevivido ni un día aquí sin ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been saved."
msgstr "Habían sido salvados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been searching for an odd, defenseless girl. None of them had signed up to fight a mage."
msgstr "Habían estado buscando a una extraña y indefensa chica. Ninguno de ellos se había inscrito para luchar contra un mago."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been some of the first to embrace her in the mercenary company."
msgstr "Algunos de los primeros en abrazarla en la compañía mercenaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been through a lot together, survived one battle after the other, and still Sarah worried the same each time for Kate."
msgstr "Han pasado por mucho juntos, han sobrevivido a una batalla tras otra, y aún así Sarah se preocupaba por Kate cada vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been together for little more than a month, a fleeting moment across the whole of her life, and still that fraction of her life loomed larger than most others."
msgstr "Han estado juntos poco más de un mes, un instante efímero en toda su vida, y aún esa fracción de ella se alzaba como una sombra mayor que la mayoría de los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been trained to deal with pickpockets and other lowlives."
msgstr "Estaban entrenados para lidiar con ladrones y otros malvivientes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had been trained to fight in battles against other soldiers, few knew anything about magic, other than to run away."
msgstr "Habían sido entrenados para luchar en batallas contra otros soldados; pocos sabían nada de magia, salvo huir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had believed in victory, but now they had a taste of it."
msgstr "Creían en la victoria, pero ahora habían saboreado el amargo sabor de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had believed in victory, but now they had tasted defeat."
msgstr "Habían creído en la victoria, pero ahora habían saboreado la derrota."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had clearly been wrong on the latter, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Claramente se habían equivocado en lo segundo, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had conquered a great city, were rich on loot. They had a reason for being in good spirits."
msgstr "Habían conquistado una gran ciudad y estaban ricos en botín; tenían motivo para estar de buen humor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had considered buying a new one, but they could not have justified the price."
msgstr "Habían considerado comprar una nueva, pero no podían justificar el precio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had continued to make good distance in the days that followed."
msgstr "Continuaron avanzando con buen ritmo en los días siguientes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had crowded around a young man with a thin frame and long, flowing blonde hair, reaching to his shoulders."
msgstr "Se habían aglomerado alrededor de un joven de complexión delgada y cabello rubio largo y ondulado que le llegaba hasta los hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had cut so deep into her army."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had defeated the Tribes, but victory was not so clean."
msgstr "Habían derrotado a las tribus, pero la victoria no fue tan limpia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had developped into quite a team over the few days spend together."
msgstr "Se habían convertido en un equipo bastante sólido durante los pocos días que pasaron juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had discussed strategy, he had offered some words of comfort, but in the end there wasn't much else he could offer."
msgstr "Habían discutido estrategias; él había ofrecido algunas palabras de consuelo, pero al final no había mucho más que pudiera ofrecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had done many things together in their short time, violating the law and each other. Yet despite all these things, Sarah had kept a great part of herself hidden."
msgstr "Han hecho muchas cosas juntos en su breve tiempo, violando la ley y el uno al otro. Sin embargo, a pesar de todo ello, Sarah ha mantenido gran parte de sí misma oculta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had driven her out as a foolish girl, but she would return to them a warrior."
msgstr "Los habían expulsado como a una niña tonta, pero volverían a ellos como guerrera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had each other, and it was all they needed."
msgstr "Tendrían el uno al otro, y eso era todo lo que necesitaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had exchanged glances, kisses and touches. Still this felt more intimate than any of it."
msgstr "Se habían intercambiado miradas, besos y caricias. Sin embargo, esto se sentía más íntimo que todo ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had explored every corner of the castle together, for years, they had been inseparable."
msgstr "Habían explorado cada rincón del castillo juntos durante años; habían sido inseparables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had feared the Tribesmen, as well they should have, but now they learned they were as mortal as any other man."
msgstr "Tuvieron miedo de los tribales, como debían, pero ahora aprendieron que eran tan mortales como cualquier otro hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had gambled a lot on the hope that they might kill her and break apart her army."
msgstr "Apostaron mucho por la esperanza de que pudieran matarla y desmantelar su ejército."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had gathered in a wide circle around her, and in their midsts, Samayra performed as only she could."
msgstr "Se reunieron en un amplio círculo alrededor de ella, y entre ellos, Samayra se desempeñó como solo ella podía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had hoped this would be the case."
msgstr "Esperaban que fuera así."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They had it empty for a while after the last girl decided to run away."
msgstr "Los tenían vacíos por un tiempo después de que la última chica decidiera huir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had just scrapped the frost off one of the rigging chains and despite wearing gloves, each of their hands were swollen and red from the cold."
msgstr "Acababan de quitar el hielo de una de las cadenas del aparejo y, aunque llevaban guantes, cada uno de sus manos estaban hinchadas y rojas por el frío."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They had kept their plans well hidden, but Barion saw me as a friend, and he confided in me shortly before the meeting began."
msgstr "Habían mantenido sus planes bien ocultos, pero Barion me veía como un amigo y me confió todo poco antes de que comenzara la reunión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had kissed before, but this...this time it was different."
msgstr "Se habían besado antes, pero esta...esta vez era diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had left her a shabby blanket as a cloak, or perhaps, to cover herself up in hopes not to look at her anymore."
msgstr "Les dejaron una manta raída para que la usara como capa, o tal vez, para cubrirse a sí misma con la esperanza de no tener que mirarla más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had left the city, Sarah realized only now."
msgstr "Sarah se dio cuenta de que habían abandonado la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had looked on with even greater surprise when they saw the mercenaries leave, not through the western gates for Lethram, but the long abandoned eastern gates to nowhere."
msgstr "Se quedaron mirando con aún mayor sorpresa al ver que los mercenarios se habían marchado, no por las puertas occidentales hacia Lethram, sino por las largas puertas orientales abandonadas, hacia ninguna parte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made a fool out of her."
msgstr "Los habían hecho una tonta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made camp deep in the forest."
msgstr "Acamparon profundamente en el bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made good progress and she had seen few if any signs of bandits."
msgstr "Habían avanzado con buen ritmo y apenas había visto señales de bandidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had made her a slave."
msgstr "La habían hecho esclava."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had managed Marius, but what had she won, truly?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had marched from the capital straight towards the province of Dianthus, home of the Achillea family and center of the rebellion."
msgstr "Habían marchado desde la capital directamente hacia la provincia de Dianthus, hogar de la familia Achillea y centro de la rebelión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had marched on longer than usual, making up time by pushing themselves to keep going through the first hours of the night."
msgstr "Han marchado más de lo habitual, ganando tiempo forzándose a seguir avanzando durante las primeras horas de la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had met for a moment when the old soldier pulled on the chain and dragged her through a door, off to the back of the auction house. Wherever it was he wanted to go, he seemed to be in a hurry."
msgstr "Se habían detenido un momento cuando el viejo soldado tiró de la cadena y arrastró a Sarah hacia una puerta, llevándola al fondo de la casa de subastas. A dondequiera que él quisiera ir, parecía estar apurado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had nearly lost everything."
msgstr "Habían perdido casi todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had never dared to speak of what their relationship was, but Sarah knew it had gone too far many times."
msgstr "Nunca se habían atrevido a hablar de qué era su relación, pero Sarah sabía que había llegado demasiado lejos en muchas ocasiones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had never spoken of it explicitly, but Sarah was no fool to the reality of life."
msgstr "Nunca lo habían dicho explícitamente, pero Sarah no era tonta para la realidad de la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had not been expecting to have to do any real work tonight, that much was clear to her."
msgstr "Eso era claro para ella: no habían esperado tener que hacer ningún trabajo real esta noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had not expected this enemy. But they had also not expected that an attack could happen everywhere all at once."
msgstr "No se habían esperado a este enemigo. Pero tampoco se habían imaginado que un ataque pudiera ocurrir en todas partes al mismo tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had once been so organized, so efficient."
msgstr "Solían ser tan organizados, tan eficientes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had only just entered when he lifted her up form the ground with his arms."
msgstr "Acababan de entrar cuando él la levantó del suelo con sus brazos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had only just stumbled inside when Sarah could feel both pair of hands on her body."
msgstr "Acababan de entrar tambaleándose cuando Sarah sintió ambas manos sobre su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had planned to use one of the main roads from the coast to the capital to transport their army."
msgstr "Habían planeado utilizar una de las carreteras principales que conectan la costa con la capital para transportar a su ejército."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had practiced a degree of restraint, her husband choosing to finish outside of her most evenings."
msgstr "Habían practicado un grado de contención, su esposo eligiendo terminar fuera de ella la mayoría de las noches."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had prepared, but would it be enough?"
msgstr "Habían preparado todo, pero ¿sería suficiente?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had pretended to defend it from the walls, only to sneak out of the city from the other side, and flank them."
msgstr "Habían fingido defenderla desde las murallas, solo para salir sigilosamente de la ciudad por el otro lado y flanquearlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had sat her down somewhere, but nobody told her anything. There was only the darkness."
msgstr "La habían sentado en algún lugar, pero nadie le dijo nada. Solo había oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had seemed no less real."
msgstr "Parecían igual de reales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had set themselves towards her like a project."
msgstr "Se habían colocado frente a ella como un proyecto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had shown kindness to her when she first came to the camp."
msgstr "Les habían mostrado amabilidad cuando ella llegó por primera vez al campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had spend a lifetime perfecting the sideway glance. To see without seeing. Notice without being noticed."
msgstr "Habían pasado una vida perfeccionando la mirada de reojo. Ver sin ser vistos. Notar sin ser notados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had spend the last few years learning to listen obediently, or suffer the consequences."
msgstr "Habían pasado los últimos años aprendiendo a obedecer, o sufrir las consecuencias."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had suffered only a few casualties, and inflicted a hundred times over what they had suffered."
msgstr "Han sufrido solo unas pocas bajas e infligido cien veces más de lo que han padecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived the fall of Lethram. Survived their torturous journey. Land."
msgstr "Han sobrevivido a la caída de Lethram. Han sobrevivido a su tortuoso viaje por tierra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived the raids by the Tribesmen. They had survived the merciless frost. And now, she was rewarded."
msgstr "Habían sobrevivido a los asaltos de los tribales. Habían sobrevivido al implacable frío. Y ahora, ella era recompensada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived."
msgstr "Han sobrevivido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had survived. They would survive longer."
msgstr "Han sobrevivido. Sobrevivirán más tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had talked so long that night."
msgstr "Habían hablado tanto esa noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had taught her a lesson. Now she would return the favor and teach the Tribes her lessons of war."
msgstr "Les habían enseñado una lección. Ahora ella devolvería el favor y les enseñaría a la tribu sus lecciones de guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had their torches, but she was standing in the darkness. They missed her."
msgstr "Tenían sus antorchas, pero ella se mantenía en la oscuridad. La extrañaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to be decisive."
msgstr "Tenían que ser decisivos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to make time, but Sarah also knew that the city and its many tall buildings offered countless chances of an ambush."
msgstr "Tenían que ganar tiempo, pero Sarah también sabía que la ciudad y sus muchos edificios altos ofrecían infinitas oportunidades de emboscada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to, Sarah realized, because the harbor was filled with more ships than she had ever seen in her life."
msgstr "Tenían que hacerlo, se dio cuenta Sarah, porque el puerto estaba lleno de más barcos de los que jamás había visto en su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had to, Sarah realized, if only to preserve the books."
msgstr "Tenían que hacerlo, se dio cuenta Sarah, solo para preservar los libros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had weighed on Sarah's mind all day."
msgstr "Les habían pesado a Sarah todo el día."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They had wine or beer, so I went for wine."
msgstr "Teníamos vino o cerveza, así que opté por el vino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had won."
msgstr "Han ganado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They had, quite a lot of it in fact. But most it had revolved around the union kingdoms and Rosanna itself."
msgstr "Tuvieron, de hecho, mucha cantidad. Pero la mayoría de eso giró en torno a los reinos unidos y a Rosanna misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hate her. In her they see the cause of their circumstance. They see in her the reason for why they and their families have been made so low."
msgstr "Les odian. En ella ven la causa de su situación. Ven en ella la razón por la que ellos y sus familias han sido hechos tan bajos."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They hate our Order. Always have. Why, I don't know."
msgstr "Les odian a nuestra Orden. Siempre lo han hecho. No sé por qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated him, she saw that in their eyes, but she also knew none of them would put a stop to his."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated their new masters still, but they hated their own men more."
msgstr "Los odiaban aún a sus nuevos amos, pero más a sus propios hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hated them for how they allowed all of this to happen."
msgstr "Los odiaban por haber permitido que todo esto sucediera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They have brought her to one of the communal slave tents, and befor her, the masses of her people are huddled up."
msgstr "Los han traído a una de las tiendas comunales de esclavos y, frente a ella, se aglomeran las masas de su pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They have failed, at the very least to seize me."
msgstr "Me han fallado, por lo menos en lo que respecta a tocar mi coño."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They have found no trace of Thomas..."
msgstr "No han encontrado rastro de Thomas..."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "They have grown up on victory and conquest and known nothing of defeat."
msgstr "Han crecido con la victoria y la conquista, desconociendo el fracaso."

msgctxt "speaker:Ragged Man"
msgid "They have lost sight of you."
msgstr "Te han perdido de vista."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "They have money. That is not the same as well."
msgstr "Tienen dinero. Eso no es lo mismo que estar bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They have no interest in sharing their spoils with those conquered, so the men are fixed with these belts to keep them in line."
msgstr "No tienen interés en compartir su botín con los conquistados, por lo que amarran estos cinturones a los hombres para mantenerlos bajo control."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They have to sneak about and be quiet, speak in hushed tones. And each time they do, they remind everyone of where they truly stand."
msgstr "Tienen que moverse sigilosamente y mantenerse en silencio, hablar con voz susurrada. Y cada vez que lo hacen, recuerdan a todos dónde están realmente situados."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They haven't done so yet?"
msgstr "¿Aún no lo han hecho?"

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They haven't received a shipment since these reports started. They tell me that this has never happened before."
msgstr "No han recibido un envío desde que comenzaron estos informes. Me dicen que esto nunca había ocurrido antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They heaped up around her feet and not before long, she was standing naked in the tent, same as Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Se amontonaron alrededor de sus pies y no pasó mucho tiempo antes de que ella estuviera desnuda en la tienda, igual que Lady Carolyn."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They hid away in a void beyond where anyone could reach them. A place from which they themselves did not even know to return."
msgstr "Se ocultaron en un vacío más allá de donde nadie podría alcanzarlos. Un lugar del que ni siquiera sabían volver."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They hide in the place beyond, observing the passing of this world."
msgstr "Se esconden en ese lugar más allá, observando el paso de este mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hold a trial, so much a mockery that it cannot even be called that in jest."
msgstr "Celebran un juicio, tan ridículo que ni siquiera puede llamarse eso en broma."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They hold back my head and pour more drink down my throat than I've ever gotten down before or after."
msgstr "Me sujetan la cabeza y vierten más bebida en mi garganta de lo que jamás he tragado antes o después."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They honored her command, but Sarah could see she had lost some of their respect."
msgstr "Ella honró su orden, pero Sarah podía ver que había perdido algo de su respeto."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They hope to threaten each of us, and in turn, hope that one of us will strike a bargain with them."
msgstr "Esperan amenazar a cada uno de nosotros y, a su vez, esperan que alguno de nosotros haga un trato con ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They hurled insults at them, taunted them with stories of how much greater the tribesmen were than them."
msgstr "Nos lanzaron insultos y nos provocaron con relatos sobre lo mucho que los tribales superaban a nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They identify, correctly, that the Union Kingdoms are fragmented and easily turned against one another."
msgstr "Identifican correctamente que el Reino Unido está fragmentado y puede ser fácilmente convertido contra sí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They initially joined the line, awaiting their turn, but upon being noticed, Hassar stood up and waived for them to advance ahead of the line."
msgstr "Inicialmente se unieron a la fila esperando su turno, pero al ser notados, Hassar se levantó y les hizo señas para que avanzaran antes que los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They insisted they eat more food, and out of obligation, all of them did."
msgstr "Insistieron en comer más, y por obligación, todos lo hicieron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They joked among themselves, rather to share one tribesmen than be left with a Rosannan man all to yourself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They kept living as if they would return home to their holdings in a few months."
msgstr "Vivían como si en unos meses volverían a sus posesiones en casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept locked to their own keeps, having little interest in the people outside of what they could extract from them."
msgstr "Mantuvieron sus fortalezas bajo llave, mostrando poco interés en las personas fuera de lo que podían extraer de ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They kept telling him to sue for peace. Strike a settlement with Mythra...but he just wouldn't listen..."
msgstr "Seguían diciéndole que pidiera la paz. Que llegara a un acuerdo con Mythra... pero él simplemente no quería escucharlo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept the hood over her head for long enough that Sarah began to doubt what time it was."
msgstr "La capucha se quedó puesta sobre su cabeza durante tanto tiempo que Sarah comenzó a dudar de qué hora era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept their watch, but for the rest of the night, no attack came."
msgstr "Mantuvieron la guardia, pero el resto de la noche pasó sin que llegara ningún ataque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kept walking along the hallway."
msgstr "Continuaron caminando por el pasillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They killed him."
msgstr "Lo mataron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kissed again."
msgstr "Se besaron otra vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They kissed in between the words."
msgstr "Se besaron entre las palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew better than anyone their own strengths."
msgstr "Sabían mejor que nadie sus propias fortalezas."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They knew it as surely as they knew all others things."
msgstr "Lo sabían con la misma certeza con que conocían todo el resto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew that for the most part, their poverty protected them from any real looting."
msgstr "Sabían que, en gran medida, su pobreza los protegía de cualquier saqueo real."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "They knew the path that would lead to a final victory."
msgstr "Sabían el camino que llevaría a la victoria final."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They knew they couldn't really attack her, and so they didn't."
msgstr "Sabían que no podían atacarla realmente, y por eso no lo hicieron."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They knew they had to wait here, to gather up all our strength before pressing into the palace."
msgstr "Sabían que debíamos esperar aquí, para reunir todas nuestras fuerzas antes de avanzar hacia el palacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They know the seasons as well as anyone by now. It's possible that they've adapted."
msgstr "Ya conocen las estaciones como cualquiera; es posible que se hayan adaptado."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They know what she is, and you know the laws."
msgstr "Ellos saben qué es ella, y tú conoces las leyes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They laid beneath the calming shade of the oak tree for so long that Sarah could hardly recall the passing of time."
msgstr "Se tendieron bajo la sombra calmante del roble durante tanto tiempo que Sarah apenas recordaba el paso del tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They laid the foundations for the world to shape itself in the only way that it ever could."
msgstr "Ellas pusieron los cimientos para que el mundo se moldeara a sí mismo de la única manera en que siempre pudo hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They lashed out and killed many of the rival Gods."
msgstr "Se lanzaron a matar a muchos de los dioses rivales."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They laugh, and they insult, and they make their jokes."
msgstr "Ríen y se insultan entre sí, haciendo chistes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They laughed, not just for her situation, but they laughed because they felt relieved about how they viewed the world."
msgstr "Rieron, no solo por su situación, sino porque se sentían aliviados al ver el mundo de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They learned to weave, with approval of the Gods, their Divine nature into all manners of creations."
msgstr "Aprendieron a tejer, con la aprobación de los Dioses, su naturaleza divina en todas las formas de creación."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They left me and my brothers and sisters behind in the capital to face a punishment for their crimes, but we are innocent."
msgstr "Me dejaron a mí y a mis hermanos y hermanas atrás en la capital para enfrentar un castigo por nuestros delitos, pero somos inocentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They left me there, satisfied that by now whatever had been growing in me was surely dead."
msgstr "Los dejaron allí, convencidos de que lo que crecía en mí ya debía estar muerto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They left."
msgstr "Se fueron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They let the heat from their passions fade as they lay in each others arms."
msgstr "Dejaron que el calor de sus pasiones se desvaneciera mientras yacían en los brazos el uno del otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They lifted her up, positioned her, then continued fucking."
msgstr "La levantaron, la colocaron y continuaron follando."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They like to pretend that it has never been conquered since it was first built, but that's not true."
msgstr "Les gusta fingir que nunca ha sido conquistada desde su construcción inicial, pero eso no es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They like to pretend that it has never been conquered since it was first constructed, but that's not true."
msgstr "Les gusta fingir que nunca ha sido conquistada desde su construcción inicial, pero eso no es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "They like to raid, capture strays and attack merchant caravans."
msgstr "Les gusta saquear, capturar a los vagabundos y atacar las caravanas de comerciantes."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They like to test new girls, so be on your guard."
msgstr "Les gusta probar con las nuevas muchachas, así que ten cuidado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They listened as it slowly warmed, until finally, the water boiled."
msgstr "Escucharon cómo se calentaba lentamente, hasta que finalmente el agua hirvió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They lived and breathed in a world of pointless cruelty and oppression, it was their oxygen."
msgstr "Vivían y respiraban en un mundo de crueldad e indiferencia sin sentido; era su oxígeno."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They look towards her with panic, the way slaves perceive all new things as a source of danger."
msgstr "Ellas miran hacia ella con pánico, como los esclavos perciben todo lo nuevo como una fuente de peligro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her with an odd mix of fear and gratitude."
msgstr "La miraron con una extraña mezcla de miedo y gratitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her with hungry eyes, desperate for what she would give them."
msgstr "La miraron con ojos hambrientos, desesperados por lo que ella les daría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked at her, those blessed few, as though she had gone mad, and they feared seeing their beloved commander lost to madness. For if she could break, how did they stand any chance?"
msgstr "Miraban a ella, esos pocos benditos, como si hubiera perdido la razón, y temían ver a su amada comandante arrastrada por la locura. Porque si ella podía romperse, ¿qué posibilidad tenían ellos de resistir?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They looked on with dispassionate interest. They cared little for the Union Kingdoms, but they cared for a spectacle."
msgstr "Los observaban con un interés desapasionado. No les importaba mucho el Reino Unido, pero sí se interesaban por el espectáculo."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They lookin for someone to get them off."
msgstr "Buscan a alguien con quien follar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They loomed over them, the way the sides of a canyon might."
msgstr "Se alzaban sobre ellos como los flancos de un cañón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They loved her."
msgstr "Los amaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made a clattering noise as they hit the ground."
msgstr "Hicieron un ruido de cascabel al impactar con el suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made a decent team in the kitchen and a decent team at this as well."
msgstr "Formaron un equipo excelente en la cocina y, en esto también, un equipo excelente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made an odd pair, but nobody paid them much mind."
msgstr "Formaban un par extraño, pero nadie les prestaba mucha atención."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made an odd pair, their bodies so disproportionate to one another, and still Sarah found it hard to hate him now."
msgstr "Formaban un extraño par, sus cuerpos tan desproporcionados entre sí, y aún así a Sarah le resultaba difícil odiarlo ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made an odd trio."
msgstr "Formaban un extraño trío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made eye contact, and with her eyes, Sarah told him to go faster."
msgstr "Se miraron a los ojos y, con la mirada, Sarah le indicó que acelerara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made eye contact."
msgstr "Se miraron a los ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made it, finally, they made it...to Lethram."
msgstr "Lo lograron, por fin, lo lograron... llegaron a Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made their beds and turned in for the night."
msgstr "Se hicieron la cama y se acostaron para pasar la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made their way to a small room in the back of the building."
msgstr "Se dirigieron a una pequeña habitación en el fondo del edificio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They made way for the nearby large oak where Sarah had strung up the laundry line."
msgstr "Se abrieron paso hacia el gran roble cercano donde Sarah había tendido la cuerda para colgar la ropa."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "They make a hundred times more in trade with us than they could ever hope to loot."
msgstr "Ganan cien veces más en el comercio de lo que jamás podrían robar."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They make a lotta noise but they ain't much trouble."
msgstr "Hacen mucho ruido pero no causan muchos problemas."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They make mention of tracks, left on the outer steps, that could only be made by tens of thousands of horses."
msgstr "Mencionan huellas en los peldaños exteriores, que solo podrían haber sido hechas por decenas de miles de caballos."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They make up the country as much as all nobles do."
msgstr "Ellas conforman el país tanto como lo hacen todos los nobles."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They manage the day to day affairs for our Order."
msgstr "Ellos se encargan de los asuntos diarios de nuestra Orden."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They marched her to the court house and chained her to one of the benches."
msgstr "La llevaron al tribunal y la ataron a uno de los bancos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They marched him to the bridge of the three sisters, along with his entire family."
msgstr "Los llevaron al puente de las tres hermanas, junto con toda su familia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They marched in silence for a while, but Sarah soon realized it would be too far."
msgstr "Marcharon en silencio durante un tiempo, pero Sarah pronto se dio cuenta de que sería demasiado lejos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They marched in stoic unison. Perfectly trained. Perfectly armed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They might consider a small coronation to be a sign of weakness."
msgstr "Podrían considerar que una pequeña coronación es un signo de debilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They might forget...but I'm afraid you won't."
msgstr "Pueden olvidarlo... pero tengo miedo de que tú no lo olvides."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They might have an understanding in this moment, but Sarah was sure he would betray her if she ever told him the truth."
msgstr "En este momento podrían tener un entendimiento, pero Sarah estaba segura de que lo traicionaría si alguna vez le contaba la verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They might have been orcs, but Sarah knew those eyes well enough, for men had them too."
msgstr "Podrían haber sido orcos, pero Sarah conocía esos ojos de sobra, pues los tenían también los hombres."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They might put a knife in your ribs, but they won't smile in your face as they do it."
msgstr "Podrían clavar un cuchillo en tus costillas, pero no te sonreirán a la cara mientras lo hacen."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They might smile to your face, but those are the snakes you should look out for the most."
msgstr "Pueden sonreírte en la cara, pero esos son los serpientes por los que debes tener más cuidado."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They missed one."
msgstr "¡Se equivocaron!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved like a horde, and not one of them seemed to care to preserve themselves."
msgstr "Se movían como una horda, y ninguno de ellos parecía preocuparse por preservarse a sí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved quick, cutting and dashing through the crowds."
msgstr "Se movían rápido, cortando y zambulléndose entre la multitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved rapidly, crossing the distance. In what seemed like no time at all, they had crossed from the horizon to halfway."
msgstr "Se movían rápidamente, cubriendo la distancia. Parecía que no había pasado ni un instante cuando ya habían cruzado desde el horizonte hasta la mitad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved slowly, but steadily."
msgstr "Se movían despacio, pero con firmeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved swiftly, approaching her from the center and each of her flanks."
msgstr "Avanzaban con rapidez, acercándose desde el centro y desde cada uno de sus flancos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved to another stall, and another stall."
msgstr "Se desplazaron hacia otra jaula y luego a otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They moved with great speed, but from such a distance, they appeared slow."
msgstr "Se movían con gran velocidad, pero desde tan lejos parecían lentos."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "They must understand that against the full might of our Empire, they could not hope to resist."
msgstr "Deben comprender que contra el poder entero de nuestro Imperio, no pueden esperar resistir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They navigated through the storm with ease, though how they did it, Sarah had no idea."
msgstr "Navegaron por la tormenta con facilidad, aunque Sarah no tenía idea de cómo lo habían logrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They needed some time to sprout, but by now she was hoping to see at least some result."
msgstr "Necesaban algo de tiempo para brotar, pero ahora ya esperaba ver al menos algún resultado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They needed to feel the water on every facet of their bodies, and so each of them, man or woman, abandoned all sense of shame and leapt into the water naked."
msgstr "Necesitaban sentir el agua sobre cada faceta de sus cuerpos, y así cada uno de ellos, hombre o mujer, abandonó toda sensación de vergüenza y saltó al agua desnudos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They officers work most directly with their own units. They see their own men every day."
msgstr "Los oficiales trabajan más directamente con sus propias unidades. Ven a sus propios hombres todos los días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They often, correctly, believed they wouldn't live very long and had best make up for their short lives by living them twice as hard."
msgstr "A menudo, con razón, creían que no vivirían mucho y lo mejor era compensar sus vidas cortas viviendo el doble de intensamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They only knew when it was too late."
msgstr "Solo lo sabían cuando ya era demasiado tarde."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They only made it a few steps before the girl's legs gave out."
msgstr "Solo lograron dar unos pasos antes de que le fallaran las piernas a la chica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They only wanted her body. And so long as she gave them that, they'd let her have her quiet resentments."
msgstr "Solo querían su cuerpo. Y mientras ella les diera eso, la dejarían tener sus resentimientos en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Mythran Officer"
msgid "They paid some merchants to ship them across the sea and now they're being a pain in my ass."
msgstr "Pagaron a algunos mercaderes para que los transportaran por el mar y ahora son una molestia en mi culo."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They pitched his commander's tent, he dissapeared inside, and he hasn't come out since."
msgstr "Montaron la tienda de su comandante, se adentró en ella y no ha salido desde entonces."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They poured out from the gate like a river of ink."
msgstr "Se derramaron desde la puerta como un río de tinta."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They prepared a ritual which they believed would allow the Empress to reach out to this new world and contact their Gods."
msgstr "Prepararon un ritual que creían permitiría a la Emperatriz conectar con este nuevo mundo y contactar a sus dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They pressed on, neither speaking, not until the torment becam too much and their exhaustion broke them."
msgstr "Avanzaron sin pronunciar palabra, hasta que el tormento se volvió insoportable y el agotamiento los quebró."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They propose a marriage."
msgstr "Proponen casarse conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They put her down off the the side, on a pair of logs that function as improvised benches."
msgstr "Los pusieron al costado, sobre un par de troncos que funcionaban como bancos improvisados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They quickly ate breakfast and gathered up their camp before moving deeper into the forest."
msgstr "Comieron rápidamente el desayuno y recogieron su campamento antes de adentrarse más en el bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They quickly rode through the snow-covered streets of Calshure and came upon the keep."
msgstr "Rodearon rápidamente las calles cubiertas de nieve de Calshure y llegaron al castillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They rained their arrows on the Knights, but the thick plated armor of the Knights and their horses protected them."
msgstr "Llovían sus flechas sobre los Caballeros, pero la gruesa armadura de placas de estos y sus caballos les protegía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They rarely spoke of these moments between husband and wife."
msgstr "Raramente hablaban de esos momentos entre marido y mujer."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They razed them, enslaved the people."
msgstr "Los arrasaron y esclavizaron al pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They reached for the water in a manic frenzy, as though fearing it might not be real, but their hands and thirsty mouths confirmed that it was."
msgstr "Llegaron al agua en un frenesí maniaco, como si temieran que no fuera real, pero sus manos y bocas sedientas confirmaron que lo era."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They really sprouted?"
msgstr "¿De verdad brotaron?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They remained a moment longer like this, until Marion finally pulled out from her and rolled over onto the bed next to her."
msgstr "Se quedaron un momento más así, hasta que Marion finalmente se separó de ella y se dio la vuelta para tumbarse en la cama al lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They remained in their embrace, longer than either remembered."
msgstr "Permanecieron en su abrazo, más tiempo del que ninguno recordaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They rested by the fire, drinking the wine they had brought, and before long, were back at it again."
msgstr "Se quedaron junto al fuego, bebiendo el vino que habían traído, y antes de lo esperado, volvieron a hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They rode the rest of their trip in silence."
msgstr "Continuaron el resto del viaje en silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They rushed out from the cell into the cold dark."
msgstr "Salieron corriendo de la celda hacia el frío y la oscuridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They sacrificed much in wealth as well."
msgstr "También sacrificaron mucho en riqueza."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They said that?"
msgstr "¿Dijeron eso?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They said you know these forests better than most, is that true?"
msgstr "¿Dijeron que conoces estos bosques mejor que la mayoría, ¿es cierto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat back down at Alaric's camp."
msgstr "Se sentaron de nuevo en el campamento de Alaric."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat her down on the front bench, still tied up."
msgstr "La sentó en el banco delantero, aún atada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat in silence for a moment."
msgstr "Se sentaron en silencio por un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat near the edge of the campfire, keeping watch over the the ruined city."
msgstr "Se sentaron cerca del borde del fuego, vigilando la ciudad en ruinas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat still by the side of the road, waiting for a death that seemed less horrid than the enduring suffering of the frost."
msgstr "Se sentaron quietos al borde del camino, esperando una muerte que parecía menos horrible que el sufrimiento duradero del frío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat together for a while longer."
msgstr "Se sentaron juntos un poco más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sat together for what felt like nearly an hour, until finally, a great door opened up."
msgstr "Se sentaron juntos durante lo que pareció casi una hora, hasta que finalmente se abrió una gran puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They saw her, but they didn't really look at her."
msgstr "La vieron, pero no la miraron de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They saw the creature, sure, but who did really?"
msgstr "La vieron, claro, pero ¿quién realmente la miró?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "They say all Tribesmen are good at making boys."
msgstr "Dicen que todos los hombres de las tribus son expertos en hacer chavos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They say it used to be one the busiest towns in the central kingdoms, until one day it simply vanished from the face of the earth."
msgstr "Dicen que solía ser una de las ciudades más concurridas de los reinos centrales, hasta que un día simplemente desapareció del mapa."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They say it's the spirits."
msgstr "Dicen que son los espíritus."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They say that a pussy, fucked enough times by the same dick, will shape itself to match the shape of that dick."
msgstr "Dicen que un coño, después de ser follado tantas veces por la misma polla, se moldea para adoptar la forma de esa polla."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They say that if the spirits like you, they'll give you easy dreams and heal your body."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "They say these girls are tired of working, and so they just leave without telling anyone."
msgstr "Dicen que estas chicas están cansadas de trabajar y, por eso, simplemente se van sin decir nada a nadie."

msgctxt "speaker:Young woman"
msgid "They says jobs plenty, good pay too."
msgstr "Dicen que hay muchos puestos de trabajo y el pago es bueno."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They see Mythra as the ultimate prize. The fattest hog for the slaughter."
msgstr "Ellas ven a Mythra como el premio supremo. La cerda más gorda para el matadero."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They seem a lot easier to take off."
msgstr "Parecen mucho más fáciles de quitar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seemed as singular and lonely as she herself felt."
msgstr "Parecían tan singulares y solitarios como ella misma se sentía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seemed eager to help, and Sarah knew the power that mages could offer."
msgstr "Parecían dispuestos a ayudar, y Sarah conocía el poder que los magos podían ofrecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seemed ordinary enough, the kind of wear and tear any palace might go through, except for the fact that all the scratches ran along line."
msgstr "Parecían lo bastante ordinarios, el tipo de desgaste que cualquier palacio podría sufrir, salvo por el hecho de que todas las rayas corrían a lo largo de una línea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seemed to somehow burn brighter here than anywhere else."
msgstr "Parecían arder con una intensidad que en ningún otro lugar se podía encontrar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seemed very casual and joyful to Sarah. How she had been, she wondered, when all she knew was castle life."
msgstr "Para Sarah parecían muy relajados y alegres. Se preguntaba cómo habría sido ella, cuando todo lo que conocía era la vida en el castillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seize her and pull her towards the center of the tent."
msgstr "Los agarran y la arrastran hacia el centro de la tienda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They seized her hands, guiding them to their shafts."
msgstr "Los agarraron de las manos y las guiaron hacia sus vergas."

msgctxt "speaker:Tirion"
msgid "They send back a letter, be as you are, do as you do. Continue servicing your town."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They sent children to a school for war?"
msgstr "¿Enviarían a los niños a una escuela de guerra?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They show her the cell where she will live, together with eight other women."
msgstr "Le muestran la celda donde vivirá, junto con otras ocho mujeres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They shrieked, high-pitched, like vermin when the fire consumed them."
msgstr "Gritaron con un chillido agudo, como las plagas cuando el fuego las consumía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They signaled to the people that things were returning to normal."
msgstr "Señalaron a la gente que las cosas volvían a la normalidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They simply devoured and tore apart life."
msgstr "Solo devoraban y despedazaban la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They simply had no choice. Alone, nobody could hope to survive the desert."
msgstr "Simplemente no tenían otra opción. Solos, nadie podía esperar sobrevivir al desierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They simply sat in their halls, extracting wealth and women, and putting down any resistance with brute force."
msgstr "Simplemente se sentaban en sus salones, extrayendo riqueza y mujeres, y aplastando cualquier resistencia con fuerza bruta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They sit down together on the same bed."
msgstr "Se sientan juntos en la misma cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They somehow seemed brighter here than in Lethram."
msgstr "De alguna manera, parecían más brillantes aquí que en Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They soon left Carolyn's estate behind, riding through the streets of Rahayal."
msgstr "Pronto dejaron atrás la finca de Carolyn, montando a caballo por las calles de Rahayal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They spilled their seeds to the infertile earth."
msgstr "Esparcieron su semilla en la tierra estéril."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They spoke in hushed words to one another."
msgstr "Hablaban en voz baja el uno con el otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They spoke in orcish, sparing her no concern."
msgstr "Hablaban en orco, sin darle la menor importancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They spoke to each other of how their lives had been since the fall. All they had endured and overcome since."
msgstr "Hablaban entre sí de cómo habían sido sus vidas desde la caída. De todo lo que habían soportado y superado."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "They spoke to us, freely, teaching us, instructing us, raising up our species from the mud."
msgstr "Nos hablaron libremente, nos enseñaron, nos instruyeron y nos elevaron a nuestra especie desde el lodo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They spoke, but Sarah could never shake the feeling that something seperated the two of them."
msgstr "Ellos hablaron, pero Sarah nunca pudo disipar la sensación de que algo separaba a los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "They spy on their neighbours. Rat out loyalists. Condemn them and their families to suffer at the hand of the Tribes."
msgstr "Espían a sus vecinos. Denuncian a los leales. Los condenan y a sus familias a sufrir por mano de las Tribus."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stabbed, pulled, broke and gouged eyes."
msgstr "Los clavaban, arrancaban, partían y destrozaban los ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They started to eat it, and they simply never stopped."
msgstr "Empezaron a comerlo y simplemente nunca pararon."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They started to walk again."
msgstr "Comenzaron a caminar de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stay, locked in an embrace. It doesn't take long for Thomas to fall asleep."
msgstr "Se quedan, atrapados en un abrazo. No tarda mucho en que Thomas caiga dormido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stepped out of the carriage."
msgstr "Salió del carruaje."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stepped through and the door was closed behind them, sealing the exit."
msgstr "Salieron y la puerta se cerró tras ellos, sellando la salida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They still had their lives, but such things were cheap when one had no money, family or home."
msgstr "Aún tenían sus vidas, pero tales cosas eran baratas cuando no se tenía dinero, familia ni hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stood, all together, on a massive field of grass, more like an ocean."
msgstr "Se pararon juntos en un vasto campo de hierba, más parecido a un océano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stopped by a bend in the road, looking out over a field of flowers, their colours deep blue."
msgstr "Se detuvieron junto a una curva del camino, mirando hacia un campo de flores de un azul profundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They struggled, but there was no dominance or submission, instead only a mutual exploration."
msgstr "Lucharon, pero no hubo dominación ni sumisión, solo una exploración mutua."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stumble into the hallways of Bagrad palace, for the first time since it began, feeling even a faint sense of safety."
msgstr "Se tambalean hacia los pasillos del palacio de Bagrad; por primera vez desde que comenzó todo, sienten incluso un vago sentido de seguridad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They stumbled drunkenly to the ground, falling amidst their sprawled out dresses."
msgstr "Se tambalearon hasta el suelo como borrachas, cayendo entre sus vestidos extendidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They sure seem to like you."
msgstr "Seguro que te caen bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They swapped stories of their life."
msgstr "Intercambiaron historias de sus vidas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They switched back and forth, telling stories of the wonderous parts of the world that Sarah knew only from books."
msgstr "Se alternaban, contándose historias de las maravillas del mundo que Sarah solo conocía por los libros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They switched roles, each taking the attacking role and the defending role, before swapping."
msgstr "Cambiaron de roles, cada uno asumiendo el papel atacante y el defensor antes de intercambiarlos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They swung open with a deep and heavy thud."
msgstr "Se abrieron con un profundo y pesado golpe."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They swung their blades, but could not close the distance between themselves and the spears."
msgstr "Esgrimieron sus espadas, pero no pudieron cerrar la distancia entre sí y las lanzas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They swung their curved blades with skill, finding the gaps in between the formation to strike at individual soldiers."
msgstr "Balancian sus espadas curvas con pericia, encontrando las brechas entre la formación para atacar a los soldados individuales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They take them from the tent, bind them, and take them through the city."
msgstr "Los sacan de la carpa, los atan y los conducen por la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They talk all sorts of nonesense about you, killing demons and what not."
msgstr "Hablan todo tipo de tonterías sobre ti, matando demonios y demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They talked for a while, though Sarah struggled to recall what about exactly."
msgstr "Hablaron un rato, aunque Sarah luchó por recordar exactamente sobre qué."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They tattoo their names, or their family sigils on their slaves."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They taught their followers to use magic that could harm a God."
msgstr "Les enseñaron a sus seguidores a utilizar magia capaz de dañar a un Dios."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They tax em as much as they want or as often as they want."
msgstr "Les cobran lo que quieran y con la frecuencia que deseen."

msgctxt "speaker:Ragged Man"
msgid "They tell me you have a friend that might have need of it..."
msgstr "Me dicen que tienes una amiga que podría necesitarlo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "They tell me, feed slave, I feed slave."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They tell you how to dress. Where to sleep. When to piss."
msgstr "Te dicen cómo vestirse. Dónde dormir. Cuándo orinar."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They think because we have so much, we can never lose it. They don't see how everyone else is catching up to us already."
msgstr "Piensan que, dado que tenemos tanto, nunca podemos perderlo. No ven cómo todos los demás ya nos están alcanzando."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They think he's a bit of an upstart."
msgstr "Piensan que es un novato."

msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "They think it might be an emissary."
msgstr "Pensan que podría ser un emisario."

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "They think it's the rest of the world that should learn their language."
msgstr "Pensan que es el resto del mundo quien debería aprender su idioma."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "They think themselves clever and believe that we do not know that they gather."
msgstr "Ellos se creen listos y creen que no sabemos que nos reúnen."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "They thought I could teach you a thing or two."
msgstr "Pensaron que podían enseñarte un par de cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They threw her a few glances, enough to worry her, but other than that, most seemed to ignore her."
msgstr "Lanzaron algunas miradas suaves hacia ella, suficiente para inquietarla, pero más allá de eso, la mayoría parecía ignorarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They threw their lives away, three of them trying hold off five-hundred of us. They didn't even hold us off for more than a second."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They threw up their hands and prayed to the Gods."
msgstr "Levantaron las manos y oraron a los dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They told me they had send you an invitation but I wasn't sure you'd actually show!"
msgstr "¡Me dijeron que me habían enviado una invitación, pero no estaba segura de que realmente aparecieras!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They took a quick turn, heading towards the main street of Lethram."
msgstr "Dieron una rápida vuelta hacia la calle principal de Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They took off down the road, the opposite direction of where Sigmund had gone."
msgstr "Se alejaron por el camino, en dirección opuesta a la que había tomado Sigmund."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They took so many detours, that only late at night did they finally make it back to their camp."
msgstr "Tomaron tantos desvíos que no volvieron al campamento hasta muy tarde en la noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They took us to Al'Gahaem, and there they put us to work."
msgstr "Nos llevaron a Al'Gahaem y allí nos hicieron trabajar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They tortured the people they dominated, not for any strategy, or even for any depraved joy, but only to pass the time."
msgstr "Los torturaban a los que dominaban, no por ninguna estrategia, ni siquiera por algún deleite depravado, sino solo para pasar el tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "They tried to extend their lives by feeding on the life of the world."
msgstr "Intentaron prolongar sus vidas alimentándose de la vida del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They trust me with their lives, and I will work all my life to be worthy of their trust."
msgstr "Ellas confían en mí con sus vidas, y trabajaré toda mi vida para ser digna de su confianza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They turned and left together, same as they came."
msgstr "Se giraron y se fueron juntos, igual que habían llegado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They turned back around, walking back the way they came."
msgstr "Giraron hacia atrás y caminaron de vuelta por el camino que habían seguido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They twisted round and about until they appeared back at the servant quarters, deep below the ground."
msgstr "Se retorcieron y giraron hasta que aparecieron en las cuartas de los sirvientes, muy por debajo del suelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They understand that morale is breaking down as a result of forced marches and increasingly strict rations."
msgstr "Comprenden que la moral se está derrumbando como consecuencia de las marchas forzadas y las raciones cada vez más estrictas."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They unite under a single banner, because they understand that division is weakness in war."
msgstr "Se unen bajo una sola bandera, porque entienden que la división es debilidad en la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They used everything."
msgstr "Lo usaron todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "They used this campaign on Bagrad as a cover for their mission, but the real goal was to reach the city of Nauyziri."
msgstr "Usaron esta campaña en Bagrad como cobertura para su misión, pero el objetivo real era llegar a la ciudad de Nauyziri."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They usually keep their stuff indoors, safe, but I know that whenever the weekend comes up, they need more drink than they can store in their storage room."
msgstr "Suelen guardar sus cosas adentro, a salvo, pero sé que cada vez que llega el fin de semana, necesitan más bebida de la que pueden almacenar en su bodega."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "They value my raw strength, but care nothing for Dio. They have always resented having to pay for both of us."
msgstr "Valoran mi fuerza bruta, pero no importan en lo más mínimo a Dio. Siempre han resentido tener que pagar por los dos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wade through the tent and one by one, they pull up the men of the gang."
msgstr "Avanzan por la tienda y uno tras otro sacan a los hombres de la banda."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They waited for a moment, and Alaric knocked again."
msgstr "Esperaron un momento y Alaric tocó de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked a small distance away from the others towards a pile of lumber."
msgstr "Caminaron un poco más lejos de los demás, hacia un montón de madera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked further along the road."
msgstr "Continuaron caminando por el camino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked in silence for a moment."
msgstr "Caminaron en silencio por un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked nearly as naked as the women, save for a small glittering of metal between their legs."
msgstr "Caminaron casi desnudas como las mujeres, salvo por un pequeño brillo de metal entre sus piernas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked out the door, turning around the corner of the cafe."
msgstr "Salieron por la puerta, girando en la esquina del café."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked past an empty road. Fields of grass, a few brushes and trees."
msgstr "Caminaron por una calle vacía. Campos de hierba, unos pocos arbustos y árboles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They walked."
msgstr "Caminaron."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They want to maintain good relations with their soldiers, so they break the rules and give out more than they should."
msgstr "Quieren mantener buenas relaciones con sus soldados, por lo que rompen las reglas y otorgan más de lo debido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wanted to lure her out, cause her to make a mistake. She would not give them the excuse they wanted."
msgstr "Querían atraerla fuera, hacer que cometiera un error. Ella no les daría la excusa que deseaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They watched as the soldiers rode off along different roads, gathering up everyone that lived in the town."
msgstr "Observaron cómo los soldados se alejaban por diferentes caminos, reuniendo a todos los que habitaban el pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They ways of their war, swift and quick cuts, bounced harmlessly from the Knights heavy steel."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weighed heavy to the touch, a promise of what he was going to release."
msgstr "Sentíanse pesadas al tacto, una promesa de lo que iba a liberar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They went about a corner, up a series of stairs, and then the Headmaster pushed open a door."
msgstr "Pasaron por un pasillo, subieron una serie de escaleras y luego el director abrió la puerta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They went over her success with some of the seedlings. Where she had gone right. Where she had gone wrong."
msgstr "Miraron su éxito con algunas de las plántulas. Donde había acertado. Donde había fallado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a family in the North, but only one of many and far from the most important."
msgstr "Eran una familia del Norte, pero solo una de muchas y muy lejos de ser la más importante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a man and a woman. The rest, illusion, meant to distract from the simple truths of nature."
msgstr "Eran un hombre y una mujer. El resto, ilusión, destinada a distraer de las simples verdades de la naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were a practical people, and so they reduced the bodies of their people in equal practicality."
msgstr "Eran un pueblo práctico, y así reducían los cuerpos de sus gentes con igual pragmatismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all back."
msgstr "Todos estaban de vuelta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all going to die."
msgstr "Todos iban a morir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were all here for her, Sarah realized."
msgstr "Todos estaban aquí por ella, se dio cuenta Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were already running dangerously low on medical supplies, just to deal with those currently wounded."
msgstr "Ya estaban agotando peligrosamente sus suministros médicos, solo para atender a los heridos que había."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were as much on the menu as anything they brought out on a platter."
msgstr "Eran tan apetitosos como cualquier cosa que sirvieran en un plato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were asked to explain what had happened, and so they told them."
msgstr "Les pidieron que explicaran qué había ocurrido, y así se lo contaron."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were beyond words."
msgstr "Estaban más allá de las palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They were born human, but they have undergone a transformation."
msgstr "Nacieron humanos, pero han sufrido una transformación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were certainly not a great house."
msgstr "Ciertamente no eran una gran casa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were children, and she did not have the heart to even hurt one hair on their heads, let alone keep them as hostages."
msgstr "Eran niños, y no tenía el corazón de ni siquiera lastimar un solo cabello sobre sus cabezas, mucho menos mantenerlos como rehenes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were close to the wall now. Sarah said a silent prayer that there had been no archers."
msgstr "Ya estaban cerca de la pared. Sarah murmuró una oración silenciosa pidiendo que no hubiera arqueros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were clothes, technically."
msgstr "Eran ropas, técnicamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were coming. Her hopes of getting through the day without any violence were over."
msgstr "Venían. Sus esperanzas de pasar el día sin violencia habían terminado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were conquerors. They had no desire to become a part of the lands they ruled over."
msgstr "Eran conquistadores. No tenían deseo de formar parte de las tierras que gobernaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were could be alone more, people raised fewer questions and rumors, and they found more opportunities to be together."
msgstr "Podrían estar solos más, la gente haría menos preguntas y correrían menos rumores, y encontrarían más oportunidades para estar juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were cruel men...but men still."
msgstr "Hombres crueles... pero hombres al fin y al cabo."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They were done the moment they picked up their weapons."
msgstr "Ya estaban condenados el instante en que alzaron sus armas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were dragged out by start of day for work and brought back most evenings."
msgstr "Los arrastraban desde el amanecer para trabajar y los traían de vuelta la mayor parte de las tardes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were eager for the fight, and more than that, they were even eager for a good death."
msgstr "Estaban ansiosos por la pelea, y más que eso, incluso ansiaban una buena muerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were everywhere."
msgstr "Estaban por todas partes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were friends, but before that, she was a ruler and Kate a servant."
msgstr "Eran amigos, pero antes de eso, ella era una gobernante y Kate una sirviente."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They were going to...they said they would..."
msgstr "Iban a... dijeron que irían..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They were gonna be visitin me at my home today."
msgstr "Iban a visitarme en mi casa hoy."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were greeted with a mixture of surprise and bemusement."
msgstr "Fueron recibidos con una mezcla de sorpresa y asombro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were handsome enough. Crude, but that was to be expected of soldiers."
msgstr "Eran lo suficientemente guapos. Rudos, pero eso era de esperarse en soldados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were hardly more than a few steps in when the Tribesmen began their attack."
msgstr "No habían dado apenas unos pasos cuando los tribales iniciaron su ataque."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were having sex."
msgstr "Se estaban follando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were her people still."
msgstr "Eran su gente aún."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were looking at them, in awe and worry."
msgstr "Los miraban con asombro y preocupación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were lucky. The crowd could have swamped them, but nobody did. Everyone decided not to get involved, letting them storm out the marketplace."
msgstr "Tenían suerte. La multitud podría haberlos aplastado, pero nadie lo hizo. Todos decidieron no involucrarse, permitiéndoles salir corriendo del mercado."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They were made from a mixture of magic and metal, though the exact technique has long been lost."
msgstr "Estaban hechos de una mezcla de magia y metal, aunque la técnica exacta se ha perdido hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were made to work until their hands broke, and then others would take their place."
msgstr "Estaban hechos para trabajar hasta romperles las manos, y luego otros tomarían su lugar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were more clever than she gave them credit for. They might have laid out traps, hoping that she would rush blindly after them."
msgstr "Eran más astutas de lo que ella les daba crédito. Podrían haber tendido trampas, esperando que se lanzara ciegamente tras ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were more organized than she had first assumed."
msgstr "Eran más organizados de lo que ella había asumido inicialmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were mostly City Guards, forced to fight. Their aim was poor, either by lack of practice or because they didn't want to fight."
msgstr "Eran en su mayoría Guardias de la Ciudad, obligados a luchar. Su puntería era mala, ya sea por falta de práctica o porque no querían pelear."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were moving towards Rahayal, and all that the city promised."
msgstr "Se dirigían hacia Rahayal y todo lo que la ciudad prometía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were nearing the half point, or so Belmont had told her, of what was supposed to be a two week long trip."
msgstr "Estaban cerca de la mitad del camino, o eso le había dicho Belmont, de lo que debía ser un viaje de dos semanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were no strangers so guards chasing people, but none of them had ever seen them give chase to a proper rich girl before."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not at full strength."
msgstr "No estaban en su máxima fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not born into war."
msgstr "No nacieron para la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not build to welcome trade from the outside. They were build to resist the only thing Lethram expected from the hinterlands, an attack."
msgstr "No fueron construidos para recibir comercio del exterior. Fueron forjados para resistir la única cosa que Lethram esperaba de las tierras interiores: un ataque."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They were not false memories at all. They were simply the memories of others from my race. Bleeding into me."
msgstr "No eran recuerdos falsos en absoluto. Eran simplemente los recuerdos de otros de mi raza, que se mezclaban conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not filled with rage, or hatred or any beliefs that could be opposed."
msgstr "No estaban llenos de rabia, ni de odio, ni de ninguna creencia que pudiera ser contrapuesta."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not going to wait out their fate inside of the city walls. They had come to meet them on the battlefield."
msgstr "No iban a esperar su destino dentro de los muros de la ciudad. Habían venido para encontrarse con ellos en el campo de batalla."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They were not loyal because they stood to make money from it. They were loyal because their oathsworn duty commanded it."
msgstr "No eran leales porque esperaban lucrarse de ello. Eran leales porque su juramento les lo exigía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not men of politics or rule. They were warrior with nothing left to conquer."
msgstr "No eran hombres de la política ni del mando. Eran guerreros sin nada más por conquistar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not real."
msgstr "No eran reales."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They were not so fortunate."
msgstr "No lo fueron tanto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were not sure they would wake up again."
msgstr "No estaban seguros de volver a despertar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were on the edge of the world, with an army that seemed on the edge of rebellion."
msgstr "Estaban al borde del mundo, con un ejército que parecía estar al borde de la rebelión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were only a day away from the town."
msgstr "Solo estaban a un día de la aldea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were only beginning to form their relationship, and Sarah was careful not to end up as the weaker party."
msgstr "Solo acababan de comenzar a formar su relación, y Sarah tuvo cuidado de no terminar siendo la parte más débil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were out on the edge of the world, with little more than a campfire for heat, and yet, Sarah couldn't help but feel grateful."
msgstr "Estaban al borde del mundo, con poco más que una hoguera para calentar el cuerpo, y sin embargo, Sarah no pudo evitar sentirse agradecida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were ready for everything."
msgstr "Estaban listos para todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were safe, and still they were eager for the certainty of solid ground under their feet."
msgstr "Estaban a salvo, y aun así ansiaban la certeza de tener el suelo firme bajo sus pies."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were safe."
msgstr "Estaban a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were sitting off to the side of the ship, looking out over the dock."
msgstr "Estaban sentados en el lateral del barco, mirando hacia el muelle."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They were slow, just once, and it cost them their lives."
msgstr "Fueron lentos, solo una vez, y eso les costó la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were small infractions, and in truth, given their condition after the march in the desert, Sarah would have let it slide."
msgstr "Eran faltas menores, y en verdad, considerando su estado tras la marcha por el desierto, Sarah habría dejado pasar eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were soldiers, that much was obvious, but they also seemed...young. No older than Sarah, she estimated."
msgstr "Eran soldados, eso era obvio, pero también parecían...jóvenes. No mayores que Sarah, ella estimó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were soldiers. Inflicting wounds was easy to them. Fixing wounds was a more delicate skill."
msgstr "Eran soldados. Les resultaba fácil infligir heridas, pero curarlas era una habilidad mucho más delicada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were stalling for time."
msgstr "Estaban ganando tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were standing in front of a door. It didn't have any markings that made it stand out from any of the others."
msgstr "Estaban de pie frente a una puerta. No tenía ningún símbolo que la hiciera destacar entre las demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were standing in pairs."
msgstr "Estaban en parejas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were strong, but not beyond killing."
msgstr "Eran fuertes, pero no más allá de matar."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They were sure in the way the Gods are always sure."
msgstr "Estaban seguros como los dioses siempre lo están."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were taunting him, kicking him."
msgstr "Los estaban provocando, pateándolo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were the kind you would expect on the ground where a door had swung open again and again, slowly leaving scratches in the floor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They were the only ones who understood, really understood, that strength was the only power that mattered in this new age."
msgstr "Ellos eran los únicos que comprendían, realmente comprendían, que la fuerza era el único poder que importaba en esta nueva era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were the true heart of her nation. The people that she was tasking with ruling."
msgstr "Eran el verdadero corazón de su nación. El pueblo con el que ella se encargaba de gobernar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trapped."
msgstr "Estaban atrapados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trying to bleed her army out."
msgstr "Intentaban sangrar a su ejército."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were trying to overthrow her family."
msgstr "Intentaban derrocar a su familia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They were, for the most part, farmers and craftsmen, called away from their work by their lords."
msgstr "En su mayoría, eran campesinos y artesanos, llamados a abandonar sus labores por sus señores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't alone on the ship anymore, and yet she had screamed as loudly as she always did, as she had always felt."
msgstr "Ya no estaban solos en el barco, y sin embargo ella gritó tan fuerte como siempre lo hacía, sintiéndose exactamente como siempre se había sentido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't orcs...humans...but those could be equally dangerous."
msgstr "No eran orcos... humanos... pero podían ser igualmente peligrosos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They weren't planning on defeating her army at all, they simply hoped to kill her."
msgstr "No planeaban derrotar a su ejército en absoluto; simplemente esperaban matarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "They will bring him to one of their forts, surrounded by soldiers loyal to their noble houses."
msgstr "Los llevarán a uno de sus fuertes, rodeados por soldados leales a sus nobles casas."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will descend on the world like locusts and leave empires barren as fields."
msgstr "Descenderán sobre el mundo como langostas y dejarán imperios estériles como campos."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will die good deaths."
msgstr "Morirán con una muerte digna."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They will distribute what has been conquered among those according to their rank."
msgstr "Distribuirán lo que han conquistado entre aquellos según su rango."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They will forever remember that you sacrificed their safety, to guarantee your own."
msgstr "Recordarán para siempre que sacrificaste su seguridad para garantizar la tuya propia."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "They will humiliate you. Rosanna. Your people."
msgstr "Te humillarán. Rosanna. Tu pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They will land on our shores and pick us off one by one. Each of us will retreat behind our walls, and we will let the others to themselves."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will miss it, trust me on that."
msgstr "Se lo perderán, créeme."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They will not be as ready as they perhaps could have been, but they'll be as ready as we can make them, before our window closes."
msgstr "No estarán tan preparados como quizás hubieran estado, pero estarán tan listos como podamos hacerlos antes de que se cierre nuestra ventana."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will save you in a moment."
msgstr "Los salvarán en un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "They will seek it out, even if they lose."
msgstr "Lo buscarán, incluso si pierden."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "They will tell stories..."
msgstr "Contarán historias..."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will tell tales that will move the Empire. Not instantly, but slowly."
msgstr "Contarán historias que moverán al Imperio. No de inmediato, sino con lentitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will what?"
msgstr "¿Qué harán?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They will write history books of the evil that you did. Your family will become synonymous with treason and murder."
msgstr "Escribirán libros de historia sobre el mal que has hecho. Tu familia será sinónimo de traición y asesinato."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "They will! Someone saw her through the window. They saw you walk the streets with her. People aren't fools, Jaeid."
msgstr "¡Sí! Alguien la vio a través de la ventana. La vieron caminar por las calles con ella. La gente no es tonta, Jaeid."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They will, but the Mythran empire is always occupied in one place or another."
msgstr "Lo harán, pero el imperio Mythran siempre está ocupado en un lugar u otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They won't do the same as part of a faceless army that holds no true allegiance to anyone other than an abstract Union."
msgstr "No lo harán igual, como parte de un ejército sin rostro que no tiene lealtad verdadera a nadie más que a una Unión abstracta."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They won't have to divide us. We're already divided."
msgstr "No tendrán que dividirnos. Ya estamos divididos."

msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "They won't try anything."
msgstr "No intentarán nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worked the ship deep into the night when they were called back to the captain's cabin as they always were at the end of a shift."
msgstr "Trabajaron en el barco hasta muy entrada la noche cuando los llamaron de vuelta a la cabina del capitán, como siempre al final de un turno."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worried Xan, because of their longevity, which seemed to function without any use of magic."
msgstr "Se preocupaban por Xan, debido a su longevidad, que parecía funcionar sin ningún uso de magia."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They worshipped a pantheon of gods, and the rulers of this civilization could speak to them directly, as easily as you or I can speak to each other."
msgstr "Adoraban un panteón de dioses, y los gobernantes de esta civilización podían hablar con ellos directamente, tan fácilmente como tú o yo podemos hablar entre nosotros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They worshipped him with their bodies. Cried out in pleasure as though it was as hymn. Screamed out his name as though the spirit was their god."
msgstr "Lo adoraban con sus cuerpos. Gritaban de placer como si fuera un himno. Clamaban su nombre como si su espíritu fuera su dios."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be devoured."
msgstr "Serían devoradas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be here soon."
msgstr "Pronto estarían aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would be veterans soon enough, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Pronto serían veteranos, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would break any cavalry charge."
msgstr "Serían capaces de romper cualquier carga de caballería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would charge into battle with song and drink themselves into a stupor to celebrate after."
msgstr "Cantarían con alegría y se embriagarían para celebrar después."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would clear the distance between their armies in no time at all."
msgstr "Borrarían la distancia entre sus ejércitos en un abrir y cerrar de ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would die."
msgstr "Morirían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would either be dragged along the current or drown. And the empire did not particularly care either way."
msgstr "Serían arrastrados por la corriente o se ahogarían. Y el imperio no importaba demasiado de una u otra manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would fire off their arrows from a safe distance, and on their horses, chasing them on foot would be pointless."
msgstr "Dispararían sus flechas desde una distancia segura, y perseguirlos a caballo sería inútil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would get to Rahayal in a few days, and then she would make her next move."
msgstr "Llegarían a Rahayal en unos días, y entonces ella haría su siguiente movimiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have been well on their way to Lethram by now. Sitting on a pile of gold, getting fat on good food instead of rationing."
msgstr "Habrían estado ya bien avanzados hacia Lethram. Sentados sobre una pila de oro, engordando con buena comida en lugar de racionar."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They would have even used their legions, had they not been tied down in other engagements."
msgstr "Habrían incluso utilizado a sus legiones, si no estuvieran atados por otros compromisos."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They would have killed me as gladly as I would have killed them."
msgstr "Me habrían matado tan gustosamente como yo habría matado a ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to conceive. The sooner the better."
msgstr "Tendrían que concebir. Lo antes posible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to set out soon."
msgstr "Tendrían que salir pronto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would have to travel inwards, up through the Hyral mountains. A tough journey, even when prepared. And they were not prepared."
msgstr "Tendrían que viajar hacia el interior, subiendo por las montañas de Hyral. Un viaje difícil, incluso cuando están preparados. Y ellos no lo estaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would keep running, throw away their armor, their weapons, run back to their homes and pretend to be citizens."
msgstr "Tendrían que seguir huyendo, tirar sus armaduras y sus armas, volver a sus hogares y fingir ser ciudadanos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know she was coming. Whatever this would prove to be, it had been set in motion."
msgstr "Sabrían que ella se acercaba. Sea lo que sea que esto demostrara, ya estaba en marcha."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They would know that I came from Rosanna. They would know of you. And they would sooner put the two together."
msgstr "Sabrían que vengo de Rosanna. Sabrían de ti. Y unirían ambas cosas antes que nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know the most recent information."
msgstr "Ellos sabrían la información más reciente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would know."
msgstr "Ellos lo sabrían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would land on their shores. Very soon."
msgstr "Llegarían a sus costas. Muy pronto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would live."
msgstr "Vivirían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would need a strong leader, she knew that much, but out of all them she had the least experience."
msgstr "Necesitarían un líder fuerte, lo sabía, pero de todos ellos tenía la menor experiencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would never fight for her."
msgstr "Ellos nunca lucharían por ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would rest later, she figured."
msgstr "Descansarían más tarde, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would see her."
msgstr "La verían."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "They would send in a legion, kill enough of them to send a message, then retreat."
msgstr "Enviarían una legión, matarían a suficientes de ellos para enviar un mensaje y luego se retirarían."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They would train for hours, but I'd train for days."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They would warn the others that there was a girl in the ruins, not to be messed with."
msgstr "Advertirían a los demás que había una chica en las ruinas, con la que no se debía meter."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wouldn't have sounded the horns if there hadn't been danger."
msgstr "No habrían sonado las cornetas si no hubiera peligro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They wouldn't help her here."
msgstr "No la ayudarían aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They yelled instructions at her, sometimes in orcish, sometimes in a broken human language."
msgstr "Les gritaban instrucciones, a veces en orc, otras en un humano roto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They yelled, screamed, ran."
msgstr "Gritaban, chillaban, corrían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd be back, sooner or later, this much Sarah knew, but for the moment, he was spend, as was she."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They'd bring me books and trinkets from every corner of the world."
msgstr "Me traían libros y baratijas de cada rincón del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They'd find my body dressed in military rags and ugly shoes?"
msgstr "¿Encontrarían mi cuerpo vestido con trapos militares y zapatos feos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd have to camp out, no matter way. Wait for next morning."
msgstr "Tendrían que acampar, de cualquier manera. Esperar hasta la mañana siguiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd likely call her insane, gone mad, and perhaps rightly so, she thought."
msgstr "Probablemente la llamarían loca, completamente loca, y quizás con razón, pensó ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They'd return, they were promised, but few believed so."
msgstr "Volverían, lo prometieron, pero pocos creían en eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "They'll be left to the slaughter!"
msgstr "¡Nos dejarán para el masacre!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They'll come for us, one by one. Turning one against the other."
msgstr "Vendrán por nosotros, uno a uno, volviendo a uno contra el otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They'll look for us..."
msgstr "Nos buscarán..."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They'll never believe that. They saw the creature, they-"
msgstr "Nunca creerán eso. Vieron a la criatura, lo-"

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They'll soon be ready for you to step onto the flagship."
msgstr "Pronto estarán listos para que des el paso hacia la nave insignia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They'll use force if they can, if not, they play on your emotions."
msgstr "Usarán la fuerza si pueden; de lo contrario, jugarán con tus emociones."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They're all but ready to crown you a saint."
msgstr "Están listos para coronarte como un santo."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They're all capable men, I've made sure of it."
msgstr "Son hombres capaces, lo he asegurado yo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're all nice people, but none of them is you..."
msgstr "Son gente agradable, pero ninguno de ellos es tú..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're bastards. You don't have to say it. You're safe now."
msgstr "Son unas zorra. No hace falta que lo digas. Ya estás a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They're called a lot of things, but my order, we call them voidlings."
msgstr "Se les llama de muchas maneras, pero mi orden los llamamos 'voidlings'."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They're called the Romanov Twins."
msgstr "Se les llama los Gemelos Romanov."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They're capable soldiers and you need the kinds of guards you can trust with your life."
msgstr "Son soldados capaces y necesitas el tipo de guardias en las que puedas confiar con tu vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "They're fine people, but I can't be around them for too long, so I like to wander away from the camp."
msgstr "Son personas decentes, pero no puedo estar cerca de ellos por mucho tiempo, así que me gusta alejarme del campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone now. So what is left to be feared?"
msgstr "Ya se fueron. ¿Qué queda por temer?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone."
msgstr "Están desaparecidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're gone?"
msgstr "¿Se han ido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "They're gonna hang you for this, thief."
msgstr "Te colgarán por esto, ladrón."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They're gonna park an army on every market in Lethram for a week."
msgstr "Ván a estacionar un ejército en cada mercado de Lethram durante una semana."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They're happy."
msgstr "Están contentos."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "They're here somewhere!"
msgstr "¡Están por aquí, en algún lugar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "They're holdin my ship in Lethram until I come up with the money to pay them back."
msgstr "Están reteniendo mi barco en Lethram hasta que consiga el dinero para pagarles."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "They're just so bored out of their minds they start meddling with other people's business."
msgstr "Están tan aburridos que se meten en los asuntos de otros."

msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "They're kicking up a real proper storm."
msgstr "Están causando una verdadera tormenta."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They're more worried about surviving the next winter, or the health of their crop."
msgstr "Están más preocupados por sobrevivir al próximo invierno o por la salud de su cosecha."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're mostly on this side."
msgstr "Están mayormente de este lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "They're not anymore, Sarah. They might have been once, but you're not their princess anymore."
msgstr "Ya no lo son, Sarah. Podrían haberlo sido alguna vez, pero ya no eres su princesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "They're not going to give a damn if you hang us or not. Gods, they might actually thank you for getting rid of us!"
msgstr "No nos importará si nos colgáis o no. Por los dioses, ¡quizás incluso os den las gracias por deshaceros de nosotros!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They're not good people."
msgstr "No son gente buena."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "They're not looking for a real fight, they're cowards. The only fights they want are when they outnumber their targets."
msgstr "No buscan una pelea real, son cobardes. Solo quieren pelear cuando tienen la ventaja numérica."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "They're obsessed with all of it."
msgstr "Están obsesionados con todo eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They're on the edge of mutiny as it is."
msgstr "Ya están al borde de la rebelión."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They're quiet for a long time. Kate finally breaks the silence."
msgstr "Callan en silencio durante un largo tiempo. Kate rompe finalmente el silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "They're sayin that he died from it."
msgstr "Dicen que murió a causa de eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They're sooo bright out here. I never saw them this bright before."
msgstr "Están tan brillantes aquí afuera. Nunca los había visto tan brillantes antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "They're still barricaded up in the throne room, back in the royal quarters."
msgstr "Aún están barricados en la sala del trono, en los aposentos reales."

msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "They're trouble, try and steer clear of them if you can."
msgstr "Son peligrosos, intenta mantenerles alejados si puedes."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They're trying to a cut a path straight to you."
msgstr "Están tratando de abrirse paso directamente hacia ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "They're usually never this hard workin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "They're waiting for you to give them the sign."
msgstr "Están esperando que les des la señal."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They're waiting for you to give them the sign."
msgstr "Están esperando que les des la señal."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "They're woodland spirits. They can sense the trees and the wood more clearly than any other substance."
msgstr "Son espíritus del bosque. Pueden percibir los árboles y la madera con mayor claridad que cualquier otra sustancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "They've been saying you might sail back to Rosanna...take back your home."
msgstr "Han estado diciendo que quizás volverás a navegar hacia Rosanna...a recuperar tu hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "They've been spared the worst of it."
msgstr "Han escapado a lo peor de todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They've only known each other for weeks, but already feel like old friends. She's happy not to feel so alone anymore."
msgstr "Solo se conocen desde hace semanas, pero ya sienten como viejos amigos. Ella está feliz de no sentirse tan sola."

msgctxt "speaker:Scout"
msgid "They've shut the gates to the city and they've drafted the city militia to help secure the fortifications."
msgstr "Han cerrado las puertas de la ciudad y han reclutado a la milicia urbana para ayudar a asegurar las fortificaciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "They've taken position on nearby hills, but so far, they report nothing."
msgstr "Han tomado posición en las colinas cercanas, pero hasta ahora no reportan nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "They've tried blackmail, threats and bribery."
msgstr "Ya probaron con chantaje, amenazas y sobornos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "They, along with herself, were the voices that mattered at this Union Council."
msgstr "Ellos, junto con ella misma, eran las voces que importaban en este Consejo de la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They...just dissapeared?"
msgstr "¿Ellos... ¿acaban de desaparecer?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They...just kill people?"
msgstr "¿Solo los matan?"

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "They...they said that..."
msgstr "Ellas... dijeron eso..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They...they're really thinking about all of that?"
msgstr "¿De verdad piensan en todo eso?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They...would let us starve?"
msgstr "¿Nos dejarían morir de hambre?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They...wrote down history? You mean...everything that is going to happen?"
msgstr "¿Escribieron la historia? ¿Quieres decir... todo lo que va a suceder?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "They?"
msgstr "¿Ellos?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thick and black like ink, she thought for a moment that she had knocked something over, even though she was sure she had not."
msgstr "Espesa y negra como tinta, pensó por un momento que había derribado algo, aunque estaba segura de no haberlo hecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thick and copious, she could feel his cum crawling down her throat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thick flakes of snow twirled down. The clouds hung over them like a grey blanket, blotting out any light."
msgstr "Espesos copos de nieve giraban en el aire. Las nubes se colgaban sobre ellos como una manta gris, ocultando cualquier destello de luz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thick ropes of semen spray forth, landing across her face. She closes her eyes to prevent it from going into her eyes, but she was too slow with her mouth."
msgstr "Espesas cuerdas de semen salen disparadas, cayendo sobre su rostro. Cierra los ojos para evitar que le entren en los ojos, pero es demasiado lenta con la boca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thick, green vines ran along the floor and walls of the building she was standing in."
msgstr "Espesas y verdes enredaderas recorrían el suelo y las paredes del edificio donde se encontraba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thief to prostitute."
msgstr "Ladrón a puta."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Thieves get a lashing and get run out of town."
msgstr "Los ladrones reciben azotes y son expulsados de la ciudad."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Thievin rats like you and your buddy disrupt that order for all the good citizens of Lethram. The law-abiding citizens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thin of face, and thin of frame, the woman struck her as almost frail...except for her belly."
msgstr "Delgada de rostro y delgada de estructura, la mujer le pareció casi frágil... excepto por su vientre."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Things concerning your...nature."
msgstr "Cosas relacionadas con tu... naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Things like these keep the nobles fat and happy."
msgstr "Cosas así mantienen a los nobles gordos y felices."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Things that were not meant to be, and to Sarah, it seemed as obvious that they should not be."
msgstr "Cosas que no debían ser, y para Sarah parecía tan obvio que no debían ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "Things were getting quite dark towards the end..."
msgstr "Las cosas se volvían bastante oscuras hacia el final..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Things were particularly bad on the border territories, where most of the fighting and raiding took place."
msgstr "Las cosas estaban particularmente mal en los territorios fronterizos, donde se producía la mayor parte de las batallas y los saqueos."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Things will be different."
msgstr "Las cosas serán diferentes."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Things will change...you're right about that."
msgstr "Las cosas cambiarán... tienes razón en eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Think I'm pretty."
msgstr "Creo que soy bonita."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Think no other word before. No other word after. Reduce your mind to a singular word."
msgstr "Reduce tu mente a una sola palabra. No pienses en ninguna otra antes, ni en ninguna otra después."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Think of it as an act, a performance, she told herself."
msgstr "Piénsalo como un acto, una actuación,"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Think of it like this."
msgstr "Piénsalo así."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Think of it what you will, Sarah, but I am still the leader of this company."
msgstr "Piensa en lo que quieras, Sarah, pero yo sigo siendo el líder de esta empresa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Think of what they'd do to you, if they had the chance, Sarah thought."
msgstr "Piensa en lo que harían contigo si tuvieran la oportunidad, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Think of what we could do together."
msgstr "Piensa en lo que podríamos hacer juntos."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "Think of what we will each spare the other."
msgstr "Piensa en lo que cada uno de nosotros se ahorrará al otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Think of your daughter!"
msgstr "Piensa en tu hija!"

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Think that is a wonderful idea, Sarah."
msgstr "Piénsalo, es una idea maravillosa, Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Think, Sarah. Suppose I survive the square, then what? They sound the alarm and soon the entire city garrison will descend on me."
msgstr "Piensa, Sarah. ¿Qué pasa si sobrevivo a la plaza? Entonces... ¿qué? Sonarán la alarma y pronto toda la guarnición de la ciudad descenderá sobre mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "Think?"
msgstr "¿Pensar?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thinking about her brother was too painful, and yet, even years later she still found herself thinking about him."
msgstr "Pensar en su hermano era demasiado doloroso, y sin embargo, incluso años después, seguía encontrándose pensando en él."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thinking about what?"
msgstr "¿De qué estás pensando?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thinking itself became burdensome..."
msgstr "El propio acto de pensar se volvió una carga..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thinking of him made her climax harder than normal, but it also reminded her of how this pleasure faded when compared to the real thing."
msgstr "Pensar en él hacía que su orgasmo fuera más fuerte que de costumbre, pero también le recordaba cómo ese placer se desvanecía al compararlo con lo real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thinking of him with his cock trapped in that cage made her feel sorry for him all over again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thinking that somehow, she did not deserve this."
msgstr "Pensando que de alguna manera no merecía esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Thinking, always thinking."
msgstr "Pensando, siempre pensando."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This Art is dangerous, but you are gifted. The rewards will be worth it in the end."
msgstr "Este Arte es peligroso, pero estás dotada. Las recompensas valdrán la pena al final."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "This Empire is blessed, or cursed if you might."
msgstr "Este Imperio está bendecido, o maldito si lo prefieres."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "This Estate..."
msgstr "Esta finca..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This I did."
msgstr "Esto hice yo."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This I promise you, Shah."
msgstr "Te lo prometo, Shah."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "This Orc threat? The Orcs have done nothing for decades now. They are an excuse."
msgstr "¿Esta amenaza de los Orcos? Los Orcos no han hecho nada por décadas. Son una excusa."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "This Union will be formed with your support or without it. And as you can see, I will be promoted as its leader."
msgstr "Esta Unión se formará con tu apoyo o sin él. Y como puedes ver, seré promovida como su líder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This affair between them was one thing...but the idea of standing before a crowd of people and publicly confessing..."
msgstr "Este asunto entre ellos era una cosa... pero la idea de presentarse ante una multitud y confesarlo públicamente..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This ain't as good as that lake in the desert, but it's pretty close."
msgstr "Esto no es tan bueno como ese lago del desierto, pero está bastante cerca."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This ain't no charity, blondie."
msgstr "Esto no es caridad, rubia."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "This ain't no place for your girlfriend."
msgstr "Este no es el sitio para tu novia."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This alley ain't just next to your house. It's also next to a bar."
msgstr "Este callejón no está justo al lado de tu casa, sino también junto a un bar."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This also means that our need for information regarding these partners from across the world, has been more vital to us than others in the Union."
msgstr "Esto también significa que nuestra necesidad de información sobre estos socios de todo el mundo ha sido más vital para nosotros que para otros en la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This any good?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This armor has been scraping and cutting against my skin since I stepped into this forest."
msgstr "Esta armadura ha estado raspando y cortando mi piel desde que puse pie en este bosque."

msgctxt "speaker:Officer"
msgid "This attack was a large portion of their forces, but it wasn't all of them."
msgstr "Este ataque fue una parte considerable de sus fuerzas, pero no fueron todos ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "This attitude of yours is the first thing we'll go about fixing, got that?"
msgstr "Esta actitud tuya es lo primero que vamos a arreglar, ¿entendido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This beer...where did it come from?"
msgstr "Esta cerveza... ¿de dónde salió?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This being one of the smaller markets, she could more easily walk through the crowd."
msgstr "Al ser uno de los mercados más pequeños, podía caminar por la multitud con mayor facilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This blasted town is scarce any unwed woman, and certainly none that will take a chance on a man of my prospects!"
msgstr "¡Maldita sea, este pueblo está tan escaso de mujeres solteras que no hay ninguna que se atreva a arriesgarse con un hombre de mis condiciones!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This book is three thousand years old?"
msgstr "¿Este libro tiene tres mil años?"

msgctxt "speaker:Old Tribesman"
msgid "This brings me to the last issue at hand."
msgstr "Esto me lleva al último asunto pendiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This camp...these soldiers...we were very close to disaster."
msgstr "Este campo... estos soldados... estábamos muy cerca del desastre."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This can't be...there has to be a way to stop this..."
msgstr "Esto no puede ser... tiene que haber una manera de detener esto..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This can't...I..."
msgstr "Esto no puede ser... yo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This castle, this court, it can be what you make of it, Varga. You can see yourself as seperate from it, always feeling alienated, or you can become a part of it. Add to it."
msgstr "Este castillo, esta corte, pueden ser lo que tú quieras que sean, Varga. Puedes verte a ti mismo como separado de ello, sintiéndote siempre alienado, o puedes convertirte en parte de él. Añade algo más."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "This changed when a newly risen general proposed a new strategy."
msgstr "Esto cambió cuando un general recién ascendido propuso una nueva estrategia."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This chick is so desperate, honestly, even I don't have the energy to be fucking anybody else."
msgstr "Esta perra está tan desesperada, honestamente, que ni siquiera tengo la energía para follarme a nadie más."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This city is a little more equal than where you or I came from."
msgstr "Esta ciudad es un poco más igualitaria que donde tú o yo venimos."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This city is so full of criminals, another one would come across you in no time."
msgstr "Esta ciudad está tan llena de criminales que aparecería otra frente a ti en cualquier momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This city moves fast. Too fast to hold onto grudges."
msgstr "Esta ciudad se mueve rápido. Demasiado rápido para aferrarse a rencores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This city that went on forever."
msgstr "Esta ciudad que se extendía para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This city, hell maybe this world, it's all kinda ways fucked up for people like you and me."
msgstr "Esta ciudad, quizás incluso este mundo, está todo bastante jodido para gente como tú y como yo."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This city, this world, it's a dangerous place. You go out there alone, with nothing and nobody, they'll eat you alive."
msgstr "Esta ciudad, este mundo, es un lugar peligroso. Si sales ahí solo, sin nada ni nadie, te comerán vivo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This city..."
msgstr "Esta ciudad..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, his body was outright frightening."
msgstr "A esta distancia, su cuerpo era aterrador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, it seemed massive."
msgstr "Tan cerca, parecía enorme."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, she can see the sudden uncertainty in Samayra's eyes."
msgstr "A esta distancia, ella puede ver la repentina incertidumbre en los ojos de Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, she could feel Kate's breath on her neck."
msgstr "A esta distancia, podía sentir el aliento de Kate en su cuello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, she could feel his body heat, even smell him."
msgstr "A esta distancia, podía sentir su calor corporal e incluso olerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, she could feel his warm breath on her cold skin."
msgstr "Tan cerca, podía sentir su aliento cálido sobre su piel fría."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This close, she could study more intently."
msgstr "A esta distancia, podía observarla con más atención."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "This company is at the most critical moment in its existence."
msgstr "Esta compañía se encuentra en el momento más crítico de su existencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This company is coming apart at the seams, and the only instruction you're able to hand down is to whip people until they do as you say."
msgstr "Esta empresa se está desmoronando por los costados, y la única orden que puedes imponer es azotar a la gente hasta que hagan lo que digas."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This could be a perfect opporunity to deal with both at the same time."
msgstr "Esto podría ser la oportunidad perfecta para atenderlos a ambos al mismo tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Judge"
msgid "This court will not be made a mockery of!"
msgstr "¡Esta corte no se convertirá en objeto de burla!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This crack rang out louder than another before."
msgstr "Este estallido resonó más fuerte que los anteriores."

msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "This creature, I thought it was an animal. A wild wolf, a frenzied bear, we've dealt with those things before."
msgstr "Esta criatura, pensé que era un animal. Un lobo salvaje, un oso furioso; hemos lidiado con esas cosas antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This cycle continued without fail for centures, to the point some even imagined it cursed."
msgstr "Este ciclo continuaba sin fallar durante siglos, hasta el punto de que algunos incluso lo imaginaban maldito."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This deep into the forest, there was nobody to hear, and so neither held back in their emotions."
msgstr "En lo profundo del bosque, nadie podría oírlos, por lo que ninguno se contuvo en sus emociones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This desert was filled with the remains of the fallen. One more to the pile."
msgstr "Este desierto estaba lleno de los restos de los caídos. Otro más para el montón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This desert, much like the rest of the world, tolerated no weakness."
msgstr "Este desierto, al igual que el resto del mundo, no toleraba la debilidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This dish was easy enough."
msgstr "Este plato era bastante sencillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This document outlines their strategy for attacking the Union."
msgstr "Este documento detalla su estrategia para atacar la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This does not prove beyond a doubt that they are bandits, but I suppose the evidence weighs more in that direction than any other."
msgstr "Esto no prueba más allá de toda duda que son bandidos, pero supongo que la evidencia pesa más en esa dirección que en cualquier otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This drink was new to her, and she could feel it hit her hard."
msgstr "Esta bebida era nueva para ella, y podía sentir cómo la golpeaba con fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This easy, comfortable place."
msgstr "Este lugar tan sencillo y acogedor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This endless grind."
msgstr "Este trabajo interminable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This explanation made a lot more sense for the kind of person she thought he was."
msgstr "Esta explicación tenía mucho más sentido para el tipo de persona que ella creía que él era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This far out, the city and its people looked like a great ant hill, tiny dots climbing over one another, all busy with some task, who knew what."
msgstr "A esta distancia, la ciudad y su gente parecían una enorme colmena de hormigas, diminutos puntos trepándose unos sobre otros, todos ocupados con alguna tarea, ¿quién sabe qué?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This far out, the streets were entirely abanonded."
msgstr "A esta distancia, las calles estaban completamente abandonadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This fat, cruel man, older than her father, talking about getting her pregnant..."
msgstr "Este hombre gordo y cruel, más viejo que su padre, hablando de hacerla embarazada..."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This fear and this love for her people and her empire, caused her to reach out to the gods."
msgstr "Este miedo y este amor por su pueblo y su imperio la llevaron a buscar a los dioses."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "This flower I had forged by a blacksmith into this necklace of Ghost Silver, one of the rarest metals, claimed from slain Mythran soldiers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "This flower, I plucked from the only place where it grows."
msgstr "Esta flor la arranqué del único lugar donde crece."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "This foolish expedition? Nah, still as stupid as the day we got off the road, but..."
msgstr "¿Esta estúpida expedición? No, sigue siendo tan tonta como el día en que nos bajamos del camino, pero..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This force was like nothing she'd ever felt from him. This was how strong the captain really was."
msgstr "Esta fuerza era como nada que ella hubiera sentido jamás de él. Así es como de fuerte era el capitán realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This fortress shielded her as much as it was her prison."
msgstr "Esta fortaleza la protegía tanto como era su prisión."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "This garden took quite a while to construct."
msgstr "Este jardín tardó bastante en construirse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This gave Sarah some comfort."
msgstr "Esto le dio a Sarah algo de consuelo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This gave Sarah the advantage in numbers."
msgstr "Esto le dio a Sarah una ventaja numérica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had become her life."
msgstr "Esto se había convertido en su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had been Marius' favorite."
msgstr "Esta había sido el favorito de Marius."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had been a mistake."
msgstr "Esto había sido un error."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had been her life for years now."
msgstr "Esto había sido su vida durante años."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had been the last stand of the Tribesmen."
msgstr "Este había sido el último asalto de los tribales."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had the desired effect."
msgstr "Esto tuvo el efecto deseado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This had to end."
msgstr "Esto tenía que terminar."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This has meant that my nation has always held deeper ties to the rest of the world."
msgstr "Esto ha significado que mi nación siempre haya mantenido lazos más profundos con el resto del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This has to be the origin."
msgstr "Esto debe ser el origen."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "This here bridge belongs to the Elyian Kingdom."
msgstr "Este puente pertenece al Reino de Elyia."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This here covers the basics. Learning to eliminate all senses. Using magic to sever the soul's connection. Mantras for guiding your path between."
msgstr "Esto cubre lo básico. Aprender a eliminar todos los sentidos. Usar magia para cortar la conexión del alma. Mantras para guiar tu camino entre."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This here is Nickolas, but you can just call him Nick."
msgstr "Este es Nickolas, pero puedes llamarlo simplemente Nick."

msgctxt "speaker:Ramsey"
msgid "This here is a family business, and I couldn't run it without my family."
msgstr "Esto es un negocio familiar y no podría hacerlo funcionar sin mi familia."

msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "This here is an official Mythran excavation."
msgstr "Esto es una excavación oficial de Mythra."

msgctxt "speaker:Brigand"
msgid "This here is my alley, I own it, and I can't just let anybody and everybody sleep here."
msgstr "Esta es mi callejón, lo tengo controlado y no voy a dejar que cualquiera y cualquier maldita persona duerman aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This here is pretty much the Palace of Crime in Lethram."
msgstr "Este lugar es prácticamente el Palacio del Crimen en Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Innkeeper"
msgid "This here is the Dunstin Inn. We got Dunstin Stew. And as you might suspect, I'm Ramsey Dunstin."
msgstr "Aquí está la Taberna Dunstin. Tenemos estofado de Dunstin. Y como es de suponer, soy Ramsey Dunstin."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "This here is the main road that runs closest from our current position."
msgstr "Esta es la carretera principal que discurre más cerca de nuestra posición actual."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This here is the stove. Neither me nor my dad can cook to save our lives. So if you could give it a try, that be amazin."
msgstr "Aquí está la estufa. Ni yo ni mi papá sabemos cocinar para salvar nuestras vidas, así que si te animas a probarlo, sería increíble."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This house and this land is all I own."
msgstr "Esta casa y esta tierra son todo lo que poseo."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This house is accommodating to your desires."
msgstr "Esta casa se acomoda a tus deseos."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This house resides in what is known as the Old Quarter."
msgstr "Esta casa se encuentra en lo que se conoce como el Barrio Viejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This house will pass to your son, and while you might think he has forgiven you, I cannot rely only on hope."
msgstr "Esta casa pasará a tu hijo, y aunque quizás creas que te ha perdonado, no puedo basarme únicamente en la esperanza."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This information is too important! We cannot wait!"
msgstr "¡Esta información es demasiado importante! No podemos esperar!"

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "This invention, how shall we say, balances the scales?"
msgstr "Esta invención, cómo decirlo, equilibra la balanza?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "This is Krip. He isn't much for talking, but he swings an axe harder than any man I ever met, and out here on the old road that matters more than nice words."
msgstr "Este es Krip. No le gusta mucho hablar, pero maneja el hacha con más fuerza que ningún hombre al que he conocido, y aquí, en el viejo camino, eso importa más que las palabras bonitas."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This is Laitha, one of our neighbouring worlds."
msgstr "Esta es Laitha, uno de nuestros mundos vecinos."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "This is Nathan. Nathan, this is Sarah."
msgstr "Esto es Nathan. Nathan, esto es Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is Samayra. My friend."
msgstr "Esta es Samayra. Mi amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is a book on non-native flora growth patterns."
msgstr "Este es un libro sobre los patrones de crecimiento de la flora no nativa."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This is a lesson, for you."
msgstr "Esto es una lección, para ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is a lot of money, isn't it?"
msgstr "Es mucho dinero, ¿verdad?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is a lot..."
msgstr "Esto es mucho..."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This is a map for a proposed invasion of the Union Kingdoms by several Mythran Legions."
msgstr "Este es un mapa para una invasión propuesta de los Reinos de la Unión por varias Legiones Mythran."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "This is a ritual known for settling wars, among our people."
msgstr "Este es un ritual conocido por resolver guerras, entre nuestro pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "This is a royal convoy and you either do as I say or we'll cut through the both of you!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is all so strange to get used to..."
msgstr "Todo esto es tan extraño de acostumbrarse..."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "This is all that he has. And still he clings to it. Desperate to let even a crumb slip from his fingers."
msgstr "Esto es todo lo que tiene. Y aun así se aferra a ello, desesperado por dejar caer incluso una migaja de sus dedos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is all...difficult to explain, but he said that this place was a good place, with good people."
msgstr "Esto es todo... difícil de explicar, pero dijo que este lugar era bueno, con buenas personas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is better I suppose."
msgstr "Supongo que es mejor."

msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "This is bullshit."
msgstr "Esto es una mierda."

msgctxt "speaker:Barion"
msgid "This is correct, but in recent years the tide has been higher than ususal. This has favored our city's port, but it has had unexpected consequences."
msgstr "Esto es correcto, pero en los últimos años la marea ha sido más alta de lo habitual. Esto ha favorecido el puerto de nuestra ciudad, pero ha tenido consecuencias inesperadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is dangerous."
msgstr "Esto es peligroso."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "This is enough."
msgstr "Esto es suficiente."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This is even better than yesterday! You're a natural!"
msgstr "¡Esto es aún mejor que ayer! ¡Eres una natural!"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This is even bigger than the library in Bagrad!"
msgstr "¡Esto es incluso más grande que la biblioteca de Bagrad!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is going too far, she thought."
msgstr "Esto va demasiado lejos, pensó."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "This is great news!"
msgstr "¡Esto es una gran noticia!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is how I die? Sarah could hardly bring her mind to conceive of it."
msgstr "¿Así es como muero? Sarah apenas podía concebir tal idea en su mente."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This is how I lived my early life, until many years ago, when Hassar's tribe, still a small tribe back then, raided the province and captured many slaves. The noble house, and everyone in it, was captured and made a slave."
msgstr "Así es como viví mi juventud, hasta hace muchos años, cuando la tribu de Hassar, que entonces era aún pequeña, saqueó la provincia y capturó a muchos esclavos. La noble casa, y todos sus miembros, fueron capturados y hechos esclavos."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "This is how my family came to be as it is today."
msgstr "Así es como mi familia llegó a ser lo que es hoy."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is how she lived."
msgstr "Así vivió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is how she would die. Sarah could almost laugh at the absurdity of it. All these years, only to die to a coward's trick."
msgstr "Así moriría. Sarah casi podía reírse de la absurdidad de ello. Todos estos años, solo para morir por una trampa de cobarde."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is how they lived, and this is how they died."
msgstr "Así vivían, y así morían."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is incredible!"
msgstr "¡Esto es increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is incredible..."
msgstr "Esto es increíble..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is insane. We can't go through with this."
msgstr "Esto es loco. No podemos seguir adelante con esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is it, she thinks. The fact of her body that overrules her better judgement."
msgstr "Es el momento, piensa ella. El hecho de su cuerpo que anula su mejor juicio."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is less than a day worker makes down the docks. Why even bother stealing it at all?"
msgstr "Esto es menos de lo que gana un día trabajando en los muelles. ¿Por qué molestarse en robarlo siquiera?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This is more appropriate for a dock whore."
msgstr "Esto es más apropiado para una puta de muelle."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This is more than I normally steal in a week, hell, maybe a month!"
msgstr "¡Esto es más de lo que normalmente robo en una semana, joder, ¡quizás un mes!"

msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "This is more than just an order from the city council. This is personal for them."
msgstr "Esto es más que una simple orden del consejo de la ciudad. Es algo personal para ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is most crucial...where is the fate stone?"
msgstr "Esta es la piedra del destino... ¿dónde está?"

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "This is my bed."
msgstr "Esta es mi cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Brigand"
msgid "This is my camp."
msgstr "Este es mi campamento."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This is my favorite place in the entire palace."
msgstr "Este es mi lugar favorito en todo el palacio."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "This is my gift to you, my friends!"
msgstr "¡Esto es mi regalo para ti, mis amigos!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is my home. Among the men and women of my mercenary company."
msgstr "Este es mi hogar. Entre los hombres y las mujeres de mi compañía mercenaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is my only outfit. What am I gonna wear if it's drying out?"
msgstr "Esta es mi única prenda. ¿Qué voy a ponerme si se seca?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is my true form. The other spaces in which we met...the mage's house...Bagrad...only echoes of myself."
msgstr "Esta es mi verdadera forma. Los otros espacios en los que nos conocimos... la casa del mago... Bagrad... son solo ecos de mí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is nice..."
msgstr "Esto es agradable..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is no different."
msgstr "No es diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This is not a matter of bragging. For us, it is a fact that is necessary to our survival."
msgstr "Esto no es cuestión de alardear. Para nosotros, es un hecho necesario para nuestra supervivencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "This is not a safe place."
msgstr "Este no es un lugar seguro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is not a weird getup! This is a mage's apprentice uniform!"
msgstr "¡Esto no es un atuendo extraño! ¡Es el uniforme de aprendiz de mago!"

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "This is not the other side of the sea."
msgstr "Esto no es el otro lado del mar."

msgctxt "speaker:King-On-The-Outside"
msgid "This is not your world. Nor is it ours."
msgstr "Esto no es tu mundo. Ni tampoco es el nuestro."

msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "This is nothing compared to how it looks further up."
msgstr "Esto es nada comparado con cómo se ve más arriba."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This is nothing, Sarah. A lot of things you imagine are fixed are maleable in this world."
msgstr "Esto es nada, Sarah. Muchas cosas que imaginas fijas son maleables en este mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This is nothing."
msgstr "Esto es nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This is nothing. I'm used to it."
msgstr "Esto es nada. Ya estoy acostumbrado a esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This is one of my mom's old dresses, but I think it's the same size. Maybe you can use this?"
msgstr "Es uno de los vestidos antiguos de mi madre, pero creo que es del mismo talle. ¿Quizás puedas usarlo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This is one of the hallways that leads to the Eastern wing of the Estate."
msgstr "Este es uno de los pasillos que conduce al ala este de la Mansión."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "This is one of the secret gardens. The Estate has dozens of em."
msgstr "Este es uno de los jardines secretos. La Mansión tiene docenas de ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This is quite a place."
msgstr "Este es un lugar bastante especial."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is rancid stuff."
msgstr "Esto es cosa podrida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is real wine."
msgstr "Esto es vino de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is something they've brought to you, but not to me and my brother?"
msgstr "¿Esto es algo que traen para ti, pero no para mí y mi hermano?"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This is something you do often, out there in the real world?"
msgstr "¿Es algo que haces a menudo allá afuera, en el mundo real?"

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "This is that fool Caliban's doing."
msgstr "Es obra de ese tonto, Calibán."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This is the Estate of master Gilead."
msgstr "Esta es la propiedad del señor Gilead."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This is the Receiving Hall."
msgstr "Esta es la Sala de Recepción."

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "This is the first meeting of the council since my father's death."
msgstr "Esta es la primera reunión del consejo desde la muerte de mi padre."

msgctxt "speaker:Jacob"
msgid "This is the key to the room."
msgstr "Esta es la llave de la habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Official"
msgid "This is the main gate. Obviously, it's not meant for you lot, please follow me to the service entrance."
msgstr "Esta es la puerta principal. Obviamente, no está destinada a gente como ustedes; por favor, siganme hasta la entrada de servicio."

msgctxt "speaker:Ephraim"
msgid "This is the only life I've ever known."
msgstr "Esta es la única vida que he conocido jamás."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This is the part where you introduce yourself, you slow witted-"
msgstr "Esta es la parte donde te presentas, tú lenta..."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "This is the part where you try to convince me you're better than this."
msgstr "Esta es la parte en la que intentas convencerme de que eres mejor que esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "This is the sanctum."
msgstr "Este es el santuario."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "This is the second time that I have caught you sneaking about."
msgstr "Esta es la segunda vez que te he pillado rondando por aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This is the servant quarter for the cleaning staff."
msgstr "Esta es la zona de servicio para el personal de limpieza."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is the subtlety of their craft, to make their thoughts come to you as your own."
msgstr "Esta es la sutileza de su arte, para que sus pensamientos lleguen a ti como si fueran propios."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This is the very thing that might change your life."
msgstr "Esto es exactamente lo que podría cambiar tu vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This is the way of the world everywhere. Strength dictates who can decree and who must suffer."
msgstr "Esta es la manera del mundo en todas partes. La fuerza dicta quién puede decretar y quién debe sufrir."

msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "This is the west wing, your section."
msgstr "Esta es la ala oeste, tu zona."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This is the world we're born into."
msgstr "Este es el mundo en que nacemos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is too dangerous. We need to be discreet. Anyone could walk by and see us."
msgstr "Es demasiado peligroso. Necesitamos ser discretos. Cualquiera podría pasar y vernos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is true for now, but he imagines you will grow powerful. And he is not wrong."
msgstr "Esto es cierto por ahora, pero él imagina que crecerás poderosa. Y no se equivoca."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "This is true."
msgstr "Es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is true."
msgstr "Es cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is true. You owe me no answer. I'm just a simple spirit, bored and happy to meet a new friend."
msgstr "Esto es cierto. No te debo respuesta. Soy solo un espíritu simple, aburrido y feliz de conocer a una nueva amiga."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This is what I'm gonna miss most of all."
msgstr "Esto es lo que más me voy a perder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is what happens if you're weak. The strong fuck you, and all you can do is bend over a crate and give it up."
msgstr "Esto es lo que ocurre si eres débil. Los fuertes te follarán, y todo lo que podrás hacer es doblarte sobre una caja y entregarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This is what people wage wars over. The right to sit on an uncomfortable chair and pass verdicts on tax disputes..."
msgstr "Esto es por lo que la gente libra guerras. El derecho a sentarse en una silla incómoda y dictar sentencias sobre disputas fiscales..."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "This is what you send in your place, Sarah? A slave?"
msgstr "¿Esto es lo que envías en mi lugar, Sarah? ¿Una esclava?"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This is where I go when I want to be alone. It's so hidden, I don't think even my father knows about it."
msgstr "Aquí es donde vengo cuando quiero estar sola. Está tan oculto que ni siquiera mi padre sabe de su existencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is where I'll be safe?"
msgstr "¿Aquí es donde estaré a salvo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "This is where it gets good."
msgstr "Aquí es donde las cosas se ponen interesantes."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "This is where me and Dio were send. In fact, where we met for the first time."
msgstr "Aquí es donde a mí y a Dio nos enviaron. De hecho, fue aquí donde nos conocimos por primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is where you sit all by yourself?"
msgstr "¿Es aquí donde te sientas toda sola?"

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This is who Blondie really is."
msgstr "Este es quien realmente es Blondie."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is who I really am...who we really are."
msgstr "Esta es la que realmente soy...la que realmente somos."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "This is why Gilead is so eager to start this new war and gain a foothold in the Union."
msgstr "Esta es la razón por la que Gilead está tan ansioso por iniciar esta nueva guerra y ganar terreno en la Unión."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "This is why he's kept me here in this tower."
msgstr "Esta es la razón por la que me ha mantenido aquí en esta torre."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is why you could never tell me this before...because in Xan's house, the gods would have seen and heard us..."
msgstr "Por eso nunca me pudiste decir esto antes... porque en la casa de Xan, los dioses nos habrían visto y oído..."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This is why you must remember to adhere to the first rule. You act, never allow them to act on you."
msgstr "Por eso debes recordar seguir la primera regla: tú actúas, nunca dejes que ellos actúen sobre ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This is your fault, you know that?"
msgstr "Es tu culpa, ¿lo sabes?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is your house?"
msgstr "¿Esta es tu casa?"

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "This is your leader?"
msgstr "¿Este es tu líder?"

msgctxt "speaker:Judge"
msgid "This is..."
msgstr "Esto es..."

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "This is..."
msgstr "Esta es..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This is..."
msgstr "Esto es..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This isn't a joke, let the woman go."
msgstr "Esto no es una broma, suéltala."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "This isn't like where you're from."
msgstr "Esto no es como en tu lugar de origen."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This isn't...I mean, I like you, but I don't think this is helping it go back down."
msgstr "Esto no es... quiero decir, me gustas, pero creo que esto no ayuda a que baje."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This kind of fighting, up close, personal, it was exactly the kind of brawl that her Knights were looking for."
msgstr "Este tipo de pelea, cuerpo a cuerpo y personal, era exactamente el tipo de batalla que sus caballeros buscaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Emissary"
msgid "This king was proud. Too proud to bend his head for Khan Hassar, and for this, he lost it."
msgstr "Este rey era orgulloso. Demasiado orgulloso para doblar su cabeza ante Khan Hassar, y por eso lo perdió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This land is not made for humans."
msgstr "Esta tierra no está hecha para humanos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This land where I grew up, and all the memories...and then you, and all the memories of my life after..."
msgstr "Esta tierra donde crecí, y todos los recuerdos...y luego tú, y todos los recuerdos de mi vida después..."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This late before the attack, he wants to change plans?"
msgstr "¿Tan tarde como esto antes del ataque, quiere cambiar los planes?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This life was her current truth. And it would be her only."
msgstr "Esta vida era su verdad actual. Y sería la única."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This lightness is an aberration, and your body will drive it out over time, unless you keep enforcing it."
msgstr "Esta ligereza es una aberración, y tu cuerpo la expulsará con el tiempo a menos que sigas imponiéndole."

msgctxt "speaker:Other man"
msgid "This little lady spying on us!"
msgstr "¡Esa señorita espiándonos!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This lowborn that, in these moments, towered over her."
msgstr "Esta puta de baja cuna que, en estos momentos, la superaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This lowly, nobody, of a man."
msgstr "Este miserable, este nadie de un hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This made him hard to read for Sarah. So many people were one way or another all their life, but Sakar seemed to change with each moment."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This mage world was so very different from the regular one, just outside."
msgstr "Este mundo de magos era tan diferente al normal, justo afuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This magic, it was but a tool for you. A tool to secure your real ambition, to live on your own accord."
msgstr "Esta magia, solo era una herramienta para ti. Una herramienta para asegurar tu verdadera ambición, para vivir según tus propios designios."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This man I had never met before, he knew me, out of thousands, and called me to him."
msgstr "Este hombre que nunca había conocido me conocía, entre miles, y me llamó a mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man appeared neither."
msgstr "Este hombre no aparecía en ninguna parte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man had been her saviour, but he was no ally to her, she realized. She had no allies left."
msgstr "Este hombre había sido su salvador, pero no era un aliado para ella, lo comprendió. Ya no tenía aliados."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man had made slaves of her people, killed thousands upon thousands."
msgstr "Este hombre había hecho esclavos de su pueblo y matado a miles."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man held the lease to her life. She needed to win his favor, and the easiest way to do that seemed to be through submitting herself."
msgstr "Este hombre tenía el control de su vida. Necesitaba ganarse su favor, y la forma más fácil de lograrlo parecía ser sometiéndose a él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man of such small status and power...could decide her fate."
msgstr "Este hombre de tan poco estatus y poder... podía decidir su destino."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man was old, far too old."
msgstr "Este hombre era viejo, demasiado viejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "This man who seeks to rob me of my victory by drawing daggers like some backalley cuthroat?"
msgstr "¿Este hombre que busca robarme mi victoria clavando dagas como algún matón de callejón?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man, old enough to be her father, hells older, had taken her as only a husband should."
msgstr "Este hombre, lo bastante viejo para ser su padre, ¡maldita sea, aún más viejo!, la había tomado como solo un esposo debería."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man, she thought, seemed to live at the tyrant's every whim. Could he be a good man, even if he worked for the man that enslaved her people?"
msgstr "Este hombre, pensó ella, parecía vivir a cada capricho del tirano. ¿Podría ser un buen hombre, incluso si trabajaba para el que esclavizaba a su pueblo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This man, this conqueror, he was not who she had been destined for, and yet none of that seemed to matter now."
msgstr "Este hombre, este conquistador, no era quien estaba destinado para ella, y sin embargo, nada de eso parecía importar ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This map has to be centuries old, at the least."
msgstr "Este mapa debe tener al menos siglos de antigüedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "This map...it's fine, but you need to see the real lay of the land."
msgstr "Este mapa... está bien, pero necesitas ver el verdadero relieve del terreno."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This matter is of great importance to Rosanna."
msgstr "Este asunto es de gran importancia para Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "This matter of enshrining the politic righs, I think it is most important."
msgstr "Esta cuestión de consagrar los derechos políticos, creo que es sumamente importante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This matter of the Union Council had drawn out from days to weeks now."
msgstr "Este asunto del Consejo de la Unión se ha prolongado desde días hasta semanas ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This means that no single tribe can hope to hold it, because all the other tribes would prevent it."
msgstr "Esto significa que ninguna tribu puede esperar retenerlo, porque todas las demás lo impedirían."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This means that soldiers will have to pull the converted wagons, and we don't have enough soldiers to bring all the wagons."
msgstr "Esto significa que los soldados tendrán que tirar de los carros convertidos, y no tenemos suficientes soldados para arrastrar todos los carros."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "This means you will have to pass the initiation exam."
msgstr "Esto significa que tendrás que aprobar la prueba de iniciación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This meant that if her mouth proved insufficient, he would use other parts of her."
msgstr "Esto significaba que, si su boca resultaba insuficiente, él usaría otras partes de ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This meant that it didn't just take longer to gather up the army, but they also required more training before they were battle ready."
msgstr "Esto significaba que no solo tardaría más en reunir el ejército, sino que también requeriría más entrenamiento antes de estar listo para la batalla."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This meant that they began instructing me on how to read, and allowed me to study many different fields of study, physics, biology, languages. It was a new world for me."
msgstr "Esto significaba que comenzaron a enseñarme a leer y me permitieron estudiar muchos campos del conocimiento, la física, la biología y los idiomas. Era un mundo nuevo para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This memory of her would be etched into his mind for the rest of his life."
msgstr "Este recuerdo de ella quedaría grabado en su mente para el resto de su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Founder"
msgid "This moment is the very chance that we have been working towards for centuries now."
msgstr "Este instante es la oportunidad misma hacia la que hemos estado trabajando durante siglos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This moment, right now, was when she would be most vulnerable."
msgstr "Este momento, justo ahora, es cuando ella sería más vulnerable."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This mountain is crawling with Orc tribes. We might as well just surrender ourselves now."
msgstr "Esta montaña está infestada de tribus orcos. Podríamos rendirnos ahora mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "This my home! You listen to me!"
msgstr "¡Esta es mi casa! ¡Escúchame!"

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "This necklace, I gave to my first wife, whom I had promised my heart."
msgstr "Este collar se lo di a mi primera esposa, a quien prometí mi corazón."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This new place, these new people."
msgstr "Este nuevo lugar, esta gente nueva."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This new world was summoned into ours, but all of existence covers all of existence."
msgstr "Este nuevo mundo fue convocado al nuestro, pero todo el universo abarca todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This newly developed stamina had also proven useful for Sarah in keeping up with Atilla in other ways."
msgstr "Esta nueva resistencia también ha resultado útil para Sarah en otros aspectos al mantener el ritmo con Atilla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This old man. Pathetic. Grovelling."
msgstr "¡Este viejo patético, arrastrándose como un gusano!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This one I recognize."
msgstr "Esta la reconozco."

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "This one boy, always did flirt with me, thought he'd end up marrying me one day."
msgstr "Este muchacho siempre coqueteó conmigo; pensé que algún día se casaría conmigo."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "This one is mine."
msgstr "Esta es mía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This one was fuller than any of the previous cups."
msgstr "Esta era más llena que ninguna de las copas anteriores."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This one was vast, and seemingly only grew."
msgstr "Esta era vasta y parecía crecer sin cesar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This one would be no different."
msgstr "Esta tampoco sería diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This only added to the growing claustrophobic rush that was building in her chest."
msgstr "Esto solo aumentaba la opresiva sensación de claustrofobia que se apoderaba de su pecho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This only seemed to amuse him."
msgstr "Esto solo parecía entretenerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This only seemed to entertain him."
msgstr "Esto solo parecía entretenerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This other world was summoned, but all of existence covers all of existence."
msgstr "Este otro mundo fue convocado, pero toda la existencia abarca toda la existencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This painting, and a few like it, were his only connection to her."
msgstr "Este cuadro, y unos pocos más como él, eran su único vínculo con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This part of Lethram was a bit more calm. A few merchants were pulling carts along, some wandering sailors, but compared to the hustle and bustle of the port, it was almost pleasant."
msgstr "Esta parte de Lethram era un poco más tranquila. Algunos comerciantes arrastraban carros, algunos marineros vagabundos, pero comparado con el bullicio del puerto, era casi agradable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This part of the world, with little remaining civilization, could offer no resistance to the march of nature."
msgstr "Esta parte del mundo, con poca civilización restante, no podía ofrecer resistencia alguna al avance de la naturaleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This part was familiar to her too."
msgstr "Esta parte también le era familiar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "This part, so far, it's mostly just the Lethram hinterlands."
msgstr "Esta zona, hasta ahora, es principalmente el interior de Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "This pathway is one of them. The gemstone another."
msgstr "Este sendero es uno de ellos. La gema, otro."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This place does not only offer an impressive collection. It also functions as a means to sharpen the mind, focus it."
msgstr "Este lugar no solo ofrece una impresionante colección; también funciona como un medio para afilar la mente y concentrarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place had been the center of her life for so many years now..."
msgstr "Este lugar había sido el centro de su vida durante tantos años..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This place here is my source."
msgstr "Este lugar es mi fuente."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "This place is at the edge of the world."
msgstr "Este lugar está en el borde del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "This place is dangerous enough for just about anybody, girl."
msgstr "Este lugar es peligroso para casi cualquiera, niña."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This place is giving me the creeps."
msgstr "Este lugar me da miedo."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This place might look like a mess, but I know every knife and fork and what not."
msgstr "Este lugar puede parecer un desastre, pero conozco cada cuchillo y tenedor y demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place was more like a graveyard than a castle."
msgstr "Este lugar era más bien un cementerio que un castillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place was still strange, but she could set her mind to understanding it."
msgstr "Este lugar seguía siendo extraño, pero podía poner su mente en entenderlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place was supposed to be a secret."
msgstr "Este lugar debía ser un secreto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place wasn't dying. It had died a long time ago."
msgstr "Este lugar no estaba muriendo. Había muerto hace mucho tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This place...it's still all so new. It can feel a little lonely."
msgstr "Este lugar... todavía se siente todo tan nuevo. Puede sentirse un poco solitario."

msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "This place...this city, it's all one big heap of people crawling over others to get ahead."
msgstr "Este lugar... esta ciudad, es todo un gran montón de gente arrastrándose unos sobre otros para salir adelante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This place...this town on the edge of the world."
msgstr "Este lugar... este pueblo al borde del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This port is a proper port, not meant for cock crazed whores like you."
msgstr "Este puerto es un verdadero puerto, no para zorras locas de polla como tú."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "This process of advancement...it is a gift to the Noctori, but it is a curse as well."
msgstr "Este proceso de avance... es un regalo para los Noctori, pero también es una maldición."

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "This proposal is absurd."
msgstr "Esta propuesta es absurda."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This pussy is mine. Got that?"
msgstr "Esta zorra es mía. ¿Entendido?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This quieted the girl down."
msgstr "Esto calmó a la chica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This reminder was enough for the soldiers, and they moved again, grabbing Marion, wrestling him to the ground as he tried to fight them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This room was its opposite in every sense."
msgstr "Esta habitación era su opuesto en todo sentido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This room...temporary as it was, had been one of the few things she'd achieved all on her own."
msgstr "Esta habitación... tan temporal como era, había sido una de las pocas cosas que ella había logrado por sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This seemed to bring Sarah back to herself."
msgstr "Esto pareció traer a Sarah de vuelta a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This seemed to cheer Samayra up, if only a bit."
msgstr "Esto pareció alegrar un poco a Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This seemed to restore some hapiness in her, a smile creeping on Samayra's face."
msgstr "Esto parecía restaurar algo de felicidad en ella, mientras una sonrisa se insinuaba en el rostro de Samayra."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "This seems fair."
msgstr "Esto parece justo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This ship was no longer the private sanctuary that it had been. Nick was only a few rooms away."
msgstr "Esta nave ya no era el santuario privado que había sido. Nick estaba solo a unas cuantas habitaciones de distancia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This side only she saw."
msgstr "Este lado solo lo veía ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This single moment, utterly perfect."
msgstr "Este instante único, absolutamente perfecto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This singular flower, Sarah realized, was not just remarkable."
msgstr "Esta singular flor, Sarah comprendió, no era solo extraordinaria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This small bay was a rare exception in an otherwise inhospitable land."
msgstr "Esta pequeña bahía era una excepción rara en una tierra de otro modo inhóspita."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This small home and her husband became her world."
msgstr "Esta pequeña casa y su esposo se convirtieron en su mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This small place was, as much as it existed, a place of safety in the mountains."
msgstr "Este pequeño lugar era, en la medida en que existía, un refugio seguro en las montañas."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This station lies close to the Mythran border with the jungles of Nephatim."
msgstr "Esta estación se encuentra cerca de la frontera mitrana con las selvas de Nephatim."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This stone..."
msgstr "Esta piedra..."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "This tent, it is like a sacred place to me. It has been a very long time, decades, since anyone was in here."
msgstr "Esta tienda, es como un lugar sagrado para mí. Ha pasado mucho tiempo, décadas, desde que alguien estuviera aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "This thing is humiliating! I can't keep wearing it, I won't!"
msgstr "¡Esto es humillante! No puedo seguir usándolo, ¡no lo haré!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This thing she feared and wished to grow."
msgstr "Esta cosa que temía y deseaba crecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time Caleb drank from the bottle, deeper and longer than Ephraim and Sarah had."
msgstr "Esta vez Caleb bebió de la botella, más profundo y por más tiempo que Ephraim y Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time Garret prepared the campfire."
msgstr "Esta vez, Garrett preparó la hoguera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time Sarah threw up her hands."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah levantó las manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time Sigmund awkwardly smiled."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sigmund sonrió torpemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time it was Kravel who spoke up."
msgstr "Esta vez fue Kravel quien habló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time it was Sarah's face that turned red."
msgstr "Esta vez fue la cara de Sarah la que se puso roja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time it was so clear that Sarah could not convince herself that it wasn't real."
msgstr "Esta vez era tan evidente que Sarah no podía convencerse de que no fuera real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time she could not care less if she'd be caught out by Lily for staring."
msgstr "Esta vez no le importaba en lo más mínimo que Lily la pillara mirando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time she makes an example out of them."
msgstr "Esta vez, hace de ellos un ejemplo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time she stared, but she wouldn't care if she was caught."
msgstr "Esta vez la miró, pero no le importaría si la pillaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "This time the threat is real."
msgstr "Esta vez la amenaza es real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Cassius poured the wine into her cup."
msgstr "Esta vez, Casio vertió el vino en su copa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Kravel interrupted."
msgstr "Esta vez, interrumpió Kravel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Lady Carolyn leaned forward."
msgstr "Esta vez, la Dama Carolyn se inclinó hacia adelante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Samayra couldn't help but laugh."
msgstr "Esta vez, Samayra no pudo evitar reír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Sarah clenched the bottle tighter to her chest. Adapting a stronger stance."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah apretó la botella con más fuerza contra su pecho. Adoptando una postura más firme."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Sarah could not help but listen."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah no pudo evitar escuchar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Sarah felt Samayra lean forward, kissing her instead."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah sintió que Samayra se inclinara hacia adelante y la besara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Sarah politely ate what had been offered."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah comió con educación lo que se le ofreció."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, Sarah rose from her seat."
msgstr "Esta vez, Sarah se levantó de su asiento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, both listen instantly, getting down on their knees at Captain Belmont's feet."
msgstr "Esta vez, ambos obedecen al instante, arrodillándose a los pies del capitán Belmont."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, he dropped."
msgstr "Esta vez, él cayó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, her face remained more stoic."
msgstr "Esta vez, su rostro permaneció más estoico."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, his blade swung closer."
msgstr "Esta vez, su espada se abalanzó más cerca."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "This time, however, I must confess, I have heard not so much as a whisper."
msgstr "Esta vez, sin embargo, debo confesar que no escuché ni siquiera un susurro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, instead of forcing her down, he simply released his grip and Sarah brought her mouth down herself."
msgstr "Esta vez, en lugar de forzarla a bajar, simplemente soltó su agarre y ella puso sus propios labios sobre los suyos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, it bounced off the magical barrier."
msgstr "Esta vez, rebotó contra la barrera mágica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, it was Lady Carolyn who spoke."
msgstr "Esta vez fue Lady Carolyn quien habló."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, more willingly than before, she parted her own lips and met his tongue with his."
msgstr "Esta vez, más dispuesta que antes, separó sus labios y se encontró su lengua con la suya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, no matter what sound or distraction, she kept her face down."
msgstr "Esta vez, sin importar ningún sonido o distracción, mantuvo la cabeza baja."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, not metal against stone, but soft satin, silencing each footstep."
msgstr "Esta vez, no metal contra piedra, sino suave satén, silenciando cada paso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, rather than dodge her slap, the goblin reached up and caught her wrist."
msgstr "Esta vez, en lugar de esquivar su bofetada, el goblión alcanzó hacia arriba y atrapó su muñeca."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, rather than reaching within, she began to focus on the outer lines of her body."
msgstr "Esta vez, en lugar de adentrarse, comenzó a centrarse en las líneas externas de su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, she begged him not for respite."
msgstr "Esta vez, no le pidió clemencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, she caught the thing's tail in time."
msgstr "Esta vez, logró atrapar la cola del ser a tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, she only kept her focus on her work, bobbing her head up and down his shaft to the rhythm of is groans."
msgstr "Esta vez, solo mantuvo su atención en su trabajo, moviendo la cabeza de arriba a abajo sobre su polla al ritmo de sus gemidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, she spoke the words more softly."
msgstr "Esta vez, pronunció las palabras con más suavidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, she was alone."
msgstr "Esta vez, estaba sola."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, the boredom of it was worse than any day before."
msgstr "Esta vez, el aburrimiento era peor que en cualquier otro día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, the officer did not tie her up."
msgstr "Esta vez, el oficial no la ató."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, the pains and twitches in their body were slightly deeper."
msgstr "Esta vez, los dolores y espasmos en su cuerpo fueron ligeramente más profundos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, their naked bodies brushed up against one another as they kissed."
msgstr "Esta vez, sus cuerpos desnudos se rozaron mientras se besaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, there was no hestitation."
msgstr "Esta vez, no hubo vacilación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, there was no pause, no mercy."
msgstr "Esta vez, no hubo pausa ni piedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This time, there was none of her previous resistance."
msgstr "Esta vez, no hubo ninguna de su anterior resistencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "This too is true, but are you familiar with the history of my nation?"
msgstr "Esto también es cierto, pero ¿conoces la historia de mi nación?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too was part of their marriage."
msgstr "Esto también formaba parte de su matrimonio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too was part of their youth. Their inexperience."
msgstr "Esto también formaba parte de su juventud. De su inexperiencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too was true."
msgstr "Esto también era cierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too would be part of wearing the crown, though to Sarah, it did not come easy."
msgstr "Esto también formaría parte de llevar la corona, aunque para Sarah no le resultó fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too, made her popular."
msgstr "Esto también la hizo popular."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too, she would do, to survive."
msgstr "Esto también lo haría, para sobrevivir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This too, she would endure."
msgstr "Esto también lo soportaría."

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This town is small. There aren't a lot of people."
msgstr "Este pueblo es pequeño. No hay mucha gente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This town was her last chance, and Alfred her only remaining option."
msgstr "Este pueblo era su última oportunidad y Alfred su única opción restante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This transformation had robbed him of the body of a man, but just the same, the mind of a man."
msgstr "Esta transformación le había privado del cuerpo de un hombre, pero también de la mente de uno."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This trip was one thing, but if you wanna be my deck hand, you're gonna have to learn how to work a ship proper."
msgstr "Este viaje es una cosa, pero si quieres ser mi marinero, tendrás que aprender a manejar un barco de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This unthinkable plan suddenly sounded so real. So possible."
msgstr "Este plan inconcebible sonaba de repente tan real. Tan posible."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "This very morning, in this very room!"
msgstr "¡Hoy mismo, en esta misma habitación!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This vile man...her husband..."
msgstr "Este hombre vil... su marido..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This vow seemed to calm Jaeid down."
msgstr "Este juramento pareció calmar a Jaeid."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This war cannot continue. The people will not bear it, nor will my brother."
msgstr "Esta guerra no puede continuar. El pueblo no la soportará, ni mi hermano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This war would end, one way or another."
msgstr "Esta guerra terminaría, de una forma u otra."

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "This war, it's been a great victory, and that will carry the day for some time, but the issues I raised in the meetings...those concerns have not changed."
msgstr "Esta guerra ha sido una gran victoria y eso nos dará tiempo por un buen periodo, pero las cuestiones que planteé en las reuniones... esas preocupaciones no han cambiado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was Garret, stripped of any shame or hesitation."
msgstr "Este era Garrett, despojado de toda vergüenza o vacilación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was Sarah's gamble, the only one she had."
msgstr "Esta era la apuesta de Sarah, la única que tenía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a battle in the war."
msgstr "Esto era una batalla en la guerra."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was a big deal for me."
msgstr "Para mí, esto era algo muy importante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a chance, she thought. A chance to save herself. So long as he liked her."
msgstr "Era una oportunidad, pensó. Una oportunidad para salvarse. Siempre y cuando él la quisiera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a city that existed because it willed to exist and needed to exist."
msgstr "Esta era una ciudad que existía porque lo quería y necesitaba existir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a dance more meant for one's wedding than for two women."
msgstr "Esto era una danza más propia de un matrimonio que de dos mujeres."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a dead world, inhabited by nobody."
msgstr "Este era un mundo muerto, habitado por nadie."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was a good idea."
msgstr "Era una buena idea."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a joy so abundant, it felt wrong not to share."
msgstr "Era una alegría tan abundante que sentía que era incorrecto no compartirla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a large warship, but in this place, everything felt small."
msgstr "Era un gran buque de guerra, pero en este lugar, todo parecía pequeño."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was a lot for me."
msgstr "Esto es demasiado para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a man she loved, whom it was easy to love. Kind, handsome and honest."
msgstr "Era un hombre que ella amaba, y era fácil de amar. Apuesto, bondadoso y sincero."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was a mistake you made once, and one that you will make never again."
msgstr "Esto fue un error que cometiste una vez, y uno que jamás volverás a cometer."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was a mistake! We didn't mean to-"
msgstr "¡Fue un error! No lo hicimos a propósito—"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a moment. It would come and it would go. But there was nothing here that could grow."
msgstr "Este fue un momento. Llegaría y se iría. Pero no había nada aquí que pudiera crecer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a new city. A new chance. She needed to make the most of it if she wanted to avoid sleeping on the streets like in Lethram."
msgstr "Esta era una nueva ciudad. Una nueva oportunidad. Necesitaba aprovecharla al máximo si quería evitar dormir en la calle como en Lethram."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a pain she had forgotten, one she was now happy to rediscover."
msgstr "Este era un dolor que había olvidado, uno del que ahora estaba feliz de redescubrir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a painful defeat."
msgstr "Esta fue una derrota dolorosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a real army."
msgstr "Esto era un ejército de verdad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a rude awakening from the bliss she had felt only just before."
msgstr "Este fue un despertar brusco del éxtasis que acababa de sentir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was a story that each of them wanted to be able to tell."
msgstr "Esta era una historia que cada uno de ellos quería poder contar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was always how it went with her, Sarah knew."
msgstr "Siempre fue así con ella, lo sabía Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This was always my favorite part of the castle."
msgstr "Siempre fue mi parte favorita del castillo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was an effective, not very costly, way of doing it."
msgstr "Esta era una forma efectiva, no muy costosa, de hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was an event that none of them would have missed, no matter what."
msgstr "Era un evento que ninguno de ellos habría perdido, por nada del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was closer to a bar fight, turned ugly."
msgstr "Esto se acercaba más a una pelea de bar, que había terminado mal."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was easier, she thought as she slid her hands up and down her master's cock."
msgstr "Esto era más fácil, pensó mientras deslizaba sus manos por la polla de su amo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was far from what she was used to, but given her circumstances, more than she had expected."
msgstr "Esto estaba lejos de lo a lo que estaba acostumbrada, pero dada su situación, más de lo que esperaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was her resistance, however small, to the constraining life of her duties and obligations."
msgstr "Esta era su resistencia, aunque fuera pequeña, a la vida restrictiva de sus deberes y obligaciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was her, Sarah realized. This was the real her. The version only one man would ever fully see."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was his other side, or perhaps his true side."
msgstr "Este era su otro lado, o quizás su verdadero lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was his punishment. This was what he had deserved for disobeying the captain. And wasn't it fair, Sarah thought?"
msgstr "Este era su castigo. Lo que había merecido por desobedecer al capitán. ¿No era justo?, pensó Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how all mercenaries lived. They risked their life for wealth, and then they were afforded the chance to spent it."
msgstr "Así vivían todos los mercenarios. Arriesgaban su vida por la riqueza y luego se les concedía la oportunidad de gastarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how an empire died. Violently."
msgstr "Así moría un imperio. Violentemente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how he used to take her, how only he could take her."
msgstr "Así era como él solía tomarla, cómo solo él podía tomarla."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how men got rid of their troubles, wasn't it?"
msgstr "Así es como los hombres se deshacían de sus problemas, ¿no era cierto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how the desert preyed on people."
msgstr "Así es como el desierto acechaba a la gente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how they believed it should be."
msgstr "Así creían que debía ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was how they spend most days since Sarah had entered into Belmont's service."
msgstr "Así es como pasan la mayoría de los días desde que Sarah entró al servicio de Belmont."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was it, she thought for a moment."
msgstr "Era esto, pensó por un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was it."
msgstr "Era esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was it. The day every girl dreamed of."
msgstr "Este era el momento. El día soñado por todas las chicas."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This was just a mistake...a...misunderstanding...I'm...I'm sorry..."
msgstr "Esto fue solo un error...un...malentendido...lo siento..."

msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "This was my home! My home before stupid orcs got lucky and captured me."
msgstr "¡Este era mi hogar! ¡Mi hogar antes de que los estúpidos orcos tuvieran suerte y me capturaran!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was no great romance, but Sarah realized, it was something she could live with."
msgstr "Esto no era un gran romance, pero Sarah se dio cuenta de que podía vivir con ello."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was no home."
msgstr "Esto no era un hogar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was not a land made for people."
msgstr "Esto no era una tierra hecha para la gente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was not supposed to happen. This couldn't be."
msgstr "Esto no estaba destinado a suceder. No podía ser así."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was not the first time a city had prospered for longer than usual, and so many still speculated on its inevitable defeat at the hands of man or orc."
msgstr "No fue la primera vez que una ciudad prosperó más de lo habitual, y muchos aún especulan sobre su derrota inevitable a manos del hombre o del orco."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was not the love between a husband and a wife she had always dreamed off."
msgstr "Esto no era el amor entre un esposo y una esposa que siempre había soñado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was not to say that their nations were allies, but they had managed to put their history of war to a rest."
msgstr "Esto no quiere decir que sus naciones fueran aliadas, pero habían logrado poner fin a su historia de guerras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was nothing like any of that."
msgstr "Esto no era nada como eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was one of the few prayers that Sarah permitted herself, praying that somehow, Atilla was kept safe despite the many odds that he was not."
msgstr "Esta era una de las pocas oraciones que Sarah se permitía, rezando para que, de algún modo, Atilla estuviera a salvo a pesar de todas las probabilidades de que no lo estuviera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was one of the smaller markets, more specialized in different kinds of food. Some of the other markets dealt in just about anything."
msgstr "Este era uno de los mercados más pequeños, especializado en diferentes tipos de alimentos. Algunos de los demás mercados vendían casi cualquier cosa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was one of the upsides to what her life had become, Sarah thought as the pleasure continued to grow."
msgstr "Esto era uno de los aspectos positivos a lo que su vida se había convertido, pensó Sarah mientras el placer seguía creciendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was one such night."
msgstr "Esta era una de esas noches."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was one was signficantly smaller than the one from Bagrad, but it confirmed to her that they could die."
msgstr "Esta era una señal significativamente más pequeña que la de Bagrad, pero le confirmó que podían morir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was only a farce, she told herself."
msgstr "Solo era una farsa, se dijo a sí misma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was only interrupted when Sarah felt something stabbing at her leg."
msgstr "Esto solo se interrumpió cuando Sarah sintió algo clavándose en su pierna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was only pretend."
msgstr "Esto era solo fingido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was part of what made Al'Gahaem into the trading hub that it was."
msgstr "Esto era parte de lo que convirtió a Al'Gahaem en el centro comercial y nodo logístico que era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was probably the first time in many years since there had been a proper reason to celebrate."
msgstr "Probablemente fuera la primera vez en muchos años que había una razón adecuada para celebrar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was reality. And in the real world, an axe from an orc was a lot more pressing than a goblin."
msgstr "Esta era la realidad. Y en el mundo real, un hacha de un orco era mucho más urgente que un goblin."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was short in skilled execution was made up in raw desire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was simply the nature of these people."
msgstr "Esta era simplemente la naturaleza de estas personas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was simply the rest of her life."
msgstr "Esto era simplemente el resto de su vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was so far from where she had grown up."
msgstr "Esto estaba tan lejos de donde había crecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was something different altogether."
msgstr "Esto era algo totalmente diferente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was something else. Beyond what anyone was prepared for, even the Mythrans."
msgstr "Esto era otra cosa. Algo más allá de lo que nadie estaba preparado para, ni siquiera los Mythrans."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was something he had done only once before."
msgstr "Esto era algo que él había hecho solo una vez antes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was something she was useful for..."
msgstr "Esto era para lo que ella era útil..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was still somewhat new to Sarah. Back in Rosanna, flirting with a member of the Royal family was not permitted."
msgstr "Esto seguía siendo algo relativamente nuevo para Sarah. En Rosanna, coquetear con un miembro de la familia real no estaba permitido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was strange, because nearly all things in the world had at least some resonance of magic, no matter how soft or little."
msgstr "Esto era extraño, porque casi todas las cosas en el mundo tenían al menos algún rastro de magia, sin importar cuán suave o poca fuera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the edge of the world. Far beyond where any life still thrived."
msgstr "Este era el borde del mundo. Lejos más allá de donde aún prosperaba cualquier vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the first battle, the first fight, that Sarah could actually lose, that meant anything."
msgstr "Esta fue la primera batalla, el primer combate, que Sarah pudiera realmente perder, algo que significara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the first time that she truly gave herself to him from her own volition."
msgstr "Esta fue la primera vez que se entregó a él de su propia voluntad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the gathering Gilead had told her about."
msgstr "Este era el reencuentro que Gilead le había contado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the heart of the city, the center of its economy. Ships arrived and departed to every corner of the world."
msgstr "Este era el corazón de la ciudad, el centro de su economía. Los barcos llegaban y partían hacia cada rincón del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the home of the council that governed the order, and who handed down their decrees and instructions."
msgstr "Aquí residía el consejo que gobernaba la orden y dictaba sus decretos e instrucciones."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the life she had been raised for, and as much as she disliked it, it had been imprinted on her."
msgstr "Esta era la vida para la que había sido criada, y aunque tanto la odiaba, se le había grabado en el alma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the man more responsible than any other for the downfall of her nation. For enslaving her people. Killing her brother..."
msgstr "Este era el hombre más responsable de la caída de su nación. Por esclavizar a su pueblo. Por matar a su hermano..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the man who controlled her fate. Whatever stories he might tell, the truth was that he held all the power."
msgstr "Este era el hombre que controlaba su destino. Por mucho que pudiera contar historias, la verdad es que él poseía todo el poder."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the moment where reason would come back to her. Where she would put her dress back on, run out, and convince herself she hated this."
msgstr "Este fue el momento en que la razón volvería a ella. El momento en que se pondría de nuevo su vestido, correría y se convencería a sí misma de que odiaba esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the moment."
msgstr "Este era el momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the other side of the man that had protected her. The loyalist side. The part of the man that had no problem with any of this."
msgstr "Este era el otro lado del hombre que la había protegido. El lado leal. La parte del hombre que no tenía ningún problema con todo esto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the path she had decided on, and she wouldn't allow her own emotions to drag her down. She had a destiny to meet."
msgstr "Este era el camino en el que había decidido, y no permitiría que sus propias emociones la arrastraran hacia abajo. Tenía un destino por cumplir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the peace that had settled on the lands between humans and orcs."
msgstr "Esta era la paz que había cobijado las tierras entre humanos y orcos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the real heart of Lethram, it’s world famous harbor."
msgstr "Este era el verdadero corazón de Lethram, su puerto mundialmente famoso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the real her, she realized. What she was meant to be."
msgstr "Esta era la verdadera ella, lo comprendió. Lo que estaba destinada a ser."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the room where Lady Carolyn had performed her odd ritual..."
msgstr "Esta era la sala donde Lady Carolyn había realizado su extraño ritual..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This was the state of your world, nearly a century after the fall of the old empire."
msgstr "Este era el estado de tu mundo, casi un siglo después de la caída del antiguo imperio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the surrender, the moment where the king invited the gods to kill him, should his heart be untrue."
msgstr "Esta era la rendición, el momento en que el rey invitaba a los dioses a matarlo si su corazón no era verdadero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the trade-off she made whenever she fantasized of him while touching herself."
msgstr "Esta era la contrapartida que ella hacía cada vez que se imaginaba con él mientras se masturbaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was the way of the orcs, even for a wife."
msgstr "Esto era la forma de los orcos, incluso para una esposa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was their routine. This was how he took her most nights."
msgstr "Esta era su rutina. Era así como él la tomaba en la mayoría de las noches."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was their strategy."
msgstr "Esta era su estrategia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was true, but still, his proposal struck Sarah as laughable."
msgstr "Era cierto, pero su propuesta seguía pareciendo ridícula a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what came after each battle. The mass funeral for all the soldiers too young to have made any name or fortune for themselves."
msgstr "Esto era lo que sucedía tras cada batalla. El funeral masivo para todos los soldados demasiado jóvenes para haber hecho algún nombre o fortuna por sí mismos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what had motivated the Mythrans to come all the way out here."
msgstr "Esto es lo que motivó a los Mythrans para venir tan lejos hasta aquí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what he had fought all his battles for, and he claimed his right with as little hestitation as a worker claimed his wage."
msgstr "Esto era por lo que había luchado en todas sus batallas, y reclamaba su derecho con tan poca vacilación como un trabajador reclama su salario."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what it felt like to walk the streets of a dead city. To walk streets and squares build to hosts tens-of-thousands, now emptied out."
msgstr "Así es como se sentía caminar por las calles de una ciudad muerta. Por calles y plazas construidas para acoger a decenas de miles de personas, ahora vacías."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what passed for an impressive building in this part of the world."
msgstr "Esto es lo que se consideraba un edificio impresionante en esta parte del mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what she could have, if she just stopped overthinking everything. Stopped worrying about what should be, or what others thought."
msgstr "Esto era lo que podía tener, si simplemente dejaba de sobrepensar todo. Dejaba de preocuparse por lo que debía ser o por lo que pensaban los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what she had wanted."
msgstr "Esto era lo que ella había deseado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what she needed. To draw him into her rhythm. Make him forget all the rules of proper combat."
msgstr "Esto era lo que necesitaba. Arrastrarlo a su ritmo. Hacerle olvidar todas las reglas del combate correcto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what she wanted."
msgstr "Esto es lo que ella deseaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was what the creature wanted from her. Her body."
msgstr "Esto es lo que la criatura quería de ella: su cuerpo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was where the main road split off into the Hinterlands, the far-removed backwater provinces of Rosanna."
msgstr "Aquí es donde la carretera principal se desviaba hacia las Tierras de los Fondos, las provincias remotas y atrasadas de Rosanna."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was where the new owners tried out their recent purchase."
msgstr "Aquí es donde los nuevos dueños probaban su reciente adquisición."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This was why the city gates of Lethram were build the way they were."
msgstr "Por eso las puertas de la ciudad de Lethram estaban construidas de esa manera."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This wasn't a battle anymore. They were looting, and each of them was feverishly trying to get the best piece for themselves."
msgstr "Ya no era una batalla. Estaban saqueando, y cada uno de ellos se afanaba febrilmente en conseguir el mejor botín para sí mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This wasn't any notion of sex that humans had."
msgstr "Esto no era ninguna noción del sexo que los humanos tenían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This wasn't her fight. That woman would have to make her own way through life, same as her."
msgstr "Esto no era su pelea. Esa mujer tendría que abrirse camino por la vida por sí misma, igual que ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This water is incredible."
msgstr "¡Esta agua es increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "This way child."
msgstr "Por aquí, niña."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This we can do. I will pledge to use my nation's industry to equip your armies."
msgstr "—Esto podemos hacerlo. Juro utilizar la industria de mi nación para equipar sus ejércitos."

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "This what you been after?"
msgstr "¿Esto es lo que has estado buscando?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This whole marriage might have been political for him, as it was for her, but he was still a man too."
msgstr "Este matrimonio entero podría haber sido político para él, como lo fue para ella, pero él era también un hombre."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This will allow them to be pulled across the sand."
msgstr "Esto permitirá que sean arrastrados por la arena."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "This will allow us to conduct the meeting with the proper discretion."
msgstr "Esto nos permitirá llevar a cabo la reunión con la debida discreción."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This will be what matters most on our advance."
msgstr "Esto será lo que más importará en nuestro avance."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This will be written at a later date."
msgstr "Esto será escrito en una fecha posterior."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This will get us across the bridge, and it will keep you all safe..."
msgstr "Esto nos llevará a través del puente y te mantendrá a ti y a todos los demás a salvo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This will help each of us when the Mythrans attack."
msgstr "Esto nos ayudará a todos cuando los Mythrans lancen su ataque."

msgctxt "speaker:Old Tribesman"
msgid "This will make them believe that you are yielding to me, and not the other way around."
msgstr "Esto les hará creer que te rindes a mí, y no al revés."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "This will mean it will weigh heavier on your heart than it will on those foolish rulers who spend lives without thought."
msgstr "Esto significará que pesará más en tu corazón que en aquellos gobernantes tontos que pasan la vida sin pensar."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This wine...it's incredible."
msgstr "Este vino... ¡es increíble!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This woman had attacked them, admitted it even. The soldiers would lose respect for her if she let her get away with it."
msgstr "Esta mujer los había atacado, incluso lo admitía. Los soldados perderían el respeto por ella si se la dejaban salir con eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This woman, unlike the others, was not so desperate."
msgstr "Esta mujer, a diferencia de las demás, no estaba tan desesperada."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "This word in particular belongs to the world of Laitha."
msgstr "Esta palabra en particular pertenece al mundo de Laitha."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This world appears to me very different than it does to you."
msgstr "Este mundo me parece muy diferente al que tú ves."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This world had been cruel to her, so what obligation did she owe to it?"
msgstr "Este mundo había sido cruel con ella, ¿qué obligación le debía entonces?"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This world is filled to the brim with worthless people. Best we can do is try and look out for the handful of people that matter."
msgstr "Este mundo está lleno hasta el tope de personas sin valor. Lo mejor que podemos hacer es intentar cuidar de la pequeña cantidad de personas que importan."

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "This world needs a steady hand, but that hand must also be gentle."
msgstr "Este mundo necesita una mano firme, pero esa mano también debe ser suave."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This world was absent any beauty."
msgstr "Este mundo carecía de belleza."

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "This world...it can be very cruel to a girl, all alone."
msgstr "Este mundo... puede ser muy cruel para una niña, sola."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This world...it doesn't suffer fools or weaklings..."
msgstr "Este mundo... no tolera a los tontos ni a los débiles..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This would have to do as a base."
msgstr "Esto bastaría como base."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This would mean she wouldn't have to keep paying the room at the Inn."
msgstr "Esto significaría que no tendría que seguir pagando la habitación en el posada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This would pass, and so she would bear it."
msgstr "Esto pasaría, y así lo soportaría."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This wouldn't be a thing anymore..."
msgstr "Esto ya no sería algo más..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, Sarah realized even as the tears flowed, was the truth of her life now."
msgstr "Esto, Sarah lo comprendió incluso mientras las lágrimas corrían, era la verdad de su vida ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "This, as you so kindly called her, is Sarah."
msgstr "Esta es la que tan amablemente llamaste: Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, even if it was with him, she did want to explore further."
msgstr "Esto, aunque fuera con él, aún quería explorar más."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, for a while, became their routine."
msgstr "Esto, durante un tiempo, se convirtió en su rutina."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This, it's further out even than those places."
msgstr "Esto está aún más lejos que esos lugares."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, she could do..."
msgstr "Esto, podía hacerlo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, was never even remotely on the list."
msgstr "Esto nunca estuvo ni remotamente en la lista."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This, what he was doing, was a kindness she now realized."
msgstr "Esto, lo que él hacía, era un acto de bondad que ahora comprendía."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This, what we have, it's the only thing that matters, that really matters to me."
msgstr "Esto, lo que tenemos, es lo único que importa, lo que realmente importa para mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This. This was her path back to Lethram. Back to the world."
msgstr "Esto. Este era su camino de regreso a Lethram. De vuelta al mundo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This. This was something different for them."
msgstr "Esto. Esto era algo diferente para ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This..."
msgstr "Esto..."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This..."
msgstr "Esto..."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "This...I don't know what I was thinking."
msgstr "Esto... no sé qué estaba pensando."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "This...is The Den."
msgstr "Esto... es El Refugio."

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "This...is so."
msgstr "Esto... es así."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This...it's a lot for me..."
msgstr "Esto... es demasiado para mí..."

msgctxt "speaker:Voidling"
msgid "This...pain..."
msgstr "Este... dolor..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This...this alley...these men...her body...this was real."
msgstr "Este... este callejón... estos hombres... su cuerpo... esto era real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This...this had been but a brief intermission, she thought with sad heart."
msgstr "Esto... esto había sido solo un breve intermedio, pensó con el corazón triste."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This...this is my cell..."
msgstr "Esta... esta es mi celda..."

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This...this is my house! I own it!"
msgstr "¡Esto... esto es mi casa! ¡La poseo!"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This...this is my house, boy!"
msgstr "¡Esto... esto es mi casa, muchacho!"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This...this was the least bad of a series of bad options."
msgstr "Esta... esta era la opción menos mala de una serie de opciones malas."

msgctxt "speaker:Merchant"
msgid "This...this will ruin me! I don't have that kind of money, I can't-"
msgstr "¡Esto... esto me arruinará! No tengo ese tipo de dinero, no puedo—"

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "This...unfortunate mistake..."
msgstr "Este... desafortunado error..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This...was this really how it would end..."
msgstr "¿Esto... esto era realmente cómo terminaría todo..."

msgctxt "speaker:Old Tribesman"
msgid "This...we can work out."
msgstr "Esto... lo podemos resolver."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "This...we've never had to deal with something like this before. I can predict what is predictable, but this is outside of anything we've ever seen."
msgstr "Esto... nunca hemos tenido que lidiar con algo así antes. Puedo predecir lo predecible, pero esto está fuera de todo lo que jamás hemos visto."

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "This?"
msgstr "¿Esto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "This?"
msgstr "¿Esto?"

msgctxt "speaker-name"
msgid "Thomas"
msgstr "Tomás"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas Rose, Sarah's younger brother, and heir to the throne, embraces his father."
msgstr "Thomas Rose, el hermano menor de Sarah y heredero del trono, abraza a su padre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas asserted himself again."
msgstr "Thomas se reafirmó de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas became more like the young boy she had known her brother to be. Distant, lost in books, detached."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas began to walk."
msgstr "Thomas comenzó a caminar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas broadened his shoulders."
msgstr "Thomas ensanchó los hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas broke into laughter."
msgstr "Thomas estalló en carcajadas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas came nearer."
msgstr "Thomas se acercó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas casually drops the tome back on the desk."
msgstr "Thomas deja el tomo sobre el escritorio con casualidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas chortled."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas chuckled."
msgstr "Thomas soltó una carcajada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas cleared his throat and began to speak more forcefully."
msgstr "Thomas se aclaró la garganta y comenzó a hablar con más fuerza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas considered what he was hearing."
msgstr "Thomas consideró lo que estaba escuchando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas continued."
msgstr "Continuó Thomas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas did not even protest, he simply turned around and left for his chambers."
msgstr "Thomas ni siquiera protestó; simplemente dio la vuelta y se marchó hacia su camarote."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas didn't have a religious bone in his body, but her oath still seemed to make him happy."
msgstr "Thomas no tenía ni un hueso religioso en el cuerpo, pero su juramento aún parecía hacerlo feliz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas drags himself from the bed."
msgstr "Thomas se arrastra fuera de la cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas embraces his sister."
msgstr "Thomas abraza a su hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas entered the room, softly opening and closing the door, as if he was entering hallowed ground."
msgstr "Thomas entró en la habitación, abriendo y cerrando suavemente la puerta, como si estuviera pisando un lugar sagrado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas eyed her, his deep blue eyes that could never tell a proper lie."
msgstr "Thomas la miró, con sus profundos ojos azules que nunca podían decir una mentira adecuada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas frowned."
msgstr "Thomas frunció el ceño."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas gave a drunkard's nod."
msgstr "Thomas asintió con la cabeza de un borracho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas gave his sister a soft punch on her arm, hoping to get her to lighten up."
msgstr "Thomas le dio un suave puñetazo en el brazo a su hermana, esperando que se relajara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas gestured."
msgstr "Thomas hizo un gesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas grunts, acknowledging he's awake but hoping to be spared the day's official events."
msgstr "Thomas gruñe, reconociendo que está despierto pero esperando ser eximido de los eventos oficiales del día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas had set out earlier in the day with Marion and an entourage to go stag hunting in the royal forest."
msgstr "Thomas había salido más temprano ese día con Marion y una comitiva para ir a cazar ciervos en el bosque real."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas had stopped listening, distracted by a plate of food being carried past him."
msgstr "Thomas dejó de escuchar, distraído por un plato de comida que lo pasaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas is..."
msgstr "Thomas es..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas jolted, quickly sitting upright, before realizing it was his sister."
msgstr "Thomas se sobresaltó, sentándose rápidamente antes de darse cuenta de que era su hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas laughed again."
msgstr "Thomas rió de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas laughed."
msgstr "Thomas rió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas leaned forward."
msgstr "Thomas se inclinó hacia adelante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas leaned in."
msgstr "Thomas se inclinó hacia adelante."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas leaned to Sarah again."
msgstr "Thomas se inclinó hacia Sarah de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas listened intently, nodding along."
msgstr "Thomas escuchó atentamente, asintiendo con la cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked about the table."
msgstr "Thomas miró alrededor de la mesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked at Sarah, he seemed utterly wracked and exhausted."
msgstr "Thomas miró a Sarah; parecía completamente abatido y agotado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked at Sarah."
msgstr "Thomas miró a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked at her with gratitude, thanking her with his eyes."
msgstr "Thomas la miró con gratitud, agradeciéndole con sus ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked at her with sheer exhaustion in his eyes."
msgstr "Thomas la miró con una pura fatiga en los ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked away and contemplated his sister's advice. After some time, he responded."
msgstr "Thomas apartó la mirada y reflexionó sobre el consejo de su hermana. Tras un tiempo, respondió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked down and sat in a chair in the corner."
msgstr "Thomas miró hacia abajo y se sentó en una silla en la esquina."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked up, a pained expression in his eyes."
msgstr "Thomas levantó la mirada, con una expresión de dolor en sus ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looked up, startled."
msgstr "Thomas miró hacia arriba, sorprendido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas looks at the bed."
msgstr "Thomas mira la cama."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas motioned for the guards to move forward. They seized the man, who offered up no struggle, even as they forced him to his knees."
msgstr "Thomas hizo señas a los guardias para que avanzaran. Aseguraron al hombre, quien no ofreció resistencia alguna, incluso cuando lo obligaron a ponerse de rodillas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas motioned for the man to stand up."
msgstr "Thomas indicó al hombre que se levantara."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nervously cleared his throat."
msgstr "Thomas limpió la garganta con ansiedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas never had that talent. Even her Father did not try to deny that."
msgstr "Thomas nunca tuvo ese talento. Ni siquiera su padre intentó negarlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded again."
msgstr "Thomas asintió de nuevo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded as Marion explained it."
msgstr "Thomas asintió mientras Marion lo explicaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded as he kept transfixed on the table."
msgstr "Thomas asintió mientras mantenía la mirada clavada en la mesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded at Sarah and turned back to the council."
msgstr "Thomas asintió a Sarah y volvió la atención al consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded, but still seemed to stare into the distance."
msgstr "Thomas asintió, pero seguía mirando al vacío."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded, but the words didn't seem to affect him much."
msgstr "Thomas asintió, pero las palabras no parecían afectarlo mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded, hugging her back."
msgstr "Thomas asintió, abrazándola a ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded, understanding what his sister was getting at."
msgstr "Thomas asintió, entendiendo lo que su hermana quería decir."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas nodded."
msgstr "Thomas asintió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas paused for a moment."
msgstr "Thomas se detuvo un momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas paused."
msgstr "Thomas se detuvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas performed his own clumsy bow."
msgstr "Thomas realizó su propio saludo torpe."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas put his head in his hands."
msgstr "Thomas se enterró la cabeza entre las manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas raised a chalice."
msgstr "Thomas levantó un cáliz."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas rolled his eyes."
msgstr "Thomas rodó los ojos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas rolls his eyes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas rose up from his seat, and an attendant stomped hard on the floor three times, bringing the room to a silence."
msgstr "Thomas se levantó de su asiento y un asistente pisoteó el suelo con fuerza tres veces, imponiendo silencio a la sala."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas rose up from his throne."
msgstr "Thomas se levantó de su trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas rubbed his temples."
msgstr "Thomas se frotó las sienes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sat not in his chair, but balanced on the edge of the table."
msgstr "Thomas no se sentaba en su silla, sino que estaba equilibrado sobre el borde de la mesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sat up."
msgstr "Thomas se sentó erguido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seemed excited to cross another item off the list."
msgstr "Thomas parecía emocionado por tachar otro ítem de la lista."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seemed relieved."
msgstr "Thomas parecía aliviado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seemed to grow more at ease in his role."
msgstr "Thomas parecía ir ganando mayor comodidad en su papel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seemed to sink back into his seat, his shoulders sagging."
msgstr "Thomas pareció hundirse de nuevo en su asiento, con los hombros caídos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seemed uncomfortable at being so directly confronted. Sarah decided to intercede on her brother's behalf."
msgstr "Thomas pareció sentirse incómodo al ser confrontado tan directamente. Sarah decidió intervenir en favor de su hermano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas seized the moment and leapt forward, rushing across the room."
msgstr "Thomas aprovechó el momento y saltó hacia adelante, cruzando la habitación de un salto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas shook his head."
msgstr "Thomas negó con la cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas showed a pained smile."
msgstr "Thomas mostró una sonrisa de dolor."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas shrugged."
msgstr "Thomas encogió los hombros."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas shuffled through his papers for a while, trying to find what he was looking for."
msgstr "Thomas hojeó entre sus papeles durante un rato, intentando encontrar lo que buscaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sighed and nodded."
msgstr "Thomas suspiró y asintió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sighed."
msgstr "Thomas suspiró."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas simply squeezed her hands, and repeated himself."
msgstr "Thomas simplemente apretó sus manos y repitió las mismas palabras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas slammed the table."
msgstr "Thomas golpeó la mesa."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas smiled as she spoke."
msgstr "Thomas sonrió mientras ella hablaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas smiled, comforted by the gesture."
msgstr "Thomas sonrió, reconfortado por el gesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas smiled."
msgstr "Thomas sonrió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas smiled. It was the first time Sarah had seen a genuine smile from him since their father had passed."
msgstr "Thomas sonrió. Era la primera vez que Sarah veía una sonrisa genuina de él desde que su padre había fallecido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sounded exasperated."
msgstr "Thomas sonaba exasperado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas stared past her, vacantly. He softly shook his head."
msgstr "Thomas la miró de reojo, con el vacío en los ojos. Luego negó suavemente con la cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas stood up and turned to face Sarah."
msgstr "Thomas se puso de pie y giró para enfrentar a Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas stood up, as instructed."
msgstr "Thomas se levantó, como le habían indicado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas stood up."
msgstr "Thomas se levantó."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas storms off, angrily muttering to himself."
msgstr "Thomas se retira furioso, murmurando consigo mismo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas strolled into the great hall, stopping next to his sister."
msgstr "Thomas paseó por el gran salón y se detuvo junto a su hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas suddenly sat up."
msgstr "Thomas se sentó de golpe."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas sudenly looks up, a shocked expression on his face."
msgstr "Thomas levanta la mirada de golpe, con una expresión de asombro en el rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas threw up one hand."
msgstr "Thomas levantó una mano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turned for a short moment, looking at his sister. She saw him give her a small nod, acknowledging her."
msgstr "Thomas giró brevemente la mirada hacia su hermana. Ella lo vio asentirle con un pequeño gesto, reconociéndola."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turned to his sister."
msgstr "Thomas se volvió hacia su hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turned to the spymaster."
msgstr "Thomas se volvió hacia la espiadora."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turns around before leaving."
msgstr "Thomas se da la vuelta antes de irse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turns away from her, staring off into the distance, trying to look at nothing at all."
msgstr "Thomas se aparta de ella, mirando al vacío, intentando no ver nada en absoluto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas turns to Sarah."
msgstr "Thomas se vuelve hacia Sarah."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas waived his hand to one side."
msgstr "Thomas movió su mano hacia un lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas waived his hand to the other side."
msgstr "Thomas levantó la mano hacia el otro lado."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas waived his hands."
msgstr "Thomas movió las manos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas walks over to Sarah's desk and picks up the book."
msgstr "Thomas se acerca al escritorio de Sarah y recoge el libro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas was looking down now, seemingly nervous."
msgstr "Ahora miraba hacia abajo, parecía nervioso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas was now leaning in, wanting to know more."
msgstr "Ahora se inclinaba hacia adelante, deseando saber más."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas was perfect from the day I first held him."
msgstr "Thomas fue perfecto desde el día en que lo agarré por primera vez."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas was sitting back in this throne, waiving at Sarah excitedly as she approached."
msgstr "Thomas se recostaba en ese trono, saludando a Sarah con entusiasmo mientras ella se acercaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas was the first to break that silence."
msgstr "Thomas fue el primero en romper ese silencio."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas wasn't wrong. These books are very dry."
msgstr "Thomas no estaba equivocado. Estos libros son muy secos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas waved his hand."
msgstr "Thomas levantó la mano."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas waved to the people, the heavy crown sitting akwardly atop his head."
msgstr "Thomas saludó a la gente, con la pesada corona sentándose incómoda sobre su cabeza."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas will be King after you...why should I learn any of this?"
msgstr "Thomas será rey después de ti... ¿por qué debería aprender todo esto?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas winks at his sister."
msgstr "Thomas parpadea a su hermana."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas! My brother! Your king! They've abandoned any sense of honour or decency, for what!?"
msgstr "¡Tomás! ¡Mi hermano! ¡Tu rey! ¡Han abandonado cualquier sentido del honor o la decencia, ¿por qué!?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas' voice shot up, catching the attention of some of the guests, before he quickly lowered his voice."
msgstr "La voz de Thomas subió de tono, captando la atención de algunos invitados, antes de bajarla rápidamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas' voice turned into a whimper."
msgstr "La voz de Thomas se convirtió en un gemido."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas' voiced boomed out over everyone else."
msgstr "La voz de Thomas resonó sobre todos los demás."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas, I need to take a moment, please carry on without me."
msgstr "Thomas, necesito un momento, por favor continúa sin mí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas, acting as if drunk, threw his arms around both Marion and Varga, pulling them closer."
msgstr "Thomas, actuando como si estuviera borracho, lanzó sus brazos alrededor de Marion y Varga, arrastrándolos hacia sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas, did you manage to get any sleep last night?"
msgstr "Thomas, ¿lograste dormir un poco anoche?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas, for his part, sat comfortably on the throne."
msgstr "Por su parte, Thomas se sentó cómodamente en el trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas, for his part, sat uncomfortably on the throne."
msgstr "Thomas, por su parte, se sentó incómodamente en el trono."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas, how are you keeping up?"
msgstr "Thomas, ¿cómo logras mantener el ritmo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas, now more than ever, you need to be strong. Imagining the worst will do nobody any good."
msgstr "Thomas, ahora más que nunca, necesitas ser fuerte. Imaginar lo peor no sirve de nada a nadie."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas, on the other hand, had turned inwards. He had grown more somber, and she had found him on some nights, walking through the dark unlit castle halls."
msgstr "Thomas, por otro lado, se había vuelto hacia adentro. Había crecido más sombrío, y ella lo había encontrado algunas noches caminando por los oscuros pasillos del castillo sin luz."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas, when did I ever let you carry your burdens alone?"
msgstr "Thomas, ¿cuándo te dejé que llevaras tus cargas solo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas, with little struggle, surrendered. He waved his sister goodbye and went down the hallway to his bedroom."
msgstr "Thomas, con poca resistencia, se rindió. Se despidió de su hermana y bajó al dormitorio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas."
msgstr "Tomás."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Thomas. He lived."
msgstr "Thomas. Vivió."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas. I gave him my word he would be safe."
msgstr "Thomas. Le di mi palabra de que estaría a salvo."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...even for me it is not so easy."
msgstr "Thomas... incluso para mí no es tan fácil."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...he...was afraid?"
msgstr "Thomas... ¿él... tenía miedo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thomas...what...what are they going to do?"
msgstr "Thomas... ¿qué... qué van a hacer?"

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Those Medini have always valued coin over integrity. If the price is right, he'd probably sell them his mother."
msgstr "Esos medinianos siempre han valorado la moneda por encima de la integridad. Si el precio es adecuado, probablemente vendería a su madre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those Rosannan men who had previously dared the occasional encounter, voluntary or otherwise, had now grown fearful."
msgstr "Aquellos hombres rosanan que antes habían permitido encuentros ocasionales, voluntarios o no, ahora habían cobrado miedo."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Those are elders, but don't feel too intimidated by them."
msgstr "Son ancianos, pero no te sientas intimidada por ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Those are herbivores, won't harm a fly. And they're none too bright, so not very dangerous at all."
msgstr "Son herbívoros, no dañarán a una mosca. Además, no son muy inteligentes, por lo que no representan ninguna amenaza real."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are my breasts!"
msgstr "¡Esos son mis pechos!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are not...they are barely undergarments, let alone clothes!"
msgstr "¡No pueden ser... apenas son prendas íntimas, ¡no ropa!"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those are the armies of the Tribes. Khan Hassar's armies."
msgstr "Eso son los ejércitos de las tribus. Los ejércitos del Kan Hassar."

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Those are the best days to drink."
msgstr "Son los mejores días para beber."

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "Those are the rumors, my lord. We do not yet have enough evidence to suggest that he has truly united them."
msgstr "Eso son rumores, mi señor. Aún no tenemos suficientes pruebas para sugerir que realmente los haya unificado."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those are the three deaths...the killings."
msgstr "Esos son los tres muertos... los asesinatos."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those are the three sisters."
msgstr "Aquí están las tres hermanas."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Those are transit papers, covering all the required documentation to get you and your soldiers to Mythra."
msgstr "Son documentos de tránsito que cubren toda la documentación necesaria para llevarte y a tus soldados hasta Mythra."

msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "Those are typical black, but those others turn a dark purple after a few days."
msgstr "Pero esas otras se tornan de un púrpura oscuro después de unos días."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those around her, until now acceptable, suddenly seemed amateur by comparison."
msgstr "Las que la rodeaban, hasta ahora aceptables, de repente parecían amateur en comparación."

msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Those bars are as solid as the stones here. Which is saying a lot."
msgstr "Esas barras son tan sólidas como las piedras de aquí. Lo cual dice mucho."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those brave enough to try would settle. Prosper. And like a pig grown fat, slaughtered and eaten by a rival."
msgstr "Los que tengan la valentía de intentarlo se establecerán, prosperarán y, como una cerda engordada hasta el punto de ser sacrificada y devorada por un rival,"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those days were long gone, and only the desert remained."
msgstr "Esos días se habían ido para siempre, y solo quedaba el desierto."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those desires that she knew she could control."
msgstr "Esos deseos que sabía que podía controlar."

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Those excercises are just to prepare your body for where it needs to be. A strong body is no replacement for the fundamentals of weapon training."
msgstr "Ese tipo de ejercicios solo sirven para preparar tu cuerpo para lo que realmente necesita ser. Un cuerpo fuerte no sustituye los fundamentos del entrenamiento con armas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those families that didn't flee, or failed to, quickly learned that the Tribesmen culture had no understanding of nobility or titles."
msgstr "Esas familias que no huyeron o fallaron en ello aprendieron rápidamente que la cultura de los tribales no comprendía la nobleza ni los títulos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few that dared to quickly glance at their savior."
msgstr "Aquellos pocos que se atrevieron a echar un rápido vistazo a su salvador."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few that remained were mostly there to hurl a last few insults at the official, before they also left."
msgstr "Los pocos que se quedaron estaban allí principalmente para lanzar unas cuantas últimas ofensas al oficial antes de también marcharse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those few who ran on foot were mostly caught by arrows."
msgstr "Aquellos pocos que huyeron a pie fueron atrapados mayormente por flechas."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those forests are old, but they also run deep."
msgstr "Esas selvas son antiguas, pero también profundas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those fortunate were enslaved by humans. Those less fortunate by the orcs."
msgstr "Los afortunados fueron esclavizados por humanos; los menos afortunados, por orcos."

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Those gardens don't put you off?"
msgstr "¿Esos jardines no te desalientan?"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Those gifted with such divine purpose, find the world often bending to their own will. Their own purpose."
msgstr "Aquellos dotados de tal propósito divino descubren que el mundo se dobla a menudo ante su propia voluntad. Su propio propósito."

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Those girls you've brought along, he's been winning some officers over by giving them away."
msgstr "Esas muchachas que has traído consigo, ¿le ha estado ganando a algunos oficiales regalándolas?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those girls, they're gossiping."
msgstr "Esas chicas están chismoseando."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those halls...my room...the throne...seeing my father and..."
msgstr "Esos pasillos... mi habitación... el trono... ver a mi padre y..."

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Those have been the most poorly maintained, plus, that's where their supply room is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Those highborn idiots couldn't see a trap coming if it was spelled out for them!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those impossibly beautiful eyes."
msgstr "Esos ojos de una belleza imposible."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those invited seemed confused, looking around for decorations that weren't there."
msgstr "Los invitados parecían confundidos, mirando a su alrededor en busca de decoraciones que no estaban."

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Those jungles are full of nasty spores, goblins love to grow their mushrooms there, vile things."
msgstr "Esas selvas están llenas de esporas nocivas; los goblins aman cultivar sus hongos allí, malditas cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Those male slaves chose their lives and safety over their duty to their land and their people."
msgstr "Esos esclavos varones eligieron sus vidas y su seguridad por encima de su deber hacia su tierra y su pueblo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those most at home to the city conceived of the structure as though it was a beggar in the streets. Consciously noticed, consciously ignored."
msgstr "Los más acostumbrados a la ciudad concibieron la estructura como si fuera un mendigo en las calles. Conscientemente notado, conscientemente ignorado."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Those most essential to their designs are souls of a greater size, and the greater soul dominates the lesser soul."
msgstr "Los más esenciales para sus diseños son almas de mayor tamaño, y la alma mayor domina a la menor."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those of you who cannot bear my command, I give you my word as a princess of the Rose family, that no harm will come to you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Those of you who had the privilege of truly knowing my father, knew how much he enjoyed the winter grace festival."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those parts of her that she had been raised to give to her husband in marriage, now she gave to this old man."
msgstr "Aquellas partes de ella a las que había sido educada para entregar a su esposo en el matrimonio, ahora se las entregaba a ese viejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those ravenous eyes that told so much of what they wanted to do to her."
msgstr "Esas hambrientas miradas que revelaban tanto de lo que deseaban hacerle."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those roads actually still get patrolled. Quite heavily, actually."
msgstr "Esos caminos siguen siendo patrullados, de hecho con mucha frecuencia."

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "Those speaking of your beauty, of course."
msgstr "Aquellos que hablan de tu belleza, por supuesto."

msgctxt "speaker:Cassius"
msgid "Those students who show significant talent in the martial skills are selected from among the others."
msgstr "De entre los demás se seleccionan a aquellos estudiantes que demuestran un talento significativo en las habilidades marciales."

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Those that could read, of course."
msgstr "Por supuesto, aquellos que podían leer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had failed to survive the magical infusion, she threw away."
msgstr "Aquellos que no habían sobrevivido a la infusión mágica, los tiró al basurero."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had not charged into the spearmen, had slowed down too much to perform another charge."
msgstr "Aquellos que no habían cargado contra los piqueros se habían ralentizado demasiado para realizar otra carga."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that had survived sat quietly, simply staring into the distance."
msgstr "Los que habían sobrevivido se sentaron en silencio, simplemente mirando al horizonte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that remained all eyed one another."
msgstr "Los que permanecían se miraban entre sí."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those that tried to run were swiftly burned as well."
msgstr "Los que intentaron huir también fueron quemados rápidamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those things she admired deeply."
msgstr "Aquellas cosas que admiraba profundamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those times when she had allowed Lady Carolyn to go too far with her."
msgstr "Aquellos momentos en los que permitió a Lady Carolyn ir demasiado lejos con ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Those two sons-of-bitches would not have thought twice about dragging you into the forest and raping you."
msgstr "Esos dos hijos de perra no habrían dudado ni un segundo en arrastrarte al bosque y violarte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those waiting rushed in, those done dancing, rushed out. A frenzied melee."
msgstr "Los que esperaban se precipitaron a entrar, los que acababan de bailar, salieron corriendo. Un alboroto frenético."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were a far cry from the kind of legal paperwork that Sarah struggled through."
msgstr "Eso estaba muy lejos de los trámites legales por los que Sarah luchaba."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were familiar to her."
msgstr "Eran familiares para ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were stories from every corner of the world, and she had often dreamed what they might look like."
msgstr "Eran historias de cada rincón del mundo, y a menudo había soñado con cómo podrían verse."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were the rules everyone lived by, the very rules he knew when he signed the contract."
msgstr "Aquellas eran las reglas por las que todos vivían, las mismas reglas que él conocía cuando firmó el contrato."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those were the types of terrains that the Tribesmen liked to fight on. Open, spread out."
msgstr "Eran los tipos de terreno que a los tribales les gustaba pelear: abierto y despejado."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Those who are loyal, are punished."
msgstr "Los leales son castigados."

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "Those who can walk outside the ordained paths of history."
msgstr "Aquellos que podían caminar fuera de los caminos ordenados por la historia."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who dared to say anything of the sun, the heat, were met only by angry glares."
msgstr "Aquellos que se atrevían a decir algo sobre el sol o el calor eran recibidos únicamente con miradas de odio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who fell into its claws were dismissively called Dreamers, for they would stare off into nothingness, disconnected from everything and anyone around them."
msgstr "Aquellos que cayeron en sus garras fueron despectivamente llamados Soñadores, pues miraban al vacío, desconectados de todo y de todos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who gathered knowledge for the sake of it."
msgstr "Los que reunían conocimiento por el simple hecho de hacerlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had been near the docks were lucky."
msgstr "Los que habían estado cerca de los muelles tuvieron suerte."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had been present in the throne room had managed to turn the story of her killing the beast into a tale larger than life."
msgstr "Aquellos que estuvieron presentes en la sala del trono lograron convertir el relato de su matanza de la bestia en una historia más grande que la vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had managed to escape the Tribes, had found their homes gone."
msgstr "Aquellos que habían logrado escapar a las Tribus, habían encontrado sus hogares desaparecidos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who had the hints of fertility were soon to follow."
msgstr "Aquellos que mostraban signos de fertilidad pronto los seguirían."

msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Those who keep their heads down, are left alone."
msgstr "Quienes mantienen la cabeza baja, quedan solos."

msgctxt "speaker:Voice"
msgid "Those who shape the world, rather than be shaped by it."
msgstr "Los que dan forma al mundo, en lugar de ser moldeados por él."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those who would come upon her could only marvel at her beauty and the rapture of this moment."
msgstr "Quienes pudieran acercarse a ella solo podían maravillarse ante su belleza y el éxtasis de este momento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Those with the strongest claims fought those who they imagined their most distinct rivals, those with other strong claims."
msgstr "Los que tenían las pretensiones más sólidas lucharon contra aquellos a quienes imaginaban sus rivales más distintivos, los que poseían otras pretensiones igualmente fuertes."

msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Those women are gonna eat you alive."
msgstr "Esas mujeres te comerán viva."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Those years ago. On the ship."
msgstr "Años atrás, en el barco."

msgctxt "speaker:Female Soldier"
msgid "Those? Do you even know how to play the game?"
msgstr "¿Esas? ¿Sabes siquiera jugar al juego?"

msgctxt "speaker:Male Soldier"
msgid "Those? Do you even know how to play the game?"
msgstr "¿Esos? ¿Sabes siquiera jugar al juego?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Gideon needed little encouragement, Sarah felt he still took it in stride, going faster and deeper with each thrust."
msgstr "Aunque Gideon necesitaba poco aliento, Sarah sentía que lo aceptaba con naturalidad, acelerando y profundizando con cada embestida."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Though I must admit I have received only the invitation, and know little of the topic of the council."
msgstr "Aunque debo admitir que solo he recibido la invitación y poco sé del tema del consejo."

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Though I must admit, until not so long ago, I was made to understand that you were one of the tragic casualties of the Tribes."
msgstr "Aunque debo admitirlo, hasta hace muy poco me hacían entender que eras una de las trágicas víctimas de las Tribus."

msgctxt "speaker:Founder"
msgid "Though I must admit, you are the first of your lineage to express any magical potency."
msgstr "Aunque debo admitirlo, eres la primera de tu linaje en manifestar cualquier potencia mágica."

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Though I must say I enjoyed our conversation."
msgstr "Aunque debo decir que disfruté nuestra conversación."

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Though I think this means there won't be any future offspring for the royal family of Bagrad."
msgstr "Aunque creo que esto significa que no habrá descendencia futura para la familia real de Bagrad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah could still hear the sounds of the camp around her, there was some degree of privacy here."
msgstr "Aunque Sarah aún podía oír los sonidos del campamento a su alrededor, aquí había cierto grado de privacidad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah had no doubts that if she had failed to produce a letter, his response would have been a great deal less friendly."
msgstr "Aunque Sarah no tenía dudas de que si hubiera fallado en producir una carta, su respuesta habría sido mucho menos amable."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah still had no clothes on, she found it easier to forget her shame when she was busy working."
msgstr "Aunque Sarah seguía desnuda, descubrió que era más fácil olvidar su vergüenza cuando estaba ocupada trabajando."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Sarah tried to teach them the small ways of her own people, she could not deny that as they grew, they were children of the tribes."
msgstr "Aunque Sarah intentaba enseñarles los pequeños modales de su propio pueblo, no podía negar que, a medida que crecían, eran hijos de las tribus."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though Thomas was late, few complained, after all it was the prerogative of kings to arrive when they wanted."
msgstr "Aunque Tomás llegaba tarde, pocos se quejaban; después de todo, era prerrogativa de los reyes llegar cuando querían."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though all eyes and hands were on her body, Sarah felt as if there was little she needed to do."
msgstr "Aunque todos los ojos y las manos estaban puestos en su cuerpo, Sarah sentía que no tenía mucho que hacer."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though as she grew bigger with each passing day, there were the occasional practical challenges."
msgstr "Aunque con cada día que pasaba crecía más, surgían ocasionales desafíos prácticos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though by Sarah's decree she was the head of it, the truth was that the family was a pit of vipers."
msgstr "Aunque por decreto de Sarah era su jefa, la verdad es que la familia era un nido de víboras."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though carved from wood, it was unmistakenly a rose. The petals flowed as if they were no different from the real thing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Though considered a base skill, it's actually a rather challenging one; not without risk."
msgstr "Aunque se considera una habilidad básica, en realidad es bastante difícil; no está exenta de riesgos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though despite that, Sarah could seem the faint resemblance."
msgstr "Aun así, Sarah parecía guardar una tenue semejanza."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though hard to place, it was impossible to deny that it felt good."
msgstr "Aunque difícil de precisar, era imposible negar que se sentía bien."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he didn't fill her up, she could feel him hitting the right spots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he had pulled out, his grip on her body remained, keeping her in place."
msgstr "Aunque se había retirado, su agarre sobre su cuerpo persistía, manteniéndola en su sitio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he switched between herself and Mary, it was Sarah who he desired most, and it was Sarah that spend most evenings in his bedroom."
msgstr "Aunque alternaba entre ella y Mary, era Sarah a quien él deseaba más, y era Sarah la que pasaba la mayoría de las tardes en su habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he walked, he almost moved as quickly as a man running."
msgstr "Aunque caminaba, casi se movía tan rápido como un hombre corriendo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he was older in age, close to fifty Sarah imagined, he had kept himself in strong shape."
msgstr "Aunque era mayor, Sarah imaginaba que tenía casi los cincuenta, se había mantenido en gran forma."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he was worn and battered, the armor was relatively well maintained."
msgstr "Aunque estaba gastado y maltrecho, la armadura estaba relativamente bien conservada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though he wore a plated armor, he seemed to move as if it weighed nothing."
msgstr "Aunque llevaba una armadura de placas, se movía como si pesara nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though here, she was just a girl. No title or homeland to speak of."
msgstr "Aunque aquí era solo una muchacha. Sin título ni patria de la que hablar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his expression was stern, Sarah could detect a hint of worry in his face."
msgstr "Aunque su expresión era severa, Sarah podía detectar un rastro de preocupación en su rostro."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his face and body were marked with scars, nothing about him read as dangerous, or at least not the cruel kind."
msgstr "Aunque su rostro y cuerpo llevaban marcas de cicatrices, nada en él transmitía peligro, o al menos no el tipo cruel."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though his shoulders still hung low, she hoped that his crown weighed a little less on him now."
msgstr "Aunque sus hombros aún colgaban bajos, esperaba que su corona pesara un poco menos para él ahora."

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Though his standing has faded, his reputation among the Eternal Court remains significant."
msgstr "Aunque su posición ha menguado, su reputación ante la Corte Eterna sigue siendo considerable."

msgctxt "speaker:Oryon"
msgid "Though how you did it, well...I look forward to hearing that story some day."
msgstr "Aunque no sé cómo lo lograste, bueno... me gustaría escuchar esa historia algún día."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though in theory, any man could promote himself, the truth was that the elections were hardly anything that could be called fair."
msgstr "Aunque en teoría cualquier hombre podía promoverse a sí mismo, la verdad es que las elecciones apenas podían llamarse justas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it has been years since she was last here, she can walk the hall by memory."
msgstr "Aunque han pasado años desde que estuvo por última vez aquí, puede recorrer el pasillo por memoria."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it never quite came natural to her, she learned plenty in time."
msgstr "Aunque nunca le resultó del todo natural, aprendió bastante con el tiempo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it raged, in pain at each removal, it raged at anything but her."
msgstr "Aunque rugía, con dolor en cada extracción, rugía contra todo menos contra ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it seemed near to her, Sarah quickly realized it was an optical illusion."
msgstr "Aunque parecía estar cerca de ella, Sarah pronto se dio cuenta de que era una ilusión óptica."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was a fine flower, it possessed nothing that made it dangerous. Or even magical for that part."
msgstr "Aunque era una flor hermosa, no poseía nada que la hiciera peligrosa. Ni siquiera mágica, por así decirlo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was night, the bright moon and a cloudless sky cast a pale light over everything."
msgstr "Aunque era de noche, la luna brillante y un cielo sin nubes proyectaban una luz pálida sobre todo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was now close to night, the streets were still full of life."
msgstr "Aunque ya era casi de noche, las calles aún estaban llenas de vida."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was slurred beyond comprehension, the voice was familiar enough to her that she knew who it was."
msgstr "Aunque estaba entrecortado hasta el punto de ser incomprensible, la voz era lo suficientemente familiar para ella como para saber quién era."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it was underground, a soft glow of blueish light filled up the cave."
msgstr "Aunque estaba bajo tierra, una suave luz de tono azul iluminaba la cueva."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though it wasn't easy, she slowly felt the weight of all her circumstances, slip away."
msgstr "Aunque no fue fácil, sintió lentamente cómo el peso de todas sus circunstancias se desvanecía."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though much of the city filled with awe, there was one element that forever troubled her."
msgstr "Aunque gran parte de la ciudad estaba llena de asombro, había un elemento que la perturbaba para siempre."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though none could say why, everyone could feel the item reverberate. A thing that commanded respect, awe."
msgstr "Aunque nadie podía decir por qué, todos sentían cómo el objeto vibraba. Era algo que exigía respeto y admiración."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though partially ruined, the building still impressed on each of them with its vast size."
msgstr "Aunque parcialmente destruida, la edificación seguía impresionándoles con su enorme magnitud."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she could see neither fully believed her niceties, they still appreciated them. Each smiled."
msgstr "Aunque ella no podía verlos ni creía del todo en sus amabilidades, aún las apreciaban. Cada una sonrió."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she didn't feel unsafe, she didn't want to risk getting lost in the city at night."
msgstr "Aunque no sentía peligro, no quería arriesgarse a perderse en la ciudad de noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she doubted her views of the events were quite as simple as his."
msgstr "Aunque dudaba de que su visión de los acontecimientos fuera tan sencilla como la suya."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she drank slower than the others, her smaller frame and lighter body ended up suffering nearly as much as them."
msgstr "Aunque bebía más despacio que los demás, su pequeño y ligero cuerpo acabó sufriendo casi tanto como ellos."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had always come to know him as a skilled lover, something else possessed him that night."
msgstr "Aunque siempre lo había conocido como un amante hábil, algo más lo poseía esa noche."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had become quite a bit more relaxed around her, Samayra remained always somewhat anxious."
msgstr "Aunque se había relajado bastante con ella, Samayra seguía sintiendo siempre cierta ansiedad."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had heard the stories of her father and seen the drawings in her picture book, Sarah still felt her breath stolen from her."
msgstr "Aunque había oído las historias de su padre y visto los dibujos en su libro de imágenes, Sarah todavía sintió que se le robaba el aliento."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had managed to make some progress on her own, she realized that Metis' instruction was invaluable."
msgstr "Aunque había logrado avanzar por su cuenta, se dio cuenta de que las enseñanzas de Metis eran invaluables."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had met with Maeiv a few times now, she had in truth not truly gotten to know her."
msgstr "Aunque había conocido a Maeiv algunas veces ahora, en verdad no la había conocido realmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she had set out with a clear goal, it wasn't long before Sarah found herself starting to become distracted."
msgstr "Aunque había partido con un objetivo claro, no tardó en verse distraída."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she looked forward to learning a new skill, Sarah wasn't all to sure what to make of the man himself."
msgstr "Aunque esperaba aprender una nueva habilidad, Sarah no estaba muy segura de qué pensar del tipo."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Though she might have enjoyed it, Sarah had no illusions that these men were here for their own relief."
msgstr "Aunque quizás disfrutara de ello, Sarah no tenía ilusiones de que esos hombres estuvieran allí por su propio alivio."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
